{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages","id":644997,"title":"Hunters vs mages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-29T22:48:12-07:00","id":644997,"title":"Hunters vs mages","content":"Something that has bugged me for a while. Different compacts and conspiracies hunt mages but the thing is that awakened magic drives people mad, so I would assume that (ignoring bannishers) mage hunters would be rare. Not only that but I would also assume that unless the hunter was dealing with a weaker mage that the mage would obliterate them, removing the small few hunters whom go after the awakened","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3965-andresmo23","name":"Andresmo23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T23:35:43-07:00","id":645062,"title":"","content":"Being witness of magic does not makes you mad - it makes you Unstable. But yes, you are forgetting the precise nature of encounter. That's why I treat Witch Hunters as &quot;Sleepwalkers gone wrong&quot; in that they do not have normal Sleeping Curse BUT THEY STILL HUNT MAGES.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T23:43:02-07:00","id":645064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andresmo23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages#post644997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that has bugged me for a while. Different compacts and conspiracies hunt mages but the thing is that awakened magic drives people mad, so I would assume that (ignoring bannishers) mage hunters would be rare. Not only that but I would also assume that unless the hunter was dealing with a weaker mage that the mage would obliterate them, removing the small few hunters whom go after the awakened</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters generally hunt witches, who may or may not be Awakened Mages; also, there's a reason that <i>Witchfinders</i> provides much weaker mages than the Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T00:07:38-07:00","id":645072,"title":"","content":"Well, mage defenses aren't absolute, so the trick would be hit them hard and fast before they can get a chance to breathe, and by the numbers the average mage doesn't even have a rating in every arcana. The hunter would have to be smart and brutal.<br /> <br /> When you get to conspiracies, a mage hunter can have some very effective endowments, considering the endowment creation system. Attacks that do agg damage, With defend a hunter could reduce the dice pools for a mage's attacks by up to 5, the luck to turn a hunter's successes into exceptional successes, immunity to lethal damage and/or bashing damage, or increase their relevant dice pools to 16 or above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T00:33:38-07:00","id":645105,"title":"","content":"Most Endowments turn you into a Sleepwalker. Only Advanced Armory and Relic do not (and some Relics will be an exception)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T00:39:27-07:00","id":645127,"title":"","content":"Also, the obvious Supernal Magic causing integrity breaking points is a new thing for 2ed, so it wasn't a continuity problem in 1ed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T01:40:41-07:00","id":645178,"title":"","content":"It did still fade from memory, though, which is the larger problem.<br /> <br /> In short, only use the Awakened as adversaries in Tier 3 games, and even then be prepared to die very quickly unless it's a particularly low-powered or softhearted mage (in which case why are you Hunting them?)<br /> <br /> Some of the Hunter 1e powers flat-out wouldn't work on rules-as-Mage Awakened, either (Excision) but Hunter's full of things like that. My favorite's the anti-Mummy splat in Mortal Remains that bases their schtick around something the Arisen template prohibits. Part of its toolboxey joy.<br /> <br /> Just use Witches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T01:56:49-07:00","id":645184,"title":"","content":"Reminds me a bit of <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/clef101\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.scp-wiki.net/clef101</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T02:20:25-07:00","id":645189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645184#post645184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reminds me a bit of <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/clef101\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.scp-wiki.net/clef101</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Ha, nice read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T03:06:40-07:00","id":645202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andresmo23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages#post644997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that has bugged me for a while. Different compacts and conspiracies hunt mages but the thing is that awakened magic drives people mad, so I would assume that (ignoring bannishers) mage hunters would be rare. Not only that but I would also assume that unless the hunter was dealing with a weaker mage that the mage would obliterate them, removing the small few hunters whom go after the awakened</div> </div> </div> </div>First, if you decided to make a career of hunting down monsters, you're nuts, already.<br /> <br /> Second, even with the effects of Quiescence, people can grasp enough of what's happening. It makes hunting Mages a very tricky experience for Hunters, but not an impossible one.<br /> <br /> Third, it isn't so hard to come up with ways to make someone immune to Quiescence. A lot of Hunters are more than a little touched by the supernatural themselves, anyway.<br /> <br /> And fourth, it isn't so hard. A Mage aware of her opponent is really tough for a Hunter. But so are all the splats. Cunning, surprise, preparation and a healthy dose of luck. Every Hunter need'em.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T07:57:39-07:00","id":645426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645178#post645178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, only use the Awakened as adversaries in Tier 3 games, and even then be prepared to die very quickly unless it's a particularly low-powered or softhearted mage (in which case why are you Hunting them?)</div> </div> </div> </div> This always left me with a bad taste in my mouth. <br /> <br /> Granted, that's something that I just always had an issue with. I think all supernaturals should have an innate bane, be it vampire, werewolf, mage, changeling, geister, mummy, beast, demon, what-have-you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-30-2015, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T09:01:33-07:00","id":645456,"title":"","content":"Mages do have an innate bane, Paradox. Sleepers make it worse. Unless you mean something else when you say &quot;bane.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T10:41:15-07:00","id":645558,"title":"","content":"I always assumed that any Major splat no longer counts as a Sleepwalker anymore. They're aware. I've since been made aware that this wasn't the intent of the text, but if you're running Hunter and not Mage, I'd consider ruling that Hunters don't count for the purposes of forgetting and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T12:34:59-07:00","id":645704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages do have an innate bane, Paradox. Sleepers make it worse. Unless you mean something else when you say &quot;bane.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I think what MCN means is an exploitable weakness that allows Hunters to level the playing field. Paradox is a problem for magi, but it's not really something you can exploit easily. It's more an issue the mage will have to deal with after the Hunter has already been blasted to pieces.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T13:55:24-07:00","id":645859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645704#post645704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think what MCN means is an exploitable weakness that allows Hunters to level the playing field. Paradox is a problem for magi, but it's not really something you can exploit easily. It's more an issue the mage will have to deal with after the Hunter has already been blasted to pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or does it? Any organisation larger than cell will have their &quot;libraries&quot; - and with few cases or evidence, any Hunter can deduces that mages are weaker ( or riskier ) around the Sleepers. Not only Sleepers makes Paradox worsen ( adding 9 and 8 again to rolls in 2ED ), Sleepers make natural help for Hunters in direct conflict - it's more logical to fight with spell slinging witch than the witch hunters that want to put her down. I assume any group older than few years - both Compacts and Conspiracies - will know it as to well how to bite mages.<br /> <br /> Hey, you just give me idea how Hunters are hunting Awakened - <b>By cornering them in public places. Also, threatening the lives of their close ones. Witch Hunters are typical terrorists!</b><br /> <br /> Thanks, I have mine Hunters-As-Enemies plotline for mine <b>Mage</b> game I run.<b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-30-2015, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T14:04:08-07:00","id":645867,"title":"","content":"9 and even 8 again isn't exactly much of an edge against something that can wipe you out of existence with a feeling. Or simply turn you from a hunter to a mild-mannered accountant.<br /> <br /> Hunters aren't made to hunt mages so it's probably best to keep them out of it.<br /> <br /> Hopefully we'll get second edition witch rules so we can have something similar to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-30-2015, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T15:41:08-07:00","id":645962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645867#post645867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">9 and even 8 again isn't exactly much of an edge against something that can wipe you out of existence with a feeling. Or simply turn you from a hunter to a mild-mannered accountant.<br /> <br /> Hunters aren't made to hunt mages so it's probably best to keep them out of it.<br /> <br /> Hopefully we'll get second edition witch rules so we can have something similar to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters will take what they can get. The whole point of most Hunter games is winning against superior, more powerful entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T16:49:27-07:00","id":646092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645859#post645859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, you just give me idea how Hunters are hunting Awakened - <b>By cornering them in public places. Also, threatening the lives of their close ones. Witch Hunters are typical terrorists!</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that. Hunters who figure out how Sleepers have a deleterious effect on Supernal Magic would also probably throw hapless crowds at a mage as cannon fodder. Rouse the rabble, call up the torches and pitchforks, get a good old fashioned witch hunt started. Then wait a hundred feet away with a high powered sniper rifle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T16:50:59-07:00","id":646094,"title":"","content":"I guess I'm different. I think a Mage would figure out a way to set any Hunters off the trail rather than obliterate them. If a Mage goes around putting every Hunter that comes along into the dead book then they would soon have other Mages hunting them as well. A Mage might have trouble facing an army of hunters, banishers, the Veil, and Archmages. I don't get why hunters versus supernatural creature 'x' always comes down to frontal assaults in conversation. Hunters can bring down supernaturals unintentionally just by drawing attention to them. A Hunter could be the end of a Mage without harboring any ill intent. In theory, a Mage would squash hunters, but I think in practice a hunter would never find a Mage that wasn't a complete noob or a banisher, something like that. Any Mage dumb or inexperienced enough to be found by a hunter is probably weak enough to be killed by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T17:10:15-07:00","id":646113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646094#post646094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory, a Mage would squash hunters, but I think in practice a hunter would never find a Mage that wasn't a complete noob or a banisher, something like that. Any Mage dumb or inexperienced enough to be found by a hunter is probably weak enough to be killed by one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other way to think about it is ... any mage that would be on a hunter's radar is probably powerful and un-Wise enough to have drawn that attention in the first place. So they'd be both powerful and on the low end of the Morality scale. Because, like Dave said, why else would you be hunting them? A mage that is weak is already pretty subtle, as is a mage that is Wise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T22:18:59-07:00","id":646354,"title":"","content":"Well, it also depends on the &quot;Skill&quot; level of how optimized the Mage uses his magic as well as the thematic scenario he accompanies within the game.<br /> <br /> I mean, really, a crying widow in a funeral home is probably not going to put up much of a fight most of the time in that scenario. Likewise, the corporate overlord of Chicago who regularly uses his magic to tilt the odds in his favor with the focus of a surgeon is probably going to be hard to take down. <br /> <br /> Really, I think we should establish the general competency level of the mage in question. Because while I get that mages are powerful as a template, not ever mage is going to have the same &quot;go to&quot; spells, nor will they think to use them the same way. I mean, face it, some mages are genius level intellects who can creatively manipulate spells in all sorts of whacky ways, but they probably aren't representative of &quot;all mages&quot;.<br /> <br /> Another thing to consider is the relative... difference in experience points between mage and hunter PCs. Objectively, we can determine that Mages receive about... 18+ exp worth of stuff as part of the template just counting the starting Arcana dots (the cost of the 6 default arcana dots, while I am unsure of their price in 2e probably does go to around 20 and that's not factoring the other things). Hunters meanwhile don't get as much free stuff, just the option to spend merit dots on Endowments, which I suppose to be fair tend to be rather overpowered for merit dots. Still, probably a good idea to factor that in when designing an encounter.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T01:07:25-07:00","id":646435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646113#post646113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The other way to think about it is ... any mage that would be on a hunter's radar is probably powerful and un-Wise enough to have drawn that attention in the first place. So they'd be both powerful and on the low end of the Morality scale. Because, like Dave said, why else would you be hunting them? A mage that is weak is already pretty subtle, as is a mage that is Wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are many kinds of weakness, and somebody who is quick to use blatant open magic is going to lose their support structure from fellow mages very quickly. Not because they fear those Hunters, but because they fear archmages, or simply because they are human and actually care about sleepers to some extend.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I have never used all the splat books exactly as written in my campaigns. It would make the world rather crowded. So depending on the type of campaign I run, I will focus more or less on one splatbook, increasing or reducing the power of others to better fit the story my group wants to tell. So if I run a Hunter campaign dealing with witches, I am not going to use Mage as is. There is a reason why Hunter has a neat mechanic for monster design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T07:08:59-07:00","id":646627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645456#post645456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages do have an innate bane, Paradox. Sleepers make it worse. Unless you mean something else when you say &quot;bane.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> That's not a bane. Banes are either something physical or a type of energy that the splat cannot abide. Silver and iron are banes; so is salt. Fire and sunlight are energy-based banes. <br /> <br /> Paradox is quirk of magic that makes it less than perfectly reliable and a chance to go wild. Or to make the mage go crazy-bonkers, the mage equivalent of a uncontrolled fear frenzy or promethean falling into torment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645859#post645859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or does it? Any organisation larger than cell will have their &quot;libraries&quot; - and with few cases or evidence, any Hunter can deduces that mages are weaker (or riskier) around the Sleepers. Not only Sleepers makes Paradox worsen ( adding 9 and 8 again to rolls in 2ED ), Sleepers make natural help for Hunters in direct conflict - it's more logical to fight with spell slinging witch than the witch hunters that want to put her down. I assume any group older than few years - both Compacts and Conspiracies - will know it as to well how to bite mages.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hunters have to deal with issues of secrecy as well as your average mage, vamp, or wolf. Not to mention the fact that you're bringing civilians into a fight with monsters. That's not going to go over well with a lot of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T07:26:17-07:00","id":646637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646627#post646627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's not a bane. Banes are either something physical or a type of energy that the splat cannot abide. Silver and iron are banes; so is salt. Fire and sunlight are energy-based banes.<br /> <br /> Paradox is quirk of magic that makes it less than perfectly reliable and a chance to go wild. Or to make the mage go crazy-bonkers, the mage equivalent of a uncontrolled fear frenzy or promethean falling into torment.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I don't think there's any sort of Bane that fits Mage. They're too human.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I'm glad that they don't have anything like a Bane: the illusion of balance is better handled than by enforcing a metaphysical &quot;rock, paper, scissors&quot; relationship between the splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T09:24:25-07:00","id":646848,"title":"","content":"Typically only splats that have the ability to reflexively heal themselves in a fight have banes. Changelings don't have one, and neither do sin eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T09:35:07-07:00","id":646883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646627#post646627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradox is quirk of magic that makes it less than perfectly reliable and a chance to go wild. Or to make the mage go crazy-bonkers, the mage equivalent of a uncontrolled fear frenzy or promethean falling into torment.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what the accepted lore says about Paradox. Paradox is the result of an external force, the Abyss, tainting the world and twisting magic. There's a little bit of the Abyss in Sleepers that warps magic even more when they witness it. Paradox also damages mages, like a bane, if they contain it within themselves.<br /> <br /> Granted, this is supposed to be a Mystery and your theory is probably one that is held by many an esoteric researcher, but the orthodoxy contradicts this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646627#post646627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention the fact that you're bringing civilians into a fight with monsters. That's not going to go over well with a lot of people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure there are Compacts that would not hesitate for a heartbeat to throw hapless bystanders at a mage to weaken one before moving in for the kill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T09:58:01-07:00","id":646910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645859#post645859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or does it? Any organisation larger than cell will have their &quot;libraries&quot; - and with few cases or evidence, any Hunter can deduces that mages are weaker ( or riskier ) around the Sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Magic libraries aren't a thing in my games, personally (In that, just because someone can label their merit as say &quot;The actual Truth behind the World we live in&quot;, doesn't means it'll distinguish stuff the fanbase usually discuss about, lore-wise). Observing paradox and feasibly documenting it would be kinda hard considering how those displays can wreak someone's perception. Consider: Someone somehow remembering a magical shoot-out that witnesses a manifestation paradox is more likely to believe what say, the bible says about sorcerers (communion with Satan and all) then &quot;Oh, he un-intentionally called a manifestation of the unreality that divides us from the realm of enlightenment&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645859#post645859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, you just give me idea how Hunters are hunting Awakened - <b>By cornering them in public places. Also, threatening the lives of their close ones. Witch Hunters are typical terrorists!</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You know why in movies when they need to meet the bad-guys for something they set it up on a public place? Because it's incredibly stupid to start shit in those venues. Normally you land your ass Busted, or get Wasted. Yes, that's a GTA reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T10:18:55-07:00","id":646928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645426#post645426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This always left me with a bad taste in my mouth. <br /> <br /> Granted, that's something that I just always had an issue with. I think all supernaturals should have an innate bane, be it vampire, werewolf, mage, changeling, geister, mummy, beast, demon, what-have-you.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026especially if you don't want mages to be supernatural transhumans, yes; they ought to have some supernatural vulnerabilities as well as supernatural powers. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't think that mages would have <i>one</i> bane, the way vampires or werewolves do; they'd be a lot more personal. You might consider porting <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>'s Echoes into <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>. <br /> <br /> What has never really set well with <i>me</i> is the discrepency between \u201call mortals are subject to Quiescence, save only for Sleepwalkers\u201d (which has generally been presented as \u201cSleepwalker status is the exception that proves the rule, and ought to be a soul-wrenching ordeal to obtain\u201d) and \u201call mortals who have any supernatural capabilities, no matter how minor or easily achieved, are automatically Sleepwalkers\u201d. These always struck me as being based on different underlying assumptions. <br /> <br /> That, and the notion that Sleeper vs. Sleepwalker is strictly a binary thing also bothers me: either you\u2019re completely and absolutely subject to the Sleeping Curse and always forget any encounter you have with Supernal Magic, or the Sleeping Curse has no hold on you and you have no more trouble remembering Supernal Magic than anything else. Never anything in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T10:32:20-07:00","id":646933,"title":"","content":"So you'd prefer stages of repression where the sleeper sort of remembers but dismisses it as something mundane a la Lunacy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T10:44:35-07:00","id":646943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646933#post646933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you'd prefer stages of repression where the sleeper sort of remembers but dismisses it as something mundane a la Lunacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, in fact, how it works. You only get total amnesia if misremembering something as a mundane event is absolutely impossible.<br /> <br /> The kicker for Sleeper Hunters is &quot;witnessing obvious magic&quot;, as well as being the thing that gives mages Paradox, inflicts an automatic Breaking Point on the Sleeper doing the observing. And supernaturally recovering the memory of a spell when Quiescence has taken it provokes <i>another</i> one.<br /> <br /> Also oft-forgot in these kind of conversations is that Sleeper presence doesn't cause spells to fizzle out - it wears them down <i>eventually</i>, but being a Sleeper will not prevent a mage from fireballing you in the face.<br /> <br /> The most important thing's the Breaking Point, though. Not only is the Paradox inflicted not that big an inconvieniance to the mage (it's only a point of Mana to buy it off, after all) but being a Sleeper Mage-Hunter means your career will be short, sad, and pissing Integrity. <br /> <br /> <br /> Sleepwalker is a one dot Merit. Most Tier-3 Hunters are automatically Sleepwalkers anyway. If you want to use the Awakened as enemies, use them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T10:53:08-07:00","id":646951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646848#post646848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Typically only splats that have the ability to reflexively heal themselves in a fight have banes. Changelings don't have one, and neither do sin eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alternatively the splats with banes can be considered the 'bad' splats. They are encouraged to interact with humans and may occasionally kill them. Changeling and Geist and Mage are more likely to be disconnected from the 'muggles' outside of backgrounds, Mortal Remains going so far as to suggest Hunters babysit rather than hunt the first two. Even Promethean and Mummy have detrimental human effects. Demon, too, but I don't think they have banes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T10:57:36-07:00","id":646954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646943#post646943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kicker for Sleeper Hunters is &quot;witnessing obvious magic&quot;, as well as being the thing that gives mages Paradox, inflicts an automatic Breaking Point on the Sleeper doing the observing. And supernaturally recovering the memory of a spell when Quiescence has taken it provokes <i>another</i> one.<br /> <br /> Also oft-forgot in these kind of conversations is that Sleeper presence doesn't cause spells to fizzle out - it wears them down <i>eventually</i>, but being a Sleeper will not prevent a mage from fireballing you in the face.<br /> <br /> The most important thing's the Breaking Point, though. Not only is the Paradox inflicted not that big an inconvieniance to the mage (it's only a point of Mana to buy it off, after all) but being a Sleeper Mage-Hunter means your career will be short, sad, and pissing Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This quote makes me want to run a hunter one shot, with a Mage antagonist, where I describe all events as they remember them after the fact. Including all the weird but explainable circumstantial shit that happened around the Mage, and those bizarre injuries the players received out of nowhere. Probably wouldn't even inform the players it was a Mage, just let them piece it together OoC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T10:57:56-07:00","id":646955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646951#post646951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon, too, but I don't think they have banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glitches can count as those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T11:09:51-07:00","id":646967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646943#post646943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is, in fact, how it works. You only get total amnesia if misremembering something as a mundane event is absolutely impossible.<br /> <br /> The kicker for Sleeper Hunters is &quot;witnessing obvious magic&quot;, as well as being the thing that gives mages Paradox, inflicts an automatic Breaking Point on the Sleeper doing the observing. And supernaturally recovering the memory of a spell when Quiescence has taken it provokes <i>another</i> one.<br /> <br /> Also oft-forgot in these kind of conversations is that Sleeper presence doesn't cause spells to fizzle out - it wears them down <i>eventually</i>, but being a Sleeper will not prevent a mage from fireballing you in the face.<br /> <br /> The most important thing's the Breaking Point, though. Not only is the Paradox inflicted not that big an inconvieniance to the mage (it's only a point of Mana to buy it off, after all) but being a Sleeper Mage-Hunter means your career will be short, sad, and pissing Integrity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sleepwalker is a one dot Merit. Most Tier-3 Hunters are automatically Sleepwalkers anyway. If you want to use the Awakened as enemies, use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the thing where someone uses a powerful hallucinogen to train rookie witch hunters might actually be appropriate then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T12:01:49-07:00","id":647028,"title":"","content":"Changelings do have a bane. Cold iron. It's just a very, very weak bane compared to all the others in other game lines. It bypasses their magical defenses rather than doing bonus damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T12:48:18-07:00","id":647108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646943#post646943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kicker for Sleeper Hunters is \u201cwitnessing obvious magic\u201d, as well as being the thing that gives mages Paradox, inflicts an automatic Breaking Point on the Sleeper doing the observing. And supernaturally recovering the memory of a spell when Quiescence has taken it provokes <i>another</i> one.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646943#post646943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most important thing's the Breaking Point, though. Not only is the Paradox inflicted not that big an inconvieniance to the mage (it's only a point of Mana to buy it off, after all) but being a Sleeper Mage-Hunter means your career will be short, sad, and pissing Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh; here\u2019s how I see it: hunters have to cope with Breaking Points for witnessing the supernatural anyway; that\u2019s built into Integrity. So either they\u2019ve got a means of coping with such Breaking Points (perhaps through something like 1e\u2019s Code) or they pretty much have short careers due to mental breakdown no matter <i>what</i> their prey is. And from previous times this has come up, ISTR that the tentative ruling is that a hunter who has immunized himself against Quiescence-triggered Breaking Points (assuming such a thing is possible) would <i>still</i> be subject to the memory-warping effects of Quiescence. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=646943#post646943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleepwalker is a one dot Merit. Most Tier-3 Hunters are automatically Sleepwalkers anyway. If you want to use the Awakened as enemies, use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two points: first, \u201cSleepwalker is a one-dot Merit\u201d, while true, feels like a cop-out, and gets back to the aforementioned discrepency I was talking about<b></b>: whenever someone mentions Sleepers becoming Sleepwalkers in a <b>Mage</b> game, I\u2019m always hearing about how difficult it is to do such a thing, and how rare and special Sleepwalkers are; but whenever someone mentions how much trouble hunters have in coping with the Sleeping Curse, the response is always \u201cjust give them the Sleepwalker Merit\u201d, as if it was the easiest thing in the world. So which is it? Is Sleepwalker a holy grail that most Sleepers never acquire, or is it something that you can get just by joining the right organization? <br /> <br /> Second, what if I want to play a member of the Long Night, a compact of Protestants who are trying to prepare the world for Christ's Second Coming (and who often try to redeem witches)? Or a Loyalist of Thule, a compact of occultist scholars with personal dislike for hubris? He can\u2019t be a member of a Conspiracy, because he's already a member of a Compact; so gaining a supernatural Endowment is out. But the story potential is considerable, assuming it doesn't get trampled by the Sleeping Curse. That leaves several options: <br /> <br /> 1. give the hunter the Sleepwalker Merit; <br /> 2. say that the \u201cmage\u201d isn\u2019t really a mage, but rather a much inferior \u201cwitch\u201d; <br /> 3. say that the hunter is, in fact, a Banisher; <br /> 4. let the story potential get trampled by the Sleeping Curse. <br /> <br /> The problem with the first one is that unless the Sleepwalker Merit is something that could reasonably be acquired in the course of a mage-specific Vigil, having it amounts to being a special snowflake who just happens to have immunity to the single biggest obstacle presented by the chronicle's target. <br /> <br /> The problem with the second is that it puts Mage up on a pedestal that no other gameline gets placed on. Vampire hunters? Sure! Werewolf hunters? OK! Prometheans, changelings, slashers, geists, mummies, demons, or beasts? They each have their own challenges; but they\u2019re all doable. But mages? Here; go play against these inferior mage wannabes instead, little mortals; you can't <i>handle</i> the Truth! <br /> <br /> The problem with the third is like the first: you\u2019re resorting to a special snowflake \u2014 and in this case, one that the targeted mage can legitimately claim is an abomination in its own right, worse than the mage himself. Thematically, this also threatens to undermine the character concept the \u201chunter\u201d's player was going for. <br /> <br /> The problem with the fourth should be self-evident. <br /> <br /> Frankly, the official \u201csolutions\u201d to this dilemma remind me of the old joke about the patient who goes to see the doctor, raises his right hand over his head, and says \u201cit hurts when I do this.\u201d The doctor\u2019s answer? \u201cThen don't do that.\u201d<br /> <br /> IMHO, the problem <i>can</i> be resolved in a satisfactory way if you're willing to budge <i>ever so slightly</i> on what mortals are able to achieve on their own: for instance, allowing hunter 2e\u2019s version of the Code to develop immunity against the Breaking Points caused by specific supernatural phenomena, including Lunacy and Quiescence, and also allowing mundane means to circumvent the memory-warping effects of Quiescence (Network Zero is big on recording everything; and unless the Sleeping Curse is remarkably consistent to the memory alterations done to a group of witnesses, it should be possible to develop an \u201cafter-action report\u201d Tactic that exploits the inconsistencies to piece together what <i>really</i> happened). <br /> <br /> Or, yes, something as simple as letting a hunter use Practical Experience from an encounter with Supernal Magic to buy the Sleepwalker Merit. But somehow that feels too <i>easy</i> for what the Sleeping Curse is supposed to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T13:02:34-07:00","id":647120,"title":"","content":"Both.<br /> <br /> It's a Supernatural Merit - you can't deliberately learn it, just like you can't hit the books to develop telekinesis. But unless you're interested in meta-narrative tricks, reenacting Memento, and a very definite uphill struggle, my advice is to give Hunter player characters intended for a mage-antagonistic game the Merit. Some people <i>are</i> born Sleepwalkers, and don't realize it until they see a spell. It's a contrivance, but one on the same level as &quot;this group is made up entirely of vampires&quot;. Perfectly good device.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;budging?&quot; No - absolutely not. I'm not going to undermine Mage's theme of being separated from friends and family by occult knowledge for the sake of a minority of Hunter Storytellers, not when the Merit's right there. You can either cause Paradox, <i>or</i> not suffer the downsides of being a Sleeper. Not both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T13:15:57-07:00","id":647131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, yes, something as simple as letting a hunter use Practical Experience from an encounter with Supernal Magic to buy the Sleepwalker Merit. But somehow that feels too <i>easy</i> for what the Sleeping Curse is supposed to be. </div> </div> </div>Why? They're already a Hunter, that's not an easy thing to become. The temperement of a Hunter would seem prefectly suited to becoming a sleepwalker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T13:51:57-07:00","id":647158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647131#post647131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? They're already a Hunter, that's not an easy thing to become. The temperement of a Hunter would seem prefectly suited to becoming a sleepwalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess that if someone has become a hunter because of the actions of a mage, that means she sort of remembers those actions and thus probably is a sleepwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T13:55:00-07:00","id":647161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647028#post647028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings do have a bane. Cold iron. It's just a very, very weak bane compared to all the others in other game lines. It bypasses their magical defenses rather than doing bonus damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking about that and I'd consider it more of a problem with their powers than the splat themselves, similar to Mages paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T14:38:05-07:00","id":647225,"title":"","content":"Cold Iron is an edge case. But it still fits the pattern actually. Goblin fruits mean that a changeling can sort of heal but not really. The cold iron affecting defenses is likewise sort of a bane but not really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T14:47:31-07:00","id":647231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647120#post647120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both.<br /> <br /> It's a Supernatural Merit - you can't deliberately learn it, just like you can't hit the books to develop telekinesis. But unless you're interested in meta-narrative tricks, reenacting Memento, and a very definite uphill struggle, my advice is to give Hunter player characters intended for a mage-antagonistic game the Merit. Some people <i>are</i> born Sleepwalkers, and don't realize it until they see a spell. It's a contrivance, but one on the same level as \u201cthis group is made up entirely of vampires\u201d. Perfectly good device.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may not be able to deliberately <i>learn</i> it; but you apparently <i>can</i> deliberately <i>acquire</i> it: just join, say, the Malleus Maleficatorum, or a cult; or apprentice yourself to a thaumaturge.* As for the level of contrivance: a group of hunters that all happen to be Sleepwalkers strikes me as a bit more unusual than a group of vampires, especially since there are social factors designed to bring vampires together and there are <i>no</i> factors (prior to encountering Supernal magic) that would even make people <i>aware</i> of Sleepwalker status, let alone draw them together; and on top of that, it seems even more unlikely that such a group would <i>just happen</i> to confront a mage\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026unless there\u2019s something about Sleepwalker status that subconsciously draws you to mages? If Sleepwalkers tend to cluster arond mages, then a cell of Sleepwalkers dealing with a mage wouldn\u2019t be as much of a contrivance as a cell of Sleepwalkers <i>not</i> dealing with a mage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647120#post647120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for \u201cbudging?\u201d No - absolutely not. I'm not going to undermine Mage's theme of being separated from friends and family by occult knowledge for the sake of a minority of Hunter Storytellers, not when the Merit's right there. You can either cause Paradox, <i>or</i> not suffer the downsides of being a Sleeper. Not both.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, I wasn\u2019t necessarily meaning you <i>in particular</i> budging; it was a general \u201cyou\u201d. The sorts of things I\u2019m suggesting would be more of a Hunter thing anyway; and when push come to shove, what <i>really</i> matters is whether the <i>Storyteller</i> is willing to budge. <br /> <br /> With that said, you are of course the Mage line developer and free to do with Mage whatever you want, regardless of whether it makes sense to me; and I\u2019m grateful that you\u2019re at least willing to discuss the matter. I do think you\u2019re overestimating the effects on Mage\u2019s themes of isolation that would come from the potential availability of partial immunity to and/or workarounds for the Sleeping Curse on the one hand (especially if there are mitigating factors such as the partial immunity coming at a price and the workaround requiring <i>work</i> every time you use it), and underestimating the interest that might exist for such things in the Hunter fanbase; though I could be wrong on either or both counts. <br /> <br /> Put another way, what\u2019s wrong with both causing Paradox and not suffering (some of) the downsides of being a Sleeper if you have to suffer <i>other</i> consequences instead? <br /> <br /> <hr />* You later express an interest in preserving the theme of isolation brought by the Sleeping Curse. That latter option \u2014 a Sleeper apprenticing herself to a thaumaturge in order to become a Sleepwalker \u2014 strikes me as a particularly easy way to bypass that issue entirely (which I do <i>not</i> consider to be a good thing): get your family members to learn some defensive magic from a thaumaturge, and presto! Not only are they Sleepwalkers now, but they\u2019ve also got a means to protect themselves when your enemies come calling; and they\u2019re also thaumaturges in their own right, able to pass the Sleepwalker status on to others in the same way they acquired it. <br /> <br /> Unless thaumaturgy can\u2019t be taught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T14:59:51-07:00","id":647238,"title":"","content":"In circumstances such as this it might be reasonable to insert a house rule on the order of, &quot;Mortals can remember supernal magic (though perhaps not in perfect detail) when it caused them to suffer Integrity loss, though buying back Integrity lost this way erases the memory.&quot; and &quot;Characters who've lost a few points of integrity to Supernal magic may qualify for the Sleepwalker merit, representing their gradual ascent out of the Lie.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 08-31-2015, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T15:06:36-07:00","id":647246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647231#post647231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless thaumaturgy can\u2019t be taught.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be unteachable for it to be incredibly plain that you're blowing off the investment of time and dedication involved to become a thaumaturgical practitioner. The requisite <i>several years of concerted study</i> in combination with the very real possibility that there <i>are</i> factors that prevent someone from getting the forms to yield results means saying it's a &quot;particularly easy&quot; way to bypass the Curse is laughable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T15:18:28-07:00","id":647276,"title":"","content":"The principle is still sound: there are ways to intentionally acquire certain supernatural merits, which potentially makes them a viable backdoor for deliberately turning Sleepers into Sleepwalkers. Unless some care is taken with such things, they could be used to undermine Mage's isolation theme; and even <i>with</i> precautions taken, they\u2019re a crack in the wall of isolation; if you can live with that much, what\u2019s wrong with one or two other cracks in the wall that are similarly restricted, but open things up <i>just enough</i> to increase the danger posed by mortal antagonists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T15:23:34-07:00","id":647287,"title":"","content":"Mage has an Isolation theme? I thought the theme was delving into things man was not meant to know and getting your head bitten off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T15:26:28-07:00","id":647291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647276#post647276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The principle is still sound: there are ways to intentionally acquire certain supernatural merits, which potentially makes them a viable backdoor for deliberately turning Sleepers into Sleepwalkers. Unless some care is taken with such things, they could be used to undermine Mage's isolation theme; and even <i>with</i> precautions taken, they\u2019re a crack in the wall of isolation; if you can live with that much, what\u2019s wrong with one or two other cracks in the wall that are similarly restricted, but open things up <i>just enough</i> to increase the danger posed by mortal antagonists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, one could argue that providing a viable, but highly traumatic route is closer to their themes. I can just see a Mage obsessed with revealing 'the truth' to his lover, who subjects her to all forms of supernal exposure, shredding her integrity and psyche until she finally snaps and becomes a Sleepwalker. But her experiences with the supernal are forever tainted, and he's cursed her with a life of traumatic reminders and horrific truths that she can do nothing about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T16:33:17-07:00","id":647355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647231#post647231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026unless there\u2019s something about Sleepwalker status that subconsciously draws you to mages? If Sleepwalkers tend to cluster arond mages, then a cell of Sleepwalkers dealing with a mage wouldn\u2019t be as much of a contrivance as a cell of Sleepwalkers <i>not</i> dealing with a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Subconsciously? I would say that Sleepwalkers are drawn to mages, though I wouldn't say it would be subconscious at all. What draws them to mages is the fact that they can <i>clearly remember magic</i>. If you see someone blatantly defying the laws of reality as you know them chances are you're going to go looking for answers, and chances are your search for those answers is going to draw you closer to the mages themselves.<br /> <br /> It would also probably draw you towards more Sleepwalkers in the same position, people who have also seen some shit and went looking for answers. And if that group of Sleepwalkers happen to stumble upon some answers that they really don't like then you're looking at a the beginnings of a potential Hunter cell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T17:15:19-07:00","id":647406,"title":"","content":"I think the isolation is from mortal society. I don't know how explicit the theme is portrayed, but it exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T22:20:49-07:00","id":647681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647291#post647291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, one could argue that providing a viable, but highly traumatic route is closer to their themes. I can just see a Mage obsessed with revealing 'the truth' to his lover, who subjects her to all forms of supernal exposure, shredding her integrity and psyche until she finally snaps and becomes a Sleepwalker. But her experiences with the supernal are forever tainted, and he's cursed her with a life of traumatic reminders and horrific truths that she can do nothing about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds like the forced Awakening of a Banisher, and I would expect the Guardians (and the rest of the Concilium) would soon &quot;have words&quot; with the offending mage,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T00:03:21-07:00","id":647747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647681#post647681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like the forced Awakening of a Banisher, and I would expect the Guardians (and the rest of the Concilium) would soon &quot;have words&quot; with the offending mage,</div> </div> </div> </div>It can end this way, but it also do not make this scenario very likely - heck, even Guardians could force their loved one to become Sleepwalker, just to be with her. And later kill her, if she become truly Banisher, instead of Sleepwalker or stable Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T01:53:24-07:00","id":647783,"title":"","content":"Nobody knows what makes somebody a sleepwalker and what not, but it is good to keep in mind that no Hunter is an ordinary human. If they were ordinary humans they would not end up as a Hunter, but 'forget' all the horrors they witness and they certainly would not start digging into the shadows. So is it really that much weirder to assume that all tier 2 and 3 Hunters have somehow become more than ordinary mortals, and that either having witnessed all the dark things of the world or being trained for it, somehow gave them that Sleepwalker merit or some other merit that achieves the same? Besides, if we are talking about PCs, they are by definition special and if it is NPCs you as the Storyteller are in full control and can explain anything through story anyway.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to throw tier 1 hunters against a true mage, you create a situation that will be extremely hard on the hunters, but is that truly so different from any other splat book as an opponent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T02:40:54-07:00","id":647802,"title":"","content":"This sort of thing comes up so regularly that I think it goes deeper than just a crossover between two particular gamelines. It's more about... the relationship between mages and Sleepers being completely one-sided, I guess. Hunters are just its most visible expression, since they're supposed to be humanity's vanguard in the shadows, but any interaction between them and Awakened mages can be summed up as &quot;lol, nope&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T04:59:04-07:00","id":647865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647108#post647108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two points: first, \u201cSleepwalker is a one-dot Merit\u201d, while true, feels like a cop-out, and gets back to the aforementioned discrepency I was talking about<b></b>: whenever someone mentions Sleepers becoming Sleepwalkers in a <b>Mage</b> game, I\u2019m always hearing about how difficult it is to do such a thing, and how rare and special Sleepwalkers are; but whenever someone mentions how much trouble hunters have in coping with the Sleeping Curse, the response is always \u201cjust give them the Sleepwalker Merit\u201d, as if it was the easiest thing in the world. So which is it? Is Sleepwalker a holy grail that most Sleepers never acquire, or is it something that you can get just by joining the right organization?</div> </div> </div> </div>Corollary: All Hunters themselves are rare and subjected to insane amounts of trauma, both physical and psychic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647108#post647108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may not be able to deliberately <i>learn</i> it; but you apparently <i>can</i> deliberately <i>acquire</i> it: just join, say, the Malleus Maleficatorum, or a cult; or apprentice yourself to a thaumaturge.* As for the level of contrivance: a group of hunters that all happen to be Sleepwalkers strikes me as a bit more unusual than a group of vampires, especially since there are social factors designed to bring vampires together and there are <i>no</i> factors (prior to encountering Supernal magic) that would even make people <i>aware</i> of Sleepwalker status, let alone draw them together; and on top of that, it seems even more unlikely that such a group would <i>just happen</i> to confront a mage\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026unless there\u2019s something about Sleepwalker status that subconsciously draws you to mages? If Sleepwalkers tend to cluster around mages, then a cell of Sleepwalkers dealing with a mage wouldn\u2019t be as much of a contrivance as a cell of Sleepwalkers <i>not</i> dealing with a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize the whole roleplaying process is deliberate, right? From planning plots, to character creation, to experience purchase. <br /> <br /> Do you really find that unfeasible that a group of monster hunters wouldn't come together by their many means when they realize they can retain the memory of their encounters with witch-craft? Because that's like, the angular feature upon which most social constructs are built. Things that people have in common, to spell it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647108#post647108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* You later express an interest in preserving the theme of isolation brought by the Sleeping Curse. That latter option \u2014 a Sleeper apprenticing herself to a thaumaturge in order to become a Sleepwalker \u2014 strikes me as a particularly easy way to bypass that issue entirely (which I do <i>not</i> consider to be a good thing): get your family members to learn some defensive magic from a thaumaturge, and presto! Not only are they Sleepwalkers now, but they\u2019ve also got a means to protect themselves when your enemies come calling; and they\u2019re also thaumaturges in their own right, able to pass the Sleepwalker status on to others in the same way they acquired it. Unless thaumaturgy can\u2019t be taught.</div> </div> </div> </div>With, I'd think, all the complications that could arise from y'know, belonging into a cult. That was gonna be the drawback in Mystery Cult Initiation:<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback: </b>You're in a cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T20:51:05-07:00","id":648554,"title":"","content":"I don't think you need to give the Sleepwalker Merit to all or most Hunters. Not remembering the more precise details of what a Mage did in front of you is not as dangerous as losing Integrity every time you see Supernal magic and the supernatural as a whole. I always thought Hunters didn't suffer Integrity Breaking Points for simply seeing monsters and their powers, but for how badly they might affect the Hunter and his loved ones. And even then, they would still be very hardened. Penalties for Breaking Points related to monsters would probably decrease over time. They pretty much expect horrible things to happen when dealing with monsters, and train extensively for that.<br /> <br /> As for a Tactic that lets Hunters remember Supernal magic, I don't think it's necessary. As far as I know, Tactics are meant to be used right before or in the middle of combat, not after it. Remembering something important about a Mage's spells should be Resolve + Composure or Intelligence + Composure, with teamwork rolls allowed. The spell's Potency might inflict a penalty to this extended action, which might require 5 to 15 successes based on how subtle the Mage was. The Library and Patient Merits really help in this case. However, you can only get an Exceptional Success on this extended action if you are a Sleepwalker.<br /> <br /> If the Hunters are going up against genuine Mages instead of Witches, they might be at a considerable disadvantage in regards to preparation. They could try to bargain and/or threaten the Mages' families, or look for dissidents and potential moles.<br /> <br /> I am not sure what a Bane for Mages could be. These Banes are usually for monsters with very different physiological functions, like vampires and werewolves. Perhaps some kind of Abyssal Poison? Whatever that might be, it would probably be very chaotic in behavior and hard to treat and dispel. Depending on the context of Intrusion, it could also have additional effects, like being self-replicating (Anomaly), mutagenic (Brand), hallucinogenic (Bedlam) or a beacon for more Abyssals (Manifestation). Paradox in the form of versatile substance, so to say.<br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T21:30:44-07:00","id":648570,"title":"","content":"I think the big thing is that witnessing Supernal Magic is <i>always</i> a breaking point towards Integrity. You're either effectively a Sleepwalker or you suffer a breaking point from it. With the way they're designed (unless I'm missing something which I totally could be), you can create a character whose breaking points are tailored in a way that interacting with other supernatural stuff won't affect them. You can't really do that with Supernal Magic.<br /> <br /> Seeing and interacting every day with supernatural creatures isn't going to immunize you to this. You might be used to seeing everybody you know heal up almost instantly from life threatening wounds every day, but if you aren't a Sleepwalker seeing a mage use magic to heal a papercut is still going to cause a breaking point. Regardless of how commonly you experience things like that it will still erode your sanity because that's the nature of the relationship between mortals, the Supernal, and the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-02-2015, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T21:37:53-07:00","id":648572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=648554#post648554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They could try to bargain and/or threaten the Mages' families.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be at the very top of the list of things not to do unless you want your remaining days to be very short and extremely painful, to say nothing of the fact that any mage with a modicum of foresight and intelligence has taken measures to protect family and friends. It should always be remembered that in the WOD, there really are fates worse than death, and mages are uniquely equipped to administer such punishments. If I were a Hunter, I would stick with the &quot;easy&quot; prey like vampires... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T00:24:23-07:00","id":648625,"title":"","content":"In the character creation section it lists several questions players can answer about their character to inspire background and personality, one of those questions is 'what supernatural encounter have you forgotten?' based on the idea that in the world of darkness almost everyone has had a brush with the supernatural but sanity made them forget. Sleepwalkers, those who start out with the merit, are the ones who didn't forget and that experience continues to haunt them, drawing them towards hints of the supernatural in an effort to explain what happened and that they aren't nuts. A group of hunters focused on mages would be brought together by the fact that they were already hunting supernatural knowledge when they met. Possibly even on the trail of some beastie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T00:53:04-07:00","id":648636,"title":"","content":"There's a merit in Banishers, I don't remember what it's called right now, that involves wielding Paradox as a weapons. It's one I'd be open to letting Mage-focused Sleepwalker Hunters purchase (allowing for &quot;this character doesn't suffer the personal drawbacks of being a Sleeper, but their presence can still inflict paradox&quot;). But even if the Hunter is only focused on harmful Mages, the Awakened community in general is going to see the character as an Abyssal taint/intrusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T00:55:39-07:00","id":648645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647287#post647287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage has an Isolation theme? I thought the theme was delving into things man was not meant to know and getting your head bitten off.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say those like they're conflicting themes. Your diving in leaves your old life behind. The fact that the &quot;enlightened&quot; is now utterly different and apart from those who are still staring at the cave wall is kind of central to Plato's parable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T00:55:57-07:00","id":648646,"title":"","content":"Just thought I should add that any knowledgeable compact or conspiracy would be on the watch for hunters that are especially strong willed when faced with such abominations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T07:30:01-07:00","id":648940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=648554#post648554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you need to give the Sleepwalker Merit to all or most Hunters. Not remembering the more precise details of what a Mage did in front of you is not as dangerous as losing Integrity every time you see Supernal magic and the supernatural as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though there could easily be Sleeper Hunters that roll 10+ dice on their Breaking Point rolls and have become pretty powerful via regular interaction with Mages. Basically unknowingly using Beats from supernal Magic induced breaking points as their high speed highway to becoming really dangerous and powerful quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T08:44:06-07:00","id":649004,"title":"","content":"And besides, all Supernatural Merits impart Sleepwalker status, as I understand it, including Endowments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T11:07:43-07:00","id":649126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649004#post649004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And besides, all Supernatural Merits impart Sleepwalker status, as I understand it, including Endowments.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Merits that are inherent to the character provide Sleepwalker status (e.g., psychic merits, Lucifuge endowments, etc.). Magical equipment (e.g., weapons, artifacts, potions, etc.) would not change a ordinary mortal into a Sleepwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T11:11:01-07:00","id":649127,"title":"","content":"I actually really like the idea of an &quot;After-Action Report&quot; Tactic. So yeah, everyone has rolled their Breaking Points and no one quite remembers the encounter the way it actually happened. Then you all sit down and discuss what you experienced, and where there are inconsistencies, you know magic must have been involved. You might be able to pice together something close to the actual events, even if it's not 100% accurate.<br /> <br /> I'd say on a Dramatic Failure you piece together something very different from what actually happened but believe it to be accurate. On a failure you just can't work out anything that makes sense, on a success you get a general idea of what really happened, and on an exceptional success you get a few specific details (maybe expressed by allowing you to ask questions of the Storyteller).<br /> <br /> Such a Tactic would fit really well into Thorbes' idea of a game where the ST just describes what the characters remember, instead of what *really* happened. Which, in my honest opinion, is exactly what you'd want out of an Sleeper hunters vs. Awakened Mage(s) chronicle. If you're remembering things exactly as they actually happened, either the antagonist isn't really an Awakened or you're not really sleepers. I'd much rather see in-game workarounds to the problem, like the suggested Tactic, than change the way Supernal magic affects Sleepers for the sake of the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T11:29:46-07:00","id":649142,"title":"","content":"It should probably work on Lunacy and general past-tense mind control and illusions, providing they were together, or at least nearby, when they got their minds bent, so you could still have sleepers and other dangers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T11:55:39-07:00","id":649154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649142#post649142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should probably work on Lunacy and general past-tense mind control and illusions, providing they were together, or at least nearby, when they got their minds bent, so you could still have sleepers and other dangers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. Reminds me very much of the Doctor Who series 6 premier, where they develop a couple of techniques to remind themselves when they've encountered silents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:30:04-07:00","id":649314,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how useful the tactic would actually be. I mean, the tactic only works if it's possible to rationalise the magic. And that would mean you don't need to reconstruct what happened, you know what happened, you've merely altered how it happened. To give an example, if a mage throws a fireball, the cell rationalises it as the mage firing a gun. Through differences in story they work out that it's magic... ok, but they presumably needed to suspect it was magic already and they already know what basically happened: the mage tried to kill them.<br /> That's just my thoughts on it, maybe others have a better idea how it would work.<br /> <br /> More broadly, I'm not so sure that the Lie is really the biggest problem. Sleepers still notice uncanny things happening around the mage (You lock a mage up, he appears outside, somehow; You shoot a mage, they're fine the next day etc.), and magi have lots of occult paraphenalia around which makes them look all the more like wizards. The fact you can't actually see them throw a bolt of lightning is not really that big a barrier. They're still creepy occultists who meet in secret groups and run conspiracies. You don't need to see the Nemean summon a spirit to find out he's the head of a criminal outfit and meets with other secretive groups at regular intervals (including at least two other major criminal groups).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:35:43-07:00","id":649323,"title":"","content":"If they don't make video recordings of their actions, TFV is likely to at least maintain radio contact with handlers so the mind tricks will be less effective against a conspiracy. TFV isn't the only conspiracy that might get wise. The whole point of a conspiracy is that a cell would have superiors providing oversight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T14:46:18-07:00","id":649336,"title":"","content":"From a game standpoint, what's the purpose for making people forget about magic, anyways?<br /> <br /> It seems like it just gives mages more leeway to break their own rules, while simultaneously keeping the unsubtle safe from most of their victims.<br /> <br /> It seems like a variant of Lunacy, which is designed to protect or at least hide werewolves while also promoting a flight or fight response. But why would whatever is making memories of magic disappear want to protect mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-02-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:05:21-07:00","id":649350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From a game standpoint, what's the purpose for making people forget about magic, anyways? </div> </div> </div>It's a part of The Lie. It's so fundamental to the setting, the very name of the game refers to 'Awakening' from the Lie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems like it just gives mages more leeway to break their own rules, while simultaneously keeping the unsubtle safe from most of their victims. </div> </div> </div>That's not a good thing. Most of the mage factions would very much like people to be sleepwalkers; sleepers are a problem. It makes it easier to be horrible to sleepers, but it makes it a lot harder to help them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:14:55-07:00","id":649359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649350#post649350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a part of The Lie. It's so fundamental to the setting, the very name of the game refers to 'Awakening' from the Lie.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's not a good thing. Most of the mage factions would very much like people to be sleepwalkers; sleepers are a problem. It makes it easier to be horrible to sleepers, but it makes it a lot harder to help them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate that but why, for example, is paradox 'not that big of an inconvenience to a mage,' while to mortals it causes breaking points and mental gymnastics and occasionally amnesia and keeps mortals from really having a stake in the game?<br /> <br /> Also because I'm sensing some hackles raised, try not to see this as an attack on a game, I'm just trying to figure out why the rules are the way they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:25:22-07:00","id":649364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649359#post649359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate that but why, for example, is paradox 'not that big of an inconvenience to a mage,' while to mortals it causes breaking points and mental gymnastics and occasionally amnesia and keeps mortals from really having a stake in the game?<br /> <br /> Also because I'm sensing some hackles raised, try not to see this as an attack on a game, I'm just trying to figure out why the rules are the way they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that breaking point for mortals is also an inconvenience for mages. Mages generally <i>want</i> to share their magic with those close to them, they <i>want</i> everyone to know of magic and be able to awaken themselves, they <i>want</i> magic to be a known and accepted thing. The Lie prevents that. It forces them apart from their friends and loved ones because that is a piece of their life that they are completely unable to share with them, and if they try all they'd be doing is literally driving those close to them insane. It forces them into isolation.<br /> <br /> Mages would probably love for their to be a quick and easy way to make people Sleepwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:33:30-07:00","id":649370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649364#post649364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages would probably love for their to be a quick and easy way to make people Sleepwalkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>*That doesn't involve vampires or fae helping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:48:07-07:00","id":649423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=648940#post648940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though there could easily be Sleeper Hunters that roll 10+ dice on their Breaking Point rolls and have become pretty powerful via regular interaction with Mages. Basically unknowingly using Beats from supernal Magic induced breaking points as their high speed highway to becoming really dangerous and powerful quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div> You're right. If we suppose you can use something like that system from 1ed Hunter where you can fiddle with the hierarchy of &quot;sins&quot;, but for Integrity, we can easily roll that many dice.<br /> <br /> Let's imagine a Hunter that has Resolve 3, Composure 3 and Integrity 7. He also has the Favored Weapon Merit, and is carrying said weapon. He has Meditative Mind 4, and meditated on that day. He kills a Slasher that is trying to murder a hostage. He went inside the location of the hostages with a plan in mind, so it is premeditated murder (-5 penalty). The Hunter has the Pragmatic Virtue. One of the hostages is a member of his Cell and a close friend. If we choose to ignore the -5 penalty by saying he did it for the Vigil and we spend a willpower point, this is what we roll:<br /> <br /> Resolve + Composure + Integrity + Favored Weapon + Fulfilling Virtue + Protecting Loved One + Willpower Point + Meditative Mind = 3 + 3 + 1 + 2 + 1 + 2 + 2 + 3 = 17 dice! And don't forget 10 Again.<br /> <br /> Granted, this is a very specific scenario created with bonuses in mind, but if Sleeper Hunters are going up against Mages, they better get all the bonuses they can to keep their Integrity in place. A Beat and a Willpower every now and then also help. The ST should keep Breaking Point rolls caused by witnessing Supernal magic to a minimum, methinks. The Sleeper Curse has that name for a reason, however, and so Sleeper Hunters should not be immune to such rolls.<br /> <br /> That After Action Report Tactic doesn't sound so bad, now that Charlaquin described it with more detail. Perhaps getting an Exceptional Success on said Tactic lets you re-roll a failed Breaking Point and keep the best result of the two rolls.<br /> <br /> In any case, worsening Paradox with their observation of Supernal magic should still be a risk. There could be a Tactic that increases the chance of Paradox hitting the Mage instead of the Hunters or bystanders. We already have Tactics that do borderline supernatural stuff. For example, Bait And Switch provokes a werewolf into a frenzy but makes him attack his own pack. Deprogramming lets you remove mind control. Effigy lets you trap Spirits within inanimate objects, and may work on Geister for the purposes of permanently killing Sin-Eaters, if the ST says so.<br /> <br /> So, it's not like going up against Mages instead of Witches always results in a downward spiral of Integrity loss and insanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-02-2015, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:51:25-07:00","id":649443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649370#post649370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*That doesn't involve vampires or fae helping.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems like there would be ways to get around it, with control over ghosts and spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:05:07-07:00","id":649491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649364#post649364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It forces them apart from their friends and loved ones because that is a piece of their life that they are completely unable to share with them, and if they try all they'd be doing is literally driving those close to them insane. It forces them into isolation.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, A thousands times this!<br /> <br /> The Quiescence is the basis for mages' alienation in the WOD from those people most important to them. These people cannot only not partake of, see or understand a mage's magic, using it in front of them actually risks hurting their very souls and sanity (i.e., Integrity breaking points).<br /> <br /> Awakening is glorious because of new understanding and abilities, but completely terrifying in the recognition of the mortal prison that is the Lie, and so very isolating because these new insights and powers can never truly be shared. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T17:15:20-07:00","id":649550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649423#post649423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You're right. If we suppose you can use something like that system from 1ed Hunter where you can fiddle with the hierarchy of \u201csins\u201d, but for Integrity, we can easily roll that many dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cThe Code\u201d, yes. Note that the Code has never been a \u201cfree lunch\u201d; in order to gain immunity from further degeneration checks of a particular type, you needed to saddle yourself with some psychological quirks. I'm not sure that Hunter 2e's equivalent to the Code should necessarily work the same way; but I\u2019d prefer that the general premise be similar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649423#post649423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, this is a very specific scenario created with bonuses in mind, but if Sleeper Hunters are going up against Mages, they better get all the bonuses they can to keep their Integrity in place. A Beat and a Willpower every now and then also help. The ST should keep keep Breaking Point rolls caused by witnessing Supernal magic to a minimum, methinks. The Sleeper Curse has that name for a reason, however, and so Sleeper Hunters should not be immune to such rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Broadening this a bit, I think that hunters should have an easier time than regular mortals overall dealing with encounters with the supernatural. That is, after all, the whole point of the Vigil, IMHO. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649423#post649423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That After Action Report Tactic doesn't sound so bad, now that Charlaquin described it with more detail. Perhaps getting an Exceptional Success on said Tactic lets you re-roll a failed Breaking Point and keep the best result of the two rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I didn't go into detail because that would have caused the minutiae to overwhelm the broader put I was going for: hunters ought to be able to find ways to cope with supernatural hurdles <i>without</i> resorting to becoming supernatural themselves \u2014 it's what they do. That said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649423#post649423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, worsening Paradox with their observation of Supernal magic should still be a risk. There could be a Tactic that increases the chance of Paradox hitting the Mage instead of the Hunters or bystanders. We already have Tactics that do borderline supernatural stuff. For example, Bait And Switch provokes a werewolf into a frenzy but makes him attack his own pack. Deprogramming lets you remove mind control. Effigy lets you trap Spirits within inanimate objects, and may work on Geister for the purposes of permanently killing Sin-Eaters, if the ST says so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd recommend thinking twice about borderline-supernatural Tactics; that way lies Excision. By the same token, a theme of Hunter (1e, at least) is that mortals are more dangerous than the various Greater Template types tend to give them credit for: if they have the occasional trick up their sleeves that leaves a mage thinking \u201cthat shouldn't have worked\u201d, so be it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T17:30:34-07:00","id":649559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649336#post649336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a game standpoint, what's the purpose for making people forget about magic, anyways?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always assumed, just like Lunacy and the Masquerade and the Mask (Changeling) and Covers (Demon), it's a way to explain why the whole world doesn't know about the relevant splat.<br /> <br /> If mages were public knowledge, we'd be playing a whole different game.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, in-setting it's the Lie and everything else everyone said.<br /> <br /> From a game standpoint, I figure it's just a way to explain why this is the World of Darkness, not the World of Wonders. Or World of Wizards. Whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T17:53:41-07:00","id":649572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649550#post649550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cThe Code\u201d, yes. Note that the Code has never been a \u201cfree lunch\u201d; in order to gain immunity from further degeneration checks of a particular type, you needed to saddle yourself with some psychological quirks. I'm not sure that Hunter 2e's equivalent to the Code should necessarily work the same way; but I\u2019d prefer that the general premise be similar.<br /> <br /> Broadening this a bit, I think that hunters should have an easier time than regular mortals overall dealing with encounters with the supernatural. That is, after all, the whole point of the Vigil, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Yeah. I didn't go into detail because that would have caused the minutiae to overwhelm the broader put I was going for: hunters ought to be able to find ways to cope with supernatural hurdles <i>without</i> resorting to becoming supernatural themselves \u2014 it's what they do. That said:<br /> <br /> I'd recommend thinking twice about borderline-supernatural Tactics; that way lies Excision. By the same token, a theme of Hunter (1e, at least) is that mortals are more dangerous than the various Greater Template types tend to give them credit for: if they have the occasional trick up their sleeves that leaves a mage thinking \u201cthat shouldn't have worked\u201d, so be it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not Excision, per se. I like to think of borderline supernatural Tactics and other advantages as an implicit plot hook. Is our definition of supernatural as abnormal somehow misguided? Is there a latent supernatural potential in humans as a whole, with the environment and events activating this potential like pseudo-genetics? Did humanity always have this potential, and if not, what gave it to us? Are the monsters/major splats somehow degraded or refined expressions of this potential? Is mankind evolving in response to prolonged interaction with the supernatural, so to say? Are we on the verge of generating a new species? And how much longer will the Masquerade last?<br /> <br /> Those are the kind of questions that keep many Hunters up at night, I'd say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T19:31:34-07:00","id":649630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649572#post649572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not Excision, per se. I like to think of borderline supernatural Tactics and other advantages as an implicit plot hook. Is our definition of supernatural as abnormal somehow misguided? Is there a latent supernatural potential in humans as a whole, with the environment and events activating this potential like pseudo-genetics? Did humanity always have this potential, and if not, what gave it to us? Are the monsters/major splats somehow degraded or refined expressions of this potential? Is mankind evolving in response to prolonged interaction with the supernatural, so to say? Are we on the verge of generating a new species? And how much longer will the Masquerade last?<br /> <br /> Those are the kind of questions that keep many Hunters up at night, I'd say.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, this is where the horror actually lies in Hunter. Like, yeah, you hunt monsters and monsters are scary. Ho, hum. But what's really horrifying is asking at what point you become just as much of a monster as the things you hunt. Obviously slashers are one way a hunter becomes a monster. But what about the ones who claim to be descended from the honest-to-goodness Devil and use demonic powers to fight monsters? What about the scientists who don't just kill monsters, but capture and experiment on them? What about the hellfire club that goes poking into the supernatural for a cheap thrill? What about the unaffiliated hunter who has minor psychic abilities and realizes he can use them against the monsters? How much use of supernal powers is too much? Who decides who counts as a monster and who's just one of the good guys doing what needs to be done? That's the most interesting part of Hunter to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T21:06:18-07:00","id":649730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649630#post649630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the hellfire club that goes poking into the supernatural for a cheap thrill?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Ahem,</i><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://31.media.tumblr.com/tumblr_m1qmasFHRN1qb9pa3o2_250.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> More on-topic, I agree entirely. To be honest, while a lot of people call CW's Supernatural an inspiration, I feel like some of the Batman comics are better. Literally the only difference sometimes between Bats and the people he fights is the moral code that he claims to uphold.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T01:02:30-07:00","id":649825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649359#post649359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I appreciate that but why, for example, is paradox 'not that big of an inconvenience to a mage,' while to mortals it causes breaking points and mental gymnastics and occasionally amnesia and keeps mortals from really having a stake in the game?<br /> <br /> Also because I'm sensing some hackles raised, try not to see this as an attack on a game, I'm just trying to figure out why the rules are the way they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages don't maintain the Veil (their own very loose version of the Masquerade) for their own good, they maintain it for the good of everyone else. Being a normal human is an imposed curse, that happens to hit the majority of people. That the vast percentage of the population are Sleepers doesn't mean that they're the &quot;natural&quot; state of humanity, or that they're not cursed - they are.<br /> <br /> For all that it occassionally warps the laws of physics or sends a mage's spell off-target, the Abyss' primary victims are Sleepers.<br /> <br /> If I'm involved with any crossover mechanics, Hunters won't be able to use the Code to protect against the Lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T10:23:41-07:00","id":650290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649630#post649630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, this is where the horror actually lies in Hunter. Like, yeah, you hunt monsters and monsters are scary. Ho, hum. But what's really horrifying is asking at what point you become just as much of a monster as the things you hunt. Obviously slashers are one way a hunter becomes a monster. But what about the ones who claim to be descended from the honest-to-goodness Devil and use demonic powers to fight monsters? What about the scientists who don't just kill monsters, but capture and experiment on them? What about the hellfire club that goes poking into the supernatural for a cheap thrill? What about the unaffiliated hunter who has minor psychic abilities and realizes he can use them against the monsters? How much use of supernal powers is too much? Who decides who counts as a monster and who's just one of the good guys doing what needs to be done? That's the most interesting part of Hunter to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always went with a simple rule: If you still have Integrity you're not a monster (so Ghouls and Ghosts for example are not monsters).<br /> <br /> That said. I always felt that &quot;when are you a monster&quot; wasn't actually that interesting of a question - my answer is mostly because when writing Hunter homebrew I have strict rules that Hunters are not pawns of &quot;monsters&quot; (gods are a special exception) and thus needed a definition of monster.<br /> <br /> The real questions to me are &quot;when are a danger to people&quot; and &quot;when are you too much for regular law enforcement to handle&quot;. That's the question that decides who a Hunter should target. If you're not a danger you shouldn't be hunted. If you're not too powerful or strange for law enforcement then you shouldn't be hunted by vigilanties. Just regular cops, feds and VASCU","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T10:58:03-07:00","id":650312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=649825#post649825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm involved with any crossover mechanics, Hunters won't be able to use the Code to protect against the Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you would make crossover, what would be your mechanical answer for Witch Hunters that are not Sleepwalkers, to effectivly target the Awakened as culprit? When you need to bypass the Lie?<br /> <br /> I ask, as mine <b>Mage</b> game may return to the Witch Hunters plotline, and I would rather not dwell in making every hunter meet by PCs the Sleepwalker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T11:16:37-07:00","id":650325,"title":"","content":"I think he already answered this question. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645178#post645178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, only use the Awakened as adversaries in Tier 3 games, and even then be prepared to die very quickly unless it's a particularly low-powered or softhearted mage (in which case why are you Hunting them?)<br /> <br /> Just use Witches.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T11:40:19-07:00","id":650332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650290#post650290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always went with a simple rule: If you still have Integrity you're not a monster (so Ghouls and Ghosts for example are not monsters).<br /> <br /> That said. I always felt that &quot;when are you a monster&quot; wasn't actually that interesting of a question - my answer is mostly because when writing Hunter homebrew I have strict rules that Hunters are not pawns of &quot;monsters&quot; (gods are a special exception) and thus needed a definition of monster.<br /> <br /> The real questions to me are &quot;when are a danger to people&quot; and &quot;when are you too much for regular law enforcement to handle&quot;. That's the question that decides who a Hunter should target. If you're not a danger you shouldn't be hunted. If you're not too powerful or strange for law enforcement then you shouldn't be hunted by vigilanties. Just regular cops, feds and VASCU</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're talking about the same thing using different meanings of the word monster. I don't mean &quot;at what point does a mortal character with supernatural powers begin to count as a supernatural creature?&quot;, I mean &quot;when does a well-intentioned vigilante become as reprehensible as his victims?&quot; There's some crossover in those two questions in the case of Hunter thanks to the nature of their victims, which is why I use the term monster, because it could mean either or both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-03-2015, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T12:14:18-07:00","id":650410,"title":"","content":"We are indeed using words differently.<br /> <br /> To me the core of hunter is that with inguneity, teamwork and large numbers regular human can be equal monsters. With tactics and silver a Cell of hunters can match a pack of Werewolves in combat. With the right occult knowledge and a Conspiracy to acquire resources regular humans can pull of magic that rivals the Awakened*. And of course, regular humans can be just as much of a sick twisted evil bastard as any monster.<br /> <br /> That last one requires that there's something more to being a monster than just being evil.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. I think when that question comes up it's typically asking about supernatural powers. E.G. the hypocracy sidebar in hunter core. (You can tell I'm not too interested in that sidebar because of how many of my homebrews are happy to call their Endowment magic)<br /> <br /> <br /> *I'm being completely serious. The Sons of Phobos are regular mortals who have access to flexible blood sorcerery. With a Conspiracy to provide victims and protect them from the consiquences of their actions that could match the Awakened. Also the Ascending One's most potent Elixir turns you in to a Vampire then back again - 1E mages can't do that, I don't think 2E mages can. Feel free to correct me on that Dave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T12:25:06-07:00","id":650442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650312#post650312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you would make crossover, what would be your mechanical answer for Witch Hunters that are not Sleepwalkers, to effectivly target the Awakened as culprit? When you need to bypass the Lie?<br /> <br /> I ask, as mine <b>Mage</b> game may return to the Witch Hunters plotline, and I would rather not dwell in making every hunter meet by PCs the Sleepwalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Ophidimancer pointed out, Dave has already answered: for mages vs. Sleeper hunters, his answer is &quot;don't do it&quot;. As such, your best bet is that the Hunter 2e developer doesn't share Dave's opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T12:45:14-07:00","id":650458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I appreciate that but why, for example, is paradox 'not that big of an inconvenience to a mage,' while to mortals it causes breaking points and mental gymnastics and occasionally amnesia and keeps mortals from really having a stake in the game? </div> </div> </div>Those are different things. Paradox is where the Abyss messes with the mage's magic. Sleepers forgetting magic is the Lie/sleepers curse. There's a degree of overlap in that sleepers seeing magic adds a flat bonus (+2 if memory serves) to the paradox roll, plus they can cause a paradox roll for covert magic use if the effects seem too improbable to have naturally occurred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T12:47:47-07:00","id":650459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650312#post650312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you would make crossover, what would be your mechanical answer for Witch Hunters that are not Sleepwalkers, to effectivly target the Awakened as culprit? When you need to bypass the Lie?<br /> <br /> I ask, as mine <b>Mage</b> game may return to the Witch Hunters plotline, and I would rather not dwell in making every hunter meet by PCs the Sleepwalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd handle it two ways, one mechanical the other narrative:<ul><li><b>Mechanic: </b>Sleepers exposed to supernal magic who fail their Integrity roll can opt to take a Dramatic Failure (as normal) to remember, albeit somewhat hazily, the supernatural scene. So long as they suffer the associated Condition their memory remains intact, but fades when they purchase/earn the dot back. Note, when I say the scene I don't mean that one spell, but the whole even which, given the nature of scenes, could mean one brief stint of combat or a day long journey through worlds beyond.</li> <li><b>Narrative: </b>In a hunter game especially I'd strive to highlight how mages can seem...unhinged. Not all ravening lunatics, but certainly a tad bizarre. Extreme personality quirks, behaviors and interests would be common*. This can easily be justified from the Mages' point of view as symbolic acts, Yantra, Personas, etc. But the sleepers see only a discordant fellow. Additionally, just because sleepers struggle to recall Supernal magic doesn't mean they struggle to recall the Mage, nor that they cannot suspect the Mage of being 'witchy' if his behaviors are suspect. Finally, hunters with knowledge that weird shit exists (vampires, changelings, etc.) would be allowed to reason out that <b>something</b> supernatural is up with the Mage, even if they only have circumstantial evidence to go on.</li> </ul>As for fighting against Supernal magic, well, they are pretty fucked in that department. But not appreciably less fucked than if they were, say, staring down the maw of a raging wolf, or standing in the unveiled Sybaris of a newly risen Mummy. Being outclassed is, after all, one of Hunter's running themes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*For those who've read or watched any of Nisio Isin's monogatari series, the way side characters (Gaen Izuko, Kaiki Deishuu, Oshino Meme, etc.) tend to behave is an excellent example of how I'd present Mages to sleepers.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 09-03-2015, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T13:03:55-07:00","id":650473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650442#post650442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Ophidimancer pointed out, Dave has already answered: for mages vs. Sleeper hunters, his answer is &quot;don't do it&quot;. As such, your best bet is that the Hunter 2e developer doesn't share Dave's opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mundane Sleeper hunters can certainly hunt supernal mages. However, it should come as no surprise if most of the party ends up dead, with the rest in the burn unit of the local hospital or under suicide watch at the community mental health facility balled in a fetal position, rocking back and forth while repeatedly screaming, &quot;I saw the angels, but they saw Me...&quot; (I love the potential uses of the new Prime 4 &quot;Apocalypse&quot; spell <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-03-2015, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T18:32:59-07:00","id":650830,"title":"","content":"Just so long as that sort of outcome isn't <i>inevitable</i>. (Incidentally, how would Sleepwalkers fare in that situation? Sure, they don\u2019t get the Breaking Point or the memory distortion; but neither does the mage get any Paradox for going after them like that.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T18:48:27-07:00","id":650835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650830#post650830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so long as that sort of outcome isn't <i>inevitable</i>. (Incidentally, how would Sleepwalkers fare in that situation? Sure, they don\u2019t get the Breaking Point or the memory distortion; but neither does the mage get any Paradox for going after them like that.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think mundane Sleepwalkers wouldn't fare much better. At best, they would simply remember exactly what happened to them with perfect clarity as they eat all their remaining meals through a tube.<br /> <br /> Simply, first edition Tier 1 and 2 hunters (and some Tier 3) are not normally in the same power class as most experienced supernal mage cabals. The memory and breaking point issues just make the situation even more desperate and complicated for entirely mundane humans. (I don't believe such Hunters would fare much better against major template vampire coteries or werewolf packs). As always, it's easy enough to make whatever rules and settings adjustments a group wants if hunting other major template is a priority.<br /> <br /> It should be interesting what changes are made to Hunters in the upcoming second edition, but as Dave indicated, the core mortal human weaknesses of Quiescence will remain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T19:52:15-07:00","id":650863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650835#post650835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think mundane Sleepwalkers wouldn't fare much better. At best, they would simply remember exactly what happened to them with perfect clarity as they eat all their remaining meals through a tube.<br /> <br /> Simply, first edition Tier 1 and 2 hunters (and some Tier 3) are not normally in the same power class as most experienced supernal mage cabals. The memory and breaking point issues just make the situation even more desperate and complicated for entirely mundane humans. (I don't believe such Hunters would fare much better against major template vampire coteries or werewolf packs). As always, it's easy enough to make whatever rules and settings adjustments a group wants if hunting other major template is a priority.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the issue you were addressing wasn't so much the Sleeping Curse as it was the power that mages have at their disposal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650835#post650835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be interesting what changes are made to Hunters in the upcoming second edition, but as Dave indicated, the core mortal human weaknesses of Quiescence will remain.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, nobody has been arguing that it should go away; just that hunters should have ways to cope with it. <br /> <br /> It <i>is</i> going to be interesting what Hunter 2e does in that regard. In 1e, Lunacy didn\u2019t carry a risk of Morality loss; in 2e, Lunacy triggers an Integrity Breaking Point \u2014 and if you botch that Breaking Point, it turns you into a Wolf-Blooded. It will be interesting to see whether the Moral Support Tactic will help shield hunters who know it from said Breaking Point \u2014 or, more generally, if they'll have any means of coping with Lunacy-triggered Breaking Points. <br /> <br /> Or are we going back to the bad old days of the cWoD, where we needed Imbued Hunters to be able to have \u201cmortals\u201d who could stand up to the supernaturals without getting slapped down by various ambient mind-warping effects (Delirium, the Fog, the Mists, etc.)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-03-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T20:29:22-07:00","id":650880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650863#post650863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the issue you were addressing wasn't so much the Sleeping Curse as it was the power that mages have at their disposal.<br /> <br /> FWIW, nobody has been arguing that it should go away; just that hunters should have ways to cope with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it is indeed primarily a power level issue (as does Dave by his comments), and the Quiescence significantly aggravates the disparity for mundane humans, particularly as they usually are unable to properly prepare for (or recover from) an encounter with supernal magic due to its extreme versatility and memory and Integrity issues.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650863#post650863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It <i>is</i> going to be interesting what Hunter 2e does in that regard. In 1e, Lunacy didn\u2019t carry a risk of Morality loss; in 2e, Lunacy triggers an Integrity Breaking Point \u2014 and if you botch that Breaking Point, it turns you into a Wolf-Blooded. It will be interesting to see whether the Moral Support Tactic will help shield hunters who know it from said Breaking Point \u2014 or, more generally, if they'll have any means of coping with Lunacy-triggered Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Or are we going back to the bad old days of the cWoD, where we needed Imbued Hunters to be able to have \u201cmortals\u201d who could stand up to the supernaturals without getting slapped down by various ambient mind-warping effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>I always got the impression that the one real advantage that mundane mortals have against the very top tier supernaturals like supernal mages and werewolves is sheer numbers. Humans can certainly eliminate supernal mages (and other supernaturals), but not normally without a high casualty count and rampant destruction (assuming the mages just don't use any one of a multitude of their abilities to simply escape, from basic teleportation to entering Twilight or the Shadow). Small groups of humans should have difficulty subduing a competent mage, no less an experienced and diverse cabal.<br /> <br /> As for what changes will be incorporated in Hunter 2e, your guess is as good as mine, particularly since we don't know what deficiencies from 1e the developer feels needs to be addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T20:37:23-07:00","id":650882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650863#post650863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or are we going back to the bad old days of the cWoD, where we needed Imbued Hunters to be able to have \u201cmortals\u201d who could stand up to the supernaturals without getting slapped down by various ambient mind-warping effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it seems like something that is, so far, not a problem with all tempaltes. Vampires still have their old weaknesses, and while they have ways to get around it, they aren't universal to vampires. And werewolves still have their old weakness. Both seem to have a 'power upgrade' to their abilities and white rooms do point out that in 1 vs 1 or 5 vs 5, the supernaturals have the advantage, but hunters who play smart are still likely to be able to come out victorious, particularly if they don't try for even numbers. Demons and mages seem to pose more of a problem from a hunter standpoint, demons probably less so. The idea behind battling a demon seems to fit the demon story, where you fight through 'host' and 'possessed' and everyone else the demon's made contracts with until it unleashes its final form. Mages, though, have this amnesia aura to their abilities, which seem high indeed. And a problem with the last hunter was, as Dave Brookshaw mentioned, using the actual mage stuff some of the tactics simply wouldn't work. I haven't kept up with the other second editions so I couldn't guess how they'd deal with hunters.<br /> <br /> So if we do get a Witch Finders second edition equivalent, it would be nice if the things in it were actually applicable towards mages.<br /> <br /> I like the idea behind Dataweaver's tactic, perhaps giving an effective sleepwalker merit towards mages they've encountered, but the problem with that is now you have a mage who is more powerful than before, as they're not hindered by the hunters being sleepers. Something that pops up in all sorts of hunter fiction is simple witchcraft, little tricks they've learned that can give them an edge against magic. Human occultism is something that happens a ton throughout the World of Darkness books, but there's very little in the way of rules for it, usually in a single chapter of a book where it heavily implies only evildoers touch it. It wouldn't match an Awakened mage but it may give them defenses normal mortals wouldn't have access to, and allow a hunter to create a cell with a plan towards killing a mage without being retroactively cast out of existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  giving proper credit 09-04-2015, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T20:50:32-07:00","id":650888,"title":"","content":"Hunting Awakened mages is exceedingly difficult because supernal magic is so damned versatile (much more than other template powers) and mages are so very different from one another. For instance, say you Hunter group carefully investigates people they believe are mages and prepare to fight an Acanthus or Moros. If their Obrimos or Mastigos cabal-mate shows up, the Hunters are in for a world of hurt.<br /> <br /> As I indicated earlier, mages, particularly those of a less martial bent or are more merciful, also have a myriad of abilities to easily and quickly escape most situations.<br /> <br /> Lastly, mages are still essentially human, and do not suffer from any inherent supernatural weaknesses like sunlight or silver. Even the risk of paradox is usually just an annoyance for moderately powerful mages, and not really a concern at all in a life or death struggle with mortal humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-04-2015, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T21:53:58-07:00","id":650906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650882#post650882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea behind Charlaquin's tactic</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it was Dataweaver's idea, I just expanded on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T22:02:43-07:00","id":650910,"title":"","content":"Anyone else keep reading this debate and keep thinking of the Fighters vs Wizard debates in D&amp;D?<br /> <br /> Realistically, the wizard has the upperhand in pretty much every situation if the game is not set in the early levels, with full competence, and both are equal leveled. The fighter needs things to be stacked in his favor to come out unscathed, so while we have our answer for how Mages vs Hunters would work most of the time, perhaps we should think up ways to stack things in favor of the hunters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T22:02:45-07:00","id":650911,"title":"","content":"And your expansion was very much in line with my original intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T22:09:00-07:00","id":650914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650910#post650910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else keep reading this debate and keep thinking of the Fighters vs Wizard debates in D&amp;D?<br /> <br /> Realistically, the wizard has the upperhand in pretty much every situation if the game is not set in the early levels, with full competence, and both are equal leveled. The fighter needs things to be stacked in his favor to come out unscathed, so while we have our answer for how Mages vs Hunters would work most of the time, perhaps we should think up ways to stack things in favor of the hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, not really. That debate has more to do with two party members not being able to contribute equally to the game due to lopsided class design, whereas the Hunter issue is about a game line that a lot of folks want to be able to use for crossover not meshing well with another game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T22:10:48-07:00","id":650915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650910#post650910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else keep reading this debate and keep thinking of the Fighters vs Wizard debates in D&amp;D?<br /> <br /> Realistically, the wizard has the upperhand in pretty much every situation if the game is not set in the early levels, with full competence, and both are equal leveled. The fighter needs things to be stacked in his favor to come out unscathed, so while we have our answer for how Mages vs Hunters would work most of the time, perhaps we should think up ways to stack things in favor of the hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, the key difference being hunters are designed to hunt, while fighters and wizards aren't designed to fight each other.<br /> <br /> Since mage is in editing, and so pretty much completely finished, while hunter is a concept long and far away, yes, figuring out ways to let hunters hunt would be the way to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T22:20:37-07:00","id":650921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650910#post650910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone else keep reading this debate and keep thinking of the Fighters vs Wizard debates in D&amp;D?<br /> <br /> Realistically, the wizard has the upperhand in pretty much every situation if the game is not set in the early levels, with full competence, and both are equal leveled. The fighter needs things to be stacked in his favor to come out unscathed, so while we have our answer for how Mages vs Hunters would work most of the time, perhaps we should think up ways to stack things in favor of the hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most of the mechanisms to potentially &quot;equalize&quot; normal human Hunters against mages involve overwhelming numbers, tremendous firepower and disregard for widespread casualties and damage, and supernatural assistance, most of which are generally unavailable, highly impractical, or place the Hunters firmly within Tier 3 and/or no longer really mortal.<br /> <br /> Basic humans are not balanced against most supernaturals by design, particularly in second edition where &quot;game balance&quot; among the lines has been largely disregarded, at least as indicated by Dave with respect to Mage 2e.<br /> <br /> Regardless, in anyone's individual game, it requires little effort to artificially tip the scales if you want lower tier human hunters to have a chance against high-powered supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T22:34:04-07:00","id":650925,"title":"","content":"I was just talking about the specific parallel of mundane versus magician, not the you know, specific nature of their relationship with each other. I keep thinking Globes of Invulnerability being the go to solution whenever I keep reading this thread and that just ended up letting me think of the whole Fighters vs Wizards debates.<br /> <br /> And I agree, it does take minimal effort and slight hacking to allow hunters to win without too much trouble. Really, I don't think gamebalance is at all possible anymore with the constantly expanding roster of playable options. At best, we can provide &quot;niche balance&quot; where specific splats excel better than other splats in specific areas and the relevance of such niches and their usefulness is something DM controlled to begin with. Ironically, I find this set up better balanced than previously, but that can just be rose tinting on my glasses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T23:05:19-07:00","id":650927,"title":"","content":"Regarding Dave Brookshaw's observation that he would not allow Hunters to use the Code to bypass the Lie, I agree. My post about that scenario where the Hunter rolled 17 dice for a Breaking Point was meant to illustrate how Hunters have less difficulty with justifying acts like torture, kidnapping, blackmail and murder. Witnessing Supernal magic should require Breaking Point rolls, don't get me wrong. Sleepers have a shard of the Abyss within them, after all. As pointed out in previous posts, the gift of Awakening is also a curse, since you can't share your enlightenment and versatile powers with those you care about without damaging their very souls. Such an interplay between benefits and detriments of being a supernatural entity is to expected from the World Of Darkness, and pretty much one of its defining traits.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, that chart on page 185 of GMC listing certain modifiers for Breaking Points seems to be purposefully vague. What counts as a severe supernatural occurrence for a clueless or stubborn Sleeper probably does not count for a veteran Hunter. It may even vary from Hunter to Hunter, depending on what kinds of monsters they are more familiar with and how unpleasant or downright horrifying the confrontations have been. On average, I repeat, <i>on average</i>, I think the modifier for witnessing supernatural occurrences does not exceed -3 for Hunters.<br /> <br /> Certain Hunters might be more compassionate or understanding in regards to monsters, as well. They may also have a flexible notion of what counts as baseline reality vs supernatural. One Hunter thinks physical violence is a dark but inevitable part of his job and life in general, so direct combat doesn't shake him as much. He might be horrified if he sees a vampire hypnotizing a Cell member into revealing sensitive information, or worshipping the vampire like the pinnacle of beauty.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that, while I do respect the themes of Mage that Dave is emphasizing in this thread, I also like the toolbox nature of Integrity and the fluid canon of the NWOD. These features don't necessarily have to be antagonistic or irreconcilable.<br /> <br /> That being said, you still have to worry about the dozens of advantages that Supernal magic gives, such as Wards, mind reading, teleportation, regeneration, line-of-sight attacks that deal aggravated damage, illusions, crippling transformations and a lot more. And Paradox is under no obligation to hit Mages before Hunters, or vice-versa.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it could be interesting to give more attention to diplomacy and proxy confrontations in Hunter vs Mages conflicts. Attempts at negotiation don't have to be buddy-buddy, of course. They can even be ruthless. That could highlight how power can make you see people without power as less than people, how far some are willing to go for survival and ideology, and how Mages and Hunters can become very similar monsters, be they wielding guns or lightning bolts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-04-2015, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T02:01:02-07:00","id":650984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650863#post650863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or are we going back to the bad old days of the cWoD, where we needed Imbued Hunters to be able to have \u201cmortals\u201d who could stand up to the supernaturals without getting slapped down by various ambient mind-warping effects (Delirium, the Fog, the Mists, etc.)?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something I'm starting to get worried about. But hopefully 2e Hunter introduces some measures against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 09-04-2015, 05:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T02:20:25-07:00","id":650989,"title":"","content":"Nah, it'll probably just be a one page book telling you to not bother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T04:59:10-07:00","id":651039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650915#post650915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yeah, the key difference being hunters are designed to hunt, while fighters and wizards aren't designed to fight each other.<br /> <br /> Since mage is in editing, and so pretty much completely finished, while hunter is a concept long and far away, yes, figuring out ways to let hunters hunt would be the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, Hunter is gonna take a dump at the setting expectations of other game lines like it did in 1E with stuff like tactics that allowed them to re-program werewolves (despite the fact they would have a pack right now and doing such a thing would be a grievous betrayal) or being able to strike at a mage's temple and render him/her silent. Because head-trauma totally messes up their soul connection to the realm of enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Rule of Cool and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T08:36:09-07:00","id":651237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=650915#post650915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yeah, the key difference being hunters are designed to hunt, while fighters and wizards aren't designed to fight each other.<br /> <br /> Since mage is in editing, and so pretty much completely finished, while hunter is a concept long and far away, yes, <i><b>figuring out ways to let hunters hunt </b></i>would be the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make 'em Werewolves... After all, the wolf must Hunt. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T09:08:25-07:00","id":651285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651039#post651039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, Hunter is gonna take a dump at the setting expectations of other game lines like it did in 1E with stuff like tactics that allowed them to re-program werewolves (despite the fact they would have a pack right now and doing such a thing would be a grievous betrayal) or being able to strike at a mage's temple and render him/her silent. Because head-trauma totally messes up their soul connection to the realm of enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Rule of Cool and all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who's developing Hunter 2e, and has anything been mentioned about expected changed in the new edition?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Edit</b></u>: I see that MMM indicated that Monica Valentinelli is the developer for Hunter 2E, and the focus of the new edition is the &quot;Slasher Chronicle.&quot;.<br /> <br /> Monica previously worked on Hunter: Mortal Remains (writing and editing), she wrote Hunter: Doubting Souls for Dark Eras, she co-wrote Dread Names Red List for V20 with me. Outside of OPP she developed the Firefly RPG for Margaret Weis Productions, has written for Unknown Armies, All Flesh Must Be Eaten, Mistborn, Alethea, and Eclipse Phase to name a few.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-04-2015, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T10:15:27-07:00","id":651453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651237#post651237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make 'em Werewolves... After all, the wolf must Hunt. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A connection would make sense, even if it was if only in the vein of something like, 'Some members of this compact believe that...'<br /> <br /> Those who take up the Vigil, after all, are not normal humans. Normal humans are the sort of investigators you get in most blue book games. Hunters have taken up the candle of the vigil because they see themselves as having no other option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-04-2015, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T11:25:46-07:00","id":651520,"title":"","content":"I could easily see a werewolf pack allowing a hunter to join. Or a hunter cell allowing a werewolf to join.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T11:35:00-07:00","id":651524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651453#post651453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those who take up the Vigil, after all, are not normal humans. Normal humans are the sort of investigators you get in most blue book games. Hunters have taken up the candle of the vigil because they see themselves as having no other option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many of the lower tier Hunters are indeed &quot;normal&quot; mundane humans. They may be highly motivated, trained, armed, and informed of supernatural entities and events, but plain vanilla humans nevertheless.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T11:44:07-07:00","id":651583,"title":"","content":"I didn't say they were supernatural, but they aren't normal. A normal human would put aside the hunt and get on with their lives. Hunters are driven beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T11:54:10-07:00","id":651590,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't phrase it in terms of having no choice. But yeah; the distinguishing feature between blue-book mortal and hunter seems to be that when confronted with the supernatural, hunters stare it down \u2014 not just once, but time and time again. Blue-book mortals are amateurs who occasionally encounter the supernatural; but even an independent cell of hunters, with no ties to any compacts or conspiracies, is a team of professional monster hunters who delve into the supernatural so frequently that they need some sort of touchstone (in 1e, one's Profession) to keep them from losing touch with the ordinary world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T13:02:15-07:00","id":651728,"title":"","content":"We've come full circle, and again are arguing whether the &quot;drive&quot; or &quot;professionalism&quot; of Hunters who are otherwise plain humans somehow provides them with immunity or resistance to supernatural afflictions which are supposed to affect all normal human (e.g., the Quiescence), often while retaining the actual advantages of being a normal human (e.g., Paradox).<br /> <br /> I'm obviously in the Dave camp and would not provide mortal Hunters with what effectively amounts to supernatural advantages (as well as believe the power level of lower tier Hunters generally poses little danger to major template supernaturals), but it's easy enough to adapt the setting and rules to whatever best suits individual tastes and styles. The most important thing is that everyone enjoys their own chronicles,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T13:18:56-07:00","id":651735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651728#post651728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've come full circle, and again are arguing whether the &quot;drive&quot; or &quot;professionalism&quot; of Hunters who are otherwise plain humans somehow provides them with immunity or resistance to supernatural afflictions which are supposed to affect all normal human (e.g., the Quiescence), often while retaining the actual advantages of being a normal human (e.g., Paradox).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I was stating that hunters are not normal humans as a link to werewolves.<br /> <br /> Again, I am not saying they are supernatural. I am also not saying they are related to werewolves. But they are people who take the hunt and make it central to their life. My line about them having no other option was paraphrasing from the Hunter the Vigil core book. 'Hunters are not born or built. They are forged. People don't idly make the decision to risk their lives, especially not in the pursuit of things most of humanity doesn't acknowledge exists. The Vigil is a choice that is made because all other options, including doing nothing, are far, far worse.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T14:15:58-07:00","id":651775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651735#post651735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I was stating that hunters are not normal humans as a link to werewolves.<br /> <br /> Again, I am not saying they are supernatural. I am also not saying they are related to werewolves. But they are people who take the hunt and make it central to their life. My line about them having no other option was paraphrasing from the Hunter the Vigil core book. 'Hunters are not born or built. They are forged. People don't idly make the decision to risk their lives, especially not in the pursuit of things most of humanity doesn't acknowledge exists. The Vigil is a choice that is made because all other options, including doing nothing, are far, far worse.'</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you believe that the Vigil should or does provide otherwise normal humans with immunity or resistance to supernatural afflictions such as the Quiescence or Lunacy, all while maintaining the advantages of being mortal such as Disbelief/Dissonance and Paradox? If so, the Hunters have effectively been given a supernatural enhancement regardless of whether it's actually categorized as &quot;supernatural?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T14:17:49-07:00","id":651778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651728#post651728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've come full circle, and again are arguing whether the \u201cdrive\u201d or \u201cprofessionalism\u201d of Hunters who are otherwise plain humans somehow provides them with immunity or resistance to supernatural afflictions which are supposed to affect all normal human (e.g., the Quiescence), often while retaining the actual advantages of being a normal human (e.g., Paradox).</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a rather simplistic way of putting it. For instance, you're giving the impression that those who aren't in your camp are trying to get a free lunch by disregarding the fact that every proposed mitigating factor has some sort of cost of its own. Similarly, nobody has proposed <i>full</i> immunity to said supernatural afflictions outside of the likes of the Sleepwalker Merit; all alternatives to it that have been suggested in this thread have assumed that those afflictions <i>do</i> continue to affect \u201call normal humans\u201d, including those hunters who are better able to cope with them. Even the suggestion to apply the Code has been less about eliminating the Sleeping Curse as it\u2019s been about preventing a \u201cdeath spiral\u201d by replacing the Breaking Point with a Trigger Point, and leaving the rest of the Curse untouched: improving one's ability to cope with the Curse rather than getting rid of it. <br /> <br /> That said, one suggestion that Charlaquin made deserves special note: the idea that it might be possible for a hunter to \u201cpush through\u201d the Sleeping Curse <i>on his own</i>, without deliberate supernatural assistance. There's a rough parallel to this in <b>Werewolf</b>, in that botching a Lunacy-induced Breaking Point makes you Wolf-Blooded and thus free of Lunacy. That said, I suspect that of all the suggestions that have been made here, this is the single most likely one to draw the ire of \u201cDave's camp\u201d, as it's a direct challenge to the notion that all Sleepers are victims who are utterly incapable of getting out from under Quiescence without outside aid. Never mind that the method proposed isn\u2019t something that would be available to the vast majority of mortals, and that it would be a rough and painful path to freedom even for those who find it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651728#post651728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm obviously in the Dave camp and would not provide mortal Hunters with what effectively amounts to supernatural advantages (as well as believe the power level of lower tier Hunters generally poses little danger to major template supernaturals),</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile, I disagree with the characterization of everything that might soften the likes of the Sleeping Curse as \u201ceffectively amounting to a supernatural advantage\u201d. Is Moral Support effectively a supernatural advantage because it lets a cell of hunters cope more effectively with Lunacy? <br /> <br /> Ultimately, the premise of <b>Hunter</b> is that mortals aren't as helpless as the supernaturals think. When looking at things like the Sleeping Curse from <b>Hunter</b>'s perspective, that point should be emphasized. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651728#post651728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it's easy enough to adapt the setting and rules to whatever best suits individual tastes and styles. The most important thing is that everyone enjoys their own chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, for whatever it's worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T14:48:45-07:00","id":651801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651778#post651778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s a rather simplistic way of putting it. For instance, you're giving the impression that those who aren't in your camp are trying to get a free lunch by disregarding the fact that every proposed mitigating factor has some sort of cost of its own. Similarly, nobody has proposed <i>full</i> immunity to said supernatural afflictions outside of the likes of the Sleepwalker Merit; all alternatives to it that have been suggested in this thread have assumed that those afflictions <i>do</i> continue to affect \u201call normal humans\u201d, including those hunters who are better able to cope with them. Even the suggestion to apply the Code has been less about eliminating the Sleeping Curse as it\u2019s been about preventing a \u201cdeath spiral\u201d by replacing the Breaking Point with a Trigger Point, and leaving the rest of the Curse untouched: improving one's ability to cope with the Curse rather than getting rid of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, I noted both resistance as well as immunity to supernatural afflictions, and do indeed disagree with your perspective on the setting and rules, although implied no personal insult. Such disagreements are hardly unusual or personal.<br /> <br /> My main issue with some of the suggestions is that they seek to provide such resistance while simultaneously keeping all the benefits of being a normal human. In that sense, and to adopt the food analogy, while not a &quot;free lunch,&quot; the Hunters are certainly &quot;having their cake and eating it too.&quot; At least to me, it generally feels like you and others might be trying to give the advantages of Tier 3 Hunters to the lower levels without calling it as much. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651778#post651778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, one suggestion that Charlaquin made deserves special note: the idea that it might be possible for a hunter to \u201cpush through\u201d the Sleeping Curse <i>on his own</i>, without deliberate supernatural assistance. There's a rough parallel to this in <b>Werewolf</b>, in that botching a Lunacy-induced Breaking Point makes you Wolf-Blooded and thus free of Lunacy. That said, I suspect that of all the suggestions that have been made here, this is the single most likely one to draw the ire of \u201cDave's camp\u201d, as it's a direct challenge to the notion that all Sleepers are victims who are utterly incapable of getting out from under Quiescence without outside aid. Never mind that the method proposed isn\u2019t something that would be available to the vast majority of mortals, and that it would be a rough and painful path to freedom even for those who find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more than simple agreement with Dave's perspective on comparative template power levels. Dave is the Mage developer and has explicitly ruled that Quiescence unique and not like Lunacy in all matters relevant to this discussion. Of course, you are free to disagree and disregard the canon rule, but absent a clearly conflicting ruling by the Hunter developer, it is the default state of affairs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651778#post651778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, I disagree with the characterization of everything that might soften the likes of the Sleeping Curse as \u201ceffectively amounting to a supernatural advantage\u201d. Is Moral Support effectively a supernatural advantage because it lets a cell of hunters cope more effectively with Lunacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Moral support does not lift the shard of Abyss that curses a sleeper soul, at least according to Mage cosmology. If you believe it should, I disagree but respect your choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651778#post651778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, the premise of <b>Hunter</b> is that mortals aren't as helpless as the supernaturals think. When looking at things like the Sleeping Curse from <b>Hunter</b>'s perspective, that point should be emphasized.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is suggesting that mortals are always totally helpless against the supernatural in the nWOD. However, that does not mean certain supernaturals don't possess very distinct and powerful advantages that are extremely difficult to overcome, particularly by small groups of normal humans. For instance, Dave did not suggest that Hunters never fight Awakened mages, only that it is often suicidal without the support, powers and other advantages provided at the Tier 3 level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T15:12:37-07:00","id":651819,"title":"","content":"Wait, when did I suggest a Hunter could push through quiescence on his own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T15:16:44-07:00","id":651822,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I meant Pendragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T15:25:28-07:00","id":651827,"title":"","content":"Of course people can get out of the Lie without outside help.<br /> <br /> They do so by becoming Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T15:33:25-07:00","id":651831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651801#post651801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I noted both resistance as well as immunity to supernatural afflictions, and do indeed disagree with your perspective on the setting and rules, although implied no personal insult. Such disagreements are hardly unusual or personal.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, I'm not taking it personally. Though at this point, I'm more interested in making sure my views don't get misconstrued than I am in convincing anyone of anything. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651801#post651801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main issue with some of the suggestions is that they seek to provide such resistance while simultaneously keeping all the benefits of being a normal human. In that sense, and to adopt the food analogy, while not a \u201cfree lunch,\u201d the Hunters are certainly \u201chaving their cake and eating it too.\u201d At least to me, it generally feels like you and others might be trying to give the advantages of Tier 3 Hunters to the lower levels without calling it as much.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s more than just \u201cwithout calling it as much\u201d: all suggestions for Sleepers being better able to cope with the Sleeping Curse without going all the way and removing it (the latter presumably being a Tier 3 thing) have included prices that must be paid (e.g., Trigger Points instead of Breaking Points) \u2014 I cannot stress this point enough, because without those costs, the notion wouldn't be acceptable to me, either. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651801#post651801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more than simple agreement with Dave's perspective on comparative template power levels. Dave is the Mage developer and has explicitly ruled that Quiescence unique and not like Lunacy in all matters relevant to this discussion. Of course, you are free to disagree and disregard the canon rule, but absent a clearly conflicting ruling by the Hunter developer, it is the default state of affairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The default state of affairs is that we know quite a bit about what <b>Mage</b> will have to say on the matter, and next to nothing about what <b>Hunter</b> will have to say about it. The default state of affairs is <i>also</i> that neither book is in print yet (though hopefully that will change soon). And ultimately, the <i>current</i> state of affairs isn\u2019t the be-all, end-all in a discussion that\u2019s at least partially about speculation and hopes about what the <i>final</i> state of affairs will be. Mind you, I don't hold out much hope that some means of hunters achieving Sleepwalker status on their own will be in <b>Hunter 2e</b>; Dave seems bound and determined to squash even the far more modest proposals that have been made. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651801#post651801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moral support does not lift the shard of Abyss that curses a sleeper soul, at least according to Mage cosmology. If you believe it should, I disagree but respect your choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe it should; but I also don't believe that you should <i>need</i> to lift the shard of Abyss that curses a sleeper soul in order to more effectively cope with what it does to you. Note that my suggestion for an After Action Report in no way restores peoples' memories; it merely allows the cell to figure out what actually happened, <i>despite</i> their muddled memories, and thus to develop actionable intelligence to use in their next encounter. Nothing supernatural going on there; just an entirely mundane workaround to the memory-distorting effects of the Curse. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651801#post651801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one is suggesting that mortals are always totally helpless against the supernatural in the nWOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nor have I said that anyone has. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651801#post651801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, that does not mean certain supernaturals don't possess very distinct and powerful advantages that are extremely difficult to overcome, particularly by small groups of normal humans. For instance, Dave did not suggest that Hunters never fight Awakened mages, only that it is often suicidal without the support, powers and other advantages provided at the Tier 3 level.</div> </div> </div> </div>He <i>has</i> basically said that you\u2019re not a Sleepwalker, don\u2019t bother trying. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651827#post651827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course people can get out of the Lie without outside help.<br /> <br /> They do so by becoming Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that becoming a mage required the assistance of a Watchtower, which is arguably outside help. That said, I was obviously referring to transitioning from Sleeper to Sleepwalker without outside help \u2014 something that wouldn't involve transitioning a character from <b>Hunter</b> to <b>Mage</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-04-2015, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T16:06:03-07:00","id":651885,"title":"","content":"Crudely speaking, Awakening is a matter of providing enough fuel to the rockets to escape the orbit of one world so one can be pulled into another.<br /> <br /> More or less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T16:33:48-07:00","id":651897,"title":"","content":"Is the Sleepwalker merit going to be character creation only? If not, what is the big deal here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T16:34:44-07:00","id":651898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651775#post651775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you believe that the Vigil should or does provide otherwise normal humans with immunity or resistance to supernatural afflictions such as the Quiescence or Lunacy, all while maintaining the advantages of being mortal such as Disbelief/Dissonance and Paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and I'm almost positive I was one of the first after Dave to say hunters should not be fighting mages. In addition to not having any resistance to Quiescence, they are severely outmatched on all possible levels. Yeah, right <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=645867#post645867\">there</a>.<br /> <br /> However, I don't believe hunters are normal humans and the books back that up, with frequent mentions of how they are different. It's not a supernatural thing, I never claimed it was, but if in second edition they wanted to make it a supernatural thing, where the Vigil is a supernatural pact or simply by becoming part of a compact or conspiracy you align yourself with a mystical oath and become supernatural, they already have a good head start with everything in the hunter books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T16:35:53-07:00","id":651900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651831#post651831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that becoming a mage required the assistance of a Watchtower, which is arguably outside help. That said, I was obviously referring to transitioning from Sleeper to Sleepwalker without outside help \u2014 something that wouldn't involve transitioning a character from <b>Hunter</b> to <b>Mage</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Buy the Merit. Spontaneous Sleepwalkers happen, more than Awakenings (some mages theorize they're the result of near-misses at Awakening). That frees you from Quiescence and the Breaking Point, but means you don't cause Dissonance or add Paradox dice to spells.<br /> <br /> Being a Sleepwalker isn't <i>completely</i> good news; Sleepers have one great advantage/disadvantage in that a long-lasting spell that's obviously magical cast on one will eventually get worn down by their connection to the Abyss. It's rather thin protection - a spell cursing you to get cancer or turning you into a non-sentient being will be fine, but you're at least making the mage come up with a means of getting rid of you that skirts the Lie. Sleepwalkers? No such luck.<br /> <br /> It's <i>hard</i>. It's really very hard. <br /> <br /> The Sleeping Curse means it sucks to be a Sleeper. It means it sucks to be a mage, and it sucks to be a Sleepwalker caught in the middle. The great Lie cast on Humanity by the Exarchs does not discriminate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T16:59:08-07:00","id":651935,"title":"","content":"Now, the way I frame the Awakened's relationship to Sleepers for writers is to describe it as the hyper-rich. Mages are like the 1% - they have achieved a position of immense privilege through just enough hard work and personal trial to make some of them ignore the fact that incredible, stupid, luck had an equal or larger part to play.The Lie means there's always a gulf of understanding - even the capacity for understanding - between them and everyone else. Sleepwalkers have the unenviable position of not being scarred for life by being around mages, but being nowhere near as capable - life for a Sleepwalker who's in an Order is like being Bill Gate's assistant.<br /> <br /> The Awakened vary massively in their reactions to everyone else - all positions between a committed desire to help the less fortunate to outright victim-blaming (and all Sleepers, as all mages know, are victims, whether they know it or not). But they all do it from that isolated remove. A Silver Ladder mage trying to make everyone's life a little better is like a wealthy philanthropist. They'll always be &quot;poorer&quot; than him, gnostically speaking.<br /> <br /> For Hunter... Well, mages do a lot of damage Hunters can take exception to; some mages steal souls perform human sacrifice because it's convenient, rewrite people's lives to suit themselves and treat Sleepers as annoyances or disposable resources.<br /> <br /> The problem is that being a Sleeper means you can't remember magic when it's cast in front of you, and seeing it rips chunks out of your soul. It's just a thing you have to cope with when hunting the Awakened, like &quot;vampire blood is addictive&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd love to expand on what the Awakened look like to Sleepers and Sleepwalkers - the Orders are semi-visible Mystery Cults in the World of Darkness. The Veil is for the protection of Sleepers' Integrity and magic from Dissonance, not because mages have a desire for secrecy or fear the mob like the Kindred's Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't do it in a Hunter book, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T19:15:24-07:00","id":651981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651827#post651827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course people can get out of the Lie without outside help.<br /> <br /> They do so by becoming Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the responses, Dave.<br /> <br /> Where do Proximi fall in within confines of the Lie? For instance, they clearly have some supernal power and comprehension, but do they have any access to Mage Sight and the ability to see the Truth? Are they just slightly more useful than a average Sleepwalker with a similar level of true understanding? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651935#post651935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Veil is for the protection of Sleepers' Integrity and magic from Dissonance, not because mages have a desire for secrecy or fear the mob like the Kindred's Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>Statement like that make mages' arrogance seem justified and more frightening as a group than even I've argued in this thread.<br /> <br /> Damn, I can't wait for 2e to be released!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T21:21:23-07:00","id":652090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651827#post651827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course people can get out of the Lie without outside help.<br /> <br /> They do so by becoming Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is not helping in discussion, as we talk here about Sleeping Hunters fighting Mages. Making Hunters all the time Banishers is missing the point of <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b>. It's like saying &quot;all vampire hunters must be other vampires&quot; or &quot;you do not hunt werewolves&quot;. We know it's not true and all the <b>Hunter</b> line is based on this take, not &quot;only monsters can hunt monsters&quot;.<br /> <br /> Ending discussion by saying &quot;Sleepers do not hunt Mages&quot; is very bad take for the both gamelines. If should be diffuclt, yes. It should take some training - probably. But it should be possible. Other way Awakened do not have reasons to <i>fear</i> the Sleepers. And on Sleeping Hunters we should focus on in this discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651900#post651900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Buy the Merit. Spontaneous Sleepwalkers happen, more than Awakenings (some mages theorize they're the result of near-misses at Awakening). That frees you from Quiescence and the Breaking Point, but means you don't cause Dissonance or add Paradox dice to spells.<br /> <br /> Being a Sleepwalker isn't <i>completely</i> good news; Sleepers have one great advantage/disadvantage in that a long-lasting spell that's obviously magical cast on one will eventually get worn down by their connection to the Abyss. It's rather thin protection - a spell cursing you to get cancer or turning you into a non-sentient being will be fine, but you're at least making the mage come up with a means of getting rid of you that skirts the Lie. Sleepwalkers? No such luck.<br /> <br /> It's <i>hard</i>. It's really very hard.<br /> <br /> The Sleeping Curse means it sucks to be a Sleeper. It means it sucks to be a mage, and it sucks to be a Sleepwalker caught in the middle. The great Lie cast on Humanity by the Exarchs does not discriminate.</div> </div> </div> </div>With this case I can agree - Sleepwalking is always a viable way for the hunters. But most dire problem is for the hunters that are still Sleepers. And I think they still can hunt Awakened, effectivly, and on them we should focus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651935#post651935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that being a Sleeper means you can't remember magic when it's cast in front of you, and seeing it rips chunks out of your soul. It's just a thing you have to cope with when hunting the Awakened, like &quot;vampire blood is addictive&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Tactics like proposed <i>After Action Report</i> are good solution here - they try to omit Sleeping Curse limitations, playing by it's rules. Question is - <b>How Sleeping Curse could be bypassed or used in normal Hunter enviorment?</b> We have memory loss effect, we have Integrity loss effect ( so I suspect <i>Moral Support </i>can help here ). As I think, some Tactic on using Abyss Shard in Sleepers could nice fit with both <b>Hunter</b> and <b>Mage</b> - showing that Sleepers are threat to the Awakened, even only becuase of Curse. Something with build up Paradox even more in front of public places... ( Need to think )<br /> <br /> As I'm going to run <i>Malleus Maleficarum</i> storyline later in the game - I suspect that supernatural Endowments, like Benediction or Castigatons, makes you Sleepwalker. <b>So no need for &quot;True Sight&quot; power for them? You are automaticlly Sleepwalker when you are granted them?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-05-2015, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T21:45:05-07:00","id":652096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652090#post652090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this case I can agree - Sleepwalking is always a viable way for the hunters. But most dire problem is for the hunters that are still Sleepers. And I think they still can hunt Awakened, effectivly, and on them we should focus.[/B]</div> </div> </div> </div>You act like Quiescence makes it impossible to hunt mages. It doesn't. Does it make it difficult and costly to do so for prolonged periods of time when directly confronted by Supernal magic? Yes. But that's part of the point. Hunters can go after mages just as easily as they can go after anything else. That said, as with most things, they're going to be at a disadvantage by the very nature of being a mundane human. That is a feature, not a bug. Hunters are the perpetual underdogs until they get to tier 3, that is by design.<br /> <br /> As for Quiescence itself, there is no such thing as '<i>resisting</i>' the Sleeping Curse. That should be perfectly clear by now. You either have a shard of the Abyss in your soul or you do not, it is a binary thing. However, that isn't to say there's no way to deal with the consequences of such , you just have to try a little harder is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-05-2015, 12:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T21:57:13-07:00","id":652100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652096#post652096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You act like Quiescence makes it impossible to hunt mages. It doesn't. Does it make it difficult and costly to do so for prolonged series of time when directly confronted by Supernal magic? Yes. But that's part of the point. Hunters can go after mages just as easily as they can go after anything else. That said, as with most things, they're going to be at a disadvantage by the very nature of being a mundane human. That is a feature, not a bug. Hunters are the perpetual underdogs until they get to tier 3, that is by design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think more than the breaking points the not remembering would be the biggest hurdle. Why would you hunt someone who is clearly not a magic-user and never used magic to do anything you find objectionable?<br /> <br /> A problem with the aforementioned Tactic is that, as Dave has said, it's not merely witnessing magic that causes a Breaking Point but later on remembering can cause another Breaking Point. Though I suppose the Tactic would have to focus on making the Breaking Point as easy to resist as possible, since you're surrounded by your cell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Quiescence itself, there is no such thing as '<i>resisting</i>' the Sleeping Curse. That should be perfectly clear by now. You either have a shard of the Abyss in your soul or you do not, it is a binary thing. However, that isn't to say there's no way to deal with the consequences of such , you just have to try a little harder is all. </div> </div> </div>I suppose the Knights of St George could be an exception. If you followed the idea that they are working for Abyssal creatures, the shard in their soul is the gateway to their powers, while also allowing them to act as Sleepwalkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T22:11:52-07:00","id":652103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652100#post652100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think more than the breaking points the not remembering would be the biggest hurdle. Why would you hunt someone who is clearly not a magic-user and never used magic to do anything you find objectionable?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because he's doing Bad Things? Quiescence doesn't mean you forget that the mage is responsible; only that he used magic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652100#post652100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A problem with the aforementioned Tactic is that, as Dave has said, it's not merely witnessing magic that causes a Breaking Point but later on remembering can cause another Breaking Point. Though I suppose the Tactic would have to focus on making the Breaking Point as easy to resist as possible, since you're surrounded by your cell.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I conceived it, After Action Report wouldn't actually restore memories; it would let the cell piece together what actually happened from the evidence at hand, fragmented as it may be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T22:18:11-07:00","id":652105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652090#post652090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ending discussion by saying &quot;Sleepers do not hunt Mages&quot; is very bad take for the both gamelines. If should be diffuclt, yes. It should take some training - probably. But it should be possible. Other way Awakened do not have reasons to <i>fear</i> the Sleepers. And on Sleeping Hunters we should focus on in this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normal human Hunters pursue all variety of &quot;wizards.&quot; &quot;sorcerers,&quot; and miscellaneous users of magic with varying levels of power, as indicated in the Hunter corebook and Witchfinders. Awakened supernal mages are just a very small subset of these individuals and usually the far most difficult and dangerous prey, both because they are normally the most versatile and powerful and absent supernatural merits and intervention, Quiescence cannot be avoided or circumvented. Awakened mages' lack of fear of Sleepers is well-earned and justified, and Hunters who pursue them must be the best of the best, and willing to make the brutal sacrifices necessary to overcome such elusive and potent quarry. This is a feature, not a bug, of the setting.<br /> <br /> It is only &quot;bad&quot; for both game lines if crossover &quot;game balance&quot; is a priority or necessity. However, Dave and other developers have repeatedly stated that is no longer the case.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, although Mage 2e will (hopefully) soon be released and its mechanics and setting no longer subject to alteration, since Hunter 2e is still in the early stages of development, who knows what significant changes to the game may arise that alter some of these fundamentals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-05-2015, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T22:24:53-07:00","id":652107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652103#post652103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because he's doing Bad Things? Quiescence doesn't mean you forget that the mage is responsible; only that he used magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but with the lack of magic, responsibility could be taken out of their hands. Hunters on patrol in a graveyard stumble upon a mage raising and tearing the secrets from ghosts. Without the magical element, it's just a guy yelling in a graveyard. Or a mage uses magic to compel people to attack a hunter cell. Without magic, it looks like the people are at fault. A mage rips the life out of someone with a want from their soul and it looks like the person just fell over dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I conceived it, After Action Report wouldn't actually restore memories; it would let the cell piece together what actually happened from the evidence at hand, fragmented as it may be. </div> </div> </div>Ah that's a good way to go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-05-2015, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T22:29:50-07:00","id":652109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652100#post652100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think more than the breaking points the not remembering would be the biggest hurdle. Why would you hunt someone who is clearly not a magic-user and never used magic to do anything you find objectionable?</div> </div> </div> </div>You could certainly know that magic and those who employ it exist without personally seeing or remembering it. For instance, the Quiescence does not prevent humans from knowing certain people circulate in occult circles and are feared and respected, suspecting that someone's unusual luck or influence just seems &quot;off,&quot; realizing that strange and inexplicable things seem to occur in a particular house in the neighborhood, or even being informed that an individual is a mage from a captured Sleepwalker, other supernatural predator like a vampire. or even an Awakened mage seeking to eliminate rivals. <br /> <br /> The Quiescence certainly makes adversely interacting with someone who is a Awakened mage very difficult and dangerous, including discovery, combat and recovery, but identifying someone as using magic who may be such an Awakened mage is probably one of the easier tasks for an experienced and diligent Hunter cell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T01:12:51-07:00","id":652215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652105#post652105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normal human Hunters pursue all variety of &quot;wizards.&quot; &quot;sorcerers,&quot; and miscellaneous users of magic with varying levels of power, as indicated in the Hunter corebook and Witchfinders. Awakened supernal mages are just a very small subset of these individuals and usually the far most difficult and dangerous prey, both because they are normally the most versatile and powerful and absent supernatural merits and intervention, Quiescence cannot be avoided or circumvented. Awakened mages' lack of fear of Sleepers is well-earned and justified, and Hunters who pursue them must be the best of the best, and willing to make the brutal sacrifices necessary to overcome such elusive and potent quarry. This is a feature, not a bug, of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is weird, as Kindred and Forsaken still fear the mortals. Mages - by developers - just say &quot;oh, you have Abyss Shard, that's a pitty, now do not bother me&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's like saying that vampie hunters does not hunt Kindred or werewolf does not hunt Uratha. It's very Hunter ( as gameline ) breaking assumption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652105#post652105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is only &quot;bad&quot; for both game lines if crossover &quot;game balance&quot; is a priority or necessity. However, Dave and other developers have repeatedly stated that is no longer the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is difference between &quot;mages can bend reality, deal with it&quot; and &quot;Sleepers hunters <i>cannot</i> hunt them&quot;. On first - there should be some guidlines how to make Sleepers hunt mages. On second it's just ending discussion and makes bad example for gameline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652105#post652105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nevertheless, although Mage 2e will (hopefully) soon be released and its mechanics and setting no longer subject to alteration, since Hunter 2e is still in the early stages of development, who knows what fundamental changes to the game may arise that alter some of these fundamentals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mark topics that should be taken in consideration in at least one ( better in two ) 2ED we talk about. I'm very much dislike on stand from devs &quot;do not use our mages as hunting targets, make some weak witches&quot; as both <b>Mage</b> ST and <b>Hunter</b> player. In both those roles I would want to face Awakened, even if this would be harder - just I ask for some &quot;official help&quot;, as there are &quot;official problems&quot; in running those scenarios made by game designers.<br /> <br /> And, sorry, but Quiescence is much more constantly harassing problem than blood addiction to the vampires hunters stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T01:48:29-07:00","id":652220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652215#post652215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is difference between &quot;mages can bend reality, deal with it&quot; and &quot;Sleepers hunters <i>cannot</i> hunt them&quot;. On first - there should be some guidlines how to make Sleepers hunt mages. On second it's just ending discussion and makes bad example for gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that sleepers <b>cannot </b>hunt Mages. The point is that, for PCs, the experience would be traumatic, badly stacked against them, and they'd leave (victory or failure) confused and damaged. For a lot of players that would probably feel a little like the Storyteller decided to spend four to twelve hours fucking them over without recourse.<br /> <br /> Hunters can find reason to hunt Mages, they can find evidence of magic in tertiary evidence. For instance, while they couldn't recall the necromancer rising zombies, they would know that the cemetery was defiled and all the bodies were found several blocks away looking for all the world like they walked there of their own accord. Then it's only a minor leap (and potential Integrity breaking point) to recall the Mage himself in the cemetery. Doesn't take Sherlock Holmes to conclude he did something funky.<br /> <br /> Hunters can threaten Mages, no sorcerer is perfectly prepared all the time and not all Mages are going to automatically default to harming and killing the hunters (Even powerful ones may conclude &quot;they're just harmless sleepers&quot;, the hubris is real!). Hell even if the hunters cannot defeat the Mage herself, they're presence might wither down her spells and ruin whatever scheme she had in motion, which is a form of victory. Again, it's just not terrifically rewarding for the hunters players. As a Mage it's threatening, maybe not &quot;oh god, one misstep and I'm fucked&quot; threatening, but certainly a major inconvenience at the very least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 09-05-2015, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T02:48:53-07:00","id":652240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652220#post652220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For a lot of players that would probably feel a little like the Storyteller decided to spend four to twelve hours fucking them over without recourse.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652220#post652220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it's only a minor leap (and potential Integrity breaking point) to recall the Mage himself in the cemetery. Doesn't take Sherlock Holmes to conclude he did something funky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second and especially first are problem - I understand hunting mages should not be walk in the park, but making Sleepers Hunters to be &quot;fucked over&quot;, all the time, <b>is</b> problem. Advise on making Hunters all Sleepwalkers is the same as talking to those that fight werewolves &quot;become Wolf-Blooded&quot; - yes, it is <i>some</i> solution, but used on all the time, with all PCs in the cell it's make veil of probability very thin - and by this breaking the immersion in <i>all</i> players.<br /> <br /> I <b>really</b> would like to hear what Sleepers can use to confront Awakened without going with Endowments - what Tier 1 group could use to make ambush on mage? To investigate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T02:52:28-07:00","id":652241,"title":"","content":"Eh, I think it's fine for the Mage gameline to treat Sleepers as powerless (I almost said &quot;irrelevant&quot; here, but that wouldn't have been accurate at all). That's not what many people, including myself, want. But trying to please everyone isn't a terribly good idea when designing games. The current team's vision for Mage is that the Awakened's relationship with Sleepers is entirely one-sided in terms of power and influence. So all the stories that are told in Mage will start from this assumption. I just acknowledge it and stay away from Mage.<br /> <br /> Having said that, I think a thing to remember is that Hunter: the Vigil is not like other gamelines when it comes to crossover. In many if not most Mage games, the existence and exact nature of vampires or mummies is largely irrelevant. They might exist, or they might not. If they exist, they might work like their respective books say, or they might not. It's not going to be hugely important to a cabal of mages trying to deal with an Abyssal incursion, hunting Atlantean mysteries or whatever else mages get up to. The same applies in reverse - vampires dealing with Danse Macabre politics aren't going to consider mortal willworkers important, unless they happen to be involved. But regular mortal humans? They're always there, and they always end up on the receiving end of supernatural fuckery. And not all of them are willing to take it sitting down. Thus, hunters. They're a much more consistent presence in the setting than any given supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 09-05-2015, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T03:13:00-07:00","id":652244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652240#post652240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second and especially first are problem - I understand hunting mages should not be walk in the park, but making Sleepers Hunters to be &quot;fucked over&quot;, all the time, <b>is</b> problem. Advise on making Hunters all Sleepwalkers is the same as talking to those that fight werewolves &quot;become Wolf-Blooded&quot; - yes, it is <i>some</i> solution, but used on all the time, with all PCs in the cell it's make veil of probability very thin - and by this breaking the immersion in <i>all</i> players.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are a problem if you are running crossover, hunter vs mage, yes. But that's pretty standard when it comes to crossover (and hardly restricted to Hunter), indeed as crossover problems go it's a pretty easy fix. I proposed a fix a few pages back (Integrity loss allows the Hunter to remember the supernal even that caused it), things that also come to mind include:<ul><li>Quiessence sets in only after the fact, meaning hunters can deal with the magic in the present and only later (e.g. after that story ends) do they suffer memory loss.</li> <li>The Code can provide some degree of protection against Quiessence. I know Dave said that wasn't the case, but frankly, when developer intent gets in the way of the game you want to play, you kick that intent in the face and carry on.</li> <li>Remove Quiessence entirely and come up with some new reason Mages keep hidden. For instance, perhaps traumatic exposure to the supernal dramatically increases the chance of the victim awakening Mad or as a Banisher. Or disbelief makes spells go violently haywire. Or magic incites in people a disquiet like effect, driving them to hate the Mage. Any of those would leave the Awakened community reticent to reveal their art.</li> </ul>Frankly though, Quiessence is in my mind hardly the biggest hurdle for a Hunter. That would be the sheer flexibility of supernal magic, and the fact that the Mage can probably, in a turn or two, devise some form of fuck you countermeasure for the Hunters. And lets not forget, that even without Quiessence Mages can still cast spells covertly, and are well incentivized to do so (Disbelief, sleeper Integrity damage, and Wisdom loss). Meaning that even the removal of quiessence will not necessarily make Mages easier to detect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652240#post652240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <b>really</b> would like to hear what Sleepers can use to confront Awakened without going with Endowments - what Tier 1 group could use to make ambush on mage? To investigate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sleepers can confront Mages in much the same way they confront any other supernatural: find their weakness and exploit it. In a Mages case that could mean jumping them in a dark alleyway (as weakness in unpreparedness is among their greatest faults). Similarly blowing up the building they are in, or sniping them when they walk out the front door are both highly viable. Or it could mean finding their sleeper family and holding them hostage, or figuring out the Mages objective and putting obstacles in it's way. It could also, for the less homicidal players, mean talking to the Mage and coming to some form of pact or agreement. Or perhaps converting one of the Mages acolytes to their cause, or interrupting the Mage mid summoning and letting his unbound monster tear him limb from limb. Players can be inventive when you give them some strings to follow.<br /> <br /> As for investigating, that's a little harder. They'd have to rely on tertiary evidence which, frankly, is probably all the evidence there will ever be. Mages have ample reason to keep a low profile, and one who is being especially vulgar will attract more attention that just the hunters. Attention, I might add, that the hunters might discover and make use of. Basically to fight mages hunters have to delve into the themes of Mage itself. They become investigators, looking for secrets and signs of the Mages passing while trying to find the proper leverage to get the upper hand. Or, maybe not, maybe they just put a bomb under his car and blow the fuck out of him when he goes to work. Different strokes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T03:45:30-07:00","id":652249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652240#post652240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Second and especially first are problem - I understand hunting mages should not be walk in the park, but making Sleepers Hunters to be &quot;fucked over&quot;, all the time, <b>is</b> problem. Advise on making Hunters all Sleepwalkers is the same as talking to those that fight werewolves &quot;become Wolf-Blooded&quot; - yes, it is <i>some</i> solution, but used on all the time, with all PCs in the cell it's make veil of probability very thin - and by this breaking the immersion in <i>all</i> players.<br /> <br /> I <b>really</b> would like to hear what Sleepers can use to confront Awakened without going with Endowments - what Tier 1 group could use to make ambush on mage? To investigate?</div> </div> </div> </div>But Hunters generally being fucked over all the time is <i><b>the point. </b></i>If a Hunter isn't tier 3 they are <i>meant</i> to be the underdogs. They are <i>designed </i>to be less capable than the supernaturals. They are the candles in the dark, not the vampire/werewolf/mage boogeymen. They are generally going to be at the disadvantage from the git go and it is their job to try to find a way to cheat the system and stack the deck in their own favor using the limited resources/abilities at their disposal.<br /> <br /> It isn't really until you hit Tier 3 that Hunters really get the money/equipment/training/etc. to <i>really</i> start fighting back. Pre-Tier 3 they are better at hunting monsters than your base blue book mortal, but only just, and even that is usually more due to dedication and experience than anything else. They can usually identify what they're going after and have the tools/connections to research how best to deal with such threats, but passed that they're just normal (if trained) guys going in with (hopefully) the right guns and right tactics.<br /> <br /> Again, it's once you hit the big Conspiracies where Hunters really start to get their shit together. That's where they start getting custom anti-supernatural weaponry and shit, and where they start getting man-made enhancements that make them a little bit more (or less if you want to look at it that way) than human. That's where the huge information networks come in, where the government backing comes in, where you stop being a tiny mote of light wandering aimlessly in the dark and band together to become a flood light to light up the dark of night and show the things that lurk in it what's what.<br /> <br /> ...Or at least that's how I see it. To be fair I never really got into Hunter that much so I might be completely off-base but that's always been my take on it and what's seemed most logical to me. Anyways, Hunters pre-Tier 3 can totally hunt mages or whatever else they want, but they do so at a disadvantage. That's just how it is until they get to the point where they become organized and backed hard enough to bring really impressive stuff to bear. They aren't supernatural, they are mundane, and as such have to deal with everything that mundane humans deal with. It's simply part of being a Hunter imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T04:34:26-07:00","id":652270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652249#post652249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Hunters generally being fucked over all the time is <i><b>the point. </b></i>If a Hunter isn't tier 3 they are <i>meant</i> to be the underdogs. They are <i>designed </i>to be less capable than the supernaturals. They are the candles in the dark, not the vampire/werewolf/mage boogeymen. They are generally going to be at the disadvantage from the git go and it is their job to try to find a way to cheat the system and stack the deck in their own favor using the limited resources/abilities at their disposal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but in vampire or werewolf scenarios they are not as limited as with mages. Most of the time vampire or werewolves hunters does remember thier encounters, can exploit their weaknes, make plans. ( I omit here Dominate Discipline and Gifts of Dominate and similar powers, talk about most of particular monster beings that do not have them ). <b>All</b> Mages are &quot;blessed&quot; with power to forgot them and their actions, not only Mind Adept's or Mastigos. The same is not true to other monsters - most hunters can attack <b>any</b> vampire and werewolf ( or at least majority of them ), straight from 2ED <b>Requiem</b> or <b>Forsaken</b> corebooks.<br /> <br /> And would like to here some official answers on to how to run those encounters, beside &quot;make them Sleepwalkers&quot;. Tactics, Integrity tricks, Breaking Points rules - anything to make believable that Sleeper witch hunters under Tier 3 are still a thing, when they spot wierd things in their nearby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-05-2015, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T04:39:32-07:00","id":652271,"title":"","content":"Underdogs is one thing, whipping dogs is another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T04:58:14-07:00","id":652292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652270#post652270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but in vampire or werewolf scenarios they are not as limited as with mages. Most of the time vampire or werewolves hunters does remember thier encounters, can exploit their weaknes, make plans. ( I omit here Dominate Discipline and Gifts of Dominate and similar powers, talk about most of particular monster beings that do not have them ). <b>All</b> Mages are &quot;blessed&quot; with power to forgot them and their actions, not only Mind Adept's or Mastigos. The same is not true to other monsters - most hunters can attack <b>any</b> vampire and werewolf ( or at least majority of them ), straight from 2ED <b>Requiem</b> or <b>Forsaken</b> corebooks.<br /> <br /> And would like to here some official answers on to how to run those encounters, beside &quot;make them Sleepwalkers&quot;. Tactics, Integrity tricks, Breaking Points rules - anything to make believable that Sleeper witch hunters under Tier 3 are still a thing, when they spot wierd things in their nearby.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not certain that's actually true. Doesn't Lunacy also interfere with remembering the werewolf and werewolf activity? How do hunters hunt them? Evidence. You may not have eyewitness testimony (even your own), but you can piece together a pretty good picture. And the guy who shies away from silver? Probably who is responsible.<br /> <br /> As for mages, pretty much what everyone else here has said: you find bits of circumstantial evidence that leads you to suspect your target is a mage. Then, keeping in mind they can bend reality with mind-warping horrible magic (advice: for the Hunter experience, play up the Lovecraftian elements of supernal magic and the Quiescence), you make plans to take them down hard and fast before they can &quot;kill you with their brain&quot;. Gas leaks, snipers, car bombs, back-alley baseball bat to the head, drugging their food/drink, etc. Just always keep in mind you are <i>killing/assaulting another human being</i> on <b>suspicion</b>. Seriously, most preferential Mage-Hunters <i>should</i> end up mentally damaged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T05:02:29-07:00","id":652316,"title":"","content":"Now that Mage Armor is apparently a per-scene (at best) activated ability, a Tier 1 Hunter should get on top of a building with a high-powered sniper rifle. Or, I suppose, do what they should be doing against other supernaturals: more numbers and an unflinching dedication to overwhelming violence. Get your friends, get some automatic weapons for your friends, wait for the Mage somewhere, hope the Mage doesn't know you're coming with Time (or Fate, I guess), pop out, squeeze the trigger until the thunder stops. There's no trick. There's no shortcut. Considering the responses from various Developers over the years about stuff like this, there likely won't ever be either. The Lie does not care about the Vigil.<br /> <br /> And: There are lots of things that Hunters struggle against just as much as a Mage; just because Mage happens to be a playable template doesn't mean Mage can't be one of those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T05:52:53-07:00","id":652361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652270#post652270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but in vampire or werewolf scenarios they are not as limited as with mages. Most of the time vampire or werewolves hunters does remember thier encounters, can exploit their weaknes, make plans. ( I omit here Dominate Discipline and Gifts of Dominate and similar powers, talk about most of particular monster beings that do not have them ). <b>All</b> Mages are &quot;blessed&quot; with power to forgot them and their actions, not only Mind Adept's or Mastigos. The same is not true to other monsters - most hunters can attack <b>any</b> vampire and werewolf ( or at least majority of them ), straight from 2ED <b>Requiem</b> or <b>Forsaken</b> corebooks.<br /> <br /> And would like to here some official answers on to how to run those encounters, beside &quot;make them Sleepwalkers&quot;. Tactics, Integrity tricks, Breaking Points rules - anything to make believable that Sleeper witch hunters under Tier 3 are still a thing, when they spot wierd things in their nearby.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The memory thing really, really, <i>really</i> is not as big a deal as you seem to think it is. Not being able to directly remember the magic itself is rarely going to make or break a Hunter vs Mage encounter, <i>especially</i> considering it doesn't matter until after said encounter has already happened. If you escape the encounter covered in burns you don't need to be able to remember that the mage was chucking fireballs. And it doesn't make them forget the mage or their actions, which you don't seem to be getting. It makes them reconstruct the memory of magic into something else. You still remember the person, you still have some misconstrued approximation of what they did to you (unless what they did was so out there there was literally no way you could think of it as anything else, which I feel would be fairly rare). Again, your memory may tell you that the mage was tossing around molotov cocktails, but what difference does it really make?<br /> <br /> There is nothing, and let me emphasize this more heavily, <i><b>Nothing </b></i>(nothing related to the Sleeping Curse at least) preventing Hunters in 2e from attacking mages. Nothing. Not a thing. If they want to walk up to a mage and shotgun them in the face they are perfectly capable of doing so (assuming the mage doesn't actively attempt to stop them, but that applies to anybody). The Sleeping Curse <b>does not</b>prevent you from attacking anyone. What the Sleeping Curse does is, after the fight is over, makes the Hunter forget that the mage used magic. He doesn't forget that the mage tried to fight back or did anything in that period of time, or even that the mage was there. He just misremembers what exactly it was the mage did during the conflict.<br /> <br /> A Hunter might not remember exactly why he has burn marks, or why his ear drums are busted, or why his partners twitching like he went and hugged an electric fence but he remembers the guy they were after was there and is still pretty sure all of it was his fault. The fact that he doesn't recall exactly what the mage did doesn't really change much about the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T05:54:42-07:00","id":652362,"title":"","content":"What I'm counting here is more than &quot;check wierd thing happening, preper ambush&quot; - it's all true for all supernatural. Point take for Mage Armor. I would <i>prefer</i> changes to Hunter Code for at least partial immunity to Sleeping Curse effects - like they are for the Lunacy.<br /> <br /> Other thing that comes to mine mind for Sleepers hunting mages is Tactics like this:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Make a Scene</b></span><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> &lt;Some Prequisitions&gt;<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b> &lt;Some Dice Pools, probably based on Presence &gt; <br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant. <br /> <b>Description:</b> The best way to deal with the &quot;Awakaned&quot; witch is to confront it with crowd - their magic is said to more chaotic when confronted with &quot;Sleepers&quot; mortals. So answer is simple - put sorceres in situations with lots of humans, best with weapon prepared. This Tactic is as plain as it's basic idea - cell makes a public disturbance in the place so large, random people join confrontation, just being curious. In extreme situation police or other peace keeping forces are called, and they can be swayed to interfere. The goal is to make crowd to think that witch is responsible for the problems and so it will be center of communities ire.<br /> <b>Organizations:</b> &lt;Some groups advised to work good with it. Suspects Malleus Maleficarum, probably Union. Any other? &gt;<br /> <b>Potential Modi\ufb01ers:</b> City center (+2 to all participants); hunters work in law enforcement ( +1 to hunter ); small settlement ( -2 to all participants ); hunters had some problems with law ( -1 to hunter )<br /> <b>Roll Results:</b> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The crowd thinks it's hunters fault and lead their ire on the cell. Law enforcement is send after them.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Crowd not react. No one join the scene.<br /> <b>Success: </b>Crowd joins the scene and it's ire is pointed on the &quot;Awakened&quot; witch. Her Paradox rolls have 9-again quality. If there are three or more success on this Tactic roll, Paradox roles have 8-again quality. <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> Crowd joins the scene and law enforcement is send to deal with it. Ire of the crowd is pointed on the &quot;Awakened&quot; witch. <br /> <br /> Something like this, at least, should be in <b>Hunter</b> 2ED corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T07:49:31-07:00","id":652476,"title":"","content":"I would make the 9- or 8-again rule depend wholly on the size of the crowd, instead of altering the game's assumption that the only degrees of success are <b>Success</b> and <b>Exceptional Success</b>. Also, the Paradox modifier <b><i>will only</i></b> come into play if the mage does something supernaturally obvious. If a Fate mage is keeping themselves safe by making guns pointed at her jam, then there won't be a Paradox modifier.<br /> <br /> I'd also argue that the dice pool should be based on Manipulation rather than Presence, since in most cases a hunter will be lying to the crowd about the mage. Telling the truth would more likely result in the crowd saying &quot;Whoa, this crazy lady keeps calling that guy a witch. We'd better stay out of this.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T07:54:18-07:00","id":652482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652292#post652292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not certain that's actually true. Doesn't Lunacy also interfere with remembering the werewolf and werewolf activity? How do hunters hunt them? Evidence. You may not have eyewitness testimony (even your own), but you can piece together a pretty good picture. And the guy who shies away from silver? Probably who is responsible.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just to explain the difference.<br /> <br /> With Lunacy there is a roll involved, and it is adjusted depending on the viewer's activity and numbers, as well as the relative strength of the werewolf. <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Quiessence</span></span></span> is automatic and unavoidable. If your mind cannot rationalize the magic as a normal action, instead you get amnesia, while even a failure with Lunacy lets you rationalize the werewolf as a wild animal. If your standard world view allows for werewolves, for instance if you're a werewolf hunter, it might not even reorder your memories at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-05-2015, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T08:01:27-07:00","id":652516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652096#post652096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Quiescence itself, there is no such thing as '<i>resisting</i>' the Sleeping Curse. That should be perfectly clear by now. You either have a shard of the Abyss in your soul or you do not, it is a binary thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is trying to argue otherwise. I'm certainly not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652096#post652096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, that isn't to say there's no way to deal with the consequences of such , you just have to try a little harder is all.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what we are asking for. A way to deal with the consequences. A Tactic or a Merit or something that gives hunters a way to cope with the obstacles the Sleeping Curse presents, without actually circumventing it. Something mechanical that gives you a way to piece together the tertiary evidence, or makes the Breaking Points a little less harsh, or helps you recover Integrity. As it stands, dealing with the consequences of the Lie relies entirely on player creativity, there's no actual rules support for it, and Dave seems hellbent on making sure it stays that way, which is just a little frustrating for anyone who wants to play a character who's clever enough to Sherlock Holmes the evidence and find proof positive that his target is a Mage, but is not as a player actually clever enough to do that in real life. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652292#post652292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not certain that's actually true. Doesn't Lunacy also interfere with remembering the werewolf and werewolf activity? How do hunters hunt them? Evidence. You may not have eyewitness testimony (even your own), but you can piece together a pretty good picture. And the guy who shies away from silver? Probably who is responsible.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are literally describing the proposed After-Action Report Tactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T08:09:50-07:00","id":652555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652516#post652516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is what we are asking for. A way to deal with the consequences. A Tactic or a Merit or something that gives hunters a way to cope with the obstacles the Sleeping Curse presents, without actually circumventing it. Something mechanical that gives you a way to piece together the tertiary evidence, or makes the Breaking Points a little less harsh, or helps you recover Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW there is one Merit in that vein that has been spoiled.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Actively Oblivious \u2022\u2022</b><br /> <br /> You\u2019ve lived a hard life, and long ago learned that sometimes the only way to survive realities that are just to hard to face is to not notice them in the first place. That\u2019s why you can smile while you patch up the hole in the kitchen wall and describe your dad as \u2018strict\u2019 rather than abusive. Little do you know, this ability of yours allows you to ignore the greater magical truths of the world as well as the domestic ones.<br /> <b>Effect:</b> By spending a Willpower during an incident that might cause you to suffer a Breaking Point, you can actively ignore the event and not have to make the roll. This requires concentration. This active oblivious state also protects you from \u2018seeing\u2019 events that relate to the Supernal. As a result, should you be successfully and actively oblivious, you do not count as a witness to Supernal magics and cannot be a part of a Paradox risk. (Though you do create Dissonance as this cannot be kept up indefinitely.)<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Whenever you successfully ignore a potential Breaking Point, you suffer the Strained Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Strained (New Condition)</b><br /> Take -1 to resist the next time you suffer a breaking point and must roll. If you have Strained, you may opt to not roll, and the Condition can build, any consecutive times you avoid rolling a Breaking Point contributes another -1 to your next breaking point roll to a maximum of -5. After -5, you can no longer push it away, you snap, and automatically roll for Breaking Point at -5.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The character suffers Integrity loss. Take an additional Beat atop that of the breaking point.<br /> <b>Beats:</b> N/A </div> </div> </div>Just decide that being busy shooting the Mage (maybe involving the use of certain drugs or trance states) is enough to distract yourself from the fireballs they are throwing at you and you are good to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T08:34:38-07:00","id":652607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652555#post652555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> FWIW there is one Merit in that vein that has been spoiled.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just decide that being busy shooting the Mage (maybe involving the use of certain drugs or trance states) is enough to distract yourself from the fireballs they are throwing at you and you are good to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, along with Eye for the Strange from GMC, could work nicely.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In fact, that's just a great damn Merit for hunters in general, because a lot of the stuff they deal with as Hunters is potentially Breaking-Point inducing, not just Supernal magic. And it's pretty on-point for Hunter too, to shrug off one traumatic event after another until it all builds up and suddenly hits you all at once. Thanks for pointing this one out to me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-05-2015, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:10:23-07:00","id":652666,"title":"","content":"As to mine proposed <b>Make a Scene</b> Tactic...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652476#post652476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make the 9- or 8-again rule depend wholly on the size of the crowd, instead of altering the game's assumption that the only degrees of success are <b>Success</b> and <b>Exceptional Success</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about it, as new Paradox rules in <b>Mage</b> would point to number of Sleepers - but still they make differance based on &quot;few/many/crowd&quot; kind of thing. I could rule one man for one success, or something like this, but rules in 2ED <b>Mage</b> ( at least spoiled ) are usage enough that some description working for &quot;9-again Paradox rule&quot; would work. Also, Tactics <i>should</i> work - they are extended action you practice specially with rest of your cell and pay XP for it - they should work, as their are a bit better than Merits characters use. It's their whole point they are rather sure way to exploit monster weakness.<br /> <br /> But, of course, final version of fan Tactic I can shown after I see official 2ED <b>Mage</b> corebook and it's Paradox.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652476#post652476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Paradox modifier <b><i>will only</i></b> come into play if the mage does something supernaturally obvious. If a Fate mage is keeping themselves safe by making guns pointed at her jam, then there won't be a Paradox modifier.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same tricks are in <b>Witchfinders</b> for &quot;lower&quot; witches and they work for <b>Hunter</b> game. Fate magic works for mage only if you know hunters are coming for you...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652476#post652476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also argue that the dice pool should be based on Manipulation rather than Presence, since in most cases a hunter will be lying to the crowd about the mage. Telling the truth would more likely result in the crowd saying &quot;Whoa, this crazy lady keeps calling that guy a witch. We'd better stay out of this.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more &quot;Hey! All around! See what this mean person done! &lt;Splashing the walls by the Hunters, and pointing finger on Awakened&gt;&quot; - that's why I think Presence is more logical. You <b>want</b> people to notice you and the mage, primary. You more making the fuss, than makes some direct emotional manipulation.<br /> <br /> Or in more creepy version this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GEStsLJZhzo\" data-code=\"GEStsLJZhzo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GEStsLJZhzo/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> As to the <b>Actively Oblivious</b> Merit in 2ED <b>Mage</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652555#post652555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just decide that being busy shooting the Mage (maybe involving the use of certain drugs or trance states) is enough to distract yourself from the fireballs they are throwing at you and you are good to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>It solves problems when you know you are facing the mage, yes. But it does not when you have first encounter with him - you cannot make yourself &quot;<i>actively ignore the event and not have to make the roll. (...) This active oblivious state also protects you from \u2018seeing\u2019 events that relate to the Supernal.&quot; </i>- because you would not thinking about encounter as magic in the first place. You could take mage as terrorist, but you would be then preparing for the other threat than the sorcerer at hand. Not to mention that most hunters would not live past first encounter with mage...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-05-2015, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:16:58-07:00","id":652676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652666#post652666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As to the <b>Actively Oblivious</b> Merit in 2ED <b>Mage</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It solves problems when you know you are facing the mage, yes. But it oes not when you have frist evnocunter with him - you cannot make yourself &amp;quot;<i>actively ignore the event and not have to make the roll. (...) This active oblivious state also protects you from \u2018seeing\u2019 events that relate to the Supernal.&amp;quot; </i>- because you would not thinking about encounter as magic in the first place. You could take mage as terrorist, but you would be then preparing for the other threat than the sorcerer at hand. Not to mention that most hunters would not live past first encounter with mage...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is fine. Hunters should be scarred by their first encounter with Supernal Magic, gives them more incentive to hint down the witch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:21:45-07:00","id":652691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652666#post652666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the <b>Actively Oblivious</b> Merit in 2ED <b>Mage</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It solves problems when you know you are facing the mage, yes. But it oes not when you have frist evnocunter with him - you cannot make yourself &amp;quot;<i>actively ignore the event and not have to make the roll. (...) This active oblivious state also protects you from \u2018seeing\u2019 events that relate to the Supernal.&amp;quot; </i>- because you would not thinking about encounter as magic in the first place. You could take mage as terrorist, but you would be then preparing for the other threat than the sorcerer at hand. Not to mention that most hunters would not live past first encounter with mage...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you also take Eye for the Strange, so that after reviewing the evidence you can figure out for certain if the event was natural or supernatural in origin.<br /> <br /> Or just have a Sleepwalker in the cell. I don't think one Sleepwalker on a team of several hunters strains suspension of disbelief too much. Especially since Unseen Sense is a pretty common Merit among hunters, and as a supernatural Merit would make any Hunter that has it a Sleepwalker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:22:21-07:00","id":652692,"title":"","content":"Yep. That &quot;Actively Oblivious&quot; Merit is very much the sort of thing I was looking for; the only problem I have with it is that it's pretty much the antithesis of what I'd expect of hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T09:56:27-07:00","id":652722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652676#post652676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is fine. Hunters should be scarred by their first encounter with Supernal Magic, gives them more incentive to hint down the witch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that first encounter with Supernal Magic would be Sleepers hunters last one - you know, Emotional Urging, Celestial Fire or Rotting Flesh and there are no hunters to have <b>second</b> encounter with <b>Actively Oblivious</b> Merit. Or they at least would not look for the sorcerer.<br /> <br /> And I do not mean here Awakened should not use their Arcana capabilities - they <b>should</b><b> use them, </b>it's why they are <i>monsters</i> in the first place. Only that there should be Merit, Tactics or something that could makes you resistant a bit to influence of magic.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, there are not any powers to survive first encounter with vampire or werewolf in <b>Hunter</b>, so maybe I'm going too far? Maybe unprepared, first encounter Hunters should be &quot;monsters dinner&quot;, just?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652691#post652691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why you also take Eye for the Strange, so that after reviewing the evidence you can figure out for certain if the event was natural or supernatural in origin.<br /> <br /> Or just have a Sleepwalker in the cell. I don't think one Sleepwalker on a team of several hunters strains suspension of disbelief too much. Especially since Unseen Sense is a pretty common Merit among hunters, and as a supernatural Merit would make any Hunter that has it a Sleepwalker.</div> </div> </div> </div>One Sleepwalker is fine, I think. In the end, it's only variant of Unseen Sense. Could use it with some Tactics ideas shown before and we will have some Witch Hunting ways for even Tier 1 hunters.<br /> <br /> Still, let's focus only on non-Sleepwalkers - those cells with Sleepwalkers will have much easier time to interact with Awakened,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-05-2015, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T10:26:10-07:00","id":652757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652692#post652692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. That &quot;Actively Oblivious&quot; Merit is very much the sort of thing I was looking for; the only problem I have with it is that it's pretty much the antithesis of what I'd expect of hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I just plan to do a little bit of re-fluffing with it. Rather than ignoring what's going on around you, you're denying that it has an effect on you. When other humans would be traumatized, you bottle that shit up and push it right back down. You don't have time to be scared, damn it, not when people's lives are in danger! You'll deal with those emotions later, after the fucker that did this is dead and in the ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T11:49:19-07:00","id":652856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652244#post652244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly though, Quiessence is in my mind hardly the biggest hurdle for a Hunter. That would be the sheer flexibility of supernal magic, and the fact that the Mage can probably, in a turn or two, devise some form of fuck you countermeasure for the Hunters. And lets not forget, that even without Quiessence Mages can still cast spells covertly, and are well incentivized to do so (Disbelief, sleeper Integrity damage, and Wisdom loss). Meaning that even the removal of quiessence will not necessarily make Mages easier to detect.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've stated before, I believe one of the greatest advantages of the versatility of supernal magic is that is often permits a mage to easily and quickly escape a violent encounter, whether that involves entering Twilight or the Shadow, simple teleportation through space or time, or just flying away or hiding. That is certainly a <i>very bad thing</i> if you're a Hunter. Not only have you failed in your hunt, but you now have one or more very angry mages, who likely know who you are, are very motivated to eliminate a threat, and worst of all, are very prepared for the task. The Hunters can all too easily become the hunted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652692#post652692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. That &quot;Actively Oblivious&quot; Merit is very much the sort of thing I was looking for; the only problem I have with it is that it's pretty much the antithesis of what I'd expect of hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652757#post652757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I just plan to do a little bit of re-fluffing with it. Rather than ignoring what's going on around you, you're denying that it has an effect on you. When other humans would be traumatized, you bottle that shit up and push it right back down. You don't have time to be scared, damn it, not when people's lives are in danger! You'll deal with those emotions later, after the fucker that did this is dead and in the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with Dataweaver in that &quot;Actively Oblivious,&quot; while interesting and useful for a Sleeper who's routinely exposed to supernal magic, is not really helpful or appropriate for Hunters who clearly and directly confront the supernatural because it is the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Although anyone can create any merit they wish for whatever purposes or goals, I believe attempts at circumventing the Quiescence by &quot;denying its effect on you&quot; is not a &quot;re-fluff&quot; of &quot;Actively Oblivious,&quot; but rather a significant &quot;buff,&quot; and really alters the very nature of Sleeping Curse.<br /> <br /> Moreover, &quot;Actively Oblivious&quot; does absolutely nothing to help you remember supernal magic (the very point of the merit), you are not protected by causing increased Paradox risks for the relevant scene, and the Strained condition makes it more likely you'll fail a Breaking Point roll in the future and lose Integrity (such as your next encounter with the mage). Even if only used as a framework for a similar merit, &quot;Actively Oblivious&quot; offers little real help to Hunters and forfeits important protections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T12:04:49-07:00","id":652872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652271#post652271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Underdogs is one thing, whipping dogs is another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would simply note that Hunter has three tiers of organization and power for a reason. If certain supernaturals like mages are difficult and dangerous for higher tier, experienced Hunters, then lower level normal human Hunters without such advantages would indeed be &quot;whipping dogs&quot; compared to such prey intentionally by game design. It's the reason why the Hunter books include rules for constructing lower power magic-using wizards and sorcerers who clearly are not Awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T12:26:47-07:00","id":652890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652872#post652872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would simply note that Hunter has three tiers of organization and power for a reason. If certain supernaturals like mages are difficult and dangerous for higher tier, experienced Hunters, then lower level normal human Hunters without such advantages would indeed be &quot;whipping dogs&quot; compared to such prey intentionally by game design. It's the reason why the Hunter books include rules for constructing lower power magic-using wizards and sorcerers who clearly are not Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also have rules for creating your own vampires and werewolves - but we do not see all the time the devs to said &quot;you need to use your own created vampires and wolves, not Kindred or Uratha when fighting hunters&quot;. EVEN on Tier 1 games.<br /> <br /> But we are making circles here - Sleeping Curse <i>is needed</i> for both <b>Mage</b> and <b>Hunter</b> with it's witch hunting themes on Awakened. Just, please, stop talking to us &quot;there is no problem&quot;, when at least few posters in all this topic mark there are. We pointing them clearly where they are.<br /> <br /> I mark once more - <b>we do <i><u>not want</u></i> to get rid of Sleeping Curse in Hunters vs Mages crossovers. </b>We want to use tools and advice made by devs to run it more smoothly, a bit maybe omitting some effects of it, with use of Tactics of Merits. That's it. If vampire hunters can be prepered on Blood Bonds or werewolves one can be resisted on some part of Lunacy - why not our mages hunters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T12:42:48-07:00","id":652935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652856#post652856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Dataweaver in that &amp;quot;Actively Oblivious,&amp;quot; while interesting and useful for a Sleeper who's routinely exposed to supernal magic, is not really helpful or appropriate for Hunters who clearly and directly confront the supernatural because it is the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Although anyone can create any merit they wish for whatever purposes or goals, I believe attempts at circumventing the Quiescence by &amp;quot;denying its effect on you&amp;quot; is not a &amp;quot;re-fluff&amp;quot; of &amp;quot;Actively Oblivious,&amp;quot; but rather a significant &amp;quot;buff,&amp;quot; and really alters the very nature of Sleeping Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mechanics are identical, all I'm changing is the rationale. The text definitely describes someone who is in denial, so I don't even see it as a major shift in the narrative of the Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652856#post652856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, &amp;quot;Actively Oblivious&amp;quot; does absolutely nothing to help you remember supernal magic (the very point of the merit), you are not protected by causing increased Paradox risks for the relevant scene, and the Strained condition makes it more likely you'll fail a Breaking Point roll in the future and lose Integrity (such as your next encounter with the mage). Even if only used as a framework for a similar merit, &amp;quot;Actively Oblivious&amp;quot; offers little real help to Hunters and forfeits important protections.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really care that it doesn't help with remembering what happened, I have Eye for the Strange to confirm suspicions of Magic, and as you said, not remembering the exact details of the encounter isn't all that important. I know I got singed in the fight, I remember it being from a Molotov, but my examination of the scene indicates that something magical definitely happened. Doesn't take a genius to put 2 and 2 together at that point. The point of a Hunter taking Actively Oblivious to me is just to give them a way to put off the Breaking Points. Yeah, eventually it'll add up and the character will probably end up failing a future Breaking Point harder, but that's fine, I think it's an appropriate way for a Hunter to operate. And I don't care that the character doesn't add Paradox risk while using the Merit, that has never been the point. Again, I don't want a way to cheat the Lie, I just want a way to help the character cope with its consequences that actually has some kind of mechanical weight behind it. These two Merits accomplish that goal for me very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T12:47:27-07:00","id":652939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652872#post652872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would simply note that Hunter has three tiers of organization and power for a reason. If certain supernaturals like mages are difficult and dangerous for higher tier, experienced Hunters, then lower level normal human Hunters without such advantages would indeed be &quot;whipping dogs&quot; compared to such prey intentionally by game design. It's the reason why the Hunter books include rules for constructing lower power magic-using wizards and sorcerers who clearly are not Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Witch Finders rules were never intended to \u201cclearly not be Awakened&quot;; indeed, the whole point was for them to represent the Awakened, thaumaturges, and any other kind of magic workers the Storyteller wanted to use. They were never intended to be a third kind of magician, distinct from the other two.<br /> <br /> In fact, I'd argue that \u201c\u2026and any other kind of magic workers\u201d was very nearly an afterthought, and that the main focus was on trying to approximate Mages and thaumaturges with a single, concise system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-05-2015, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T12:49:33-07:00","id":652940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652890#post652890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mark once more - <b>we do <i><u>not want</u></i> to get rid of Sleeping Curse in Hunters vs Mages crossovers. </b>We want to use tools and advice made by devs to run it more smoothly, a bit maybe omitting some effects of it, with use of Tactics of Merits. That's it. If vampire hunters can be prepered on Blood Bonds or werewolves one can be resisted on some part of Lunacy - why not our mages hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for one, mundane humans can't resist the Blood Bond (not sure about Lunacy since I haven't gone that deep into 2e werewolf). Once you' ingest the vitae you're subject to the effects of the Blood Bond, end of story. So this isn't really any different in terms of resistability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:03:32-07:00","id":652944,"title":"","content":"Fortunately, the blood bond can be avoided by not drinking vampire blood. Lunacy can be resisted with a dice roll, which can be bolstered by various methods. Quiscience cannot be resisted by a roll, nor can it be avoided short of just not hunting Magrs. Which is fine, that's an important part of the setting and I have no interest in changing that fact. But something to help cope with its completely unavoidable effects would go a long way towards making Hunters not feel completely powerless against Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:05:08-07:00","id":652947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652890#post652890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mark once more - <b>we do <i><u>not want</u></i> to get rid of Sleeping Curse in Hunters vs Mages crossovers. </b>We want to use tools and advice made by devs to run it more smoothly, a bit maybe omitting some effects of it, with use of Tactics of Merits. That's it. If vampire hunters can be prepered on Blood Bonds or werewolves one can be resisted on some part of Lunacy - why not our mages hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave, the Mage developer, has repeatedly and explicitly noted the canon rules concerning the Quiescence as well as offered some advice concerning Sleeper Hunters and Mages. You might disagree with the rules or his opinions, but it appears that the game system will not <i>officially</i> accommodate your priorities or crossover preferences (at least until Hunter 2e is released, and even then it's unlikely). Your displeasure should be directed at Dave and OPP, although many here, including myself, agree with his perspectives.<br /> <br /> Moreover, if mundane (i.e., non-supernatural) Tactics can omit certain effects of the Sleeping Curse, you are indeed demanding that the games change the fundamental nature of the Quiescence in the nWOD. The Sleeping Curse is simply not equivalent or comparable to Blood Bonds or Lunacy, although you are free to ignore anything you wish and implement house rules if it suits your personal setting and game preferences. Unfortunately, it's impossible for the default setting rules and setting to please everyone.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:13:41-07:00","id":652951,"title":"","content":"Does Monica Valentinelli, the new Hunter 2e developer, post on the OPP forums, and has she indicated how she might deal with the Awakened Mage vs. Hunter scenario in 2e, or what fundamental changes might be expected in the new edition? I didn't notice anything in my quick perusal of the Hunter forum.<br /> <br /> I'm very curious if she agrees with Dave, and hope the two games don't end up having conflicting rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  typo on Monica's name 09-05-2015, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:18:52-07:00","id":652955,"title":"","content":"I would also be very interested in Monica's views on crossover matters in general.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I hope that some common ground can be found between Mage and Hunter; but if there's an unresolvable conflict, I'd much rather Hunter stay true to Hunter's themes than to abandon them for the sake of conformity with Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-05-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:37:34-07:00","id":652972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652215#post652215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it is weird, as Kindred and Forsaken still fear the mortals. Mages - by developers - just say &quot;oh, you have Abyss Shard, that's a pitty, now do not bother me&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is funny, since the mage corebook has a witch hunter writeup in the antagonists section. <br /> <br /> Kind of a funny thing to include if mortals hunting mages isn't an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T13:45:56-07:00","id":652997,"title":"","content":"You're talking about 1e, right? Because 2e has revised the obstacles that Sleepers face to be considerably more intense than 1e posited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:09:19-07:00","id":653019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=652997#post652997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're talking about 1e, right? Because 2e has revised the obstacles that Sleepers face to be considerably more intense than 1e posited.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the major templates seem to have or will receive a significant overall power boost from the first editions, in addition to demonstrable setting and focus changes. Hunter 2e may ultimately be a very different game and setting that what it is now. For instance, we know that Hunter 2e will include the &quot;Slasher Chronicle,&quot; and presumably be the &quot;big bads&quot; of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:26:40-07:00","id":653032,"title":"","content":"I've mentioned elsewhere my thoughts concerning Hunter 2e. To summarize, it's coming out at the same time as world of darkness 2nd edition. WOD second will include monster building rules, so I'm hoping that Hunter second will be more explicitly a crossover book than Hunter first was, more like Beast (but antagonistic rather than friendly).<br /> <br /> Yes, Slasher Chronicles will be featured; but I doubt that means that all or most Hunter Chronicles are assumed to be about Slashers. Continuing the Beast comparison, Slashers should be to hunters as Heroes are to Beasts. That is, they're the default antagonists if you don't want to use crossover antagonists or blue-book monsters, and the Slasher phenomenon is connected to the Hunter phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-05-2015, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:28:05-07:00","id":653098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653032#post653032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Slashers should be to hunters as Heroes are to Beasts</div> </div> </div> </div>Eek! That's sure to raise some eyebrows after the controversies surrounding Beast and Heroes! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More seriously, it's so early we just have no idea what to expect from Hunter 2e. Since Monica was a writer on<i> Hunter</i> <i>Mortal Remains</i> (but notably not a Mage corebook author), with ts transitional edition rules and updates, it might be the best and only source of how the new edition might develop, but I would not focus too heavily on that book. Even if Monica revealed some ideas, as with Mage 2e, they would also likely evolve and change of the months of writing, development, editing and playtesting. <br /> <br /> I think the best we can hope for at this stage is that Dave and Monica have a conversation in the hopes of encouraging rules and setting consistency.***<br /> <br /> *** If they cannot reach any agreements, I would then suggest a no-holds-barred cagematch, with the winner getting to decide on crossover rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:46:31-07:00","id":653103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653098#post653098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More seriously, it's so early we just have no idea what to expect from Hunter 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026which is why I've been speaking of my hopes for the book rather than my expectations. That said, my <i>expectations</i> are that the antagonists will include vampires, werewolves, mages, created brings, changelings, mediums, mummies, demons, etc., but not <i>necessarily</i> Kindred, Uratha, Awakened, Prometheans, Lost, Sin-Eaters, Arisen, Unchained, etc. I'd <i>like</i> to see the latter, but that's no more than a wish at this point.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm going to be very disappointed if Hunter 2e becomes \u201cmortals who fight cheap knockoffs of the other gamelines, because they can't cut it in the Major Leagues\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-05-2015, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:49:52-07:00","id":653107,"title":"","content":"I forgot which game was referenced with Hunter, but it seems that the Hunter developer would defer to another game's developer when it comes to that other game, so we already have the final word from DB. I think that was actually a rule by Rich to prevent games providing conflicting rules. The Mage guy decides how Mage works and the Hunter gal does the same for Hunter, when there is crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T19:02:15-07:00","id":653354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653103#post653103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That said, I'm going to be very disappointed if Hunter 2e becomes \u201cmortals who fight cheap knockoffs of the other gamelines, because they can't cut it in the Major Leagues\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that point, we are in agreement. I believe Hunter needs more of a &quot;hook&quot; or uniqueness for the template to compete in, as you say, the Major Leagues, but I'm at a loss as to what that could be without turning Hunters into another supernatural race or providing other supernatural assistance. Since the nWOD second editions have seemed to totally eliminate the &quot;tier system&quot; first established in Hunter 1e, I'm even more curious to see how Hunter 2e handles the various power levels and organization of Hunter groups.<br /> <br /> In fact, as you indicated earlier, since the new WOD 2e corebook will have a generic monster building system, your expectations seem particularly, if a little sadly, valid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653107#post653107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot which game was referenced with Hunter, but it seems that the Hunter developer would defer to another game's developer when it comes to that other game, so we already have the final word from DB. I think that was actually a rule by Rich to prevent games providing conflicting rules. The Mage guy decides how Mage works and the Hunter gal does the same for Hunter, when there is crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like the developers and writers don't\\ talk to one another or exchange ideas. If Dave and Monica cooperatively wanted to find a way to sidestep the Quiescence or anything else, it could be done. Whether that desire exists or is believed in any way necessary is another matter entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-05-2015, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T20:29:01-07:00","id":653450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653354#post653354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, as you indicated earlier, since the new WOD 2e corebook will have a generic monster building system, your expectations seem particularly, if a little sadly, valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, in the 2015-2016 brochure, it did say &quot;Hunter: The Vigil 2nd Edition will feature The Slasher Chronicle. It employs the World of Darkness second edition rules <b>and will be compatible with other game lines.</b>&quot; (emphasis mine). So, I'd say it's pretty reasonable to speculate that the core book will focus on unpowered mortals vs. monsters built with the generalized system while Hunter will focus on Compacts and Conspiracies vs. the other gamelines via crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T20:49:20-07:00","id":653458,"title":"","content":"I hadn't considered the possibility that 2e might drop first-tier hunters, and I hope that it doesn't. To me, Practical Experience is the backbone of Hunter; and anyone who benefits from it is a hunter \u2014 including independent cells.<br /> <br /> As I see it, the &quot;hook&quot;, as branford put it, lies in defining what Practical Experience is, who can get it and why, and what you can do with it. My answers to the questions:<br /> <br /> \u00b7 it's a metagaming currency that exists solely allow hunters to grow and adapt to the supernatural quickly enough that they stand a chance of holding their own.<br /> \u00b7 Those who take up the Vigil can earn Practical Experience, because they're the ones who face off against the supernatural and this can learn and adapt to it.<br /> \u00b7 Practical Experience can give you edges that help you fight the supernatural, both mundane (such as Tactics) and supernatural (such as Endowments). Not everyone who can earn Practical Experience can spend it on the full spread of options, and the restrictions on what you can spend it on define which &quot;tier&quot; you're in., power-wise.<br /> <br /> More later; work calls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:13:39-07:00","id":653469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653450#post653450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in the 2015-2016 brochure, it did say &quot;Hunter: The Vigil 2nd Edition will feature The Slasher Chronicle. It employs the World of Darkness second edition rules <b>and will be compatible with other game lines.</b>&quot; (emphasis mine). So, I'd say it's pretty reasonable to speculate that the core book will focus on unpowered mortals vs. monsters built with the generalized system while Hunter will focus on Compacts and Conspiracies vs. the other gamelines via crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope that at least crossover angle will be done right. As I understand, <b>HtV 2ED</b> still could have Tier 1 Hunters, only it won't have as extensive rules to them as<b> WoD 2ED</b> corebook. And <b>Hunter</b> will more out emphasies of Tier 1 interactions with proper gamelines monsters - that mean in Mage area it should still lead to the problems we rise in the topic ( i.e. running Tier 1 Hunters on Awakened ). I just hope it will really solve them with Tactics or Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-06-2015, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:14:55-07:00","id":653471,"title":"","content":"I don't think Hunter 2e will differentiate between the Tiers like 1e did, but I didn't mean that I expected them to drop (for lack of a better term) Tier 1 hunters. I was just trying to use Tier-neutral language. That said, now that you mention it, I suppose that's a direction they <i>could</i> take it. I don't expect they'd go that way with it though, that would probably put off a lot of players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:20:50-07:00","id":653474,"title":"","content":"So you think that what <b>was</b> previous Tier 1 will be just in <b>WoD</b> 2ED corebook and proper Tier 2 and Tier 3 will be in <b>Hunter</b> 2ED?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:29:50-07:00","id":653480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653450#post653450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in the 2015-2016 brochure, it did say &quot;Hunter: The Vigil 2nd Edition will feature The Slasher Chronicle. It employs the World of Darkness second edition rules <b>and will be compatible with other game lines.</b>&quot; (emphasis mine). So, I'd say it's pretty reasonable to speculate that the core book will focus on unpowered mortals vs. monsters built with the generalized system while Hunter will focus on Compacts and Conspiracies vs. the other gamelines via crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may very well be correct and your reference to the new nWOD 2e core reasonable, but I don't believe a simply note that a second edition nWOD game, Hunter 2e, will unsurprisingly be &quot;compatible&quot; with other second edition nWOD game lines, all using the exact same basic role-playing system, is necessarily a commentary either way about how crossover-friendly Sleeper / normal human Hunters will be with Awakened mages. Dave's firmly expressed positions only reinforce that the Sleeper Hunter - Awakened Mage relationship may remain decidedly one-sided even if attempts are made in Hunter 2e for improved crossover.<br /> <br /> I really would love to hear Monica's thoughts about the matter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-06-2015, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:36:16-07:00","id":653482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653474#post653474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you think that what <b>was</b> previous Tier 1 will be just in <b>WoD</b> 2ED corebook and proper Tier 2 and Tier 3 will be in <b>Hunter</b> 2ED?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly possible, but since the new nWOD 2e corebook has not yet been released, and Hunter 2e is still very early in development with no apparent comments from Monica or anyone else from OPP about what fundamental or major changes might be coming to Hunter, our basis for speculation is very, very limited and involve far more hope than fact.<br /> <br /> Based on general comments by Dave and others, however, it's seems that the entire Tier system has been removed from the nWOD second edition products, and I'm fairly confident that Hunter 2e will not be an exception. What that will mean for Hunter is anyone's guess. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:47:21-07:00","id":653491,"title":"","content":"I imagine what it'll be like is focusing on making Hunters more... clandestine, seperating &quot;Field agents&quot; from the &quot;staff&quot; most likely is going to be a thing. The difference might then become who has access to what providers and contacts in the greater world. Tier as we understand it might be the mechanical equivalent of a Power Trait mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:49:48-07:00","id":653493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653474#post653474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you think that what <b>was</b> previous Tier 1 will be just in <b>WoD</b> 2ED corebook and proper Tier 2 and Tier 3 will be in <b>Hunter</b> 2ED?</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>could</i>, but I don't think it <i>will</i>. I just think the 2e core will focus on non-hunter humans and non-splat monsters, while 2e Hunter will focus on Hunters (both Compact/Conspiracy members and unaffiliated hunters) and crossover. I don't think the idea of Tiers is going to carry over into 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:51:33-07:00","id":653496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653491#post653491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine what it'll be like is focusing on making Hunters more... clandestine, seperating &quot;Field agents&quot; from the &quot;staff&quot; most likely is going to be a thing. The difference might then become who has access to what providers and contacts in the greater world. Tier as we understand it might be the mechanical equivalent of a Power Trait mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Possibly, although at this point the discussion and inquiries would probably best be moved into the Hunter forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T21:54:11-07:00","id":653498,"title":"","content":"Also, for what it's worth (since I'm pretty solidly on the side of &quot;Hunters are just going to have to deal with it&quot;) I don't think that the After-Action Report Tactic because it easily falls within the purview of how existing skills are used -- why are witnesses reporting drastically different events (one says a gas stove exploded, another says it was a fireworks accident, another says the dude had a flamethrower...and yet the burn marks are consistent with none of these things), . I would, however, enjoy a small section of the book providing equivilant rules for investigating things people can't remember. If we're really trying to make Quiescence not hurt as much with Hunters, giving them a Tactic tax seems like something that shouldn't be happening.<br /> <br /> And, hopefully, with the &quot;will be compatible with other game lines&quot;, they won't have things like being able to amputate a Mage's magic and other such silly tactics. Really, I'd love for Hunter2 to focus on the things that aren't major splats, since there's basically infinite things out there and at least the major splats tend to have some form of society keeping them in check. The one dude who woke up with tentacle hands, camouflage skin, and insatiable hunger for human spleens doesn't exactly have a mentor nor a boss to reign them in.<br /> <br /> I'm also more than confident that Hunter2 won't be kneecapping one of Mage's major themes despite it not actually interfering with any of Hunters' major themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T22:02:41-07:00","id":653504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653498#post653498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(since I'm pretty solidly on the side of \u201cHunters are just going to have to deal with it\u201d)</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny; so am I. We just happen to have different notions of what it means to &quot;deal with it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-06-2015, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T22:27:50-07:00","id":653518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653498#post653498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, hopefully, with the &quot;will be compatible with other game lines&quot;, they won't have things like being able to amputate a Mage's magic and other such silly tactics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave has commented about such Tactics many times, appeared amused, and basically suggested they be ignored as inapplicable to Awakened mages. He emphasized that in the nWOD and Hunter there were certainly a variety of &quot;mages,&quot; sorcerers, wizards and other magic using people who may be susceptible to such Tactics, but the much smaller subset of Awakened Mages most certainly would not. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653498#post653498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, I'd love for Hunter2 to focus on the things that aren't major splats, since there's basically infinite things out there and at least the major splats tend to have some form of society keeping them in check. The one dude who woke up with tentacle hands, camouflage skin, and insatiable hunger for human spleens doesn't exactly have a mentor nor a boss to reign them in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mr. Hungry Spleentastic Camo Tentacle Hands may now indeed belong to an established society<br /> <br /> Check-out the discussion about Deviant, the new nWOD game line. Dave is even the developer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T22:34:37-07:00","id":653520,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm rather excited about Deviant. Megacorporations have a special place in my heart. <br /> <br /> And yet, I'd still hope that the majority of the monsters out there aren't established splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T06:04:23-07:00","id":653782,"title":"","content":"I find it kinda weird how with almost 200 posts, no one has really touched on one of, if not the greatest weakness of the Awakened that Hunters can exploit up the wazoo: Hubris.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Awakened have all kinds of ways to fuck over those lowly Hunter pests they might as well not bother with them, and that's where Hunters can get 'em. Oh, you filled the tall building you live in with all kinds of magical barriers and booby traps? How about that, I just blew up the main supports and made the entire building crumble with you in it. Did you just put yourself on a plane so that you can read anyone's mind for killing intent before they even have a chance to act on their plan? Too bad you didn't account for my little rocket launcher that I fired from the sea. Getting past your magical defenses must've been a fluke, huh? Yeah, keep thinking that while I proceed to Step &quot;Owning Your Haughty Bitch-ass&quot;.<br /> <br /> (I may or may not have recently watched Fate/Zero)<br /> <br /> While on the subject of hubris, I feel that the whole attitude of &quot;there's just no way to work around or cope with Quiescence, deal with it&quot; is a major design flaw with Mage in general, not just on the subject of Hunters because it creates a disconnect with the theme of hubris. It's not hubris if there really is no way for ordinary folks to touch you, and ditching ordinary folks to bring on the Price of Hubris is quite the lost opportunity. After all, shock-dropping is a <i>very</i> effective means of delivering horror.<br /> <br /> It's the very reason I'm still unnerved when facing even the tacky, hoop earring ReDeads of Wind Waker. You feel like a badass because all you have to do is simply whack enemies with your sword until they explode, then you meet one of them that takes it all away as it slowly approaches you. You can do the same thing to Mage players as Sleepers of all people suddenly have them in a bind, or are killing off their comrades with alarming frequency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T06:12:36-07:00","id":653791,"title":"","content":"&quot;Guys I took out the building's supports like you said and it's not falling over. What do I do?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T07:05:33-07:00","id":653872,"title":"","content":"Personally, as far as Quiescence is concerned I'm still not seeing what the big deal going against it as written is. You can't remember magic as magic, but instead rationalize it as something else, so what? How does that really impede Hunters from hunting mages? A Hunter should generally be able to figure out whether or not someone is a mage using indirect observation. Is it absolutely foolproof? No, but honestly I don't really feel like detection should be 100% flawless, and it should accurate enough for most purposes.<br /> <br /> And again, it isn't like it does anything during any sort of confrontation. If you bust into a mages sanctum and he starts creating golems out of the ground and sending them at you you see them and recognize him a doing such. So there's no real effect during a fight to contend with, it's the same as any other kind of hunt.<br /> <br /> As for afterwards, you remember the mage as attacking you mundanely. You don't forget he was a mage assuming you go into the fight knowing that, you just don't recall him actually using magic. This still doesn't impact whether you were able to hunt the mage successfully or not. Either you did and the guys dead or you didn't and you now have much worse things to worry about than the Sleeping Curse.<br /> <br /> So I'm not really seeing what else you could really want. I mean if you're looking for ways to figure out what sort of magic the mage is using there's already mechanics for that. It's called an investigations roll to piece together whatever evidence you can find on scene, including but not limited to:<br /> <br /> - Witness Testimonies<br /> - Analysis of Structural Damage<br /> - Identification of Strange Materials and Substances<br /> <br /> You don't really need any sort of special Tactic, or Merit, or whatever to do this. It's just a normal use of skills. And while there <i>are</i> some things that you probably can't understand purely from evidence (a lot of these things you might not understand even if you <i>could</i> remember what you saw), this only makes hunting mages a little bit more difficult, but still in no way impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T07:27:18-07:00","id":653888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653791#post653791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Guys I took out the building's supports like you said and it's not falling over. What do I do?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Uh, stare at it long enough, maybe?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T09:56:07-07:00","id":654035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653791#post653791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cGuys I took out the building's supports like you said and it's not falling over. What do I do?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cCall channel 4 news!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:25:37-07:00","id":654065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=653872#post653872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, as far as Quiescence is concerned I'm still not seeing what the big deal going against it as written is. You can't remember magic as magic, but instead rationalize it as something else, so what? How does that really impede Hunters from hunting mages? A Hunter should generally be able to figure out whether or not someone is a mage using indirect observation. Is it absolutely foolproof? No, but honestly I don't really feel like detection should be 100% flawless, and it should accurate enough for most purposes.<br /> <br /> And again, it isn't like it does anything during any sort of confrontation. If you bust into a mages sanctum and he starts creating golems out of the ground and sending them at you you see them and recognize him a doing such. So there's no real effect during a fight to contend with, it's the same as any other kind of hunt.<br /> <br /> As for afterwards, you remember the mage as attacking you mundanely. You don't forget he was a mage assuming you go into the fight knowing that, you just don't recall him actually using magic. This still doesn't impact whether you were able to hunt the mage successfully or not. Either you did and the guys dead or you didn't and you now have much worse things to worry about than the Sleeping Curse.<br /> <br /> So I'm not really seeing what else you could really want. I mean if you're looking for ways to figure out what sort of magic the mage is using there's already mechanics for that. It's called an investigations roll to piece together whatever evidence you can find on scene, including but not limited to:<br /> <br /> - Witness Testimonies<br /> - Analysis of Structural Damage<br /> - Identification of Strange Materials and Substances<br /> <br /> You don't really need any sort of special Tactic, or Merit, or whatever to do this. It's just a normal use of skills. And while there <i>are</i> some things that you probably can't understand purely from evidence (a lot of these things you might not understand even if you <i>could</i> remember what you saw), this only makes hunting mages a little bit more difficult, but still in no way impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't fight what you don't know exists. You certainly can't identify what you don't know exists. If a Hunter can't remember magic ever happening, they won't know magic exists, and they can't hunt mages.<br /> <br /> I'd be fine with the idea that only 3rd tier Conspiracies can hunt mages. They have extra support. They exist to take down the bigger threads. But this idea of &quot;Nothing can touch Dave's Mages no matter what anybody else says because Dave says so&quot; is harmful to the nWoD 2e as a whole. As much as I love his work (he's easily one of my favorite devs), he's too protective of any perceived weakness applied to his baby. 1e Hunters had mana-draining devices and guns that made Vampires lose Vitae. It's not that out-there that the Conspiracies can develop counters to the Lie, even if it's rare, expensive, and filled with drawbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:44:07-07:00","id":654082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654065#post654065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this idea of &quot;Nothing can touch Dave's Mages no matter what anybody else says because Dave says so&quot; is harmful to the nWoD 2e as a whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is either an astounding failure of perspective or a deliberate and terrible exaggeration on your part unless you somehow actually think an effect that only applies to mundane humans constitutes a blanket debuff across the entire spectrum of possible antagonists.<br /> <br /> It's not a good thing to include in your argument in any case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T10:58:57-07:00","id":654089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654065#post654065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't fight what you don't know exists. You certainly can't identify what you don't know exists. If a Hunter can't remember magic ever happening, they won't know magic exists, and they can't hunt mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>As described in a few prior posts, you can certainly discover something supernatural is at play in the environment and ascertain who's likely responsible. The Quiescence certainly makes this much more difficult when it comes to Awakened mages, including preparation for the hunt, but hardly impossible. I agree with Ashenrogue that the Quiescence, while an advantage for the Awakened, is not their greatest asset or insurmountable. I believe that the versatility and power of the Awakened, individually but much more so as cabals and consilia, are what makes them such potent prey. Unless your Hunters are Tier 3, this generally applies to all the major template supernaturals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654065#post654065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be fine with the idea that only 3rd tier Conspiracies can hunt mages. They have extra support. They exist to take down the bigger threads. But this idea of &quot;Nothing can touch Dave's Mages no matter what anybody else says because Dave says so&quot; is harmful to the nWoD 2e as a whole. As much as I love his work (he's easily one of my favorite devs), he's too protective of any perceived weakness applied to his baby. 1e Hunters had mana-draining devices and guns that made Vampires lose Vitae. It's not that out-there that the Conspiracies can develop counters to the Lie, even if it's rare, expensive, and filled with drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're significantly exaggerating Dave's comments about the purported absolute secrecy and invincibility of the Awakened. He simply stated that the Quiescence affects all Sleepers, and no mundane Tactic or similar measures provides immunity (if you have an inherent supernatural merit or ability, you are a de facto Sleepwalker and immune to the Sleeping Curse). Dave also emphasized that the Curse that affects Sleepers, Sleepwalkers and Awakened alike, just in different ways. He also made the relatively obvious and banal observation that the Awakened are indeed powerful compared to normal humans, as are most of the nWOD major template. Absent the advantages and likely supernatural assistance and power available to Tier 3 Hunters, mages <i>should</i> be exceptionally difficult to take down. In fact, at least in Hunter 1e, the Tier system is supposed to represent the demonstrable differences in organization, power and resources among Hunters.<br /> <br /> I would additionally note that Dave correctly observed that a number of Hunter Tactics violated fundamental and immutable rules concerning templates besides the Awakened, and thus significant conflicts with the other nWOD game lines. As the Mage developer, Dave unsurprisingly suggested that when actually playing Mage, conflicts should be resolved in favor of Mage rules, mechanics and setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-06-2015, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T11:11:44-07:00","id":654098,"title":"","content":"I feel like the two sides of this debate are just talking past each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T11:41:45-07:00","id":654193,"title":"","content":"The impression I got from DB was Hunters can't do anything about Quiescence and shouldn't zerg a Mage. The Lie works best to hide Mages when Sleepers are unaware and it does help to keep them unaware. Hunters are likely to suspect or know Mages exist. The Quiescence actually hurts Mages once suspected by a Hunter. Not knowing what a Mage can do means you: 1) don't care what kind of person they are because magic (you don't really know what kind of person they are) 2) will assume all sorts of abilities a Mage can possess that will suggest covert overkill is the way to go. Mail them an envelope of anthrax and see what happens. If the Mage doesn't get sick, bomb their car. If the Mage survives that, try sniping from a rooftop. It keeps going on and on. It doesn't matter that you don't know the magic that keeps the Mage alive. You still know what didn't work. The more violent Hunters would likely go full lethal any time they spot a Mage. Eventually something is likely to stick. They will inform any other Hunters that they know, so the best defense a Mage has is to not be found out. Actually, that is the best defense for anything Hunters hunt. Mages are just better at hiding from mortals than others. The Lie separates Hunters and Mages like an abyss exists between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T12:02:51-07:00","id":654218,"title":"","content":"My impression is that some Hunter fans do this every time the downsides of using Paradox to attack mages are pointed out, and no matter what we do it won't be enough for them. So why support it at all? It's like demanding CAS change Mummy so that the Chosen of Shulpae are possible under Mummy's rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T12:07:43-07:00","id":654221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654218#post654218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression is that some Hunter fans do this every time the downsides of using Paradox to attack mages are pointed out, and no matter what we do it won't be enough for them. So why support it at all? It's like demanding CAS change Mummy so that the Chosen of Shulpae are possible under Mummy's rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>My impression is that other Hunter fans with different concerns also regarding crossover with Mage often get brushed off because their concerns are misconstrued as being this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-06-2015, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T12:12:38-07:00","id":654225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654221#post654221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My impression is that other Hunter fans with different concerns also regarding crossover with Mage often get brushed off because their conscerns are misconstrued as being this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. In particular, if you've been interpreting my comments through the lens of not liking the downsides of hunters using Paradox as a weapon, then you have been fundamentally misunderstanding where I'm coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T12:47:58-07:00","id":654301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654221#post654221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My impression is that other Hunter fans with different concerns also regarding crossover with Mage often get brushed off because their concerns are misconstrued as being this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe Dave is &quot;brushing off&quot; concerns about crossover. It's more that, as the Mage developer, crossover is not a priority when designing, implementing, and playing Mage, and he's not going to alter Quiescence, a very fundamental and important element of the Mage setting, no less intentionally weaken mages, because some generally lower tier characters in another game line want to be able to more easily hunt and kill Awakened mages. Dave, and other OPP developers, have explicitly stated that they are no longer designing the nWOD around &quot;game balance.&quot; Even in games like Beast which is explicitly and unusually crossover-friendly, the protagonists are certainly demonstrably more or less powerful than certain other game line templates.<br /> <br /> As always, and particularly when running a Hunter chronicle (as opposed to Mage, Vampire, Werewolf, or anything else), feel free to easily tweak the canon rules for the benefit of the Hunters. In fact, it's possible than Monica may encourage players to do so in the new edition. Rules conflicts and ambiguities may be explicit and intentional, and while possibly frustrating for some, it would hardly be the first time such a situation existed in the WOD.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T12:53:37-07:00","id":654313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654221#post654221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My impression is that other Hunter fans with different concerns also regarding crossover with Mage often get brushed off because their concerns are misconstrued as being this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Step one to circumventing that issue is to <i>not make a problem with having infamously-crossover-unfriendly Hunter cross over with specific gamelines out to be a reason to change <b>how a part of the other gameline's metaphysics work.</b></i><br /> <br /> There's number of reasons the phrase &quot;witch-hunt&quot; has the connotations it does, and the failure of plausible deniability is one of them. The archetype tends toward either occupying some degree of hypocrisy by using a level of magical power to stamp out magicians or being hypervigilant and paranoid about things that most people would not point to as evidence of supernatural meddling. Neither of these is reduced in viability by having hunters of the Awakened either be Sleepwalkers or be unhinged enough to blame a mage for something that his memories indicate is a coincidence or a mundanely-inflicted grievance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T12:59:44-07:00","id":654317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654301#post654301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe Dave is &quot;brushing off&quot; concerns about crossover. It's more that, as the Mage developer, crossover is not a priority when designing, implementing, and playing Mage, and he's not going to alter Quiescence, a very fundamental and important element of the Mage setting, no less intentionally weaken mages, because some generally lower tier characters in another game line want to be able to more easily hunt and kill Awakened mages. Dave, and other OPP developers, have explicitly stated that they are no longer designing the nWOD around &quot;game balance.&quot; Even in games like Beast which is explicitly and unusually crossover-friendly, the protagonists are certainly demonstrably more or less powerful than certain other game line templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, once again, no one in this thread wants Dave to alter how Quiessence works or to intentionally weaken mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654301#post654301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As always, and particularly when running a Hunter chronicle (as opposed to Mage, Vampire, Werewolf, or anything else), feel free to easily tweak the canon rules for the benefit of the Hunters. In fact, it's possible than Monica may encourage players to do so in the new edition. Rules conflicts and ambiguities may be explicit and intentional, and while possibly frustrating for some, it would hardly be the first time such a situation existed in the WOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that goes without saying. But what's being asked for in this thread is not a change to the rules. It's simply a way for non-sleepwalker hunters to, after experiencing the effects of Quiessence, cope with those effects. Maybe something that helps them regain lost Integrity. Maybe something that helps them, as you yourself have suggested, use tertiary evidence to form educated guesses about what it might be that is missing from their memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T13:09:38-07:00","id":654323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654317#post654317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, once again, no one in this thread wants Dave to alter how Quiessence works or to intentionally weaken mages.<br /> <br /> Sure, that goes without saying. But what's being asked for in this thread is not a change to the rules. It's simply a way for non-sleepwalker hunters to, after experiencing the effects of Quiessence, cope with those effects. Maybe something that helps them regain lost Integrity. Maybe something that helps them, as you yourself have suggested, use tertiary evidence to form educated guesses about what it might be that is missing from their memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that <i>some</i> of the suggestions to circumvent or ameliorate Quiescence or render Awakened less of a threat to Sleeper Hunters do indeed change the nature and extent of the Sleeping Curse and the canon power framework and levels of Awakened mages. We'll just have to agree to disagree.<br /> <br /> Also, do you really need special Hunter Tactics to notice something strange or potentially supernatural is happening in the Hunters' community, or even that a particular person, Awakened or otherwise, is connected, if not responsible? Not only does it appear to be a normal use of skills, abilities and contacts, as well as standard role-playing, but it's more the basis for a hunt, rather than part of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T13:17:06-07:00","id":654326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654313#post654313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Step one to circumventing that issue is to <i>not make a problem with having infamously-crossover-unfriendly Hunter cross over with specific gamelines out to be a reason to change <b>how a part of the other gameline's metaphysics work.</b></i></div> </div> </div> </div>This is that talking past each other thing. I do not want, and have never wanted, to change the way Mage's metaphysics work. I just want Hunter to have some elements that help the characters bare the burden that comes with hunting Mages as a sleeper, within the constraints of Mage's metaphysics. So ways to steel one's self against Breaking Points, ways to piece together a hypothetical picture of what may have occurred during lost time, ways to use evidence eliminate the possibility of non-magical influence and use deductive reasoning to infer magical influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654313#post654313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's number of reasons the phrase &amp;quot;witch-hunt&amp;quot; has the connotations it does, and the failure of plausible deniability is one of them. The archetype tends toward either occupying some degree of hypocrisy by using a level of magical power to stamp out magicians or being hypervigilant and paranoid about things that most people would not point to as evidence of supernatural meddling. Neither of these is reduced in viability by having hunters of the Awakened either be Sleepwalkers or be unhinged enough to blame a mage for something that his memories indicate is a coincidence or a mundanely-inflicted grievance.</div> </div> </div> </div>This all seems perfectly on-theme for Sleeper hunters vs. Awakened mages to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T13:33:00-07:00","id":654339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654326#post654326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not want, and have never wanted, to change the way Mage's metaphysics work. I just want Hunter to have some elements that help the characters bare the burden that comes with hunting Mages as a sleeper, within the constraints of Mage's metaphysics.</div> </div> </div> </div>That these elements already exist is the reason assumptions are defaulting to &quot;detractors are proposing a change to the metaphysics.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hunters of Awakened mages will tend to default to the magic-or-broken dichotomy given enough exposure. That Hunter includes a significant proportion of witch-hunters that exist outside of those two bubbles is a function of its focus as a gameline and part of the reason its &quot;witches&quot; are not all under the protection of the full strength of the Quiescence. Dissatisfaction with using the latter to get around the former gets into matters of Game Balance that neither game is particularly obligated to devote wordcount to given their respective focuses.<br /> <br /> Having a problem with the fact that hunting the Awakened necessitates outside assistance or tackling an extra degree of doubt in the act of killing one of the most humanlike monsters thusfar published is one of those things that isn't going to be resolved without changing the nature of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T13:36:27-07:00","id":654342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654218#post654218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My impression is that some Hunter fans do this every time the downsides of using Paradox to attack mages are pointed out, and no matter what we do it won't be enough for them. So why support it at all? It's like demanding CAS change Mummy so that the Chosen of Shulpae are possible under Mummy's rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a tad dismissive. The problem really arises from the perceptions of Hunter as the 'vs. crossover' book. Hunters vs Vampires, Hunters vs Mummies, etc. Now mind you, some of those lines are just as traumatic and one sided an encounter as mages (breaking points for witnessing the supernatural are hardly restricted to Awakening). However, Mage is the only line that outright says &quot;mortals are helpless victims of the lies&quot;, though mortal helplessness is implied in most of the other games. But it's understandable that if you tell a player their character, whom they've poured their heart and time into, is &quot;a helpless victim with no recourse&quot; they aren't going to take it super well.<br /> <br /> That said, the general opposition to the Sleepwalker solution seems misplaced. It's a contrivance, sure, but all stories are contrivances. And certainly it's no less contrived than a group of vampire hunters, or god-machine conspiracy theorists. Hunters need a reason to unite, and being traumatized by an event all their friends mysteriously forgot is as valid a reason as any. Sleepwalker is a cheap merit, achievable through a variety of avenues, its not shackled to any powers or restrictions (like Wolf-Blooded or Ghouls). Sure it removes the ability to use Paradox as a weapon, but from the looks of it 2nd ED will dissolve that option almost entirely as Paradox seems just as likely to screw over the hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:00:32-07:00","id":654371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654326#post654326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is that talking past each other thing. I do not want, and have never wanted, to change the way Mage's metaphysics work. I just want Hunter to have some elements that help the characters bare the burden that comes with hunting Mages as a sleeper, within the constraints of Mage's metaphysics. So ways to steel one's self against Breaking Points, ways to piece together a hypothetical picture of what may have occurred during lost time, ways to use evidence eliminate the possibility of non-magical influence and use deductive reasoning to infer magical influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, hopefully The Code still allows for replacing Breaking Points, then. The other three things truly seem to be possible with normal usage of Skills and roleplaying to me. Anything further than that, unfortunately, <i>is</i> a change to Mage's metaphysics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:05:18-07:00","id":654403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654323#post654323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that <i>some</i> of the suggestions to circumvent or ameliorate Quiescence or render Awakened less of a threat to Sleeper Hunters do indeed change the nature and extent of the Sleeping Curse and the canon power framework and levels of Awakened mages. We'll just have to agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, some of them may. I would prefer that be a matter open to discussion though, rather than all suggestions related to Hunter/Mage Crossover being automatically dismissed as changing the themes of Mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654323#post654323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do you really need special Hunter Tactics to notice something strange or potentially supernatural is happening in the Hunters' community, or even that a particular person, Awakened or otherwise, is connected, if not responsible? Not only does it appear to be a normal use of skills, abilities and contacts, as well as standard role-playing, but it's more the basis for a hunt, rather than part of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there were no Merits or Tactics for things that are already covered by normal use of Skills and roleplaying, there would be no non-supernatural Merits or Tactics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654339#post654339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That these elements already exist is the reason assumptions are defaulting to &quot;detractors are proposing a change to the metaphysics.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And that this assumption is made by default is the reason these suggestions keep being brought forth. I think if the detractors felt they were being listened to, they would not feel the need to speak so loudly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654339#post654339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters of Awakened mages will tend to default to the magic-or-broken dichotomy given enough exposure. That Hunter includes a significant proportion of witch-hunters that exist outside of those two bubbles is a function of its focus as a gameline and part of the reason its &quot;witches&quot; are not all under the protection of the full strength of the Quiescence. Dissatisfaction with using the latter to get around the former gets into matters of Game Balance that neither game is particularly obligated to devote wordcount to given their respective focuses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the &quot;hunters need more help fighting Awakened&quot; camp has a problem with non-Awakened witches being an option to hunt, merely with the suggestion that if a hunter is a Sleeper, Awakened are not among his options to hunt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654339#post654339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a problem with the fact that hunting the Awakened necessitates outside assistance or tackling an extra degree of doubt in the act of killing one of the most humanlike monsters thusfar published is one of those things that isn't going to be resolved without changing the nature of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good thing I don't have a problem with that, then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-06-2015, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:11:03-07:00","id":654420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654371#post654371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, hopefully The Code still allows for replacing Breaking Points, then. The other three things truly seem to be possible with normal usage of Skills and roleplaying to me. Anything further than that, unfortunately, <i>is</i> a change to Mage's metaphysics.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only non-supernatural Merit I can think of that *isnt* covered by normal usage of Skills and roleplaying is Resources, and even that could arguably be covered by roleplay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:54:25-07:00","id":654470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654317#post654317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, once again, no one in this thread wants Dave to alter how Quiessence works or to intentionally weaken mages.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sure, that goes without saying. But what's being asked for in this thread is not a change to the rules. It's simply a way for non-sleepwalker hunters to, after experiencing the effects of Quiessence, cope with those effects. Maybe something that helps them regain lost Integrity. Maybe something that helps them, as you yourself have suggested, use tertiary evidence to form educated guesses about what it might be that is missing from their memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>But an alteration to Quiescence is exactly what you're asking for. The canon ruling for the Sleeping Curse is that the <i>only</i> means of breaking it is gaining personal supernatural power, be it through supernatural merits (the Sleepwalker merit itself being included) or gaining a major template. There are no non-mystic means of removing the abyssal shard from your soul. If you want to remove the shard of the abyss from your soul there are options to go about doing those, but the hard answer to that is none of them are mundane, some sort of magic is always going to be involved. <br /> <br /> There is no getting used to it. There is no working through it. There is no resisting it. That's just how it is. What you are asking is for that to change. You can purchase the Sleepwalker merit, you can purchase some other form of supernatural merit that bestows some form of personal power, or you can gain a major template. Those are your options to breaking the Sleeping Curse. Again, anything else is asking for a change in how Quiescence works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T14:58:11-07:00","id":654474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654403#post654403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that this assumption is made by default is the reason these suggestions keep being brought forth. I think if the detractors felt they were being listened to, they would not feel the need to speak so loudly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, as is well known, &quot;repeat the same statement louder and slower&quot; is the universal panacea for miscommunication and not the hallmark of Einstein-defined insanity.<br /> <br /> Conversation on a topic begins with the not-unreasonable assumption that if a person does not mention or otherwise make clear a deficiency in their understanding of the topic in the startup (particularly in a known limited-content format like text) then they are familiar with the basics of it or have at least given a fair amount of thought and attention to it. If you have a problem that has obvious solutions A and B and solution A already exists within the framework of the topic, outside-framework solution B is the next proposed go-to. If solution B is then shot down and solution A is suggested and approved of, you have wasted everybody's time in a manner that could be avoided by phrases as simple as &quot;have I overlooked anything?&quot; or &quot;I've been looking over the rules for X and I'm not sure if I've understood them correctly.&quot;<br /> <br /> I spent a sizeable chunk of at least two large threads making several variants of an exhortation to read the books to people who were complaining about problems that didn't exist or calling for the inclusion of tools that were already present; I didn't care for it then and I don't care for it now. It costs nothing to be clear about what you know and what options you've considered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think the &quot;hunters need more help fighting Awakened&quot; camp has a problem with non-Awakened witches being an option to hunt, merely with the suggestion that if a hunter is a Sleeper, Awakened are not among his options to hunt. </div> </div> </div>The kind of exercises in paranoia that the Quiescence necessitate of Sleeper hunters pursuing the Awakened require rather more narrative legwork than most people are likely to find enjoyable and Hunter does not have Beast's mechanical advantages or crossover-facilitation mandate. &quot;Just use Witches&quot; is a suggestion presumably made with those points in mind.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind habitually scanning the interactions of every other remotely suspicious individual in your sphere of influence at the expense of your mundane life and no small amount of your soundness of mind, then the focus of Hunter as it relates to heavily-obfuscated supernatural beings remains intact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:06:30-07:00","id":654477,"title":"","content":"Wow, the thread got rather overtly hostile pretty suddenly, almost as if people have taken Dave's post as permission to bag on supporters of the &quot;hunters could use some more support&quot; camp.<br /> <br /> That is, the focus has largely shifted from discussion of the games to discussion of the fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-06-2015, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:17:07-07:00","id":654485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654477#post654477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, the thread got rather overtly hostile pretty suddenly, almost as if people have taken Dave's post as permission to bag on supporters of the &quot;hunters could use some more support&quot; camp.<br /> <br /> That is, the focus has largely shifted from discussion of the games to discussion of the fans.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree, there's certainly no need to personalize the discussion or imply hostility. It's not like we're discussing the Mage Arcadia vs.Changeling Arcadia debate* <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">* And, for the record, no matter what Dave says, they're definitely the same Arcadia. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:47:24-07:00","id":654497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654470#post654470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But an alteration to Quiescence is exactly what you're asking for. The canon ruling for the Sleeping Curse is that the <i>only</i> means of breaking it is gaining personal supernatural power, be it through supernatural merits (the Sleepwalker merit itself being included) or gaining a major template. There are no non-mystic means of removing the abyssal shard from your soul. If you want to remove the shard of the abyss from your soul there are options to go about doing those, but the hard answer to that is none of them are mundane, some sort of magic is always going to be involved.<br /> <br /> There is no getting used to it. There is no working through it. There is no resisting it. That's just how it is. What you are asking is for that to change. You can purchase the Sleepwalker merit, you can purchase some other form of supernatural merit that bestows some form of personal power, or you can gain a major template. Those are your options to breaking the Sleeping Curse. Again, anything else is asking for a change in how Quiescence works.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That's not what I want to do. I don't want to break the curse, I don't want to remove the shard, I don't want to resist Quiessence, I don't want to work through the Lie. All I want is to do <i>exactly as you've been suggesting</i> and figure shit out by deductive reasoning. I just want some damn Merits or something that help me do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T15:51:52-07:00","id":654501,"title":"","content":"I think I was misconstrued, but I don't really know what everyone is talking about anymore, so I can't be sure. I'm lost.<br /> <br /> I don't think Hunters should use Paradox to attack Mages. I don't think Hunters should be able to overcome the Lie. If a Hunter is going after a Mage then they should figure out how to get around the Lie, as appropriate for Sleeper or Sleepwalker whichever they may be. I suppose a supplement that covered Mages in Hunter should suggest how to go about the hunt. A conspiracy might have some way to nerf a Mage in a limited way as they sometimes do to other monsters, but the Endowment should work with, not against, Mage mechanics.<br /> <br /> Hunters do need a way to deal with Breaking Points in general as they will bleed Integrity no matter what they face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 09-06-2015, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:00:57-07:00","id":654522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654420#post654420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only non-supernatural Merit I can think of that *isnt* covered by normal usage of Skills and roleplaying is Resources, and even that could arguably be covered by roleplay.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, I guess I was a little unclear -- by roleplay I just meant actually going through the motions/steps of investigating instead/in addition to rolling Investigation. Though, in the same sense that you could shoplift an outfit and make up a story about how you TOTALLY own a Yacht (the bathroom is only 10x9 now that I've added the helipad, don't you know, such a shame, taxes these days, really) while going to the Yacht Club instead of having the Barfly merit, I could ABSOLUTELY get behind some sort of Merit in Hunter2 that denotes a familiarity and ease with which the Hunter is able to piece together the real story from cover-ups and/or see a newspaper article as a cover-up for *something*, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> And my belief that such a merit would be an increase in skill rather than a newly-obtained one via the merit is to such an extent that I basically gave my Hunters that ability during a rather lengthy Hunter Chronicle. I called it Hunter Sense, and it tingled. It usually involved a lack of full details (summarizing a series or articles about a housefire rather than reading them all verbatim), and NEVER involved telling them what truly happened unless they looked into it. The best example I could give, I suppose, is the ghoul from Lullay Lullay, who talks about being on his side of the curtain means knowing things are up. &quot;When you've been backstage, you can't unsee that shit, you can't look through a newspaper or listen to the radio, glossing over most stories, wihtout catching those patterns and telltales hidden in the margins.&quot;<br /> <br /> All that, of course, not relating specifically to Mages, but still including them in that.<br /> <br /> And, perhaps, that's the middle-ground here: acknowledging, in the Hunter book, how hard it is to Hunt Mages, but that it's possible, and then maybe a little sidebar about penalties and such to the investigative rolls involving Quiescence (and saying what's possible to find out) to both show that it's possible to find out what's going on and to show how hard it is.<br /> <br /> Really, I'd be terribly surprised if there ISN'T something like a Mental Style merit about investigating things in Hunter2. And, obviously, even more surprised if it's completely unable to be used against Mages.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also Changeling Arcadia is obviously the Fallen reflection of Mage Arcadia &gt;.&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:09:21-07:00","id":654527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654470#post654470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But an alteration to Quiescence is exactly what you're asking for. The canon ruling for the Sleeping Curse is that the <i>only</i> means of breaking it is gaining personal supernatural power, be it through supernatural merits (the Sleepwalker merit itself being included) or gaining a major template. There are no non-mystic means of removing the abyssal shard from your soul. If you want to remove the shard of the abyss from your soul there are options to go about doing those, but the hard answer to that is none of them are mundane, some sort of magic is always going to be involved.<br /> <br /> There is no getting used to it. There is no working through it. There is no resisting it. That's just how it is. What you are asking is for that to change. You can purchase the Sleepwalker merit, you can purchase some other form of supernatural merit that bestows some form of personal power, or you can gain a major template. Those are your options to breaking the Sleeping Curse. Again, anything else is asking for a change in how Quiescence works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except you're forgetting one thing: Having absolutely no workarounds for Quiescence <b>hurts one of Mage's core themes</b>. It's not just a concern for Hunter (and never would be considering that Hunters are supposed to be the underdogs), but giving absolutely no recourse or ways to circumvent the Sleeping Curse means that you lose out a lot on delivering the main form of horror that Mage has to offer. I don't care what Dave has to say about the matter, I came seeing a horror game, I'm gonna play a horror game, dammit.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I'm not saying that the nature of Quiescence should be changed, I'm just saying there should at least be one workaround for it. After all, what is the main function of the Quiescence in Mage's setting? To explain why mages and magic are a big secret, it's Mage's Masquerade, Lunacy, Mask, etc.. So if there are at least some workarounds for those, why dig in your heels for Mage exclusively? I'm also not saying that said workarounds should be free from consequences in the least. At best, Hunters are trading one set of consequences for another, at worst, they're making things far worse for the vain, empty hope of doing some good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654485#post654485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* And, for the record, no matter what Dave says, they're definitely the same Arcadia. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Preach, head-canon brother. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:18:16-07:00","id":654530,"title":"","content":"Which theme is that? Mage <i>is</i> a horror game, about obsession with the occult and what it drives the protagonists to do. Part of that is the separation of what mages can see from everyone else, to isolate them so they forget about the collatoral damage from chasing Mysteries. Quiescence is part of that.<br /> <br /> That they don't fear the mob like vampires do doesn't make them not horror protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:26:03-07:00","id":654535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654530#post654530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which theme is that? Mage <i>is</i> a horror game, about obsession with the occult and what it drives the protagonists to do. Part of that is the separation of what mages can see from everyone else, to isolate them so they forget about the collatoral damage from chasing Mysteries. Quiescence is part of that.<br /> <br /> That they don't fear the mob like vampires do doesn't make them not horror protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hubris. Apologies for not clarifying that in my previous post. I simply felt there was no need to repeat myself before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:32:48-07:00","id":654539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654535#post654535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hubris. Apologies for not clarifying that in my previous post. I simply felt there was no need to repeat myself before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hubris is pride that leads to a self-inflicted fall. Classically, trespass against the Greek gods. Mages get themselves killed by the Mysteries they chase, all by themselves.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Besides, having mage-hunters is what Banishers are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 09-06-2015, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:44:52-07:00","id":654569,"title":"","content":"I've said it before, but mages being under no threat whatsoever from Sleepers goes beyond the issue of a Hunter/Mage crossover. And, like I also said, Hunter crossovers aren't in the same category as others. Because where vampires may or may not exist in a given chronicle, and may or may not be Kindred if they do, mortals are always around. And always end up victims of the supernatural. Mage 2e hammers home their utter helplessness about it more than any other splat. It's a fundamental part of the vision for the gameline, but one people take issue with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:47:15-07:00","id":654570,"title":"","content":"I always saw quiescence as something like a black box around magic. A mage can use the box to hide behind, so an observer might never find the mage, but enough observers and somebody find the mage. Finding the mage does not mean knowing the mage, however. If you witness a magic event, it is like you are thrust to the opposite side of the box. You could walk around the box and see the effect, but you would not know how the effect was creating, you would have a lie instead of the truth as explanation. I see people suggesting workarounds should be possible, means to walk around the box. The box is not altered or changed. The box remains a black box hiding all within. I see people suggesting a workaround would be a hack of the box, split it open or go through it. I don't think that is intended when &quot;workaround&quot; is used. Sleepwalkers, supernaturals, and awakened hack the box. Sleepers can only walk around and maybe they find something on the other side, more often not. If quiescence was absolute like it is being conveyed by some (presumably unintentionally) then how could sleepwalkers exist or mages awaken? This is how the two sides are talking by each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:47:28-07:00","id":654571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654530#post654530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which theme is that? Mage <i>is</i> a horror game, about obsession with the occult and what it drives the protagonists to do. Part of that is the separation of what mages can see from everyone else, to isolate them so they forget about the collatoral damage from chasing Mysteries. Quiescence is part of that.<br /> <br /> That they don't fear the mob like vampires do doesn't make them not horror protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>To follow, in 2e, what mages see and know is truly the central element of the horror. No matter how bleak the nWOD, the Lie is still somewhat of a comfort. When mages Awaken, they learn the dark Truth about the world, that angels, demons, shades, etc. are real and watching you, that the anti-reality of the Abyss curses almost everyone's souls and threatens to tear existence apart, and unknowable Exarchs effectively rule over humanity with their symbols of tyranny and oppression, to say nothing of the various and sundry supernatural phenomena, effects and entities a mage learns about and encounters once he joins the supernatural world and explores the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> Awakening no doubt opens the door to great mundane and mystical power and influence, but mages often need that power to survive. Now that they are awake, untold and immeasurable horrors are far more likely to notice them than ever before. The world is a nightmare few can fathom, and they experience it every minute of every day in all its terrible glory. Due to their Sight, there's simply no way they can avoid the constant knowledge that the supernatural, supernal and otherwise, is constantly infecting everything around them. <br /> <br /> Mages might not generally fear the proverbial Sleeper peasants with their torches and pitchforks, but they have more than enough to occupy their attention and keep them awake at night. If the Hunters knew the full Truth, they would certainly go insane, or least not bother with mages, a <i>relatively</i> benign group of fellow <i>humans</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:48:31-07:00","id":654572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654539#post654539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hubris is pride that leads to a self-inflicted fall. Classically, trespass against the Greek gods. Mages get themselves killed by the Mysteries they chase, all by themselves.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Besides, having mage-hunters is what Banishers are for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having gods or other powerful forces smack your ass down is certainly horrible, but having Sleepers do it? Absolutely no comparison. There just isn't. Why deny that delicious experience?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:55:31-07:00","id":654574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654572#post654572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having gods or other powerful forces smack your ass down is certainly horrible, but having Sleepers do it? Absolutely no comparison. There just isn't. Why deny that delicious experience?</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that Hubris? Hubris is about you being your own worst enemy, about your reach exceeding your grasp. Mages being clearly above Sleepers is almost necessary to reinforce this theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T16:58:07-07:00","id":654576,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm with Ophidimancer on that one...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:01:23-07:00","id":654579,"title":"","content":"I think Sleepwalkers and the existing &quot;Sleeper witnesses cause obvious magic to risk Paradox&quot; rules amply cover any subverting &quot;but the true danger was the little guy&quot; stories.<br /> <br /> That the little guys then get horribly mentally mutilated by the Abyss they aren't even aware of, and then forgetting what they did - <i>that's</i> delicious. Everyone loses!<br /> <br /> <br /> Case in point - here is an actual Merit from Awakening 2e, written months ago, gone off to layout already. It does what some people in this thread have asked for.<br /> <b>Liar (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Integrity<br /> Unfortunately, your very being strengthens the Lie. Your soul has been twisted by the Abyss and your presence warps the Supernal. <br /> Effect: A character with this merit increases Paradox risk around her by two dice instead of one, and adds two dice to Dissonance rolls. She has the Open Condition against Abyssal entities.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's as good a &quot;modifies Paradox&quot; Merit as you're getting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:03:47-07:00","id":654580,"title":"","content":"Hubris is also misjudging that those beneath you pose no threat as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Banishers while great as a Mage antagonist are mages themselves aren't they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:10:31-07:00","id":654583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654569#post654569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've said it before, but mages being under no threat whatsoever from Sleepers goes beyond the issue of a Hunter/Mage crossover. And, like I also said, Hunter crossovers aren't in the same category as others. Because where vampires may or may not exist in a given chronicle, and may or may not be Kindred if they do, mortals are always around. And always end up victims of the supernatural. Mage 2e hammers home their utter helplessness about it more than any other splat. It's a fundamental part of the vision for the gameline, but one people take issue with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awakened mages are not under &quot;no threat,&quot; it's just that the nature of the Sleeping Curse, the versatility and power of supernal magic, and careful organization and social structure, makes them inscrutable and extremely dangerous. Note also that there are other &quot;wizards, sorcerers, witches, warlocks, etc.&quot; and other magic using humans besides the Awakened that are easier targets in the nWOD.<br /> <br /> Not all supernatural prey is the same. To use a normal hunter analogy, hunting rodents or foul is normally easier than deer which is easier still than powerful carnivores like bears and the great cats. They all can be taken down, but the efforts, training and resources needed vary widely. Supernatural prey is no different, and in Hunter, the Tier system distinguishes who can expect to be able to find and kill what. Think of Tier One Sleeper Hunters as untrained, young, out-of shape hunters armed with a .22LR, and the Awakened as the African Lion of the supernatural world. Absent luck, significant assistance and great numbers, it's not going to turn-out well for the young hunters. <br /> <br /> Plain vanilla humans, all hundreds of millions of them armed to the teeth, are a danger to all supernaturals, Awakened mages and others, and justify the Veil, Masquerade and other group secrecy. However, a small group of relatively average Sleepers should not be a serious threat to those who know the Truth and bend reality to their whims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:26:34-07:00","id":654589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654574#post654574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is that Hubris? Hubris is about you being your own worst enemy, about your reach exceeding your grasp. Mages being clearly above Sleepers is almost necessary to reinforce this theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is discounting the threat Sleepers can pose not being your own worst enemy?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YY9g-0d7BK0\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;You can get past my defenses? Oh, that's adora-<b>SHIIIIIIIIT!!!</b>&quot;</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654579#post654579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Sleepwalkers and the existing &quot;Sleeper witnesses cause obvious magic to risk Paradox&quot; rules amply cover any subverting &quot;but the true danger was the little guy&quot; stories.<br /> <br /> That the little guys then get horribly mentally mutilated by the Abyss they aren't even aware of, and then forgetting what they did - <i>that's</i> delicious. Everyone loses!<br /> <br /> <br /> Case in point - here is an actual Merit from Awakening 2e, written months ago, gone off to layout already. It does what some people in this thread have asked for.<br /> <b>Liar (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Integrity<br /> Unfortunately, your very being strengthens the Lie. Your soul has been twisted by the Abyss and your presence warps the Supernal.<br /> Effect: A character with this merit increases Paradox risk around her by two dice instead of one, and adds two dice to Dissonance rolls. She has the Open Condition against Abyssal entities.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's as good a &quot;modifies Paradox&quot; Merit as you're getting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't you admit that Paradox is more of an inconvenience for mages than anything? Sure, pile it on and it gets really bad, but dabbling a little really isn't. Perhaps it wasn't from you, but from someone else? I knew that was said on this thread somewhere and I don't feel like back-tracking to find it right now.<br /> <br /> At best, Paradox is a lucky side effect that a Sleeper Hunter unwittingly delivered rather than a legitimate weapon. This is compounded by the fact that the Hunter perspective on the Sleeping Curse would be something like &quot;These witches are so good that they can chuck fireballs at you then make you believe it was really molotov cocktails.&quot;, and that's assuming they know about it in the first place.<br /> <br /> No, Paradox is really a non-option when it comes to dealing with mages. Exploiting their hubris is where it's at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 09-06-2015, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:28:02-07:00","id":654591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654579#post654579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Sleepwalkers and the existing &quot;Sleeper witnesses cause obvious magic to risk Paradox&quot; rules amply cover any subverting &quot;but the true danger was the little guy&quot; stories.<br /> <br /> That the little guys then get horribly mentally mutilated by the Abyss they aren't even aware of, and then forgetting what they did - <i>that's</i> delicious. Everyone loses!</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like the kicker in 2e, that if a mage doesn't contain a Paradox, everyone but the mage is usually at greater risk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654579#post654579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Case in point - here is an actual Merit from Awakening 2e, written months ago, gone off to layout already. It does what some people in this thread have asked for.<br /> <b>Liar (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Integrity<br /> Unfortunately, your very being strengthens the Lie. Your soul has been twisted by the Abyss and your presence warps the Supernal.<br /> Effect: A character with this merit increases <b>Paradox risk around her by two dice instead of one</b>, and adds two dice to Dissonance rolls. She has the Open Condition against Abyssal entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I though Paradox is invoked when a mage Reaches beyond his abilities or performs obvious magic in front of Sleppers, with the<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/\" target=\"_blank\"> paradox dice pool determined by the mage's gnosis</a>, with greater numbers of Sleepers simply adding dice tricks like 8 and 9 again and rote quality to the paradox roll. Has this changed since the blog post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:37:54-07:00","id":654593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654589#post654589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is discounting the threat Sleepers can pose not being your own worst enemy?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/YY9g-0d7BK0\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;You can get past my defenses? Oh, that's adora-<b>SHIIIIIIIIT!!!</b>&quot;</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I did not expect to see the &quot;Batman can't be Exalted because he's 'human' in his own setting&quot; argument reemerge in this setting with this example.<br /> <br /> Tien is a supernaturally powerful martial artist and Cell is an inherently durable nigh-immortal artificial being. That's about as far as one gets from &quot;normal human faces off against enlightened wizard&quot; in terms of comparable concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654591#post654591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I though Paradox is invoked when a mage Reaches beyond his abilities or performs obvious magic in front of Sleppers, with the<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/paradoxical/\" target=\"_blank\"> paradox dice pool determined by the mage's gnosis</a>, with greater numbers of Sleepers simply adding dice tricks like 8 and 9 again and rote quality to the paradox roll. Has this changed since the blog post?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You can also risk Paradox in other ways \u2013 <b>casting an obviously magical effect in front of Sleepers adds a die</b>, or using a spell that you\u2019ve burned your Wisdom over previously. If you have a Paradox dice pool, you also bag an extra die for each previous paradox roll your character has prompted in a scene. <b>Multiple</b> Sleeper witnesses apply a dice trick to the Paradox roll \u2013 a single witness doesn\u2019t, but a handful of people will give it 9-again, light traffic 8-again and a crowd gives it the rote quality.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-06-2015, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:51:48-07:00","id":654598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654497#post654497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. That's not what I want to do. I don't want to break the curse, I don't want to remove the shard, I don't want to resist Quiessence, I don't want to work through the Lie. All I want is to do <i>exactly as you've been suggesting</i> and figure shit out by deductive reasoning. I just want some damn Merits or something that help me do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I think what you, specifically, are asking for isn't necessarily what the other people in this thread are asking for. But lets completely ignore that for right now and cover what it is you are actually looking for. <br /> <br /> First off, what sort of Merits are you wanting? What do you actually want them to do? The entire deductive reasoning thing is what the Investigation skill is for. You can already take specialties in it to notice patterns in conflicting reports, and then another specialty specifically for investigating cases involving mages.<br /> <br /> You already have Eye for the Strange if you <i>really</i> need to find evidence as to whether the events involved the supernatural or not, in which you can use the piece of evidence obtained from that to try to figure out what <i>kind</i> of magic is potentially being used. Good Time management helps do all of this quickly, before evidence the trail goes cold and possibly even before the mage realizes someones really putting together some sort of case from whatever they left behind. Get dots in an occult-based Library to help smooth things over when trying to determine what you're dealing with and how to handle it. Honestly, at this point there really isn't much difference between hunting a mage and hunting a mundane serial killer or something.<br /> <br /> So using the usual methods you should be able to track down the mage in question. Sure, you might not see/remember them <i>using</i> any magic, but you could probably surmise just from previous reports that some sort of mind fuckery was going on around this person and chances are you wouldn't be able to recall whether or not you saw anything directly anyways. So you're going into the situation on the assumption that you probably won't be able to see magic for what it is anyways, or that whatever the mage does it inherently manifests slightly differently for each person viewing it. <br /> <br /> As for the actual hunt itself, this is where things can't really be mapped out very easily. What the mage notices from his/her end and how they respond is going to vary <i>wildly</i> from person to person. The Hunters would likely have at least a vague notion of what sort of abilities they'll be going against just from the information they'd have gathered so far, so they likely wont be going in <i>completely</i> unprepared. The more they know about mages in general the better off they'd be going in but regardless any sort of head on confrontation is likely to be somewhat dangerous. <br /> <br /> So once again we get to afterwards. Accepting that they aren't going to ever be able to correctly remember their own encounter with the mage they'll have to do their best to piece together from their own conflicting reports and memories what they <i>think</i> had happened.<br /> <br /> Now let me first state that I wouldn't like this to be written up as a Tactic, simply because I don't see it being written up with the attention to detail that I feel is required for this. If it were written up as a Tactic it would probably end up as an if you succeed your roll you piece everything back together perfectly with 0 consequences mechanic, essentially bypassing Quiescence altogether. The reason I don't find this appropriate is that there are things that fractured memories and physical evidence could <i>not</i> put together. You might recall the mage chucking a molotov at you and setting your coat ablaze, but simply knowing that fire was involved and remembering firebombs wouldn't and shouldn't give you the nuanced actuality of the events. Just and throwing could involve the mage tossing around bolts of raw force while summoning up spirits of fire. Having shards of rock lodged in your arms isn't going to tell you whether he was magically chucking them at you or teleporting them into your body. And then there are the truly strange things with which you can't understand as anything but magic and forget altogether. Again, I don't feel that having it as a Tactic, or even a Merit really, would be good for this. I think that good ol' investigation + in character assumptions handle this the best.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T17:57:52-07:00","id":654609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654593#post654593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not expect to see the &quot;Batman can't be Exalted because he's 'human' in his own setting&quot; argument reemerge in this setting with this example.<br /> <br /> Tien is a supernaturally powerful martial artist and Cell is an inherently durable nigh-immortal artificial being. That's about as far as one gets from &quot;normal human faces off against enlightened wizard&quot; in terms of comparable concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because you're taking the argument too literally. The argument is more about the theme presented than a literal comparison.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/l8NC5nne0j0\" target=\"_blank\">This video presents a more literal comparison</a>, but I didn't want to use it because Kiritsugu is clearly using an Endowment-equivalent in the fight, and I'm arguing for pure Sleepers taking mages down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T18:01:17-07:00","id":654612,"title":"","content":"Oh man if I had known that arguing for 16 pages would get us a Mage spoiler my forum life would be WAY different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T18:05:55-07:00","id":654615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654609#post654609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because you're taking the argument too literally. The argument is more about the theme presented than a literal comparison.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/l8NC5nne0j0\" target=\"_blank\">This video presents a more literal comparison</a>, but I didn't want to use it because Kiritsugu is clearly using an Endowment-equivalent in the fight, and I'm arguing for pure Sleepers taking mages down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then rest peacefully, because pure Sleepers can take Mages down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T18:11:42-07:00","id":654616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654579#post654579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Case in point - here is an actual Merit from Awakening 2e, written months ago, gone off to layout already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awakening 2e has gone to layout, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T18:29:26-07:00","id":654623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654615#post654615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Then rest peacefully, because pure Sleepers can take Mages down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages usually aren't that hard to kill, all things considered. While they <i>could</i> be prepared for just about anything that anyone could throw at that, they almost always aren't. How many mages would really check for explosives everywhere they went? How many would check for drugs/poison every time they ate something? How many would have the proper defense to stop an unexpected rifle round to the head at noon? While nearly religious use of Fate and Time could indeed thwart pretty much any surprise attacks on a mage, most mages aren't going to be that paranoid about it without being given a reason to be. Now fighting a mage head on is a completely different story, with Quiescence not playing much of a role in the nigh futility of that at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T18:30:26-07:00","id":654624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654598#post654598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I think what you, specifically, are asking for isn't necessarily what the other people in this thread are asking for. But lets completely ignore that for right now and cover what it is you are actually looking for. <br /> <br /> First off, what sort of Merits are you wanting? What do you actually want them to do? The entire deductive reasoning thing is what the Investigation skill is for. You can already take specialties in it to notice patterns in conflicting reports, and then another specialty specifically for investigating cases involving mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>That something can be done with normal Skill use is not a reason not to have a Merit to be better at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654598#post654598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You already have Eye for the Strange if you <i>really</i> need to find evidence as to whether the events involved the supernatural or not, in which you can use the piece of evidence obtained from that to try to figure out what <i>kind</i> of magic is potentially being used. Good Time management helps do all of this quickly, before evidence the trail goes cold and possibly even before the mage realizes someones really putting together some sort of case from whatever they left behind. Get dots in an occult-based Library to help smooth things over when trying to determine what you're dealing with and how to handle it. Honestly, at this point there really isn't much difference between hunting a mage and hunting a mundane serial killer or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>All good ways to go about it. Glad these exist. I would ideally like some that are more specifically focused on Hunter-Mage interactions, but in general these are the kinds of things I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654598#post654598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So using the usual methods you should be able to track down the mage in question. Sure, you might not see/remember them <i>using</i> any magic, but you could probably surmise just from previous reports that some sort of mind fuckery was going on around this person and chances are you wouldn't be able to recall whether or not you saw anything directly anyways. So you're going into the situation on the assumption that you probably won't be able to see magic for what it is anyways, or that whatever the mage does it inherently manifests slightly differently for each person viewing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far, so good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654598#post654598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the actual hunt itself, this is where things can't really be mapped out very easily. What the mage notices from his/her end and how they respond is going to vary <i>wildly</i> from person to person. The Hunters would likely have at least a vague notion of what sort of abilities they'll be going against just from the information they'd have gathered so far, so they likely wont be going in <i>completely</i> unprepared. The more they know about mages in general the better off they'd be going in but regardless any sort of head on confrontation is likely to be somewhat dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>liking what I'm reading.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654598#post654598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So once again we get to afterwards. Accepting that they aren't going to ever be able to correctly remember their own encounter with the mage they'll have to do their best to piece together from their own conflicting reports and memories what they <i>think</i> had happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, sounds like about what I'd want out of sleeper hunters vs. awakened mages game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654598#post654598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now let me first state that I wouldn't like this to be written up as a Tactic, simply because I don't see it being written up with the attention to detail that I feel is required for this. If it were written up as a Tactic it would probably end up as an if you succeed your roll you piece everything back together perfectly with 0 consequences mechanic, essentially bypassing Quiescence altogether. The reason I don't find this appropriate is that there are things that fractured memories and physical evidence could <i>not</i> put together. You might recall the mage chucking a molotov at you and setting your coat ablaze, but simply knowing that fire was involved and remembering firebombs wouldn't and shouldn't give you the nuanced actuality of the events. Just and throwing could involve the mage tossing around bolts of raw force while summoning up spirits of fire. Having shards of rock lodged in your arms isn't going to tell you whether he was magically chucking them at you or teleporting them into your body. And then there are the truly strange things with which you can't understand as anything but magic and forget altogether. Again, I don't feel that having it as a Tactic, or even a Merit really, would be good for this. I think that good ol' investigation + in character assumptions handle this the best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't have a problem with that level of abstraction, and wouldn't see it as &quot;bypassing Quiessence.&quot; Second, my suggestion for the tactic didn't provide a complete picture of the events even on an exceptional success. It only gave a general idea, and the possibility of a few specific details. Of course, I'm not married to that idea. Just an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T18:35:06-07:00","id":654628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654623#post654623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages usually aren't that hard to kill, all things considered. While they <i>could</i> be prepared for just about anything that anyone could throw at that, they almost always aren't. How many mages would really check for explosives everywhere they went? How many would check for drugs/poison every time they ate something? How many would have the proper defense to stop an unexpected rifle round to the head at noon? While nearly religious use of Fate and Time could indeed thwart pretty much any surprise attacks on a mage, most mages aren't going to be that paranoid about it without being given a reason to be. Now fighting a mage head on is a completely different story, with Quiescence not playing much of a role in the nigh futility of that at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hell my first session as a Mage ended up with me almost getting one-shot with a shotgun. Just, right in the chest. 9-again, decent dicepool, Mind armor subtracting some dice, boom. Only didn't die because I had a werebear on my side who was suddenly. . .a size 15 bear or something. Kinda distracted him from taking the second shot. Good times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T18:47:07-07:00","id":654633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654598#post654598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I think what you, specifically, are asking for isn't necessarily what the other people in this thread are asking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me chime in here and say that what Charlaquin is asking for is pretty much what I've been asking for, too. <br /> <br /> I'm speaking just for myself, of course \u2014 though I suspect that you'll find that this will be true of more of the non-\u201cDave camp\u201d fans than not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T19:17:27-07:00","id":654666,"title":"","content":"Vegita is clearly a Mage, &quot;I am the hype!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T21:49:05-07:00","id":654739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654609#post654609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because you're taking the argument too literally. The argument is more about the theme presented than a literal comparison.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/l8NC5nne0j0&amp;quot;]This</a> video presents a more literal comparison[/URL], but I didn't want to use it because Kiritsugu is clearly using an Endowment-equivalent in the fight, and I'm arguing for pure Sleepers taking mages down.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Kiritsugu is <i>also a mage</i>.<br /> 2) He's not particularly effective during the HGW, anyway as he only ends up killing Kayneth through trickery.<br /> 3) The regular mages in the Nasuverse aren't Awakened level, only those capable of True Sorcery are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T00:06:26-07:00","id":654825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654666#post654666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vegita is clearly a Mage, &quot;I am the hype!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In spirit, I suppose. The DBverse makes a clear distinction between Ki and magic, though. So maybe he's closer to that of a werewolf equivalent? He <i>did</i> have an alternate form once.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654739#post654739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Kiritsugu is <i>also a mage</i>.<br /> 2) He's not particularly effective during the HGW, anyway as he only ends up killing Kayneth through trickery.<br /> 3) The regular mages in the Nasuverse aren't Awakened level, only those capable of True Sorcery are.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) This is true, he's more of a Banisher than anything. Another reason I didn't use the video as an example initially. Although to be fair, a Hunter using Endowments would fight in the same exact manner.<br /> 2) Um, he wins the HGW (or at least, the closest anyone would get to winning anyways), so I think it's safe to say he was pretty damn effective.<br /> 3) True, but that's only because of scale. If Nasuverse mages were just as powerful, it would be the same deal.<br /> <br /> Remember, I'm talking about themes here, not exact, literal comparisons. Point is: Kiritsugu is taking advantage of Kayneth's arrogance to manipulate and defeat him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T02:02:13-07:00","id":654885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654825#post654825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) This is true, he's more of a Banisher than anything. Another reason I didn't use the video as an example initially. Although to be fair, a Hunter using Endowments would fight in the same exact manner.<br /> 2) Um, he wins the HGW (or at least, the closest anyone would get to winning anyways), so I think it's safe to say he was pretty damn effective.<br /> 3) True, but that's only because of scale. If Nasuverse mages were just as powerful, it would be the same deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) He's not a Banisher, he's just a mage that places a huge emphasis on non-magical fighting, much to his detriment.<br /> 2) There were a lot of reasons for that, none of which had to do with Kiritsugu actually being able to accomplish anything.<br /> 3) Except every example you've given has involved <i>another mage</i> fighting mages, so it's a complete wash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, I'm talking about themes here, not exact, literal comparisons. Point is: Kiritsugu is taking advantage of Kayneth's arrogance to manipulate and defeat him. </div> </div> </div>Except what he eventually <i>successfully</i> exploits is Kayneth caring about Sola-Ui; <i>not</i> Kayneth's hubris. His only effective attack against Kayneth directly was full out use of magic, the attack on the hotel fails utterly as do his attacks with conventional weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T02:19:03-07:00","id":654906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654633#post654633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me chime in here and say that what Charlaquin is asking for is pretty much what I've been asking for, too.<br /> <br /> I'm speaking just for myself, of course \u2014 though I suspect that you'll find that this will be true of more of the non-\u201cDave camp\u201d fans than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're asking for, then, belongs in a Hunter book, not a Mage book. \u200bThe Mage line developer talking about Mage should be treated as irrelevant and ignored, as the tools you're looking for have no place in any supplement or core book designed to help the running of Mage, nor do they have any place in a Mage game being run as a Mage, and not crossover, game. Talking about what you'd like to see out of Hunter is fine, obviously, especially with 2e still being early enough in development where the discussion may prove helpful, but you shouldn't expect any support for running Hunter in Mage, nor should you care all that much about what Mage has to say when it comes to running Hunter, potential inspirations aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T02:20:06-07:00","id":654908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's because you're taking the argument too literally. The argument is more about the theme presented than a literal comparison.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l8NC5nne0j0&amp;feature=youtu.be\" target=\"_blank\">This video presents a more literal comparison</a>, but I didn't want to use it because Kiritsugu is clearly using an Endowment-equivalent in the fight, and I'm arguing for pure Sleepers taking mages down. </div> </div> </div>As much as I'm a fan of Fate/Zero (and believe me, I truly am) the example given here is not particularly flattering towards Hunter. True it showcases the methods a Hunter might use to oppose a Mage (Traps, guns, etc.) but it also shows how a Mage can, with a single spell, negate every single one of those threats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654885#post654885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except what he eventually <i>successfully</i> exploits is Kayneth caring about Sola-Ui; <i>not</i> Kayneth's hubris. His only effective attack against Kayneth directly was full out use of magic, the attack on the hotel fails utterly as do his attacks with conventional weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, however, is the better take away. Mages are human, and just as prone to love, fear and stupidity as they are to hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 09-07-2015, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T04:17:34-07:00","id":655020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654885#post654885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) He's not a Banisher, he's just a mage that places a huge emphasis on non-magical fighting, much to his detriment.<br /> 2) There were a lot of reasons for that, none of which had to do with Kiritsugu actually being able to accomplish anything.<br /> 3) Except every example you've given has involved <i>another mage</i> fighting mages, so it's a complete wash.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Well, I said <i>more</i> like a Banisher than anything. The Nasuverse is <i>vastly</i> different from the WoD, so you can't make any real direct comparisons.<br /> 2) Oh sure, he totally didn't devise and implement a successful plan that not only saved the world, but also took out a rival Servant (after killing his Master I might add), greatly strengthening his own Servant, and greatly weakening a rival Servant all at the same time.<br /> 3) Nope, and since I've already gone over the reasons why, I'm not repeating myself here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654885#post654885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except what he eventually <i>successfully</i> exploits is Kayneth caring about Sola-Ui; <i>not</i> Kayneth's hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that, were it not for Lancer's intervention, Kayneth would've been done for, right? And <i>all</i> because of his hubris, I might add.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654885#post654885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His only effective attack against Kayneth directly was full out use of magic, the attack on the hotel fails utterly as do his attacks with conventional weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kiritsugu hardly used any magic at all, and any of the magic he <i>did</i> wield could be powerful Endowments and/or other supernatural Merits. <i>That's</i> the point I'm trying to make here, and even then, it wouldn't be my first example due to said Endowments/supernatural Merits. I merely pointed out this fight as an example more as a &quot;Okay fine, here's something a little more related to get the point across&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654908#post654908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I'm a fan of Fate/Zero (and believe me, I truly am) the example given here is not particularly flattering towards Hunter. True it showcases the methods a Hunter might use to oppose a Mage (Traps, guns, etc.) but it also shows how a Mage can, with a single spell, negate every single one of those threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course mages can negate nearly everything a Hunter could throw at them. But therein lies the rub: If you're so invulnerable to this lowly Hunter's clumsy and random weapons, why even bother with them? The Sleeper will just forget what you did anyways, how can they even begin to touch you?<br /> <br /> Except when the Hunter fights smart and learns how to work around those obstacles, right when you least expect it. That's what I'm talking about here. It's not a matter of directly countering the mage's magic, can't be done. Creativity and wits wins the day instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654908#post654908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, however, is the better take away. Mages are human, and just as prone to love, fear and stupidity as they are to hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem with that is, I could say the exact same thing about werewolves, changelings, sin-eaters, and sometimes even vampires and prometheans (not too sure about mummies, demons, and beasts though, as I don't have any of their books). We're talking about hunting mages exclusively. Though that aside, it's still a valid point nonetheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T06:30:52-07:00","id":655064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654589#post654589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is discounting the threat Sleepers can pose not being your own worst enemy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy, considering all the other threats that mages face. Discounting the threat from Sleepers is a mage being their own mediocre enemy, at best. Like I said, the theme of Hubris basically requires that mages have something to be hubristic <i>about</i>, and being clearly more capable and prescient than Sleepers in just about everything, as the Supernal supercedes the Fallen, is how that's done.<br /> <br /> Of course, the one area in which mages don't have a leg up over Sleepers is in the moral arena, but that's on purpose, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T06:55:53-07:00","id":655074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654579#post654579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Liar (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Integrity<br /> Unfortunately, your very being strengthens the Lie. Your soul has been twisted by the Abyss and your presence warps the Supernal.<br /> Effect: A character with this merit increases Paradox risk around her by two dice instead of one, and adds two dice to Dissonance rolls. She has the Open Condition against Abyssal entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>What frightens me the most about that is... since the only prerequisite is Integrity, does that mean <i>Banishers</i> could take it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T07:11:21-07:00","id":655083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655074#post655074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What frightens me the most about that is... since the only prerequisite is Integrity, does that mean <i>Banishers</i> could take it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. It would make them blow themselves up faster, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T07:14:52-07:00","id":655088,"title":"","content":"Unless the abyss was smart enough to leave them alive because they're such a good source of paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T07:43:31-07:00","id":655107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655074#post655074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What frightens me the most about that is... since the only prerequisite is Integrity, does that mean <i>Banishers</i> could take it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm? Last I checked, Banishers had Wisdom just like any other mage. Has Dave spoiled something that says otherwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T08:05:03-07:00","id":655162,"title":"","content":"Yes. In 2E they have integrity. That's one of the things that makes them a banisher. Their own magic causes them breaking points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T10:35:52-07:00","id":655304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655020#post655020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Oh sure, he totally didn't devise and implement a successful plan that not only saved the world, but also took out a rival Servant (after killing his Master I might add), greatly strengthening his own Servant, and greatly weakening a rival Servant all at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because sniping the one Master of the bunch who summoned his Servant <i>by accident</i> and didn't really care about the Grail and taking advantage of the presence of not-Cthulhu to force a rival to un-curse the Servant he barely worked with for ideological reasons in the middle of a threat sufficient to temporarily <i>change the terms of the War</i> was Kerry's crowning achievement, yes.<br /> <br /> The borderline-mundane serial killer acting as the entry node for a magical apocalypse with severe magically-induced mental and communicative inhibition standing out in the open isn't what I'd call a sterling example of hubris answered by Gunman, and the degree to which the Servants' own agendas complicated the matter had vastly more influence on Kiritsugu's getting to the final round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T12:28:00-07:00","id":655396,"title":"","content":"I feel like if we're going to use Kiritsugu as a stand in for Hunters, then the instances we should be citing are instead the times where a) he blew up the building Kayneth was holed up in (because while that didn't work, it's a great example of thinking outside of the box, albeit an extreme one, and it <i>should</i> have worked), and b) his actual act of killing Kayneth, which involves him blackmailing Kayneth when he was near his lowest point, and then betraying his expectations in a very fatal way.<br /> <br /> If you're a hunter fighting a mage, you need to fight like a terrorist.<br /> <br /> If you're a hunter, you should probably be thinking like a terrorist all the time anyways.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Truth be told, I think Kiritsugu might win against an Arrow or a thearch, but not against a councilor, and certainly not against a Guardian. For perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-07-2015, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T12:46:05-07:00","id":655419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655074#post655074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What frightens me the most about that is... since the only prerequisite is Integrity, does that mean <i>Banishers</i> could take it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Banishers taking the Liar Merit, at least to me, seems like a feature, not a bug. It emphasizes the problems and themes of Banishers in 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654906#post654906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're asking for, then, belongs in a Hunter book, not a Mage book. \u200bThe Mage line developer talking about Mage should be treated as irrelevant and ignored, as the tools you're looking for have no place in any supplement or core book designed to help the running of Mage, nor do they have any place in a Mage game being run as a Mage, and not crossover, game. Talking about what you'd like to see out of Hunter is fine, obviously, especially with 2e still being early enough in development where the discussion may prove helpful, but you shouldn't expect any support for running Hunter in Mage, nor should you care all that much about what Mage has to say when it comes to running Hunter, potential inspirations aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I fall squarely in the &quot;Dave Camp&quot; in these discussions, suggesting that the Hunter 2e developer can do whatever she wants in Hunter doesn't solve the concerns of those expressing alternative opinions, regardless of whether I personally believe there's even a problem than needs solving.<br /> <br /> People who are interested in Mage - Sleeper Hunter interactions, including both Mage and Hunter fans, would like canon rules and mechanics that are consistent among all game lines. If Hunter 2e chooses to ignore fundamental and immutable concepts from Mage 2e, it creates an irreconcilable conflict, and make this debate far worse.<br /> <br /> Although crossover is not a priority in Mage (and apparently all known 2e game lines except Beast), and each developer should and must be concerned primarily with their own game line, explicit and knowingly contentious rules and setting conflicts should, to the extent possible, be avoided.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-07-2015, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T12:50:45-07:00","id":655426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655396#post655396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're a hunter fighting a mage, you need to fight like a terrorist.<br /> <br /> If you're a hunter, you should probably be thinking like a terrorist all the time anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've apparently definitively solved the debate on whether Hunters become monsters by fighting monsters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T12:53:36-07:00","id":655429,"title":"","content":"Mortals can always call on werewolves, since they can do automatic aggravated damage by eating their flesh for essence. Maybe there will be a wolf-blooded witch finder compact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T12:59:49-07:00","id":655433,"title":"","content":"Hunter could do with having two options on endowments. One for Hunter-only games that use the simplified versions of the other splats, and another for storytellers with the books who want to do a proper crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T13:01:33-07:00","id":655434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655426#post655426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've apparently definitively solved the debate on whether Hunters become monsters by fighting monsters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if deadly effectiveness is your concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T13:10:17-07:00","id":655439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655429#post655429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals can always call on werewolves, since they can do automatic aggravated damage by eating their flesh for essence. Maybe there will be a wolf-blooded witch finder compact.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wolf-blooded humans are de facto Sleepwalkers, not Sleepers. The use of supernatural abilities or allies to fight Awakened Mages also doesn't solve the discussed problem of how mundane, moral human Sleepers can effectively fight the Awakened by themselves.<br /> <br /> Additionally, in nWOD, the various supernatural &quot;nations&quot; have no inherent antipathy. As a matter of the default setting, there's no general reason or advantage for werewolves to knowingly attack the Awakened and potentially start a local war to the detriment of them both. Moreover, supernatural Hunters do not normally have such cordial relations with werewolves that they can request they attack other supernaturals, no less receive a positive response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655433#post655433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter could do with having two options on endowments. One for Hunter-only games that use the simplified versions of the other splats, and another for storytellers with the books who want to do a proper crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a lot of duplicative work and would take-up a great deal of precious space in a corebook for what amounts to crossover rules.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-07-2015, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T13:17:34-07:00","id":655441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655439#post655439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf-blooded humans are de facto Sleepwalkers, not Sleepers. The use of supernatural abilities or allies to fight Awakened Mages also doesn't solve the discussed problem of how mundane, moral human Sleepers can effectively fight the Awakened by themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just said they can call werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, in nWOD, the various supernatural &quot;nations&quot; have no inherent antipathy. As a matter of the default setting, there's no general reason or advantage for werewolves to knowingly attack the Awakened and potentially start a local war to the detriment of them both. </div> </div> </div>As a matter of the default setting there's no reason to believe killing an Awakened would start a 'local war' or that it would be to the detriment of them both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moreover, supernatural Hunters do not normally have such cordial relations with werewolves that they can request they attack other supernaturals, no less receive a positive response. </div> </div> </div>If there was a wolf-blooded compact, they could. That's why I said that part. About a wolf-blooded compact.<br /> <br /> You seem very argumentative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T13:19:14-07:00","id":655443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=654579#post654579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Case in point - here is an actual Merit from Awakening 2e, written months ago, gone off to layout already. It does what some people in this thread have asked for.<br /> <b>Liar (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: Integrity<br /> Unfortunately, your very being strengthens the Lie. Your soul has been twisted by the Abyss and your presence warps the Supernal.<br /> Effect: A character with this merit increases Paradox risk around her by two dice instead of one, and adds two dice to Dissonance rolls. She has the Open Condition against Abyssal entities.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's as good a &quot;modifies Paradox&quot; Merit as you're getting.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm partially happy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Good Merit for those Abyss twisted Hunters on most &quot;monstrual&quot; part of eqausiton without proper Endowments. Now give me Tactics like proposed <i>After Action Rapor</i><i>t</i> or mine <i>Make a Scene </i>and I could see really advanced Sleeper Hunters cell as medium threat to the lone Mage - <b>exaclty</b> what I was looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T13:32:52-07:00","id":655450,"title":"","content":"The specifics of politics between supernatural &quot;nations&quot; is incredibly vague when its down crossover wise. Pretty much everyone is assumed to be in general indifferent over other splats except for Beasts.<br /> <br /> The reason for the werewolf pack going after the mage cabal can be as personal as being mortal enemies and its the Hunter's job to ensure they both destroy each other via feeding them the right information. There doesn't need to be any &quot;major politics&quot; involved, just manipulating the people directly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T13:39:52-07:00","id":655456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655441#post655441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just said they can call werewolves.<br /> <br /> As a matter of the default setting there's no reason to believe killing an Awakened would start a 'local war' or that it would be to the detriment of them both.<br /> <br /> If there was a wolf-blooded compact, they could. That's why I said that part. About a wolf-blooded compact.<br /> <br /> You seem very argumentative.</div> </div> </div> </div>This entire debate concerned how normal human Sleeper Hunters at the lower Hunter Tiers can effectively hunt Awakened Mages by themselves.<br /> <br /> As wolf-blooded humans and werewolves are Sleepwalkers (and werewolves a major template!), not Sleepers, and would be inherently both immune to the Quiescence and employing supernatural powers, with all due respect, your ideas don't really solve the problems or address the issues of this particular debate.<br /> <br /> My note about some potential setting issues and inconsistencies with your suggestions were very secondary to the discussion, and I have no objection to a wolf-blooded compact, besides the fact that you can do anything you want in your own chronicle. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T13:55:15-07:00","id":655487,"title":"","content":"BTW: I'm not wedded to my proposed <i>After Action Report</i> notion being a Tactic or a Merit \u2014 though I would note that nearly every Tactic is technically something that could be achieved with just the underlying skills; and those that aren't are the most suspect of being &quot;supernatural bennies in disguise\u201d (e.g., Excising). Tactics \u201cmerely\u201d allow you to be more efficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:14:23-07:00","id":655510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655456#post655456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As wolf-blooded humans and werewolves are Sleepwalkers (and werewolves a major template!), not Sleepers, and would be inherently both immune to the Quiescence and employing supernatural powers, with all due respect, your ideas don't really solve the problems or address the issues of this particular debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except like I said, if hunters had access to a wolf-blooded compact they could call upon assistance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My note about some potential setting issues and inconsistencies with your suggestions were very secondary to the discussion, and I have no objection to a wolf-blooded compact, besides the fact that you can do anything you want in your own chronicle. </div> </div> </div>Thank you, I appreciate that. I think you could have local wars too, in your own chronicle, if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-07-2015, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:22:43-07:00","id":655512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655510#post655510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except like I said, if hunters had access to a wolf-blooded compact they could call upon assistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, certainly. They wouldn't be Sleeper hunters; but there could certainly be wolf-blooded compacts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:29:51-07:00","id":655554,"title":"","content":"I'm just waiting for someone to mention Hitler at this point. - Besides myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:32:02-07:00","id":655555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655512#post655512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, certainly. They wouldn't be Sleeper hunters; but there could certainly be wolf-blooded compacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>And since wolf-blooded can act as ritemasters for pack rites, and a cell could be considered a pack, certain rituals like Great Hunt and possibly Moon's Mad Love, could act to protect Sleeper members of their cells from the deleterious affects of Supernal magic on the human mind. Or there could simply be another one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:32:14-07:00","id":655556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655510#post655510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except like I said, if hunters had access to a wolf-blooded compact they could call upon assistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The need to call upon Sleepwalkers like wolf-blooded or employing other supernatural means appears to effectively be an admission that normal human Sleeper Hunters cannot, by themselves, effectively hunt Awakened mages. <br /> <br /> I certainly wasn't implying that wolf-blooded, no less werewolves, wouldn't have a <b><i>much</i></b> easier time hunting the Awakened, only that it really sidesteps the problem raised in this thread that some believe plain vanilla mortals should have some canon mundane means to successfully hunt Awakened mages, particularly methods to overcome the Quiescence or avoid breaking-points..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:35:55-07:00","id":655558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655556#post655556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The need to call upon Sleepwalkers like wolf-blooded or employing other supernatural means appears to effectively be an admission that normal human Sleeper Hunters cannot, by themselves, effectively hunt Awakened mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've stated, repeatedly, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651898#post651898\">to you</a>, I don't believe normal human sleepers can effectively hunt Awakened mages, nor should they.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:44:37-07:00","id":655580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655558#post655558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I've stated, repeatedly, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=651898#post651898\">to you</a>, I don't believe normal human sleepers can effectively hunt Awakened mages, nor should they.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, a simple miscommunication, as we apparently are in agreement concerning the basic issue under discussion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:49:20-07:00","id":655597,"title":"","content":"I don't know why; but whenever I hear that claim, I find myself thinking of the white-room game balance mentality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:50:58-07:00","id":655598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655554#post655554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just waiting for someone to mention Hitler at this point. - Besides myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Hunter cell could only summon the vile shade of Hitler from the deep, dank depths of the Underworld, he no doubt would be able to offer them some protection from the Quiescence and other dark powers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I hesitate to even begin to suggest names for such a disturbing Hunter Tactic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T14:55:03-07:00","id":655600,"title":"","content":"Or a mage could summon Astral Robot Jetpack Hitler. What now Hunters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T15:10:23-07:00","id":655622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655555#post655555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And since wolf-blooded can act as ritemasters for pack rites, and a cell could be considered a pack, certain rituals like Great Hunt and possibly Moon's Mad Love, could act to protect Sleeper members of their cells from the deleterious affects of Supernal magic on the human mind. Or there could simply be another one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Won't be a pack without a totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T15:11:00-07:00","id":655624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655597#post655597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why; but whenever I hear that claim, I find myself thinking of the white-room game balance mentality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you're referring to the ability of Sleepers to effectively hunt the Awakened, as emphaszied by Dave, it's certainly more than the typical &quot;white room&quot; template vs. template combat comparison (which I loathe with the heat of a thousand suns!).<br /> <br /> It's not too difficult to acknowledge very broad basic power discrepancies among certain groups or in-setting roadblocks. Awakened mages and Sleeper Hunters are both human, except the former have significant powers, abilities and advantages, with no inherent non-human weakeness (e.g., sunlight, silver, etc). Even a newly Awakened mage is &quot;protected&quot; by the Quiescence and has significant and versatile powers that should present a serious challenge to even a small group of highly-experienced, combat-trained Sleepers. This is expressly acknowledged by the Mage developer and is an intentional part of the nWOD setting. Lower Tier Hunters are supposed to be underdogs, and some prey is more difficult than others.<br /> <br /> The desire by you and others for some canon Tactics or other mundane means to offer basic Sleeper Hunters a real fighting chance against the Awakened only emphasizes the point.<br /> <br /> Of course, we can get into some real &quot;white room&quot; discussions like who would win a bar fight, a Blood Talon Rahu or an Obrimos Adamantine Arrow? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T15:21:53-07:00","id":655661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655064#post655064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Easy, considering all the other threats that mages face. Discounting the threat from Sleepers is a mage being their own mediocre enemy, at best. Like I said, the theme of Hubris basically requires that mages have something to be hubristic <i>about</i>, and being clearly more capable and prescient than Sleepers in just about everything, as the Supernal supercedes the Fallen, is how that's done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're talking about removing a golden opportunity in Mage. I'm sorry, but mere semantics is not gonna deter me away from experiencing such a golden opportunity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655396#post655396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like if we're going to use Kiritsugu as a stand in for Hunters, then the instances we should be citing are instead the times where a) he blew up the building Kayneth was holed up in (because while that didn't work, it's a great example of thinking outside of the box, albeit an extreme one, and it <i>should</i> have worked), and b) his actual act of killing Kayneth, which involves him blackmailing Kayneth when he was near his lowest point, and then betraying his expectations in a very fatal way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not forget how he very well could've killed Kayneth were it not for Lancer. That, and blowing up the building could've very well been merely a tactic to draw Kayneth out, rather than trying to kill him. While such speculation is at best unproven, it can still serve as an example of how sleeper Hunters can manipulate mages, which is another means of exploiting hubris.<br /> <br /> &quot;I can literally control minds, you think you can manipulate me? Wait, what's that ticking noise?&quot;<br /> <br /> By the way, having Kiritsugu as a stand-in for Hunters is not what I want here. There's a reason why posting that fight as an example <i>wasn't</i> my first choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T15:54:14-07:00","id":655684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655661#post655661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then you're talking about removing a golden opportunity in Mage. I'm sorry, but mere semantics is not gonna deter me away from experiencing such a golden opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in your games you can change literally anything you want. The base assumption of the game as presented in the books don't match up with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T17:24:37-07:00","id":655734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655661#post655661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's not forget how he very well could've killed Kayneth were it not for Lancer. That, and blowing up the building could've very well been merely a tactic to draw Kayneth out, rather than trying to kill him. While such speculation is at best unproven, it can still serve as an example of how sleeper Hunters can manipulate mages, which is another means of exploiting hubris.<br /> <br /> &quot;I can literally control minds, you think you can manipulate me? Wait, what's that ticking noise?&quot;<br /> <br /> By the way, having Kiritsugu as a stand-in for Hunters is not what I want here. There's a reason why posting that fight as an example <i>wasn't</i> my first choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Misunderstood the argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-08-2015, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T17:54:24-07:00","id":655744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655684#post655684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in your games you can change literally anything you want. The base assumption of the game as presented in the books don't match up with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna disagree with you there, but if that's the way you think it is, then I would have to say it's a flaw in the design.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T17:59:18-07:00","id":655747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655744#post655744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm gonna disagree with you there, but if that's the way you think it is, then I would have to say it's a flaw in the design.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you've got the word of the developer on this one. Ashenrogue's reading undoubtedly matches Dave's stated intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T18:03:17-07:00","id":655749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655597#post655597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know why; but whenever I hear that claim, I find myself thinking of the white-room game balance mentality.</div> </div> </div> </div>He needs to be very specific about it, I guess. I think it would be good if the game was made for mages to be more vulnerable, but that's not what the game is about.<br /> <br /> On terms of power, you're dealing with one of the most versatile beings in the World of Darkness and while a newly Awakened mage might get sloppy and get stabbed a few times in a dark alley because someone saw the look in his eyes when he deigned to gaze upon a Sleeper, that will just lead to the same mage, later, being a more prepared and more deadly foe.<br /> <br /> So in the end the best ways for Sleepers to deal with mages, though despite all the merits I don't believe it would be likely to occur in the first place, would be to call for outside assistance, whether externally by reaching out to a pack, or making a deal with something so that they can gain some modicum of power themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655622#post655622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Won't be a pack without a totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are talking about the default setting, where a totem is not a requirement of a pack. It's a fine houserule if you want to run with it, but has no bearing on the conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655624#post655624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, we can get into some real &quot;white room&quot; discussions like who would win a bar fight, a Blood Talon Rahu or an Obrimos Adamantine Arrow? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to dole out double digit dice pools of aggravated damage favors the werewolf.<br /> <br /> Chomp chomp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T18:36:13-07:00","id":655768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655744#post655744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm gonna disagree with you there, but if that's the way you think it is, then I would have to say it's a flaw in the design.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can disagree if you like. As Charlaquin said, we've already got a ruling as to how these things work and how the base setting is from the head mage developer. This isn't a debate, it is fact. You can dislike it, houserule it, and try to deny it all you like but the rulings and intent have been clearly stated. You are, of course, free to pick and choose how you'd like it to be at your own table, but know that it explicitly goes against the setting as written and intended as presented in the book. Which isn't necessarily a bad thing mind you, it's just the way of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655749#post655749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being able to dole out double digit dice pools of aggravated damage favors the werewolf.<br /> <br /> Chomp chomp.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be true, but one of mages greatest strengths comes from their ability to potentially no sell a lot of methods of attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-07-2015, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T19:17:58-07:00","id":655824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655661#post655661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you're talking about removing a golden opportunity in Mage. I'm sorry, but mere semantics is not gonna deter me away from experiencing such a golden opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Not removing something. It really wasn't there in the first place.<br /> 2. Wouldn't be even more delicious then if a Sleeper were able to prevail against a Mage given the current assumptions with Integrity and Quiescence? Why are you advocating for changing the system? Just set up a situation where a Sleeper gets a Mage despite the disadvantages. Aren't you the one removing the golden opportunity by trying to lessen the handicap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T19:27:46-07:00","id":655849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655768#post655768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be true, but one of mages greatest strengths comes from their ability to potentially no sell a lot of methods of attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1E, my Perfected Adept stood a better than even chance of winning a toe-to-toe fight with a werewolf, even without time to prepare in advance. In 2E, Gauru form is a terrible, terrible thing to face. If a mage has time, sure, she can make something happen. If you're just going from &quot;zero to sixty&quot; in a bar fight situation, unless the mage is preloaded with spells, the werewolf is likely going to win. The huge trait bonuses, fast weapons (teeth and claws have +3 Initiative), massive amounts of damage, and ability to shrug off harm are hard to overcome. The Obrimos, if skilled in Life, might theoretically use a spell to trigger a submission response or some other instinctive reaction, but probably won't be able to muster up enough direct damage with Forces or Prime or whatever to get it done before the werewolf eviscerates her. Then you must also contend with the fact that the more you hurt the werewolf, the more you risk Death Rage\u2014at which point some options, like mental influence, become much more difficult.<br /> <br /> Many factors come into play in this situation: experience level, luck of the rolls, and so on, but by default, a werewolf is no pushover in a straight fight. In 1E, various supernatural creatures like mages, vampires, and changelings could specialize in physical prowess and at least stand a good chance against a werewolf. In Second Edition, werewolves a lot more dangerous physically, and Gauru is nasty. And the thing is, the werewolf can do it reflexively if she has any kind of decent Harmony. So while the mage is spending a turn trying desperately to get some kind of spell active (but can activate Mage Armor reflexively), the werewolf has transformed into a much faster, much stronger form, with a good Initiative bonus for her unarmed attacks. If she grapples, which she can do <i>with her teeth</i>, she really puts the pressure on the mage, who will find it very difficult to escape.<br /> <br /> Smart mages, even those skilled in battle, don't go picking fights with lycanthropes. At least not in an arena that favors the werewolf.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T19:43:25-07:00","id":655866,"title":"","content":"All of this is true. <i>But,</i> creative use of magic can make it incredibly difficult for werewolves to even <i>use</i> their combative abilities. Nullify their momentum, restrict attack velocity, redirect lines of fire, twist gravity in ways that make it nearly impossible to move let alone fight. While Space magic is probably the best at no selling melee combat Forces is nothing to sneeze at. When I refer to mages no selling methods of attack I'm talking about making it literally impossible to reach/harm them. Like I said, Space probably does it best with things like Ban and Alter Direction, but Forces should also be able to really make it difficult to engage them close up.<br /> <br /> Not to say these methods are foolproof. They can be overcome, but they should at least buy enough time for the mage to <i>really</i> get going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T19:59:00-07:00","id":655878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655866#post655866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can be overcome, but they should at least buy enough time for the mage to <i>really</i> get going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/-tsusbTdSq-Q/U6zfx8_X6yI/AAAAAAAAAHE/OuH24-W8rf8/s1600/488848.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:14:48-07:00","id":655892,"title":"","content":"It is true that Forces could make it difficult to approach the mage, although the mage has little time to make it happen. That's part of the problem. The werewolf shifts and is up in your face right now. You need a spell to work, which means the factors must be a certain way lest you get caught up in your own magic. Sometimes you must account for the size of your opponent, you won't have time to use many Yantras, etc., so not working with an optimal dice pool. But yes, certainly you could use Control Gravity or Turn Momentum to slow down or disorient your foe. Those spells won't let you win on their own, but they at least give you some breathing room. The problem is that you might not win Initiative, either.<br /> <br /> A completely average werewolf (Str 2, Dex 2, Sta 2, Wits 2, Com 2) has Initiative 8 while using teeth/claws, not counting Merits or other abilities. The average mage has an Initiative of 4-5, say, but even a fast mage is still looking at 6-7. So the werewolf has the better chance of going first, can reflexively shift into Gauru and pounce on you, and once you're grappled, Control Gravity or Turn Momentum or the like aren't going to help you much. Then that werewolf (a Blood Talon Rahu) is hitting you next turn with 8-again on her vicious attacks (that probably have major bonus damage), plus other Gifts available to that werewolf can throw a monkey wrench into the mage's plans. Unchained might actually let you escape those spells, she can cripple your Defense, or maybe hit you with Incite Fury and leave you berserk, unable to properly cast spells as you fly into a single-minded rage. She might stun you or knock you down, costing you your action, then set upon you while you're down.<br /> <br /> A werewolf is highly dangerous in a fight just at the drop of a hat. She needs almost no time to become a dangerous killer. The mage might thwart her with a single spell, if that spell works as intended and is cast in time. Otherwise, the mage must spend at least a turn or two getting some spell active that will even up the odds. By that time she's probably crippled or in such a disadvantageous position that it's impossible to regain momentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:29:01-07:00","id":655899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655892#post655892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is true that Forces could make it difficult to approach the mage, although the mage has little time to make it happen. That's part of the problem. The werewolf shifts and is up in your face right now. You need a spell to work, which means the factors must be a certain way lest you get caught up in your own magic. Sometimes you must account for the size of your opponent, you won't have time to use many Yantras, etc., so not working with an optimal dice pool. But yes, certainly you could use Control Gravity or Turn Momentum to slow down or disorient your foe. Those spells won't let you win on their own, but they at least give you some breathing room. The problem is that you might not win Initiative, either.<br /> <br /> A completely average werewolf (Str 2, Dex 2, Sta 2, Wits 2, Com 2) has Initiative 8 while using teeth/claws, not counting Merits or other abilities. The average mage has an Initiative of 4-5, say, but even a fast mage is still looking at 6-7. So the werewolf has the better chance of going first, can reflexively shift into Gauru and pounce on you, and once you're grappled, Control Gravity or Turn Momentum or the like aren't going to help you much. Then that werewolf (a Blood Talon Rahu) is hitting you next turn with 8-again on her vicious attacks (that probably have major bonus damage), plus other Gifts available to that werewolf can throw a monkey wrench into the mage's plans. Unchained might actually let you escape those spells, she can cripple your Defense, or maybe hit you with Incite Fury and leave you berserk, unable to properly cast spells as you fly into a single-minded rage. She might stun you or knock you down, costing you your action, then set upon you while you're down.<br /> <br /> A werewolf is highly dangerous in a fight just at the drop of a hat. She needs almost no time to become a dangerous killer. The mage might thwart her with a single spell, if that spell works as intended and is cast in time. Otherwise, the mage must spend at least a turn or two getting some spell active that will even up the odds. By that time she's probably crippled or in such a disadvantageous position that it's impossible to regain momentum.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, this is mostly going to depend on exact arcana and build (as per the usual). We know that mage armor is reflexive in 2e and has different effects based off of the one being used. We also know that at least the Time shield specifically messes around with initiative, and that the Death shield downgrades damage types. Long story short, it depends heavily on the mage. I also think you're underestimating how quickly a mage can turn lethal. Spells don't need anything higher than a single success nowadays, and while you likely aren't going to be able to get an extremely high number of factors piled into a spell at the drop of a hat, you usually don't need to. A mage only needs a single turn to mind control you, a single turn to create an unpassable barrier, a single turn to cause any number of status effects, conditions, or tilts, etc. While mages are nearly unstoppable with prep, they're nothing to sneeze at even when caught off guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:32:51-07:00","id":655902,"title":"","content":"Oh boy..., I was just trying to inject some levity in the thread when I raised the werewolf vs. mage bar fight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;White room (white bar?)&quot; fights simply don't account for the innumerable variables in combat even attempting to emulate real circumstances. For instance, are the characters armed with fetishes, imbued items or mundane weaponry, can the environment be used offensively or defensively, is the protection of patrons or other innocents a priority, is back-up or other allies available, or just plain luck. The abilities provided by XP progression are also not necessarily equivalent among different templates, and truly min/max combat characters would be so usually specialized if translated to reality as to be ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <b><i>However</i></b>, if I was to engage in such a foolish discussion, which of course I would never do, I would suggest the Obrimos simply levitate the werewolf up and as far away as possible, and then take all the time or actions she deemed necessary. Last I checked, there were exceedingly few werewolf abilities that permitted flight. If that didn't work, mages above a certain medium XP level have the fairly unique ability to cause significant aggravated damage at a distance, This should be employed immediately and with abandon.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, no Wise mage of any Path, Order or Legacy should get into a bar fight with any lycanthrope without sufficient preparation (I believe mages learn this in their first day of Arrow training). There are more than ample uses of Forces, Prime and other Arcanum to get the hell out of Dodge quickly and easily, and then later carefully and patiently prepare to put down that rabid and mangy excuse for a canine at a time, place and manner of her choosing. It should not be thought of as a &quot;retreat,&quot; so much as a temporary and limited &quot;strategic withdrawal.&quot;<br /> <br /> But, as I stated earlier, I would never engage in such pointless and unproductive conjecture... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We should be discussing far more important things, like why Dave is sadly all wrong and obviously delirious after finalizing the Mage 2e opus, and how Mage Arcadia is really the same place as Changeling Arcadia...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Just to keep with the point of the thread, no human Sleeper Hunter would stand a chance against either the mage or werewolf in that hypothetical bar fight. In fact, anyone with a lick of sense should avoid that bar entirely! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-07-2015, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:47:21-07:00","id":655953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655899#post655899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again, this is mostly going to depend on exact arcana and build (as per the usual). We know that mage armor is reflexive in 2e and has different effects based off of the one being used. We also know that at least the Time shield specifically messes around with initiative, and that the Death shield downgrades damage types. Long story short, it depends heavily on the mage. I also think you're underestimating how quickly a mage can turn lethal. Spells don't need anything higher than a single success nowadays, and while you likely aren't going to be able to get an extremely high number of factors piled into a spell at the drop of a hat, you usually don't need to. A mage only needs a single turn to mind control you, a single turn to create an unpassable barrier, a single turn to cause any number of status effects, conditions, or tilts, etc. While mages are nearly unstoppable with prep, they're nothing to sneeze at even when caught off guard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust me: I've been playing <b>Mage: The Awakening </b>since its release, I have worked on and extensively played most of the 2E game lines (including <b>Mage</b> and <b>Werewolf</b>), and I have right in front of me the latest developed copy of the 2E rules. I'm not underestimating anything. As well, remember we're talking about an Obrimos of the Adamantine Arrow here, so not guaranteed to have Death, Mind, Time or the like, or have them at high levels. Ultimately, Mind is one of the best bets for stopping the fight before it starts, which I'd call a &quot;win,&quot; but the question was about Blood Talon Rahu vs. Adamantine Arrow Obrimos.<br /> <br /> Spells need only a single success to take effect at all the configured factors, yes, but you have to take everything into account. Like Withstand, or the chosen opponent's ability to shrug off harm like nobody's business. Various Mage Armors can help, definitely\u2014Death is good, although you're still taking damage, even if it's downgraded, and Time helps you avoid getting hit. Casting a mind control spell might help you out...for a turn or two, unless you can get it with more advanced factors, but that means greater difficulty. If you put so much effort into increasing its duration, you still have to worry about Potency, lest it have no effect at all on the rampaging beast. Even my character in a 2E game has failed spellcasting rolls with 6-7 dice before, when the dice gods were vengeful.<br /> <br /> This is what I mean. Much of the mage's ability depends on multiple factors. It's <i>possible </i>that one spell with one casting roll could propel her to victory. It's not always <i>likely</i>, though. Conversely, the werewolf is a reliable death-dealing machine. She attacks fast, she hits hard, she keeps on coming, and she has tremendous advantages up close (grappling and status-inflicting effects, especially). The Rahu's magic helps make her a better killer. She's less versatile than our hypothetical mage, but trades that versatility for special focus in killing up close and personal. The mage is going to lose if she has to go hand-to-hand with the werewolf, and has one turn at most to change the nature of the fight such that she doesn't <i>have </i>to duke it out in a straight fight. That's not a whole lot of margin for error. The werewolf doesn't have to work very hard to be super-deadly in battle. It's pretty much all reflexive stuff that she can do right from the outset. The mage doesn't have as many inherent advantages.<br /> <br /> If I wasn't so busy trying to finish another project tonight, I'd stat up a couple characters and roll out a &quot;bar fight&quot; scene, just because it's fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:51:40-07:00","id":655954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655899#post655899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think you're underestimating how quickly a mage can turn lethal. Spells don't need anything higher than a single success nowadays, and while you likely aren't going to be able to get an extremely high number of factors piled into a spell at the drop of a hat, you usually don't need to. A mage only needs a single turn to mind control you, a single turn to create an unpassable barrier, a single turn to cause any number of status effects, conditions, or tilts, etc. While mages are nearly unstoppable with prep, they're nothing to sneeze at even when caught off guard.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, you're also underestimating werewolves. What Claire is speaking about is just a werewolf without gifts, while what you're speaking of is a mage with all arcana. If you wanted to throw all the gifts in, you'll have to deal with Hit and Run to interrupt spells and hit a mage with aggravated damage, Fog of War to make spells target something else and hit the mage with aggravated damage, Fearless Hunter to throw off mind control and inflict aggravated damage, or just Incite Fury to turn the mage from a spell-caster to a broken bottle-wielding thug.<br /> <br /> With the added benefit that the Uratha don't need to be in gauru to eat people. It just helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-07-2015, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:54:02-07:00","id":655959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655953#post655953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have right in front of me the latest developed copy of the 2E rules..<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't drop a line like that without at least a small spoiler! It's just cruel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I believe you wrote the 2e versions of Life, Forces and Time. Care to share a spell or three that differs from 1e? Please!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:55:02-07:00","id":655961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655953#post655953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Trust me: I've been playing <b>Mage: The Awakening </b>since its release, I have worked on and extensively played most of the 2E game lines (including <b>Mage</b> and <b>Werewolf</b>), and I have right in front of me the latest developed copy of the 2E rules. I'm not underestimating anything. As well, remember we're talking about an Obrimos of the Adamantine Arrow here, so not guaranteed to have Death, Mind, Time or the like, or have them at high levels. Ultimately, Mind is one of the best bets for stopping the fight before it starts, which I'd call a &quot;win,&quot; but the question was about Blood Talon Rahu vs. Adamantine Arrow Obrimos.<br /> <br /> Spells need only a single success to take effect at all the configured factors, yes, but you have to take everything into account. Like Withstand, or the chosen opponent's ability to shrug off harm like nobody's business. Various Mage Armors can help, definitely\u2014Death is good, although you're still taking damage, even if it's downgraded, and Time helps you avoid getting hit. Casting a mind control spell might help you out...for a turn or two, unless you can get it with more advanced factors, but that means greater difficulty. If you put so much effort into increasing its duration, you still have to worry about Potency, lest it have no effect at all on the rampaging beast. Even my character in a 2E game has failed spellcasting rolls with 6-7 dice before, when the dice gods were vengeful.<br /> <br /> This is what I mean. Much of the mage's ability depends on multiple factors. It's <i>possible </i>that one spell with one casting roll could propel her to victory. It's not always <i>likely</i>, though. Conversely, the werewolf is a reliable death-dealing machine. She attacks fast, she hits hard, she keeps on coming, and she has tremendous advantages up close (grappling and status-inflicting effects, especially). The Rahu's magic helps make her a better killer. She's less versatile than our hypothetical mage, but trades that versatility for special focus in killing up close and personal. The mage is going to lose if she has to go hand-to-hand with the werewolf, and has one turn at most to change the nature of the fight such that she doesn't <i>have </i>to duke it out in a straight fight. That's not a whole lot of margin for error. The werewolf doesn't have to work very hard to be super-deadly in battle. It's pretty much all reflexive stuff that she can do right from the outset. The mage doesn't have as many inherent advantages.<br /> <br /> If I wasn't so busy trying to finish another project tonight, I'd stat up a couple characters and roll out a &quot;bar fight&quot; scene, just because it's fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately I don't have the Forces spell list in front of me so I can only guess at it's potency compared to that of Space (since we have more relevant information via spoilers on that than we do on Forces), but if it is anywhere close to that I'm not seeing much of a problem. Not sure if you can answer this, but do mages get as many dots spread across their arcana as they did in 1e or has that dropped a bit? Also, duration isn't that big of a deal. You only need a stalling spell to last a turn or two, just long enough to cast another stalling spell with greater duration using the time gained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-07-2015, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:55:24-07:00","id":655963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655953#post655953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I wasn't so busy trying to finish another project tonight, I'd stat up a couple characters and roll out a &quot;bar fight&quot; scene, just because it's fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, I would pay you in, umm ... cookies? Poetry? Uhh .. what do you like ... to do this and post about it. NDA material redacted, of course, no one wants you to get in trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:55:53-07:00","id":655964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655768#post655768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can disagree if you like. As Charlaquin said, we've already got a ruling as to how these things work and how the base setting is from the head mage developer. This isn't a debate, it is fact. You can dislike it, houserule it, and try to deny it all you like but the rulings and intent have been clearly stated. You are, of course, free to pick and choose how you'd like it to be at your own table, but know that it explicitly goes against the setting as written and intended as presented in the book. Which isn't necessarily a bad thing mind you, it's just the way of things.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655824#post655824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Wouldn't be even more delicious then if a Sleeper were able to prevail against a Mage given the current assumptions with Integrity and Quiescence? Why are you advocating for changing the system? Just set up a situation where a Sleeper gets a Mage despite the disadvantages. Aren't you the one removing the golden opportunity by trying to lessen the handicap?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said I was advocating for changing the system? Clearly, you have misunderstood me the whole time.<br /> <br /> I never did want the system to change as written, presented, or intended. What I disagree with is the whole notion that <i>&quot;Hurr durr, you can't get past the Sleeping Curse, go hunt weaker witches instead lolz&quot;</i>. Just because it causes Sleepers to forget mages ever used magic and is a Breaking Point doesn't mean they can't work around it. Let me repeat that, work <b>around</b> it. Not lessen it, not remove it, but work around it.<br /> <br /> It's still a big obstacle and would certainly make hunting Awakened problematic in the long term without any supernatural aid, but not for one or two instances. An Awakened would be like that really tough boss fight. If you were faced with those all the time, yes you would be completely screwed, but that doesn't mean you can't have <i>any</i> of them at all.<br /> <br /> The proposed <i>After Action Report</i> and <i>Make a Scene</i> Tactics would be just fine for something like this, and <i>maybe</i> (keyword maybe) some more and some non-supernatural Merits. That, and also focusing on exploiting a mage's hubris as well. That last part is really all I was adding to the discussion. I never advocated for changing the system.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/kRfrNeBspEE\" target=\"_blank\">I think this video explains what I'm talking about</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 09-07-2015, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:56:47-07:00","id":655965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655959#post655959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't drop a line like that without at least a small spoiler! It's just cruel. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I believe you wrote the 2e versions of Life, Forces and Time. Care to share a spell or three that differs from 1e? Please!</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a Seer of the Throne beholden to Dave, my Exarch master. I'll not part the veil of the Lie unless he deems it so!<br /> <br /> ... but I can tell you that lots of spells from each of those Arcana work differently from their 1E counterparts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:01:31-07:00","id":655968,"title":"","content":"Hey, is there any room on that bar fight? I still need practice getting combat all sorted out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah, no hunter is going to stand up against mid tier experiance supernaturals of any sort without stacking the deck in their favor, whether it be getting the drop of their opponent, sheer overkill in terms of weaponry... or vehicular assault. And even that might not work with enough experience points.<br /> <br /> Case in point, maxed out Rending Claws wreck even hitech combat walkers and tanks. I'm sure Mages can do the same via some sort of &quot;turn Durability to 0&quot; spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:03:39-07:00","id":655970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655965#post655965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am a Seer of the Throne beholden to Dave, my Exarch master. I'll not part the veil of the Lie unless he deems it so!<br /> <br /> ... but I can tell you that lots of spells from each of those Arcana work differently from their 1E counterparts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Dave is a kind and generous god, whose spoiler bounty is legendary. One of such benevolence surely would not object to sharing small pearls from the wisdom contained in Mage 2e!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:08:15-07:00","id":656002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655961#post655961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately I don't have the Forces spell list in front of me so I can only guess at it's potency compared to that of Space (since we have more relevant information via spoilers on that than we do on Forces), but if it is anywhere close to that I'm not seeing much of a problem. Not sure if you can answer this, but do mages get as many dots spread across their arcana as they did in 1e or has that dropped a bit? Also, duration isn't that big of a deal. You only need a stalling spell to last a turn or two, just long enough to cast another stalling spell with greater duration using the time gained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forces is <i>very </i>potent, I can tell you. Especially with the changes to the spellcasting system (and the removal of the &quot;covert&quot; and &quot;vulgar&quot; divide). Spells now align properly to dot level and Practice, no matter the particular force involved. It's flashy, to be sure, and some of its spells are ridiculously good at controlling a fight simply by dint of controlling the forces involved in that fight. If you can't hit an opponent, you can't hurt her, at least if you're limited to physical attacks. But Turn Momentum must account for the subject's Size, which is larger than default if said subject is a Gauru-form werewolf. Then you must take into account Reach, if you want to use more advanced factors, and penalties from increasing non-Primary Factors, and things like that. And then there's Paradox, since you're probably having to Reach further than normal to do all this in the one turn you might have before the werewolf tackles you.<br /> <br /> There's a lot at play here. And as nofather mentioned (and I mentioned before him), Incite Fury is kind of a nasty move. If it works, the mage goes berserk and will have a hard time casting any spells. She'll have to make a Resolve + Composure roll to do anything other than attack with any weapons at hand, and even if she succeeds suffers a -3 to all actions other than attacking the nearest target. That puts a hurt on the game plan right there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655963#post655963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man, I would pay you in, umm ... cookies? Poetry? Uhh .. what do you like ... to do this and post about it. NDA material redacted, of course, no one wants you to get in trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd have to limit things to stripping out the mechanical details, but I might do it. I have to finish my work, first! :P We'll have to decide on experience level, though. I'll apply the same amount of Experiences to both participants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:16:00-07:00","id":656021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655954#post655954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, you're also underestimating werewolves. What Claire is speaking about is just a werewolf without gifts, while what you're speaking of is a mage with all arcana. If you wanted to throw all the gifts in, you'll have to deal with Hit and Run to interrupt spells and hit a mage with aggravated damage, Fog of War to make spells target something else and hit the mage with aggravated damage, Fearless Hunter to throw off mind control and inflict aggravated damage, or just Incite Fury to turn the mage from a spell-caster to a broken bottle-wielding thug.<br /> <br /> With the added benefit that the Uratha don't need to be in gauru to eat people. It just helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I know their gifts and how they work, and I was taking those into account even if I didn't explicitly say so. Hit and run <i>might</i> work, again, depending on exactly how the mage is attacking and what arcana they have (Just being an Obrimos Arrow doesn't really tell me enough here), same with Fog of War. Again, the big issue here is really lack of information about both the characters in question and the exact capabilities of the arcana being used. I can make an educated guess based off of what we know, but again, specifics depend pretty heavily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-08-2015, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:22:11-07:00","id":656029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656002#post656002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a lot at play here. And as nofather mentioned (and I mentioned before him), Incite Fury is kind of a nasty move. If it works, the mage goes berserk and will have a hard time casting any spells. She'll have to make a Resolve + Composure roll to do anything other than attack with any weapons at hand, and even if she succeeds suffers a -3 to all actions other than attacking the nearest target. That puts a hurt on the game plan right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>If any major template could make a Resolve + Composure roll, it's mages. I would also imagine that a number of spells or Arcana should be able to force a Clash of Wills against Incite Fury.<br /> <br /> However, as I stated before, a smart mage never permits herself to engage in unprepared combat, no less mano a mano with a rampaging, befanged ball of fur. If such a situation occurs, the mage should use all the ample means at her disposal to immediately escape. Thereafter, at her leisure, she can carefully plan the very slow and extraordinarily painful demise of the insolent mongrel (and any witnesses) who dared thought to challenge her personal safety. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:31:09-07:00","id":656032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656029#post656029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If any major template could make a Resolve + Composure roll, it's mages. I would also imagine that a number of spells or Arcana should be able to force a Clash of Wills against Incite Fury.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Resolve + Composure is a good roll for most mages. However, she has to make that every turn or else attack in a blind rage. Even if she succeeds, all her other actions are at -3\u2014including spellcasting rolls. That hurts, when every die counts in this situation. I'm sure a great many spells could help lift the Berserk Condition (Clear Thoughts comes to Mind), but that's also another action you're taking aside from attacking, while the werewolf is focusing her attention on attacking.<br /> <br /> It's not that mages are helpless without preparation, or that they never stand a chance against a werewolf. Neither of those were true in 1E, and they're certainly not now. My point is that this particular scenario is playing right into the werewolf's wheelhouse. The mage is fighting an uphill battle here against a foe with a lot of inherent advantages for this sort of fight. She's definitely better off if she manages to get away, now has some idea of what she's up against, and prepare for a future conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:31:41-07:00","id":656034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656029#post656029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If any major template could make a Resolve + Composure roll, it's mages. I would also imagine that a number of spells or Arcana should be able to force a Clash of Wills against Incite Fury.<br /> <br /> However, as I stated before, a smart mage never permits herself to engage in unprepared combat, no less mano a mano with a rampaging, befanged ball of fur. If such a situation occurs, the mage should use all the ample means at her disposal to immediately escape. Thereafter, at her leisure, she can carefully plan the very slow and extraordinarily painful demise of the insolent mongrel (and any witnesses) who dared thought to challenge her personal safety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if she tries to use a spell to force a Clash of Wills against Incite Fury, she's wasting an action getting rid of a debuff against an opponent who may not be as hindered. And sometimes the attempt will be a -3 penalty too.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I somehow doubt Mages can afford to be level 20 D&amp;D wizards all the time, especially if the reason there is a fight in the first place is an immediate thing that cannot be easily undone. Teleporting out of the area might be possible, it might not. And even if she can take her revenge in a manner like that, that doesn't mean she is the victor.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:38:54-07:00","id":656038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655964#post655964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said I was advocating for changing the system? Clearly, you have misunderstood me the whole time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems so. So ... you're just taking objection to Dave saying &quot;just use Witches?&quot; Well I guess we are more in agreement than I thought. I think he was just being a tad hyperbolic in stating how much of a challenge Mages are to witch hunters. I don't take it that literally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:39:53-07:00","id":656039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656034#post656034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seriously, I somehow doubt Mages can afford to be level 20 D&amp;D wizards all the time, especially if the reason there is a fight in the first place is an immediate thing that cannot be easily undone. Teleporting out of the area might be possible, it might not. And even if she can take her revenge in a manner like that, that doesn't mean she is the victor.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The nWOD is a cruel and unforgiving place. A &quot;victory&quot; in the supernatural world is any fight you can walk away from. Enacting vengeance later is just a bonus. <br /> <br /> I think a better question than essentially inquiring if unprepared mages prioritize escape and revenge when confronted by violence, is just asking about the number of old and powerful mages, particularly those who have interesting stories about foolish youthful bar fights. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:49:45-07:00","id":656046,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem with escape from werewolves is it then allows werewolves to use their preptime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:56:25-07:00","id":656049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656046#post656046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem with escape from werewolves is it then allows werewolves to use their preptime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Werewolves are quite good at tracking fleeing prey. Of course, mages have some ways to fool even heightened senses\u2014it's kind of hard to follow a scent trail if your prey has just teleported across the state. But then <i>again</i>, if a werewolf has tasted her prey's blood she can sense his location no matter the distance or barrier....<br /> <br /> So, yeah, many factors at play here. Many ways this could go either direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:57:02-07:00","id":656050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656046#post656046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem with escape from werewolves is it then allows werewolves to use their preptime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Preparation and planning almost always favors mages due to their versatility and the advantages of spellcasting without time constraints.<br /> <br /> Of course, preparation also means any battle might no longer be one on one, no less in a cramped bar, and cabal vs. pack combat adds near limitless new variables.<br /> <br /> It's definitely best if both werewolves and mages stick with beating-up puny humans when they're out drinking. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T21:59:54-07:00","id":656052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656039#post656039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The nWOD is a cruel and unforgiving place. A &quot;victory&quot; in the supernatural world is any fight you can walk away from. Enacting vengeance later is just a bonus.<br /> <br /> I think a better question than essentially inquiring if unprepared mages prioritize escape and revenge when confronted by violence, is just asking about the number of old and powerful mages, particularly those who have interesting stories about foolish youthful bar fights. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was speaking about situations where escape might actually make things worse. For example, run away or defend your family.<br /> <br /> Or run away and fail to stop said opponent from delivering an item of doom that will make revenge impossible for plot reasons.<br /> <br /> I mean, leaving battle is valid if you want to live, but sometimes you're not able to do that without making things worse for you.<br /> <br /> Group combat favors the pack I believe. While mages get tons of options, Werewolves can do some pretty ridiculous teamwide buffs or massive area controls... that specifically do not hinder pack members. This includes humans and wolf blooded who sign on the pack, but perhaps we should just leave out nonwerewolves, ya?<br /> <br /> And for the record, I think vampire probably wins in terms of elders who lived long enough to get powerful, but I just don't think they're all awake at the same time.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-08-2015, 01:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T22:10:02-07:00","id":656056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656052#post656052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And for the record, I think vampire probably wins in terms of elders who lived long enough to get powerful, but I just don't think they're all awake at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hold on! You're not seriously suggesting that we add a<i> third </i>major template to our hypothetical bar fight <u><i>and</i></u> assume they're all very high experience / power characters??? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That way lies madness!<br /> <br /> If that's the case, however, an archmage can erase bars from existence, and therefore no combat shall occur (or will never have occurred, since if reality changed, bars never existed)! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-08-2015, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T22:17:18-07:00","id":656065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656056#post656056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's the case, however, an archmage can erase bars from existence, and therefore no combat shall occur (or will never have occurred, since if reality changed, bars never existed)! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And of course the most expedient way to accomplish this is targeted Aponoia.<br /> <br /> One subjective chapter later, they all meet in a tavern\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T22:30:14-07:00","id":656078,"title":"","content":"I just want to note that this is one of the most fun and cordial &quot;white room&quot; discussion I've ever observed, with ample good humor and totally devoid of personal insults and nastiness, questions about mathematical ability, or irrational fan defensiveness about favored splats.<br /> <br /> I'm just so proud... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T22:55:15-07:00","id":656098,"title":"","content":"We've actually run white room scenarios on the forums before, though it was probably at least one forum version before this one. It was three signature characters Prince Vidal, Max Roman, and the Nemean in a featureless room with three turns of prep. They basically got a ten second countdown and then went at it. I'm pretty sure the Nemean died first. Man, I wish the forum archives weren't 404-ing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T23:03:21-07:00","id":656112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656098#post656098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've actually run white room scenarios on the forums before, though it was probably at least one forum version before this one. It was three signature characters Prince Vidal, Max Roman, and the Nemean in a featureless room with three turns of prep. They basically got a ten second countdown and then went at it. I'm pretty sure the Nemean died first. Man, I wish the forum archives weren't 404-ing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nemean was the mage I am assuming. I know who Max is, and Prince Vidal sounds like a vampire, so that means the other has got to be a mage. Unless I am reading things wrong.<br /> <br /> So, can anyone sum that up?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T23:11:29-07:00","id":656116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656112#post656112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nemean was the mage I am assuming. I know who Max is, and Prince Vidal sounds like a vampire, so that means the other has got to be a mage. Unless I am reading things wrong.<br /> <br /> So, can anyone sum that up?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Prince Vidal was from City of the Damned: New Orleans, circa 2005.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T23:16:08-07:00","id":656117,"title":"","content":"The Nemean is the Hierarch of Boston, from Boston Unveiled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T23:21:01-07:00","id":656118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656117#post656117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nemean is the Hierarch of Boston, from Boston Unveiled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He also makes another appearance in the Fallen World Anthology's, &quot;The Unmurdered Man.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T23:28:48-07:00","id":656119,"title":"","content":"I just spent like 20 minutes trying to find his stats in Boston Unveiled, only to realize that his stat block is actually the Mage Core. Doh!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T23:33:12-07:00","id":656123,"title":"","content":"He'd be a hell of a powerhouse in 2e given the streamlining of the arcana. Even in 1e he looks to have a lot of dots thrown into various things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-08-2015, 02:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T00:01:59-07:00","id":656162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656002#post656002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forces is <i>very </i>potent, I can tell you. Especially with the changes to the spellcasting system (and the removal of the &quot;covert&quot; and &quot;vulgar&quot; divide). Spells now align properly to dot level and Practice, no matter the particular force involved. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Since we're discussing Obrimos, I meant to ask earlier, how's the combat (or escape) utility of the shiny new and improved Prime in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T00:59:27-07:00","id":656199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656162#post656162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we're discussing Obrimos, I meant to ask earlier, how's the combat (or escape) utility of the shiny new and improved Prime in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like all the Arcana, Prime is useful in combat in many ways, more so if you're clever with it. Where it excels is in combating magic, or using magic both offensively and defensively. Imbuing items, discerning truths, veiling or shielding against magic, controlling magical forces in the world, that kind of thing. You can use it to fight, but it's better at supporting magical warfare than waging said warfare directly. Forces has far more variety in immediate &quot;This spell can be used to mess people up&quot; options due to its nature, but Prime is equally powerful in a more subtle way. If Forces is the storm, Prime is the global weather systems that set storms in motion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T01:13:38-07:00","id":656207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656199#post656199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like all the Arcana, Prime is useful in combat in many ways, more so if you're clever with it. Where it excels is in combating magic, or using magic both offensively and defensively. Imbuing items, discerning truths, veiling or shielding against magic, controlling magical forces in the world, that kind of thing. You can use it to fight, but it's better at supporting magical warfare than waging said warfare directly. Forces has far more variety in immediate &quot;This spell can be used to mess people up&quot; options due to its nature, but Prime is equally powerful in a more subtle way. If Forces is the storm, Prime is the global weather systems that set storms in motion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. Your description does make Prime seem like it has notably diminished utility when not dealing with other Awakened or supernal magic.<br /> <br /> No doubt, Forces is probably best when you're an Obrimos dealing with angry werewolves in bars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T01:40:59-07:00","id":656221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656199#post656199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like all the Arcana, Prime is useful in combat in many ways, more so if you're clever with it. Where it excels is in combating magic, or using magic both offensively and defensively. Imbuing items, discerning truths, veiling or shielding against magic, controlling magical forces in the world, that kind of thing. You can use it to fight, but it's better at supporting magical warfare than waging said warfare directly. Forces has far more variety in immediate &quot;This spell can be used to mess people up&quot; options due to its nature, but Prime is equally powerful in a more subtle way. If Forces is the storm, Prime is the global weather systems that set storms in motion.</div> </div> </div> </div>How useful is Prime when <i>not</i> dealing with other mages and supernal magic? Can it mess around with other miscellaneous forms of magical stuff, like relics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T02:19:17-07:00","id":656278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656002#post656002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forces is <i>very </i>potent, I can tell you. Especially with the changes to the spellcasting system (and the removal of the &quot;covert&quot; and &quot;vulgar&quot; divide). Spells now align properly to dot level and Practice, no matter the particular force involved. It's flashy, to be sure, and some of its spells are ridiculously good at controlling a fight simply by dint of controlling the forces involved in that fight. If you can't hit an opponent, you can't hurt her, at least if you're limited to physical attacks. But Turn Momentum must account for the subject's Size, which is larger than default if said subject is a Gauru-form werewolf. Then you must take into account Reach, if you want to use more advanced factors, and penalties from increasing non-Primary Factors, and things like that. And then there's Paradox, since you're probably having to Reach further than normal to do all this in the one turn you might have before the werewolf tackles you.<br /> <br /> There's a lot at play here. And as nofather mentioned (and I mentioned before him), Incite Fury is kind of a nasty move. If it works, the mage goes berserk and will have a hard time casting any spells. She'll have to make a Resolve + Composure roll to do anything other than attack with any weapons at hand, and even if she succeeds suffers a -3 to all actions other than attacking the nearest target. That puts a hurt on the game plan right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, my Mage's foolproof plan for dealing with surprise Werewolves attacking is to take the Beat and surrender. Unless their stated goal is to kill me (which it probably won't be, as that is qualitatively identical to the ST dropping a big rock on my character) it works every time!<br /> <b>If</b> their goal is to kill me and <b>if </b> I survive their first action alive and ungrappled (which would honestly surprise me), and assuming I am an Obrimos that only has access to published 2e stuff, reversing gravity on myself seems like a good first step. Get some distance and time to think something up, and I don't have to worry about them withstanding the spell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T02:48:00-07:00","id":656286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656207#post656207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks. Your description does make Prime seem like it has notably diminished utility when not dealing with other Awakened or supernal magic.<br /> <br /> No doubt, Forces is probably best when you're an Obrimos dealing with angry werewolves in bars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it makes you feel better, I'm fairly certain Prime was one of the Arcana pointed to as &quot;let's make this better&quot;. I'm rather sure it only gained things (the whole Truth stuff) and still does what it used to, though that's sort of a wild guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T06:54:59-07:00","id":656478,"title":"","content":"Q: What does an 800 pound Werewolf do when facing a Mage?<br /> A: Anything it wants.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T07:16:14-07:00","id":656491,"title":"","content":"Cast <i>Shield from Inertia</i> first round, assuming you're still alive, and that should no-sell the Werewolf long enough to ramp.<br /> <br /> Alternatively: it's a barfight, why are we even using supernatural powers? Just punch the fucker and relieve some stress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T07:22:09-07:00","id":656496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656478#post656478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Q: What does an 800 pound Werewolf do when facing a Mage?<br /> A: Anything it wants.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Suuuure, anything he wants. *Mastigos Chortle*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T08:12:09-07:00","id":656552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656278#post656278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, my Mage's foolproof plan for dealing with surprise Werewolves attacking is to take the Beat and surrender. Unless their stated goal is to kill me (which it probably won't be, as that is qualitatively identical to the ST dropping a big rock on my character) it works every time!<br /> <b>If</b> their goal is to kill me and <b>if </b> I survive their first action alive and ungrappled (which would honestly surprise me), and assuming I am an Obrimos that only has access to published 2e stuff, reversing gravity on myself seems like a good first step. Get some distance and time to think something up, and I don't have to worry about them withstanding the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but any melee werewolf is going to have a ridiculous jump range. because the speed and jump boosts are on the same Gift list as the strength buffs and rend tanks powers. Your reverse gravity spell on yourself might not give you enough distance. <br /> <br /> In terms of metagaming though, your plan works for everything except &quot;final bosses&quot;, so that's lovely, right? More exp = win in everyone's books, so taking beats from losses is valid.<br /> <br /> What does Shield from Inertia do btw?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T08:22:55-07:00","id":656564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656552#post656552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does Shield from Inertia do btw?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the energy from being touched would turn into momentum for you, unmitigated by your mass and with zero tranference to you beyond momentum.<br /> <br /> Mainly it's a <i>Lensman</i> reference, I honestly don't know if it's a legitimate spell in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 09-08-2015, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T08:31:01-07:00","id":656576,"title":"","content":"Actually I think that would just make them do even more damage. <br /> <br /> And they could still just do stuff like set you on fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T09:20:15-07:00","id":656622,"title":"","content":"I suppose it would make it look funnier as you flailed around in horror, agony and disbelief as the werewolf ate you.<br /> <br /> But basically if you're going to deny a werewolf could kill a mage, you're <i>far </i>on the side of hunters not ever being able to kill a mage. Because a hunter is basically werewolf-lite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2015, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T09:35:13-07:00","id":656629,"title":"","content":"Also good luck casting spells with the Berserk condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T10:34:27-07:00","id":656699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656576#post656576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I think that would just make them do even more damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, because physics. Also, you could cast it on the Werewolf, instead, that way they couldn't even bite you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And they could still just do stuff like set you on fire. </div> </div> </div>Because <i>fire</i> is going to work great against an Obrimos.<br /> <br /> For the record I think that a werewolf going full Gauru against an unprepared Mage would chunky salsa the Mage before the Mage even got to think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T10:49:04-07:00","id":656710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656699#post656699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, because physics. Also, you could cast it on the Werewolf, instead, that way they couldn't even bite you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Assuming said spell is valid, the werewolf has no ability to contest the gift and other things.<br /> <br /> I believe Rose said earlier that such a spell cannot work on a werewolf as easily as other it would other melee combatants because of the size inherent size increase of Gauru<br /> requiring advanced factors; explained, the spell needs to be stronger to negate an opponent of greater mass, making it much harder to work. But that might be for a different spell, I'll go check the logs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: The spell is Turn Momentum on page 22 of this thread, which probably is close enough to the proposed spell to rely on mostly the same rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because <i>fire</i> is going to work great against an Obrimos.<br /> <br /> For the record I think that a werewolf going full Gauru against an unprepared Mage would chunky salsa the Mage before the Mage even got to think. </div> </div> </div>As for fire, well, it depends on what buffs are on the Obrimos. I mean, fire <i>would </i>kill the mage if he doesn't specifically negate it. And I'm certain that in the case of a &quot;prevent all fire from reaching me&quot; spell, that becomes a Clash of Wills I believe, because there's no such thing as total invincibility and powers have to roll off against each other. Granted though, Obrimos mages do get more mileage from Pyrotechnics, because Werewolf Elemental gifts are priced very high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-08-2015, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T10:55:24-07:00","id":656733,"title":"","content":"Ah, wait, I misread the description you gave. I thought it <i>stopped</i> the mage from moving. Bouncing round like a pinball requires an entirely different response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T11:33:29-07:00","id":656774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656733#post656733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, wait, I misread the description you gave. I thought it <i>stopped</i> the mage from moving. Bouncing round like a pinball requires an entirely different response.</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't bounce like a pinball, either. What would happen, assuming it was cast on the Mage, is that the mage would obtain an instantaneous velocity calculated as if the Mage's mass were a limit approaching zero; the Mage would then fly in a straight line until hitting another object, at which point their relative velocity would instantaneously be zero (because effectively massless and 100% energy transfer). The Mage would suffer no deleterious effects of acceleration, but would still be susceptible to a bite attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T11:46:50-07:00","id":656777,"title":"","content":"I'm not liking a mage's chances fighting a werewolf in a small enclosed space like bar while unprepared for the encounter. Such a situation definitely favors the inherent advantages of the werewolf.<br /> <br /> I would recommend the mage first employ any available means to quickly escape and prepare to fight the werewolf later on more advantageous terms. Even if the werewolf could track the mage, just a little extra time and a better environment could dramatically change the odds.<br /> <br /> If escape was not practical (e.g., protecting innocents in the bar, etc.), and assuming the mage had at least one Arcana at 4 dots, she should attempt the biggest ranged aggravated damage she can muster, using any necessary mana at her disposal and risking Paradox, to try to kill or incapacitate the werewolf in one shot, or at least inflict significant damage that is immune to the werewolf's improved healing abilities. Even without an instant kill, the werewolf might not want to risk a continued encounter where more aggravated damage and death is even a possibility. A draw is as good as a victory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T12:02:47-07:00","id":656783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656774#post656774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They wouldn't bounce like a pinball, either. What would happen, assuming it was cast on the Mage, is that the mage would obtain an instantaneous velocity calculated as if the Mage's mass were a limit approaching zero; the Mage would then fly in a straight line until hitting another object, at which point their relative velocity would instantaneously be zero (because effectively massless and 100% energy transfer). The Mage would suffer no deleterious effects of acceleration, but would still be susceptible to a bite attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really can't shake off the feeling that said spell probably is difficult to pull off on the spot. I'm certain it's possible and doable by the rules, I just wonder about its viability and reliability. I haven't looked up Mage 2e much beyond some of the previews, but I keep having the feeling that making a spell behave exactly like as you describe might be impractical compared to other options.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Moving on from Werewolf versus Mage, you know what I think is probably worse for a Hunter to face than a pack or cabal? <br /> <br /> A pack/cabal made up of Mages <i>and Werewolves</i>. <br /> I mean, really, think about it. Monster mashes give up a whole lot of their specialization in a particular field, but they get plenty of reach and flexibility to make up for it. They're harder to counter as different members would have different weaknesses on top of having a wider variety of powers with less overlap. <br /> <br /> Using MMO analogies, Werewolves would Tank in a manner similar to WoW Paladins and Warriors. Mages... would be mages and clerics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656777#post656777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not liking a mage's chances fighting a werewolf in a small enclosed space like bar while unprepared for the encounter. Such a situation definitely favors the inherent advantages of the werewolf.<br /> <br /> I would recommend the mage first employ any available means to quickly escape and prepare to fight the werewolf later on more advantageous terms. Even if the werewolf could track the mage, just a little extra time and a better environment could dramatically change the odds.<br /> <br /> If escape was not practical (e.g., protecting innocents in the bar, etc.), and assuming the mage had at least one Arcana at 4 dots, she should attempt the biggest ranged aggravated damage she can muster, using any necessary mana at her disposal and risking Paradox, to try to kill or incapacitate the werewolf in one shot, or at least inflict significant damage that is immune to the werewolf's improved healing abilities. Even without an instant kill, the werewolf might not want to risk a continued encounter where more aggravated damage and death is even a possibility. A draw is as good as a victory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How much damage does an aggravated spell do pray tell?<br /> Werewolves have a bunch of options to negate damage that might make even that unreliable depending on how you rule certain things. Plenty of Gifts and merits give armor and damage reduction.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T12:24:41-07:00","id":656803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656783#post656783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Moving on from Werewolf versus Mage, you know what I think is probably worse for a Hunter to face than a pack or cabal?<br /> <br /> A pack/cabal made up of Mages <i>and Werewolves</i>.<br /> I mean, really, think about it. Monster mashes give up a whole lot of their specialization in a particular field, but they get plenty of reach and flexibility to make up for it. They're harder to counter as different members would have different weaknesses on top of having a wider variety of powers with less overlap.<br /> <br /> Using MMO analogies, Werewolves would Tank in a manner similar to WoW Paladins and Warriors. Mages... would be mages and clerics.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Hunter cells are not careful and judicious in a given area, I can certainly envision a scenario where the local supernatural community bands together to eliminate their pesky &quot;Hunter problem.&quot;<br /> <br /> Such a scenario, while likely quite rare and short-lived, should pose a terminal problem for even Tier 3 Hunters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656783#post656783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How much damage does an aggravated spell do pray tell?<br /> Werewolves have a bunch of options to negate damage that might make even that unreliable depending on how you rule certain things. Plenty of Gifts and merits give armor and damage reduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the 2e previews, mages now have a number of means that inflict set amounts of damage, often aggravated with the expenditure of Reach and mana, that bypass Defense and armor. However, all the relevant rules have not yet been fully revealed, particularly if other supernaturals would have a means to counter such attacks.<br /> <br /> As Dave has repeatedly explained, these types of attacks are normally extremely inefficient or just plain overkill in most situations, but when a angry lycanthrope is charging at you in a bar, mana conservation, Paradox risk, and gratuitous gore are clearly not the mage's greatest concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T12:36:19-07:00","id":656809,"title":"","content":"Wait, if energy is conserved in this and the mage's mass is -&gt;0 then they're going to end up going at the speed of light because KE = 1/2 mv^2, so as m-&gt; 0 V-&gt; infinity.<br /> <br /> And god help you if the &quot;mage's mass stays at 0&quot; thing also applies to relativistic mass. You'll end up knocked into last week. Literally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:02:51-07:00","id":656838,"title":"","content":"Well, Berserker's Might doesn't count as Defense or Armor. It's just &quot;once per turn and for 1 Essence, treat a single source of damage as being reduced by Glory&quot;. As it doesn't describe any criteria for what is or not affect by the attack, I think this applies to any form of damage, whether it be falling, explosives, silver bullets, or magic attacks.<br /> So, assuming said werewolf had around 3-4 dots in Glory, the Mage's spell would be treated as if it were 3-4 damage weaker even if it ignores all armor and defense.<br /> <br /> Of course, not every wolf gets Berserker's Might, but it'd certainly make the direct option to killing a werewolf much harder. Even if we low ball it every Gauru form werewolf has double digit HP. So, I really doubt you could one shot said werewolf without dice exploding.<br /> <br /> Although yeah, I think whoever wins in that fight probably has to wait a few weeks recovering as both sides can deal agg to each other. IF they can't see healers at all that is.<br /> <br /> <br /> And Bran, we don't need to include all the supernaturals in a city to break a hunter cell.<br /> <br /> Consider all of the combos due to the teamwork provided by a mixed group. Let me put an example.<br /> Mage uses Time magic to at the first sign of combat give their most agile characters extra initiative. Werewolf character in the same group activates Pack Triumphs Together at the first sign of combat, causing everyone to act at the highest rolled initative on their side. Because of the Mage's buff and a lucky roll, EVERYONE in the pack is treated as though they had an initiative of 20, meaning, they ALL get to go first... even though they were ambushed.<br /> <br /> And that's without me really thinking of how to break the game with mixed splat combos. <br /> <br /> Hunters would be hard pressed to beat that combo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 09-08-2015, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:33:53-07:00","id":656859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656838#post656838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Bran, we don't need to include all the supernaturals in a city to break a hunter cell.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the discussion starts to consider <i>groups</i> of supernaturals, whether of the same template or mixed, it changes the entire discussion, and the Hunters, Sleepers or otherwise, will likely suffer substantially greater disadvantages than the often discussed one-on-one battles or small groups of Hunters vs. a single supernatural. Once teamwork, Hunter's greatest asset, is essentially equalized, absent <i>substantial</i> might, primarily supernatural, the Hunters will generally be doomed.<br /> <br /> A battle between an experienced werewolf pack and Awakened cabal, however, would be much less certain, although the various permutations would be near limitless. (If it occurred in our hypothetical bar, regardless of who won, the bar would likely be little more than ash and splinters by the end of the battle). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T14:16:01-07:00","id":656919,"title":"","content":"<i>Acceleration</i>, the spell, makes the subject always go first, too, or delay to reflexively interrupt anyone else then go back to first next turn. Although we do helpfully point out that if more than one person in a combat has an &quot;I go first&quot; effect (like a Time mage and a vampire with Celerity), you Clash of Wills it.<br /> <br /> An adept (so, four dots in an arcanum) can do aggravated damage to a target equal to Potency with no recourse, no resistance, and no allowance for being a supernatural creature. the only limit would be how many dice penalties the mage could take off her spellcasting pool while only using the one yantra she's allowed in a single turn of casting. It will do 4 aggravated wounds, each additional wound will reduce the mage's pool by 2. Against a hunter? probably a dead hunter, though the circumstances will probably invoke Paradox (that adept would only have one free Reach, so will be eating paradox dice for casting the spell instantly, for casting it at range, and for making the damage aggravated. That all adds up). But, as I say - most likely one dead hunter and one mage with some resistant bashing damage from absorbing the paradox.<br /> <br /> Against a Werewolf, though, it only works <i>as long as they aren't transformed</i>. Once a werewolf takes war form, they a) have an unexpectedly high number of Health dots and b) are no longer Size 5, so the mage has to take <i>more</i> dice penalties to cast on them to start with. They'll still do <i>lots</i> of agg, more than almost any other supernatural being is able to throw out, but it probably won't kill the werewolf.<br /> <br /> And the werewolf, already in war form, will immediately flip out into Death-Rage when they take those aggravated wounds. The mage will enjoy the moral victory of having hurt her foe badly, before her spleen goes on vacation elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T14:25:31-07:00","id":656927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656919#post656919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Acceleration</i>, the spell, makes the subject always go first, too, or delay to reflexively interrupt anyone else then go back to first next turn. Although we do helpfully point out that if more than one person in a combat has an &quot;I go first&quot; effect (like a Time mage and a vampire with Celerity), you Clash of Wills it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that's interesting, I don't think I've seen a Forces spell mess with Initiative like that before. If it's still a Forces spell, that is.<br /> <br /> Edit: Doh! I was wrong, it was a Time spell, of course. Gah, faulty memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":1018,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","user":"Ophidimancer","date":". 09-08-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:00:45-07:00","id":656969,"title":"","content":"Acceleration? No, it's Time 3 spell.<br /> <br /> If the mage knows she's fighting werewolves and has Spirit 2, she can Clash of Wills whenever someone uses a Gift on her, as well.<br /> <br /> Now, if the mage in our increasingly-unlikely scenario is a <i>master</i> (of any Arcanum)... Well... That's like the aggravated-damage adept scenario only more so. Instead of doing levels of damage, a master can Unmake or Make her Arcanum in the subject's pattern in fatal ways - if it's a Forces mage you're after, we'll say Unmaking Forces to remove all electrical activity from the poor sob that pissed off someone who lists &quot;mastery of the universes' fundamental energies&quot; on her resume.<br /> <br /> Unlike doing health boxes of damage, this one's actually withstood. Her Potency will be reduced, assuming she casts successfully to start with, by the subject's Stamina. If she has <i>any</i> successes left, the subject dies. Instantly. No matter how much health he has. Her Potency <i>starts</i> at 5, so she would instantly slay all but Olympic athletes, but we'll be generous and assume the person fighting her knows what she is so is going to spend willpower and raise his passive resistance to, say, 6 (assuming he had stamina 4). That's still only -2 dice, though, against a character who has a base dice pool of <i>at least</i> 10, and will probably be spending willpower herself on top of whatever the one yantra she's allowed in a single-turn spell uses. The Paradox will be about the same as the adept, but her foes' chance of survival is a lot slimmer. As with all passive resistances, Withstood spells do not give you more resistance for having a Supernatural Tolerance Trait. All that matters is your Stamina, give or take a +2 for burning Willpower.<br /> <br /> As before, however, if the werewolf's in war form he's probably got a superhuman Stamina, and like the adept she'll be bleeding dice to account for his massive size. If so, and the master casts her death spell but didn't build a potency high enough... Nothing happens. And then the werewolf kills her.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:05:40-07:00","id":656972,"title":"","content":"I never knew size mattered so much for mages.<br /> <br /> It was fun figuring how my PC turns from a 5'10 152 pound twig to and 8'9, 500 pound hulk, but outside of the immediate changes to the form I didn't think it would make much difference.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, only object-affecting abilities, in werewolf, are impacted by size.<br /> <br /> So is mage magic 'standardized' at the size of the mage?<br /> <br /> And as an aside, their contact with the Supernal, which I think they use to bring their Truths to the world, does that work via a sort of portal between them and the Supernal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-08-2015, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:07:40-07:00","id":656980,"title":"","content":"That's properly terrifying to hear. So a Time Master could, for instance, entirely unmake the temporal flows within the Werewolf, leaving it stuck out of time for a few minutes? Though, I'd think the practical option would be to shuffle their ass back in time on turn one to a point where they can prepare slightly better for the forthcoming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:21:52-07:00","id":657009,"title":"","content":"It would be easier for her to kill everyone in the bar. <br /> <br /> Except that she's <i>in</i> the bar, and she's not got time to sort out a target exemption.<br /> <br /> A Time Master would probably not be in the fight to start with. And if she found herself accidentally in the fight, she'll have suddenly made different choices in the hours leading up to the fight that meant she wasn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:22:20-07:00","id":657011,"title":"","content":"So... maybe Vehicular options are more reliable than I thought in a Hunters Vs Mage struggle? What's the justification given for size being a spell factor fluff wise that is?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, based on the details given, the instakill mechanics for some reason sound like they work better against other mages than other supernaturals, specifically, the more monstrous kinds of beings. I'm assuming there's a defense against that in MvM conflicts via Clash of Wills?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:24:59-07:00","id":657017,"title":"","content":"Mages have Clash of Wills mechanics coming out of their pointy hats, as long as they've remembered to set them up. They can Clash <i>anything</i> with the right spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:29:26-07:00","id":657021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657017#post657017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages have Clash of Wills mechanics coming out of their pointy hats, as long as they've remembered to set them up. They can Clash <i>anything</i> with the right spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it, so that probably deters rocket tag save or die, then? Well, from the instagib spells that is.<br /> <br /> Am I right in assuming that once your target starts stacking on superhuman Stamina, like say +6, the Make and Unmake spells start being less effective?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:31:39-07:00","id":657023,"title":"","content":"It means the mage's inherent Potency is no longer sufficient to go over their Stamina. They will have to take dice penalties to make it high enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:37:32-07:00","id":657035,"title":"","content":"At the levels needed to cast Un/Making spells, assuming you're casting it as a rote, anything above ~12 Stamina probably becomes really hard to pull off in a single turn. At least that's what I'd guess based off of spoiled information. <br /> <br /> Though here's a question, are the Un/Making spells all resisted by Stamina or could things like the Mind or Fate versions require stats like Resolve or Composure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:37:58-07:00","id":657038,"title":"","content":"They could indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:40:18-07:00","id":657044,"title":"","content":"For the sake of the white room, we must ignore rotes. If the master has her instant-death spell as a rote, then she's re-rolling failures on the spellcasting roll. <br /> <br /> And if she gets an exceptional success, one of the things she can do is remove the Withstood property of the spell. In which case, our increasingly-beleaguered Werewolf is simply shit out of luck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:44:42-07:00","id":657049,"title":"","content":"One has to wonder what a person is doing frequently enough to warrant having a instant-death rote, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:44:52-07:00","id":657050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657044#post657044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the sake of the white room, we must ignore rotes. If the master has her instant-death spell as a rote, then she's re-rolling failures on the spellcasting roll.<br /> <br /> And if she gets an exceptional success, one of the things she can do is remove the Withstood property of the spell. In which case, our increasingly-beleaguered Werewolf is simply shit out of luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see! Well, Masters are seeming to get scarier the more I know about them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657049#post657049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One has to wonder what a person is doing frequently enough to warrant having a instant-death rote, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You never know when you need to strike someone down, and as everyone knows, overkill is best kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-08-2015, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:48:17-07:00","id":657055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657049#post657049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One has to wonder what a person is doing frequently enough to warrant having a instant-death rote, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a white-room combat, Arc, sanity has no place here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:50:44-07:00","id":657068,"title":"","content":"You can see why it becomes difficult to maintain a high Wisdom when you hit mastery. Not because of any specific mechanical effect of having high Arcana, but because mages at that level wield power that even gods could envy. With such power, when the temptations are great, your Obsessions drive you to enforce your will on the world, and not much can stop you, what keeps you from doing whatever you want?<br /> <br /> The answer is &quot;Nothing. Nothing at all.&quot; If martial artists earn the discipline to not kill with their bare hands even after they've gained that power, what discipline must it require when you can <i>strike an embodiment of universal force from existence</i>? You can conjure cars, computers, riches beyond the imagination from <i>nothing</i>. You can create life, minds, or rip them from their very moorings in this universe and <i>unmake </i>them, or send them to far-flung realms. Time itself becomes a playground for the Master of Time. For the Master of Mind, an entire world of thinking beings is within her grasp. Power? No Sleeper knows true Awakened power. The world's most powerful leaders know nothing of the sort. An assassin kills a target. A supernatural monster eviscerates a target. A Time Master can shatter that target's history or cast it through time into the future. The Master of Space creates not barriers but instead <i>rips you from space entirely</i>, leaving you unable to interact with the world from which you were removed.<br /> <br /> There is power, and then there is magic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:51:55-07:00","id":657069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657055#post657055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a white-room combat, Arc, sanity has no place here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah; so the white room is padded\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:54:01-07:00","id":657071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657055#post657055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a white-room combat, Arc, sanity has no place here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>ACK, NO! Once you walk into a white-room, you can never leave! Must break it with more logical questions before I lose all my Integrity again!<br /> *rolls Intelligence+Wits to think up logical questions, fails*<br /> <br /> GAAAAH!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:55:26-07:00","id":657072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657069#post657069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah; so the white room is padded\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Who needs sanity when you've got magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:58:50-07:00","id":657074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657072#post657072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who needs sanity when you've got magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would someone want to play a magical serial killer when there's so many better things you can be doing with magic?!<br /> <br /> *Can feel a part of his brain casually frying*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:01:21-07:00","id":657078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657072#post657072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who needs sanity when you've got magic?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Famous Last Words, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, barring intervention from higher powers, yeah, no Hunter is touching a Master without really extraordinary circumstances. Maxed out Supernaturals vs each other is a game where all manner of factors and dice rolls can affect the outcome in major ways. For Hunter, the game has to be rigged into their favor to counteract the fact that every other player at the Monopoly board owns every other building at high development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:01:48-07:00","id":657080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657074#post657074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would someone want to play a magical serial killer when there's so many better things you can be doing with magic?!<br /> <br /> *Can feel a part of his brain casually frying*</div> </div> </div> </div>And who says that being a magical serial killer and all of those better things are mutually exclusive? Why can't we have our cake and stab it too?<br /> <br /> And speaking of general left-handedness, I'm not sure if this would have made it into the new core at all, but can mages still willingly taint their own spells with the Abyss to gain a boost in power? If so, will we get new rules for it in the 2e core and if not do you think it would work about the same way as it did in 1e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 09-08-2015, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:07:31-07:00","id":657241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657044#post657044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the sake of the white room, we must ignore rotes. If the master has her instant-death spell as a rote, then she's re-rolling failures on the spellcasting roll.<br /> <br /> And if she gets an exceptional success, one of the things she can do is remove the Withstood property of the spell. In which case, our increasingly-beleaguered Werewolf is simply shit out of luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a question I've had since I saw your post over at rpg.net with the guy casting Fate spells on that mob boss (though I'm pretty sure I have the answer): does Supernatural Tolerance factor in to spells being Withstood? I rather like the idea of an Elder Vampire being harder to Unmake by Master of Death than a newly embraced Vampire, but I get the impression that if Supernatural Tolerance factored in then your have mentioned it in the past few posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","user":"Enokh","date":".  autocorrect is the devil 09-08-2015, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:19:26-07:00","id":657247,"title":"","content":"Think that was covered <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/590098-2ed-potency-and-withstanding-spells?p=590176#post590176\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:19:48-07:00","id":657248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657241#post657241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually a question I've had since I saw your post over at rpg.net with the guy casting Fate spells on that mob boss (though I'm pretty sure I have the answer): does Supernatural Tolerance factor in to spells being Withstood? I rather like the idea of an Elder Vampire being harder to Unmake by Master of Death than a newly embraced Vampire, but I get the impressing that if Supernatural Tolerance factored in then your have mentioned it in the past few posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is &quot;no, supernatural tolerance does not apply&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656969#post656969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with all passive resistances, Withstood spells do not give you more resistance for having a Supernatural Tolerance Trait. All that matters is your Stamina, give or take a +2 for burning Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:27:37-07:00","id":657254,"title":"","content":"Well look at me, both being right yet not noticing the thread that answers my question.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, thanks for the replies and the links/quotes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:36:37-07:00","id":657264,"title":"","content":"And if that really bugged you (it doesn't at all bother me, but I could see it bothering some folks, or being problematic in crossover play), here's a quick house rule for you: use the supernatural being's Tolerance Trait as its Withstand trait, or the usual Withstand trait, whichever is higher. This still gives more potent supernatural beings a better chance at resisting, though it may be unnecessary\u2014chances are, higher Supernatural Tolerance means higher Attributes anyway, but just in case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:53:22-07:00","id":657273,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the only problem I'd have with it is for crossover play and crossover games are surprisingly common in my gaming group. Within Mage itself it seems perfectly fine. I actually very much like the idea of Withstood effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:59:00-07:00","id":657280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657009#post657009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be easier for her to kill everyone in the bar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe some would consider that a feature, not a bug.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657055#post657055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a white-room combat, Arc, sanity has no place here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, &quot;this is the <i>World of Darkness</i>, sanity has no place here.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657071#post657071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ACK, NO! Once you walk into a white-room, you can never leave! Must break it with more logical questions before I lose all my Integrity again!<br /> *rolls Intelligence+Wits to think up logical questions, fails*</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe you confusing the &quot;white room&quot; with the &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cube_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">white cube</a>&quot; or hypercube. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657049#post657049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One has to wonder what a person is doing frequently enough to warrant having a instant-death rote, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to know what self-respecting Master of reality wouldn't have <i>at least</i> one instant-death rote. Of all people (to the extent you can really still call them people), they know exactly the dangers that pursing the Mysteries entails, and the necessity of both preparation and overwhelming force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-08-2015, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T19:05:24-07:00","id":657283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657068#post657068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can see why it becomes difficult to maintain a high Wisdom when you hit mastery. Not because of any specific mechanical effect of having high Arcana, but because mages at that level wield power that even gods could envy. With such power, when the temptations are great, your Obsessions drive you to enforce your will on the world, and not much can stop you, what keeps you from doing whatever you want?<br /> <br /> The answer is &quot;Nothing. Nothing at all.&quot; If martial artists earn the discipline to not kill with their bare hands even after they've gained that power, what discipline must it require when you can <i>strike an embodiment of universal force from existence</i>? You can conjure cars, computers, riches beyond the imagination from <i>nothing</i>. You can create life, minds, or rip them from their very moorings in this universe and <i>unmake </i>them, or send them to far-flung realms. Time itself becomes a playground for the Master of Time. For the Master of Mind, an entire world of thinking beings is within her grasp. Power? No Sleeper knows true Awakened power. The world's most powerful leaders know nothing of the sort. An assassin kills a target. A supernatural monster eviscerates a target. A Time Master can shatter that target's history or cast it through time into the future. The Master of Space creates not barriers but instead <i>rips you from space entirely</i>, leaving you unable to interact with the world from which you were removed.<br /> <br /> There is power, and then there is magic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds deliciously sociopathic, inhuman and monstrous. If the entirety of Mage 2e fully conveys this mood and is truly backed by the new mechanics, I have no doubt the book will exceed our already high expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T19:48:07-07:00","id":657306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657283#post657283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds deliciously sociopathic, inhuman and monstrous. If the entirety of Mage 2e fully conveys this mood and is truly backed by the new mechanics, I have no doubt the book will exceed our already high expectations.</div> </div> </div> </div>People have often asked &quot;Is <b>Mage </b>a horror game?&quot; Yes. It always has been. 1E did it, too, but 2E's changes help reinforce that, in my opinion. The horror of <b>Mage </b>is a slow-burn kind, the slide into decadence as far removed from the life of the average person as is the life of a blood-drinking immortal, or a lupine lycanthrope. Where you realize that you've become the thing you hated, working your fingers to the bone for a heartless tyrant of the office\u2014a creature only concerned with his own influence, his own well-being, using others like puppets to serve his own ends. You'd have done anything then to keep your family fed. Now you've all but lost contact with the ex and your kid. You use people for what little you need from them, heedless of their petty little lives and petty little concerns. Of what importance is a struggle to make ends meet when you grapple with the secrets of the universe? It's easy to forget where you came from when you literally wield the power of a god.<br /> <br /> Not that <b>Mage </b>is solely a game of horror, or that every master becomes an uncaring asshole. But the potential is there. The sheer power in what you can do distances you from mortal life just as much as the Embrace, the First Change, whatever. So yes, you could use <b>Mage </b>for that, and yes, it will exceed your expectations. This thing is a work of beauty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T20:21:04-07:00","id":657316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657306#post657306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People have often asked &quot;Is <b>Mage </b>a horror game?&quot; Yes. It always has been. 1E did it, too, but 2E's changes help reinforce that, in my opinion. The horror of <b>Mage </b>is a slow-burn kind, the slide into decadence as far removed from the life of the average person as is the life of a blood-drinking immortal, or a lupine lycanthrope. Where you realize that you've become the thing you hated, working your fingers to the bone for a heartless tyrant of the office\u2014a creature only concerned with his own influence, his own well-being, using others like puppets to serve his own ends. You'd have done anything then to keep your family fed. <b>Now you've all but lost contact with the ex and your kid. You use people for what little you need from them, heedless of their petty little lives and petty little concerns. Of what importance is a struggle to make ends meet when you grapple with the secrets of the universe?</b> It's easy to forget where you came from when you literally wield the power of a god.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655965#post655965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a Seer of the Throne beholden to Dave, my Exarch master. I'll not part the veil of the Lie unless he deems it so!</div> </div> </div> </div>I never before fully appreciated how well you and Dave immersed yourselves in the (evil? hubristic? scary?) Awakened mage state of mind. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> More seriously, I believe one of the primary problems with Mage 1e was that the same themes were mostly portrayed as now, but the mechanics didn't really back the purported power mages claimed to possess. The 2e spoilers and other tidbits, particularly some of the revised Arcanum and retooled spellcasting system (I will not miss covert vs. vulgar!), look like they should hopefully address some of the prior edition's deficiencies.<br /> <br /> And, master mages really seem f@ckin' frightening! Compared to them, human Sleepers just seem so very...<i> small</i>. <br /> <br /> I cannot even imagine what Dave has in store for 2e Archmages, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T21:00:48-07:00","id":657356,"title":"","content":"Archmages, if they need a book in 2e, probably are best left for a supplement somewhere down the line.<br /> <br /> More important books are neccesary first; especially revisions on the Order and Seer books, supplements providing Legacies, and datasheets involving uses for Arcanum and ways the Abyss can screw over with the world. Possibly Crossover and Setting books too.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm certain that some of us have their own feelings on if we really need books of archmastery level mages, but objectively, other books need to be released before that becomes an option. <br /> <br /> Hm, reminds me of those attempts at providing a Hunter T4 setup. Don't think hat's possible without some degree of I don't know, transhumanism?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T21:37:26-07:00","id":657372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657280#post657280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe you confusing the &quot;white room&quot; with the &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cube_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">white cube</a>&quot; or hypercube. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I want to know what self-respecting Master of reality wouldn't have <i>at least</i> one instant-death rote. Of all people (to the extent you can really still call them people), they know exactly the dangers that pursing the Mysteries entails, and the necessity of both preparation and overwhelming force.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Is there a difference?<br /> <br /> 2) I'm not suggesting masters are all together, nor am I suggesting that masters would assume a sunshine and fluffy bunnies approach will always work.<br /> <br /> But a rote is not just a thing you create. If simply using a spell designed for murder requires some fucked up intent that can do the wrong way indulged in too much, what does that say about making a rote?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T22:38:10-07:00","id":657415,"title":"","content":"So, quick question, and I apologize if this has been addressed elsewhere: If you're using a spell that's withstood by stamina on a vampire, and that vampire has Resilience (which adds directly to stamina), would the combined stamina+resilience value be used for the spell, or is it the attribute alone that's counted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/671-the-lone-gunman","name":"The Lone Gunman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T22:45:12-07:00","id":657420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lone Gunman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657415#post657415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, quick question, and I apologize if this has been addressed elsewhere: If you're using a spell that's withstood by stamina on a vampire, and that vampire has Resilience (which adds directly to stamina), would the combined stamina+resilience value be used for the spell, or is it the attribute alone that's counted?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know, but probably the combined since it says to add the Resilience dots directly to Stamina and then states it may raise Stamina above the normal limits for Blood Potency; if it didn't actually modify the Stamina itself the second part wouldn't be needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T23:20:26-07:00","id":657429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lone Gunman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657415#post657415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, quick question, and I apologize if this has been addressed elsewhere: If you're using a spell that's withstood by stamina on a vampire, and that vampire has Resilience (which adds directly to stamina), would the combined stamina+resilience value be used for the spell, or is it the attribute alone that's counted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely. Resilience modifies the vampire's actual Stamina trait; it'd be the same case as if you had buffed a target's Stamina with a Life spell, only the Resilience is always active. Further, they can spend Vitae to increase their Withstand rating, unless Dave or Rose think otherwise. I say that because of this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vampire: The Requiem Second Edition, p. 91</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Vitae, any Kindred can accomplish massive bursts of physical prowess. By spending a point of Vitae, he may add two dice to rolls involving his choice of Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina for the turn. This does not increase traits derived from these Attributes. <b>However, it will increase relevant resistances.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I bring it up at all is that you could read the bolded bit as being equivalent to spending Willpower to boost a Resistance trait. I know that because I specifically brought it up during development; by 1E rules-as-written, spending Vitae to strengthen you in, say, a grapple, would only work when you were actively rolling\u2014it was useless when resisting. Well, that doesn't make any sense. So I know that the passage I highlighted specifically calls out that you can boost resistance traits with Vitae. Can you do it against magic? Well, it doesn't say you can't, and vampires use hostile magic on one another all the time, so....<br /> <br /> I believe the rules as intended would allow vampires to boost their Withstand ratings by spending Willpower <i>and </i>Vitae. The Kindred can be remarkably resilient, which fits well enough to me. Of course, groups are encouraged to discuss how they want to handle this in their own games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T23:57:37-07:00","id":657458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657429#post657429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, absolutely. Resilience modifies the vampire's actual Stamina trait; it'd be the same case as if you had buffed a target's Stamina with a Life spell, only the Resilience is always active. Further, they can spend Vitae to increase their Withstand rating, unless Dave or Rose think otherwise. I say that because of this:<br /> <br /> Originally posted by Vampire: The Requiem Second Edition, p. 91<br /> With Vitae, any Kindred can accomplish massive bursts of physical prowess. By spending a point of Vitae, he may add two dice to rolls involving his choice of Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina for the turn. This does not increase traits derived from these Attributes. However, it will increase relevant resistances.<br /> <br /> <br /> The reason I bring it up at all is that you could read the bolded bit as being equivalent to spending Willpower to boost a Resistance trait. I know that because I specifically brought it up during development; by 1E rules-as-written, spending Vitae to strengthen you in, say, a grapple, would only work when you were actively rolling\u2014it was useless when resisting. Well, that doesn't make any sense. So I know that the passage I highlighted specifically calls out that you can boost resistance traits with Vitae. Can you do it against magic? Well, it doesn't say you can't, and vampires use hostile magic on one another all the time, so....<br /> <br /> I believe the rules as intended would allow vampires to boost their Withstand ratings by spending Willpower <i>and </i>Vitae. The Kindred can be remarkably resilient, which fits well enough to me. Of course, groups are encouraged to discuss how they want to handle this in their own games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like p. 91 was phrased that way to prevent players from using Vitae to create two extra temporary health levels every turn. Unless Exarch Dave or Rose rules differently, or a specific spell has an unusually potent effect on vampires (e.g., possibly some Forces or Death practices?), I would agree that Resilience, as well as the &quot;Physical Intensity&quot; mechanic from V:tR 2e, p 91, would raise a vampire's stamina to Withstand relevant spell effects.<br /> <br /> Heck, Vampires are immortal, undead, blood-sucking monstrosities. They <i>should</i> be damn difficult to permanently put down. Mages simply need to be creative when dispatching such wretched abominations. Sunlight and fire spells are also highly recommended. There also should be more than sufficient non-Withstood (against stamina) spells than can be effectively deployed against the fiends.<br /> <br /> Edit: Does our friendly bar-hopping Obrimos Arrow need to &quot;have words&quot; with some arrogant Venture when he's done with the werewolf? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-09-2015, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T00:46:58-07:00","id":657494,"title":"","content":"Vamps also get +Blood potency to resistances while in frenzy, which should hopefully count. I do like the awesomeness of the power here for mages - that each Master has an obliteration spell at the ready - and the only barrier to using it is *politeness* - it brings the horror of the setting to the fore. Why not kill your wife's lover? Heck, int' she guilty too? Aint like nobody will miss someone who *never existed*. Almost like you never killed anyone at all...<br /> <br /> However, I also want an occasional shift at horror in the other direction; not just &quot;look what I have done&quot; but also &quot;shitohshitohshitthere's-a-fucking-monster-coming-for-me.&quot; I want there to be some threats that aren't put-downable with a single roll. It sounds like creatures from the abyss and lower depths may provide this (as will any more convuluted mystery). Having a vampire in frenzy crashing through the barroom and resisting your first couple of spells as she flings herself at you will keep the edge of threat in the narrative present as well as in the cosmic backdrop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T01:54:57-07:00","id":657547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Lone Gunman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657415#post657415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, quick question, and I apologize if this has been addressed elsewhere: If you're using a spell that's withstood by stamina on a vampire, and that vampire has Resilience (which adds directly to stamina), would the combined stamina+resilience value be used for the spell, or is it the attribute alone that's counted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking your Stamina off Withstood spell's Potency is not a derived trait, but a function of Stamina - resiliance is written the way it is so that vampires don't add it to their Health dots.<br /> <br /> So yes, vampires would add it to Stamina for withstanding stamina-withstood spells. Similar with mummies burning Pillars, werewolves changing form, mages buffing Attributes, etc. Given that you don't get to add a Power Stat on, it's only fair - and supernatural means of boosting your attributes become very, very important when fighting mages.<br /> <br /> Problem is, can you boost them all? And can the mage come up with a way to kill you that ignores what you're good at to hit your weakness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T02:03:34-07:00","id":657553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657547#post657547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Taking your Stamina off Withstood spell's Potency is not a derived trait, but a function of Stamina - resiliance is written the way it is so that vampires don't add it to their Health dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't Resilience actually increase a vampire's Stamina, and hence his Health (V:tR,2e, p.141)? I believe you meant that using &quot;Physical Intensity&quot; (V:tR,2e, p.91) to increase Stamina dice rolls and resistances doesn't increase Health because it's a derived trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T02:33:11-07:00","id":657567,"title":"","content":"Also - I thought the vamp/wolf/mummy etc would have to know that the spell was coming. Which they wouldn't without some special ability to sense magic. <br /> <br /> Fun tactical shifts all around. The battlefield of resistances/supernatural tolerances is changed thus - perhaps devaluing the definition of the term &quot;Supernatural tolerance&quot; - but the repercussions for mage are quite delicious. <br /> <br /> It seems on paper that each splat could win - albeit, by going for a tactical strike out of stealth. If your enemy gets the drop on you, its most likely nuts for you. Wouldn't a car-bomb finish most mages, if they didn't see it coming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T02:46:17-07:00","id":657573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657567#post657567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also - I thought the vamp/wolf/mummy etc would have to know that the spell was coming. Which they wouldn't without some special ability to sense magic.<br /> <br /> Fun tactical shifts all around. The battlefield of resistances/supernatural tolerances is changed thus - perhaps devaluing the definition of the term &quot;Supernatural tolerance&quot; - but the repercussions for mage are quite delicious.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you even suspect someone's a mage, and they just might be looking at you, a good rule of thumb is to buff early and often, then leave immediately .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657567#post657567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems on paper that each splat could win - albeit, by going for a tactical strike out of stealth. If your enemy gets the drop on you, its most likely nuts for you. Wouldn't a car-bomb finish most mages, if they didn't see it coming?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fist, there's no stealth or car bombs in the &quot;white room.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More importantly, although mages are hardly omniscient, they do have ample means to help avoid surprises. Most of the Time and Fate Arcanum are useful in this regard, and most other Arcanca can passively enhance a mage's senses to help avoid ambushes and traps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-09-2015, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T02:47:54-07:00","id":657574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657567#post657567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also - I thought the vamp/wolf/mummy etc would have to know that the spell was coming. Which they wouldn't without some special ability to sense magic.<br /> <br /> Fun tactical shifts all around. The battlefield of resistances/supernatural tolerances is changed thus - perhaps devaluing the definition of the term &quot;Supernatural tolerance&quot; - but the repercussions for mage are quite delicious.<br /> <br /> It seems on paper that each splat could win - albeit, by going for a tactical strike out of stealth. If your enemy gets the drop on you, its most likely nuts for you. Wouldn't a car-bomb finish most mages, if they didn't see it coming?</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking mages out in a single surprise attack is typically the best way to deal with, and yes, car bombs should typically work wonderfully when dealing with a mage. Unless they just happened to have some sort of defense up at the time they're just a normal human. Now if other mages have been dying to crap lately paranoia kicks in and things start to get substantially harder as they <i>do</i> start to prep for these things, but as long as you don't do anything to spook them (and they aren't already really paranoid) it really isn't that hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T04:25:48-07:00","id":657637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=655749#post655749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are talking about the default setting, where a totem is not a requirement of a pack. It's a fine houserule if you want to run with it, but has no bearing on the conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware, the totem <b>is </b>a requirement for a pack. It's the thing that binds them spiritually. I've done a cursory scan thru the book and nothing specifies it isn't required. Otherwise? Anything could be a pack, with, or without Uratha involved.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T04:42:02-07:00","id":657646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=656002#post656002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot at play here. And as nofather mentioned (and I mentioned before him), Incite Fury is kind of a nasty move. If it works, the mage goes berserk and will have a hard time casting any spells. She'll have to make a Resolve + Composure roll to do anything other than attack with any weapons at hand, and even if she succeeds suffers a -3 to all actions other than attacking the nearest target. That puts a hurt on the game plan right there.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm wondering is how mages interact with the Rahu Hunter aspect. Do they neglect casting in such a situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T04:56:34-07:00","id":657651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657637#post657637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I'm aware, the totem <b>is </b>a requirement for a pack. It's the thing that binds them spiritually. I've done a cursory scan thru the book and nothing specifies it isn't required. Otherwise? Anything could be a pack, with, or without Uratha involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>A totem is an important member of a pack, but not a necessary one. They're there to help give the werewolves a representative in the Hisil. If you have a problem with a hunter compact of wolf-blooded forming packs, you can make it a lodge and give them a lodge totem, but as you noted there's no rule about totems being a requirement for packs. Which is a good thing, considering totems can die and you suddenly don't stop caring as much about your cousin, and not all werewolf players want to get involved with the spirit aspect of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657646#post657646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm wondering is how mages interact with the Rahu Hunter aspect. Do they neglect casting in such a situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah, good point. There goes preptime. But if the mage is one who puts on armor and defensive spells every day as part of their normal routine they still do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-09-2015, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T04:58:18-07:00","id":657654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657074#post657074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would someone want to play a magical serial killer when there's so many better things you can be doing with magic?!<br /> <br /> *Can feel a part of his brain casually frying*</div> </div> </div> </div>Banishers come to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T07:39:53-07:00","id":657878,"title":"","content":"Speaking of paranoia, given the way things seem to be going, I would expect everything to gang up on ever Mage they can find after the first one went nuclear, resulting in a sort of Mage exile. Vampires and Werewolves are some of the most fractious cannibalistic beings, but they would set aside differences among themselves and each other in a war against Mages. I guess that fits the isolation theme. Mage society would make it clear if you mess with other nasties, you're on your own. Anything likely to come into conflict with a Mage has a huge number advantage as they can replenish their numbers much easier than Mages. Mummy doesn't count since that game was designed to be crossover unfriendly. Seems like all the talk is white room. A Mage would find a peaceful solution or face the consequences, death or finding some way to appease the other side or running and hiding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:00:47-07:00","id":657891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657878#post657878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage society would make it clear if you mess with other nasties, you're on your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Adamantine Arrow would explicitly disagree, as would the Silver Ladder.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T08:06:24-07:00","id":657895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657878#post657878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like all the talk is white room. A Mage would find a peaceful solution or face the consequences, death or finding some way to appease the other side or running and hiding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throughout the fiction, a running theme with mages is them involving themselves in things without concern for a larger picture, or much in the way of self-awareness. In the Danse Macabre, for instance, Prince Maxwell managed to find a mage willing to help him steal the secrets of the Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> They're Awakened from the Lie all the other supernatural templates are muddied up in, they seem to have as much respect for the supernatural templates as they do Sleepers. Maybe slightly more, viewing them as spiders or scorpions instead of ants. Individual perspectives may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T09:15:02-07:00","id":657984,"title":"","content":"Counterpoint - the Mage in &quot;There are no Owls in Seattle&quot; whose first words upon the vampire walking into her shop are &quot;oh shit&quot;.<br /> <br /> And who finds out what he hires her to find out. He just doesn't like the answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T09:18:34-07:00","id":657986,"title":"","content":"To be fair, my reaction to seeing a scorpion would be &quot;oh shit&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T09:20:11-07:00","id":657991,"title":"","content":"I thought she was a Second Sight character, maybe a witch. That was a good story, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T10:56:34-07:00","id":658141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657878#post657878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of paranoia, given the way things seem to be going, I would expect everything to gang up on ever Mage they can find after the first one went nuclear, resulting in a sort of Mage exile. Vampires and Werewolves are some of the most fractious cannibalistic beings, but they would set aside differences among themselves and each other in a war against Mages. I guess that fits the isolation theme. Mage society would make it clear if you mess with other nasties, you're on your own. Anything likely to come into conflict with a Mage has a huge number advantage as they can replenish their numbers much easier than Mages. Mummy doesn't count since that game was designed to be crossover unfriendly. Seems like all the talk is white room. A Mage would find a peaceful solution or face the consequences, death or finding some way to appease the other side or running and hiding.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an extremely bad idea. If the other supernaturals starting randomly ganging up on mages just because one of them did something stupid, then chances are the rest of the mages would also group up to deal with the threat to their society. Sure, one mage being killed because they did something stupid is passable, but when others start getting picked off at random for no good reason the ones responsible are going to be tracked down and taken care of. All in all the ones responsible are probably going to be given the Banisher/Reaper/Scelesti treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T12:47:20-07:00","id":658281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657991#post657991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought she was a Second Sight character, maybe a witch. That was a good story, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also didn't think the character was an Awakened. However, it doesn't really change Dave's point.<br /> <br /> An old and experienced vampire, no less the Prince of a city, is normally a significant supernatural threat to anyone, or at least a <i>very</i> big diplomatic and social inconvenience, even a mage.<br /> <br /> I like your spider and scorpion example. Although you'll likely survive an encounter with a such a dangerous insect, it's still frightening, and you might be far worse off even after it's dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  typo 09-09-2015, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:31:05-07:00","id":658332,"title":"","content":"Prince Maxwell then killed that mage and told the rest of the mages they wouldn't do anything about it because they didn't like the guy anyway. That is the problem with mages. They have no reason whatsoever to defend some idiot that goes around causing trouble. What motivation would the mages have to fight the vampires and werewolves? All they have to do is say we can kill each other or say it's finished. Mages have better things to do than fight stupid wars against others. Mages won't gang up on the others because that would require that they accept them as serious threats to each and every individual mage. Hubris would prevent that. No playing both sides. Either mages have the wisdom not to fight or the hubris to not view others as a threat as long as they won't attack en masse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:34:07-07:00","id":658337,"title":"","content":"So in regard to the general sentiment of &quot;Hunters can't hunt Mages because the Sleeping Curse prevents them from realizing Mages exist&quot;... that's not actually true, is it? I remember multiple mentions of the Orders as Mystery Cults with Sleepers in them, and Sleepers knowing that Mages are Mages, they just can't actually be physically present when obvious magic is going down for the sake of their Integrity. Is this correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:40:13-07:00","id":658346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658337#post658337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in regard to the general sentiment of &quot;Hunters can't hunt Mages because the Sleeping Curse prevents them from realizing Mages exist&quot;... that's not actually true, is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's about as far an exaggeration as one can make without tacking on additional active drawbacks to the task, yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=647120#post647120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>[\u2026U]nless you're interested in meta-narrative tricks, reenacting Memento, and a very definite uphill struggle, </b>my advice is to give Hunter player characters intended for a mage-antagonistic game the [Sleepwalker] Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:51:09-07:00","id":658352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658332#post658332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the problem with mages. They have no reason whatsoever to defend some idiot that goes around causing trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite true. The Adamantine Arrow have an ancient duty to protect mages and humans in general. The Silver Ladder might also take umbrage, considering they view all of mage kind as part of one nation and generally have a dim view of non-humans as it is. That's reason enough for many, I would say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:51:14-07:00","id":658353,"title":"","content":"How does that jive with the bit on &quot;letting Sleepers glimpse the Orders&quot; from the Orders blog, and there being a relatively lengthy segment on playing Sleepers in the new Mage Core itself, according to the Supporting Cast blog?<br /> <br /> To be more specific:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> W<span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">hat I must reiterate, though, is that the Sleeper\u2019s belief or non-belief in magic has absolutely nothing to do with whether their souls are injured by witnessing spells, and the Orders employ hundreds of staff who </span></span></span><i>know</i><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> that they work for mages, and that mages exist, but can\u2019t be allowed to actually </span></span></span><i>see</i><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> any magic for their own safety. Such is the Curse, forever cutting the Awakened off from their own species.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","user":"Juhn","date":". 09-09-2015, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:55:41-07:00","id":658358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658353#post658353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that jive with the bit on &quot;letting Sleepers glimpse the Orders&quot; from the Orders blog, and there being a relatively lengthy segment on playing Sleepers in the new Mage Core itself, according to the Supporting Cast blog?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how you'd have trouble getting that to jive, seeing as what I'm highlighting is that &quot;Hunters are prevented from realizing mages exist&quot; is an extreme stretch of the material and that Dave's expressed position in this thread is &quot;it's more difficult than most people would likely prefer to bother with&quot; rather than &quot;it's impossible.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T13:59:24-07:00","id":658360,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry, I thought you were saying the opposite of what you were saying. I'd read that as &quot;it's so difficult it's essentially impossible&quot;, rather than just &quot;it's hard, but Sleepers hunting Mages without being Sleepwalkers is not outside the bounds of credulity&quot;. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:03:45-07:00","id":658366,"title":"","content":"You can tell someone you're a mage. They can even believe you. It's just that if they see you casting magic they'll get a chunk ripped off their soul and forget about it afterwards.<br /> <br /> (The bulk of the advice for playing Sleepers in Mage 2e itself revolves around negotiating the social contract of... Well, the section's called &quot;How To Forget&quot; and the entire chapter opens with a quote from Memento, so you get the idea.)<br /> <br /> A Sleeper can even figure out that something was probably magic after the fact, but that's not remembering what actually happened - if they get their memory magically restored, they have another breaking point and then forget again.<br /> <br /> Mages move in a lot of circles mortal occultists frequent. They can perform all sorts of feats for you, as long as you don't see them do it. Someone in a Mystery Cult that's linked to the Guardians, Seers, or Silver Ladder might even know that there's people with real magical power in the world. Their soul, however, is too bound by the Abyss to let them grasp it.<br /> <br /> I actually think a game of Sleepers of the edge of mage society, knowing that they can't trust what they remember happened half the time and slowly being driven mad by their exposure to supernal magic, would be pretty neat. Of undoubtedly limited appeal, though, which is why I say to make hunters Sleepwalkers <i>unless you're interested in that kind of game</i>. What you can't do with Mage as written is have Sleeper characters who act like Sleepwalkers but increase Paradox risk. If you don't want to make hunters Sleepwalkers and you don't want that weird Nolan-esque feeling to the game, you shouldn't use the Awakened but knock up your own Witches instead.<br /> <br /> But, of course, the material on playing a Sleeper in Mage isn't necessarily aligned to the hostility of a hunter. Do you, as an Awakened character, try to tell your boyfriend what you're experiencing? If someone's badly injured, should you risk their Integrity to heal them? Many mages try to use their powers for whatever they think is Sleepers' own good, but Sleepers are incapable of giving informed consent - how far do you go in adjusting your friends, relatives, rivals' lives?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 09-09-2015, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:17:39-07:00","id":658373,"title":"","content":"I have a question about the specifics of Quiescence just to clear things up about something I was wondering since I mentioned hunters thinking a necromancer was just a guy yelling in a graveyard.<br /> <br /> Summoning ghosts and spirits, would that cause Quiescence? It is an obvious magical thing to see, and seeing ghosts and spirits can hit a normal human Sleepers Breaking Points for witnessing something traumatic or terrifying but those can be adapted to, so you can have a sleeper who 'ain't afraid of no ghost.' But then, at least in first edition, there were spells to allow for the summoning of ghosts. Would the act of summoning be considered a Supernal 'obvious act' of magic that caused Quiescence, or would it be considered a 'fallen world' magic because it dealt with a ghost?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:19:57-07:00","id":658377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658366#post658366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, of course, the material on playing a Sleeper in Mage isn't necessarily aligned to the hostility of a hunter. Do you, as an Awakened character, try to tell your boyfriend what you're experiencing? If someone's badly injured, should you risk their Integrity to heal them? Many mages try to use their powers for whatever they think is Sleepers' own good, but Sleepers are incapable of giving informed consent - how far do you go in adjusting your friends, relatives, rivals' lives?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a slippery slope from &quot;He's no good for you; I read his thoughts, he's cheating on you&quot; to &quot;No way, I'm not even going to give him a chance with you&quot; or &quot;Here are the types of guys you can date, <i>if </i>they pass my inspection.&quot; And that's just a mild slope!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:23:35-07:00","id":658379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658373#post658373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about the specifics of Quiescence just to clear things up about something I was wondering since I mentioned hunters thinking a necromancer was just a guy yelling in a graveyard.<br /> <br /> Summoning ghosts and spirits, would that cause Quiescence? It is an obvious magical thing to see, and seeing ghosts and spirits can hit a normal human Sleepers Breaking Points for witnessing something traumatic or terrifying but those can be adapted to, so you can have a sleeper who 'ain't afraid of no ghost.' But then, at least in first edition, there were spells to allow for the summoning of ghosts. Would the act of summoning be considered a Supernal 'obvious act' of magic that caused Quiescence, or would it be considered a 'fallen world' magic because it dealt with a ghost?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, when a mage casts a Vulgar spell their Nimbus flashed. If the Immediate Nimbus also responds to certain acts of magic under the &quot;On occasion, it becomes visible even to Sleeping eyes albeit in a muted, toned-down form.&quot; clause then maybe that will provoke the Sleeping Curse. Just a guess, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:24:53-07:00","id":658380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658366#post658366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can tell someone you're a mage. They can even believe you. It's just that if they see you casting magic they'll get a chunk ripped off their soul and forget about it afterwards.<br /> <br /> (The bulk of the advice for playing Sleepers in Mage 2e itself revolves around negotiating the social contract of... Well, the section's called &quot;How To Forget&quot; and the entire chapter opens with a quote from Memento, so you get the idea.)<br /> <br /> A Sleeper can even figure out that something was probably magic after the fact, but that's not remembering what actually happened - if they get their memory magically restored, they have another breaking point and then forget again.<br /> <br /> Mages move in a lot of circles mortal occultists frequent. They can perform all sorts of feats for you, as long as you don't see them do it. Someone in a Mystery Cult that's linked to the Guardians, Seers, or Silver Ladder might even know that there's people with real magical power in the world. Their soul, however, is too bound by the Abyss to let them grasp it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope we see some &quot;day in the life&quot; examples of mage culture and society and how it interacts with Sleeper society in the new Mage core or the announced supplements, including their various Sleepwalker and Sleeper associates, agents, family and friends. It would really help grok what being an Awakened mage actually means and feels like in the nWOD and reinforce the horror and alienation themes of the game, particularly their often deleterious effects on innocents, including those closest to them in the old mortal lives. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658366#post658366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think a game of Sleepers of the edge of mage society, knowing that they can't trust what they remember happened half the time and slowly being driven mad by their exposure to supernal magic, would be pretty neat. Of undoubtedly limited appeal, though, which is why I say to make hunters Sleepwalkers <i>unless you're interested in that kind of game</i>. </div> </div> </div> </div>It does sound interesting, but indeed probably limited for a game line. It seems perfect, however, for fiction, either stand-alone or included in Mage books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:40:34-07:00","id":658392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658352#post658352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not quite true. The Adamantine Arrow have an ancient duty to protect mages and humans in general. The Silver Ladder might also take umbrage, considering they view all of mage kind as part of one nation and generally have a dim view of non-humans as it is. That's reason enough for many, I would say.</div> </div> </div> </div>The other two would disagree on the reason and argue for a peaceful resolution as would the Free Council. The Seers would taken advantage and kill all the idiot mages fighting a needless war. Mages would likely have the foresight to make first contact and say we will leave you alone as long as you leave us alone. Individuals will have problems and may deal with them as they wish along with whatever allies they can muster. If a mage gets out of hand, you can let us know and <i>we</i> will deal with them. Your actually arguing the point that Mages should have destroyed themselves a long time ago. The Arrow and Ladder are held in check for precisely the reason that they would do some really dumb things without the others, which would do other dumb things or destroyed themselves if left to their own devices.<br /> <br /> There would be an uneasy peace between all that mages would be invested in. Mages would know to keep things low key. Don't go nuclear. Seek peaceful resolution. When you kill, you better not get caught. If someone gets out of bounds, they would be dealt with. There would be fights and the occasional battle, but mages would keep the peace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:50:47-07:00","id":658403,"title":"","content":"All that's quite possible, but all I was disagreeing with was your statement that &quot;Mage society would make it clear if you mess with other nasties, you're on your own.&quot; A good chunk of the Orders explicitly would have another mage's back because of their espoused values, and many of the rest would do so out of solidarity. They do have reasons to defend mages, even if they might be idiots.<br /> <br /> The way you talk about it, you make it sound like mages have no loyalty to one another at all and wouldn't bat an eye at letting another mage be killed, and I don't think that's true for all mages, or even mage society in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":1018,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","user":"Ophidimancer","date":". 09-09-2015, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:00:52-07:00","id":658429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658358#post658358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure how you'd have trouble getting that to jive, seeing as what I'm highlighting is that &quot;Hunters are prevented from realizing mages exist&quot; is an extreme stretch of the material and that Dave's expressed position in this thread is &quot;it's more difficult than most people would likely prefer to bother with&quot; rather than &quot;it's impossible.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that an extreme stretch by any measure?<br /> <br /> How does a Hunter Hunt something they don't know exists?<br /> <br /> Do you argue that they can know mages exist? How? Anything that could be considered evidence is wiped from their minds. Are they told by a mage? That's even more ridiculous. Why would a mage reveal himself to someone who wants them dead? If they did, why would the Hunter (or sleepers in an Order as mentioned elsewhere in this thread) believe them? There's no proof. Who would take someone's word on something like that? The first response would be &quot;prove it&quot; and then the mage can't. They'll be written off as crazy.<br /> <br /> Reasoning that Hunters can somehow just &quot;put it together&quot; despite absolutely no proof whatsoever is just as silly. Why would they have any reason to question it? If they did have a reason, why would they have reason enough to Hunt someone over it? If it was suspicious, they'd have more reason to blame it on something they already know. One of the hundreds of far more obvious supernatural critters, like Vampires or Prometheans.<br /> <br /> There is no way for a Hunter to know mages exist. A Hunter cannot hunt something they don't know exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:01:06-07:00","id":658431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658377#post658377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a slippery slope from &quot;He's no good for you; I read his thoughts, he's cheating on you&quot; to &quot;No way, I'm not even going to give him a chance with you&quot; or &quot;Here are the types of guys you can date, <i>if </i>they pass my inspection.&quot; And that's just a mild slope!</div> </div> </div> </div>But Awakened mages actually will <i>know</i> if someone's bad for someone else; they see the Truth\u2122. If a Sleeper doesn't listen, they're simply acting like ungrateful and ignorant children, and should be ignored for their own good. <br /> <br /> The &quot;slippery slope&quot; is of no concern when helping those so obviously unable to help themselves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:09:00-07:00","id":658436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658429#post658429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything that could be considered evidence is wiped from their minds. Are they told by a mage? That's even more ridiculous. Why would a mage reveal himself to someone who wants them dead? If they did, why would the Hunter (or sleepers in an Order as mentioned elsewhere in this thread) believe them? There's no proof. Who would take someone's word on something like that? The first response would be &quot;prove it&quot; and then the mage can't. They'll be written off as crazy.<br /> <br /> Reasoning that Hunters can somehow just &quot;put it together&quot; despite absolutely no proof whatsoever is just as silly. Why would they have any reason to question it? If they did have a reason, why would they have reason enough to Hunt someone over it? If it was suspicious, they'd have more reason to blame it on something they already know. One of the hundreds of far more obvious supernatural critters, like Vampires or Prometheans.<br /> <br /> There is no way for a Hunter to know mages exist. A Hunter cannot hunt something they don't know exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you miss the part where Dave said that the Orders in 2ed are going to be semi public organizations? There will be proof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:19:13-07:00","id":658443,"title":"","content":"It is entirely possible to believe something exists, even observe signs of its existence, without ever witnessing the thing itself. Hell it's been outright stated that there are Sleepers who <b>know</b> Mages exist, they just cannot observe or recall Supernal magic (much in the same way I know Blackholes exist, even though they cannot actually be seen).<br /> <br /> Take the hunter scenario I put forward several pages back: You've got a group of hunters who wake up with foggy memories. They recall overhearing a report of suspicious activity at the local cemetery, where they went and met a man (whom they remember fairly well) doing...something. The details of the scene are foggy. However, what they do know is that the following day two of them were injured with what looked like human claw and bite marks, seventeen of the most recent graves are now empty, and the bodies that were in those graves cropped up three blocks away looking to all eyes as though they'd walked there on their own.<br /> <br /> Now I don't think it's too big a leap for those hunters to think, &quot;That man we met yesterday is some scary necromancer.&quot; Though they might also tag on, &quot;And he fucked with our memories!&quot; They might also leap to conclusions like, &quot;He must be using some form of blood magic, like those vampires we stamped out last year&quot; or &quot;He's clearly possessed!&quot; Because off the mark judgement about the supernatural are a common theme of Hunter. But it's fair to say that they can absolutely reason out that he's a risk, even if they cannot recall the exact act of animating the dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:31:54-07:00","id":658482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658443#post658443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is entirely possible to believe something exists, even observe signs of its existence, without ever witnessing the thing itself. Hell it's been outright stated that there are Sleepers who <b>know</b> Mages exist, they just cannot observe or recall Supernal magic (much in the same way I know Blackholes exist, even though they cannot actually be seen).</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what you mean and I've already stated my point on the argument, but I don't think this line of logic really fits. Your memory isn't just distorted it's distorted to make the magic seem like something more rational happened. Why would you think a mage did something magical like turn a friend into a pillar of flame, when you recall your friend accidentally setting himself on fire?<br /> <br /> Your point about the black holes fits with that, too. Black holes are rational to you, but they're not black holes, they're Supernal verges, your mind is just making you believe they're black holes because it makes more sense to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take the hunter scenario I put forward several pages back: You've got a group of hunters who wake up with foggy memories. They recall overhearing a report of suspicious activity at the local cemetery, where they went and met a man (whom they remember fairly well) doing...something. The details of the scene are foggy. However, what they do know is that the following day two of them were injured with what looked like human claw and bite marks, seventeen of the most recent graves are now empty, and the bodies that were in those graves cropped up three blocks away looking to all eyes as though they'd walked there on their own. </div> </div> </div>See, it seems like you would remember those injuries coming from some crazed homeless person you stumbled upon who bit and clawed at you, or maybe you were afraid because it was a cemetery at night and freaked out at each other. Because you remember it is as something that makes more sense, that fits into your world view, you don't remember it as 'mysterious event that might have been magic.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-09-2015, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:41:07-07:00","id":658519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658482#post658482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your memory isn't just distorted it's distorted to make the magic seem like something more rational happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The scene after a Sleeper witnesses <b>a spell</b> \u2013 whether they caused it to crumble under Dissonance or not \u2013 they forget about it. Their memory warps, and they rationalize the event away <b>or</b> substitute a non-magical equivalent.&quot;<br /> <br /> Zombies and good luck are not spells and even remotely eclectic hunters or other mortal investigators have a broader toolbox for rationalizing the magic of an Awakened soul into some other source of supernatural power. If you know fire spirits are a thing you're not going to discount the possibility that the man with the gold watch made a deal with a fire spirit to be able to set your friend on fire instead of doing so under his own power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:42:01-07:00","id":658520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658482#post658482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what you mean and I've already stated my point on the argument, but I don't think this line of logic really fits. Your memory isn't just distorted it's distorted to make the magic seem like something more rational happened. Why would you think a mage did something magical like turn a friend into a pillar of flame, when you recall your friend accidentally setting himself on fire?<br /> <br /> Your point about the black holes fits with that, too. Black holes are rational to you, but they're not black holes, they're Supernal verges, your mind is just making you believe they're black holes because it makes more sense to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That explains it for normal people, but Hunters are different they <b>know</b> magic exists. Perhaps not supernal magic, but they aren't exactly the most discerning folks. A hunter could quite reasonably rationalize supernal magic as some lesser form of sorcery, witchcraft, blood sorcery, psychic phenomena. This is nWoD after all, and those things are just as real, observable and provable as a Blackhole is to us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658482#post658482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, it seems like you would remember those injuries coming from some crazed homeless person you stumbled upon who bit and clawed at you, or maybe you were afraid because it was a cemetery at night and freaked out at each other. Because you remember it is as something that makes more sense, that fits into your world view, you don't remember it as 'mysterious event that might have been magic.'</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are a paranoid, violent vigilante who has had repeat run-ins with bizarre fallen magics then I think &quot;he's a necromancer who fucked with my head&quot; is pretty reasonable. At least after the fact, when you are trying to put the details together and discovering they don't even begin to add up. This is especially the case for a group of hunters, who may all remember events differently, or external hunters who having not witnessed the spell are quite free to think something fucking weird went down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 09-09-2015, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:51:42-07:00","id":658553,"title":"","content":"FWIW, this post is intended solely to clarify where I've been coming from.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658366#post658366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think a game of Sleepers of the edge of mage society, knowing that they can't trust what they remember happened half the time and slowly being driven mad by their exposure to supernal magic, would be pretty neat. Of undoubtedly limited appeal, though, which is why I say to make hunters Sleepwalkers <i>unless you're interested in that kind of game</i>. What you can't do with Mage as written is have Sleeper characters who act like Sleepwalkers but increase Paradox risk. If you don't want to make hunters Sleepwalkers and you don't want that weird Nolan-esque feeling to the game, you shouldn't use the Awakened but knock up your own Witches instead.<br /> <br /> But, of course, the material on playing a Sleeper in Mage isn't necessarily aligned to the hostility of a hunter. Do you, as an Awakened character, try to tell your boyfriend what you're experiencing? If someone's badly injured, should you risk their Integrity to heal them? Many mages try to use their powers for whatever they think is Sleepers' own good, but Sleepers are incapable of giving informed consent - how far do you go in adjusting your friends, relatives, rivals' lives?</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone posted a &quot;Intentionally Obtuse&quot; Merit, or something to that effect. When they did, I commented that it was representative of the sort of &quot;doing an end run around the Curse&quot; stuff that I've been advocating (in that it allows a Sleeper to avoid taking a Breaking Point for witnessing Supernal Magic), but that it wasn't really suitable for hunters. I'm assuming it is an official Merit, as it was said to have come from a leak (though I haven't personally seen said leak). As well, the way it was described gives the impression that, while it gives what could be characterized as a supernatural benefit, the Merit itself isn't supernatural, instead relying exclusively on the Sleeper's psychology.<br /> <br /> As mentioned before, and in keeping with Dave's post above, this isn't really suitable for a hunter's more antagonistic relationship with a mage; but it <i>does</i> demonstrate how a Sleeper, without supernatural assistance, could have some means of coping with the Curse, making long-term interactions with mages and their magic viable without an Integrity death-spiral. And that's really all that I was looking for. <br /> <br /> That, and I don't mind Nolan-esqe hunter games. I'm not interested in Sleeper hunters &quot;who behave like Sleepwalkers except that they trigger Paradox&quot;; the closest I've suggesting such a thing has involved trading off some of the traditional problems of being a Sleeper for other problems. This preserves the notion that the Curse sucks no matter who you are, just in different ways. While this isn't strictly in accordance with Dave's intentions, I think it's mostly compatible with them.<br /> <br /> Note that I haven't addressed the power differential between mages and hunters. Once coping mechanisms for the Curse are in play so that a hunter cell can deal as effectively with mages as with, say, changelings or werewolves, you still have to deal with the versatility and power that a mage commands. That's where hunter determination and ingenuity are <i>really</i> put to the test.<br /> <br /> As for witches: I'm hoping that if Hunter 2e actually has witches in it (as opposed to relying on WoD2e to supply approximations of the various major gamelines), witches will be flexible enough in their definition to approximate Second Sight thaumaturges to Awakened mages (complete with power, versatility, and even the Sleeping Curse) and everything in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:58:20-07:00","id":658572,"title":"","content":"Dataweaver, the Merit is called Actively Oblivious, and it is official, though I think it was from first drafts, so it may or may not end up looking the same in the final product. It wasn't from a leak, it was from one of Dave's open development blog posts. I think the one about Proximi.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yep, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/supporting-cast-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">here it is</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-09-2015, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T16:30:42-07:00","id":658604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658519#post658519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zombies and good luck are not spells and even remotely eclectic hunters or other mortal investigators have a broader toolbox for rationalizing the magic of an Awakened soul into some other source of supernatural power. If you know fire spirits are a thing you're not going to discount the possibility that the man with the gold watch made a deal with a fire spirit to be able to set your friend on fire instead of doing so under his own power.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can rationalize Supernal magic into 'regular' magic because it's something you agree exists then Quiescence is not a problem for Sleepers, except for the fallout from failing Breaking Points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-09-2015, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T16:35:35-07:00","id":658609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658443#post658443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is entirely possible to believe something exists, even observe signs of its existence, without ever witnessing the thing itself. </div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and don't believe you even need to cite black holes for the proposition. Far simpler, you just observed the phenomena of &quot;religion,&quot; observed by <i>billions</i> of people across the our world in a myriad of forms.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Heck, some people's religion explicitly includes what many would consider &quot;magic.&quot; <br /> <br /> Believing in the existence of supernal magic and Awakened mages is hardly a leap of faith for people in the WOD.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658443#post658443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take the hunter scenario I put forward several pages back: You've got a group of hunters who wake up with foggy memories. They recall overhearing a report of suspicious activity at the local cemetery, where they went and met a man (whom they remember fairly well) doing...something. The details of the scene are foggy. However, what they do know is that the following day two of them were injured with what looked like human claw and bite marks, seventeen of the most recent graves are now empty, and the bodies that were in those graves cropped up three blocks away looking to all eyes as though they'd walked there on their own.<br /> <br /> Now I don't think it's too big a leap for those hunters to think, &quot;That man we met yesterday is some scary necromancer.&quot; Though they might also tag on, &quot;And he fucked with our memories!&quot; They might also leap to conclusions like, &quot;He must be using some form of blood magic, like those vampires we stamped out last year&quot; or &quot;He's clearly possessed!&quot; Because off the mark judgement about the supernatural are a common theme of Hunter. But it's fair to say that they can absolutely reason out that he's a risk, even if they cannot recall the exact act of animating the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's less of a situation of &quot;foggy&quot; memories, than either total amnesia or having clear and &quot;rationale,&quot; albeit totally wrong, memories. Suffering the accompanying Breaking Points and potentially losing Integrity, i.e., a damaged soul, also has serious repercussions. <br /> <br /> I would additionally note that any rationalizations for those who have knowledge of the supernatural could include scenarios where the mage is seen as an unfortunate <i>victim</i> of supernatural forces or entities, and thus needs to be <i>saved</i> by the Hunters, whether the mage wants &quot;saving&quot; or not. Such an encounter would not go well...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658572#post658572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dataweaver, the Merit is called Actively Oblivious, and it is official, though I think it was from first drafts, so it may or may not end up looking the same in the final product. It wasn't from a leak, it was from one of Dave's open development blog posts. I think the one about Proximi.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yep, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/supporting-cast-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">here it is</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Actively Oblivious&quot; is hardly a panacea for Sleeper Hunters. It requires the character to ignore the supernal magic, a bad situation for a Hunter, and it largely only delays the damage, rather than prevent it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T16:36:01-07:00","id":658610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658604#post658604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can rationalize Supernal magic if magic is something you agree exists then Quiescence is not a problem for Sleepers, except for the fallout from failing Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What I must reiterate, though, is that the Sleeper\u2019s belief or non-belief in magic has absolutely nothing to do with whether their souls are injured by witnessing spells, and the Orders employ hundreds of staff who know that they work for mages, and that mages exist, but can\u2019t be allowed to actually see any magic for their own safety.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T16:45:43-07:00","id":658613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658610#post658610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;What I must reiterate, though, is that the Sleeper\u2019s belief or non-belief in magic has absolutely nothing to do with whether their souls are injured by witnessing spells, and the Orders employ hundreds of staff who know that they work for mages, and that mages exist, but can\u2019t be allowed to actually see any magic for their own safety.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Knowledge and belief in supernal magic or the supernatural generally does not mean Sleeper will rationalize an experience with spells cast by a supernal mage as &quot;fallen&quot; magic, and hence supernatural.<br /> <br /> In fact, in Dave's spoiler about the Lie, &quot;<a href=\"http://&#91;QUOTE=Charlaquin;n658572]Dataweaver, the Merit is called Actively Oblivious, and it is official, though I think it was from first drafts, so it may or may not end up looking the same in the final product. It wasn&#39;t from a leak, it was from one of Dave&#39;s open development blog posts. I think the one about Proximi.EDIT: Yep, &#91;URL=&amp;quot;&#91;url]http://theonyxpath.com/supporting-cast-mage-the-awakening/&amp;quot;]here&#91;/url] it is&#91;/URL].&#91;/QUOTE]\" target=\"_blank\">I'll Lie To You</a>,&quot; he states (and you previously cite),<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>Quiescence: The scene after a Sleeper witnesses a spell \u2013 whether they caused it to crumble under Dissonance or not \u2013 they forget about it. Their memory warps, and <b>they rationalize the event away or substitute a <i>non-magical</i> equivalent</b>. Convincingly reminding them (including using magic to do so) causes them to suffer another Breaking Point, and then forget again.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>(emphasis added)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-09-2015, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T16:51:51-07:00","id":658615,"title":"","content":"I don't even know who's arguing for what anymore. I'm just going to say that I think it's eminently possible for hunters to hunt mages. Not easy, by a long shot, but possible. I don't think it's beyond the pale for a Vigil to be held against the Awakened. I would bet that not a few cells have been started by those same Sleeper cultists who have turned against their former masters, probably after being traumatized witnessing vulgar (lower case v, I'm betting that is still useful terminology in Awakened parlance) magic. They'd know enough to figure out the clues about who is or is not a mage despite whatever memory alterations the Quiescence forces on them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T17:02:21-07:00","id":658645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658615#post658615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even know who's arguing for what anymore. I'm just going to say that I think it's eminently possible for hunters to hunt mages. Not easy, by a long shot, but possible. I don't think it's beyond the pale for a Vigil to be held against the Awakened. I would bet that not a few cells have been started by those same Sleeper cultists who have turned against their former masters, probably after being traumatized witnessing vulgar (lower case v, I'm betting that is still useful terminology in Awakened parlance) magic. They'd know enough to figure out the clues about who is or is not a mage despite whatever memory alterations the Quiescence forces on them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe almost everyone would agree with most, if not all, your comments.<br /> <br /> Apart from some amusing distractions about mage vs. werewolf bar fights and whatnot, I believe the pertinent issues have always been confusion over the exact nature and effects of the Quiescence, whether it's effects could be overcome by mundane means by Sleeper Hunters, and more generally, whether such low-tier, normal human Hunters &quot;realistically&quot; stood much of a chance successfully hunting the Awakened, with their power and versatility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T17:07:13-07:00","id":658651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658609#post658609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Actively Oblivious&quot; is hardly a panacea for Sleeper Hunters. It requires the character to ignore the supernal magic, a bad situation for a Hunter, and it largely only delays the damage, rather than prevent it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted. I was just clarifying for Dataweaver what the Merit he was referencing was called and where it was from. He's said that he doesn't find it suitable for hunters, but that it is the kind of thing he's been looking for.<br /> <br /> I can only speak for myself, but for me at least, the fact that Acively Oblivious is not a panacea is precisely the reason it appeals as a Merit to help Sleepers (hunters or otherwise, honestly) cope with Quiessence. As I've said repeatedly, I don't want a way for Sleepers to act like Sleepwalkers but still cause Paradox. That would be changing the metaphysics of Mage, which I don't want any more than you do. What I do want is ways to help manage its effects, that come with their own drawbacks, and that work within the constraints of Mage's metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Actively Oblivious fits that bill almost to the letter, except that as you pointed out, ignoring the supernatural is kind of the opposite of what most Hunters do. But the point is, it's a great example of the kind of thing I'm looking for. The fact that you still look at it and say &quot;but it doesn't work for what you want because it's not a Panacea&quot; indicates that you're still not understanding what it is that I actually want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T17:09:30-07:00","id":658652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658609#post658609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cActively Oblivious\u201d is hardly a panacea for Sleeper Hunters. It requires the character to ignore the supernal magic, a bad situation for a Hunter, and it largely only delays the damage, rather than prevent it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; I know. I never cited it as a panacea for Sleeper Hunters; I cited it as evidence that it\u2019s reasonable to have coping mechanisms available to Sleepers that aren\u2019t themselves supernatural, and that basically exchange one drawback (having chunks of your soul ripped out whenever you witness magic) for another (in this case, sticking your head in the sand whenever the supernal comes by). The fact that it's from a first draft makes it somewhat suspect, in that it may have subsequently been dropped; but the fact that it has even been under consideration in the first place says something too.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd! Count this as a +1 to everything that Charlaquin just said. I'd rephrase that last part slightly, though: <i>if</i> you (in general, not just branford) <i>do</i> still think that Charlaquin and I (and likely others) are asking for \u201cpanaceas\u201d and ways that amount to being a Sleepwalker who inflicts Paradox, you\u2019re still misunderstanding what we're saying.<br /> <br /> (And the fact that I\u2019m seeing people on both sides of this debate assuming that they know what the other side is saying but that the other side is misunderstanding them\u2026 &quot;What we have heah\u2026 is a failiah, to communicate!\u201d)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-09-2015, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T17:23:33-07:00","id":658661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658652#post658652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; I know. I never cited it as a panacea for Sleeper Hunters; I cited it as evidence that it\u2019s reasonable to have coping mechanisms available to Sleepers that aren\u2019t themselves supernatural, and that basically exchange one drawback (having chunks of your soul ripped out whenever you witness magic) for another (in this case, sticking your head in the sand whenever the supernal comes by). The fact that it's from a first draft makes it somewhat suspect, in that it may have subsequently been dropped; but the fact that it has even been under consideration in the first place says something too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While I obviously don't know the current state of the merit in the final Mage opus, my only minor point was that the trade-offs were significant for the very little protection it provided Sleepers dealing with supernal magic. The fact that it's essential component dealt with the <i>avoidance</i> of such magic as the means of dealing with it made it seem, at least to me, as a poor framework for comparable merits or tactics for Hunters. Regardless, I believe lower-tier Sleeper Hunters can still pursue the Awakened, but that it is an extremely arduous task, which will likely slowly destroy the Hunters, even if they successfully manage to take down their prey.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I'm anxious to read Mage 2e and the entire finalized material dealing with Sleepers and the Quiescence, as well as read if Hunter 2e intends to directly deal with this issue, and if so, how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T17:43:32-07:00","id":658689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658661#post658661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I obviously don't know the current state of the merit in the final Mage opus, my only minor point was that the trade-offs were significant for the very little protection it provided Sleepers dealing with supernal magic. The fact that it's essential component dealt with the <i>avoidance</i> of such magic as the means of dealing with it made it seem, at least to me, as a poor framework for comparable merits or tactics for Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; I wouldn't use it as a <i>framework</i> for comparable merits or Tactics for hunters; I\u2019m merely using it to establish the principle that exchanging one serious drawback of the Sleeping Curse for another drawback is a reasonable one, and doesn\u2019t necessarily count as \u201clifting the Abyssal shard\u201d, \u201chaving your cake and eating it too\u201d, or similar accusations. As long as this Merit is kept, there is canonically at least one way to do something about the Sleeping Curse, even if you\u2019re a Sleeper. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658661#post658661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless, I believe lower-tier Sleeper Hunters can still pursue the Awakened, but that it is an extremely arduous task, which will likely slowly destroy the Hunters, even if they successfully manage to take down their prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile, I\u2019d rather Sleeper hunters have as much ability to cope with Quiescence as they do with Lunacy and Disquiet. If they don't discover and implement these methods, then yes; their hunt will slowly destroy them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658661#post658661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nevertheless, I'm anxious to read Mage 2e and the entire finalized material dealing with Sleepers and the Quiescence, as well as read if Hunter 2e intends to directly deal with this issue, and if so, how.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T17:55:37-07:00","id":658690,"title":"","content":"Yeah, again, Dataweaver, merits like that probably belong in Hunter 2e or a supplement, not Mage, so there's probably gonna be a bit of a wait on it being properly satisfied, one way or the other, at least in an official capacity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T17:57:05-07:00","id":658691,"title":"","content":"True enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T20:00:58-07:00","id":658844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658690#post658690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, again, Dataweaver, merits like that probably belong in Hunter 2e or a supplement, not Mage, so there's probably gonna be a bit of a wait on it being properly satisfied, one way or the other, at least in an official capacity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figured it went without saying that these suggestions were in regard to Hunter, since Mage is past the point in Development where they'd be able to add Merits and such anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T21:04:16-07:00","id":658874,"title":"","content":"I argue for anything is possible even if some things are improbable. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When it comes to things that can be observed but not seen, why reach for straws? Just use wind, gravity even. What about van der Waals forces? Black holes and religion are theoretical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T21:23:27-07:00","id":658877,"title":"","content":"The key point here is that <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> isn't about belief or disbelief; that\u2019s a <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> thing. <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> is about sight and blindness, or understanding and ignorance. People can believe in magic all they want; but the Lie doesn\u2019t let them <i>see</i> it. <br /> <br /> (Well, technically it doesn\u2019t let them <i>remember</i> seeing it; but the larger point still holds. There's a reason Dave renamed 1e's \u201cDisbelief\u201d to \u201cDissonance\u201d.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T21:53:19-07:00","id":658919,"title":"","content":"Like electromagnetic radiation, the farther away from what you can see the more harmful it is to you (sleeper).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T04:50:47-07:00","id":659239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657044#post657044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if she gets an exceptional success, one of the things she can do is remove the Withstood property of the spell. In which case, our increasingly-beleaguered Werewolf is simply shit out of luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, does that mean if you face a powerful being with high resistance attributes, like a high level Spirit, a Mage might be best of not trying to beat their opponents Withstand attribute? Instead the mage should take as few penalties to their roll as possible and hope for an exceptional success to remove their opponent's resistance outright?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T04:54:39-07:00","id":659240,"title":"","content":"As we, finally, come to conclusion that Sleeper Hunters can hunt Awakened - only they would blame it sometimes on other, non-Supernal magic sources, because Quiescence - I have one question left:<br /> <br /> <b>How about &quot;blue book&quot; mortals that first exposure to supernatural is our Awakened spell - can they become Sleeper Hunters, even when their first &quot;weird stuff&quot; that normally lead to hunters life is take from their memories by </b><b>Quiescence effect?</b> In other words - <b>Can hunter start from hunting mages in 2ED paradigm? Or does he need other phenomena first exposure?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T05:25:47-07:00","id":659255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659240#post659240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As we, finally, come to conclusion that Sleeper Hunters can hunt Awakened - only they would blame it sometimes on other, non-Supernal magic sources, because Quiescence - I have one question left:</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe this was the generally accepted conclusion, especially as it possibly contradicts the quote from the book saying that sleepers substitute the memory for a non-magical equivalent. But I can't say for sure whether &quot;non-magical&quot; means &quot;mundane&quot; or &quot;non-supernal&quot; in this context. I prefer the former, as rationalizing supernal magic as fallen magic makes no sense for me as that wouldn't really result in a substituted memory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659240#post659240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How about &quot;blue book&quot; mortals that first exposure to supernatural is our Awakened spell - can they become Sleeper Hunters, even when their first &quot;weird stuff&quot; that normally lead to hunters life is take from their memories by </b><b>Quiescence effect?</b> In other words - <b>Can hunter start from hunting mages in 2ED paradigm? Or does he need other phenomena first exposure?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think mortals could still be left with the feeling that either their memory was changed, or reality was warped, as their recollection of an event could just make no sense. Of course the events as remembered were completely possible and mundane, but that does not necessarily make the sequence of events plausible. Of course, this would not result in knowing that someone is a Mage, only that someone was central to all the weirdness.<br /> <br /> That compact that hunts reality deviants makes so much sense under this paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T05:43:25-07:00","id":659265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658689#post658689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah; I wouldn't use it as a <i>framework</i> for comparable merits or Tactics for hunters; I\u2019m merely using it to establish the principle that exchanging one serious drawback of the Sleeping Curse for another drawback is a reasonable one, and doesn\u2019t necessarily count as \u201clifting the Abyssal shard\u201d, \u201chaving your cake and eating it too\u201d, or similar accusations. As long as this Merit is kept, there is canonically at least one way to do something about the Sleeping Curse, even if you\u2019re a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I\u2019d rather Sleeper hunters have as much ability to cope with Quiescence as they do with Lunacy and Disquiet. If they don't discover and implement these methods, then yes; their hunt will slowly destroy them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say &quot;having your cake and eating it too&quot; would only be valid if said Hunter was taking said Abyssal Shard and going around stabbing people with it.<br /> <br /> Which would be interesting idea for a compact to be honest, beyond simply using the Knights that is.<br /> <br /> Personally, I can easily see the Lie not acting fast enough in where a cell of Hunter race to document everything in a fight to with a mage before forgetting it after the scene is done and have to reference the documentation later. A cell's version of memento. Also useful with Hunters who have to fight Kindred. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T06:06:07-07:00","id":659295,"title":"","content":"Or Hunters could just start using bodycameras. I'm sure Network Zero would be more than willing to fire up a Kickstarter for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T06:10:34-07:00","id":659297,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, I am not a big expert on Mage, but how does the magic interact with modern surveillance equipment? Does the Lie change that? Because I would expect any well-organized hunter group to always have cameras running while working. Best way for some after-hunt tactical discussions even when vampires turn up blurry and changelings looking like normal humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T06:32:39-07:00","id":659322,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the camera would record what happened correctly, but any Sleepers who watched the recording would take a Breaking Point and then rationalize or forget what they saw on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T06:35:32-07:00","id":659323,"title":"","content":"I want also to point out that now movie <b>Memento</b> is literal evidence of Sleeper Hunter going after Mage that all the time is wrapping his mind by Quiescence... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UFuFFdK7i44\" data-code=\"UFuFFdK7i44\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/UFuFFdK7i44/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T07:29:17-07:00","id":659363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659322#post659322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the camera would record what happened correctly, but any Sleepers who watched the recording would take a Breaking Point and then rationalize or forget what they saw on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are other methods of documentation other than visual.<br /> <br /> I can easily see a cell building up case via whiteboard of things that they have done, haven't done, where the enemy was and where he/she wasn't via their own written documentation and second hand accounts and verification. Information is cheap in this age and pieces are both easy to assemble and easier to see where they don't.<br /> <br /> Trust, on the other hand, is a bigger issue but either cells have dealt with it or not long for this world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T08:07:33-07:00","id":659380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659322#post659322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the camera would record what happened correctly, but any Sleepers who watched the recording would take a Breaking Point and then rationalize or forget what they saw on it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that's correct. If a Hunter manages to record the event, everything from video and audio recordings to drawings, when he viewed the material after the fact, he would suffer another Breaking Point, and again forget or rationalize the original event. This would happen each time he viewed the recording, and would be a swift means to insanity.<br /> <br /> There's no cheating The Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T08:12:35-07:00","id":659382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659380#post659380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that's correct. If a Hunter manages to record the event, everything from video and audio recordings to drawings, when he viewed the material after the fact, he would suffer another Breaking Point, and again forget or rationalize the original event. This would happen each time he viewed the recording, and would be a swift means to insanity.<br /> <br /> There's no cheating The Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With mundane methods at any rate. There might be supernatural means to cheat it, but that's largely what most GMs would treat as a plot point/mystery if it happened in an awakened centric game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T08:59:00-07:00","id":659419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659382#post659382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> With mundane methods at any rate. There might be supernatural means to cheat it, but that's largely what most GMs would treat as a plot point/mystery if it happened in an awakened centric game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed. However, if an otherwise normal human Sleeper character gains an inherent supernatural merit or advantage, they become a Sleepwalker, and will longer subject be subject to the Quiescence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:13:53-07:00","id":659424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659380#post659380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's correct. If a Hunter manages to record the event, everything from video and audio recordings to drawings, when he viewed the material after the fact, he would suffer another Breaking Point, and again forget or rationalize the original event. This would happen each time he viewed the recording, and would be a swift means to insanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes Network Zero seem like an extremely risky faction to join. You never know when you might accidentally catch a Mage on camera and slowly destroy your own soul as you review the footage without even knowing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:21:35-07:00","id":659432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659380#post659380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that's correct. If a Hunter manages to record the event, everything from video and audio recordings to drawings, when he viewed the material after the fact, he would suffer another Breaking Point, and again forget or rationalize the original event. This would happen each time he viewed the recording, and would be a swift means to insanity.<br /> <br /> There's no cheating The Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is always cheating the Lie. If that wasn't true, then we would A) no Mages whatsoever, B) no conflict what soever, C) and pretty boring ass game.<br /> <br /> I personally try to avoid the C option as best as I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:47:50-07:00","id":659458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658431#post658431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Awakened mages actually will <i>know</i> if someone's bad for someone else; they see the Truth\u2122.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to see the truth doesn't means your interpretation of it is more enlightened than anyone else's, that's the way Hubris happens, and one of the most fundamental human traits Mages sport.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:55:10-07:00","id":659464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659424#post659424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Makes Network Zero seem like an extremely risky faction to join. You never know when you might accidentally catch a Mage on camera and slowly destroy your own soul as you review the footage without even knowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one ever said being a Hunter was easy or without its peculiar risks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659432#post659432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is always cheating the Lie. If that wasn't true, then we would A) no Mages whatsoever, B) no conflict what soever, C) and pretty boring ass game.<br /> <br /> I personally try to avoid the C option as best as I can.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends how you define &quot;cheating.&quot; According to the <i>Gospels of Dave</i>, the only means for a Sleeper to no longer be subject to the Quiescence is for them to Awaken or somehow acquire an inherent supernatural merit, advantage or template (including the one dot Sleepwalker Merit).<br /> <br /> However, if you mean that in <i>your</i> chronicles, Sleepers can use mundane means to escape the Lie, that fine, but it's clearly not the canon Mage setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-10-2015, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:55:47-07:00","id":659465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659458#post659458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being able to see the truth doesn't means your interpretation of it is more enlightened than anyone else's,</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't it, though? I mean it kinda is more enlightened if you can see the truth and the other person explicitly doesn't and can't.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T09:57:58-07:00","id":659468,"title":"","content":"No. Take the different paths. In 2e? Everyone in a cabal using Mage sight would see different stuff. Everything is relative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T10:00:01-07:00","id":659470,"title":"","content":"Ahh, I meant the difference between Mages and Sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T10:03:27-07:00","id":659471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659458#post659458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Being able to see the truth doesn't means your interpretation of it is more enlightened than anyone else's, that's the way Hubris happens, and one of the most fundamental human traits Mages sport.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First, my original post was in jest, and meant to emulate the attitude of mages in the setting. The Hubris was intentional.<br /> <br /> However, mages do indeed know and understand <i><b>far</b></i> more than Sleepers. They have means to read minds, view the past and future, follow the strands of destiny, and even perceive and convey the Truth (with the revised 2e Prime).<br /> <br /> Who wouldn't want their dating advice? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-10-2015, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T10:08:54-07:00","id":659477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659471#post659471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, mages do indeed know and understand <i><b>far</b></i> more than Sleepers. They have means to read minds, view the past and future, follow the strands of destiny, and even perceive and convey the Truth (with the revised 2e Prime).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except their ability to understand that information is still human. A mage can look into someones mind and still think they can get over their alcoholism by simply being told not to drink, or they can look into the past and future and assume an abused spouse stays with their significant other because they enjoy being beaten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T10:15:22-07:00","id":659491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659477#post659477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except their ability to understand that information is still human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The Knowing Practice does give a mage access to unvarnished understanding, free of the need to interpret. A conjunctional Knowing of Mind and Time can allow a mage to know, with absolute certainty, that the drunk won't be rehabilitated simply through talk. Same thing using Mind and Time to read a person and see for themselves that they don't enjoy being abused. Even without Time, a mage could use Mind to delve into the person's Oneiros and find that out as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T10:15:50-07:00","id":659498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659477#post659477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except their ability to understand that information is still human. A mage can look into someones mind and still think they can get over their alcoholism by simply being told not to drink, or they can look into the past and future and assume an abused spouse stays with their significant other because they enjoy being beaten.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I was getting at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T10:47:03-07:00","id":659529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659477#post659477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except their ability to understand that information is still human. A mage can look into someones mind and still think they can get over their alcoholism by simply being told not to drink, or they can look into the past and future and assume an abused spouse stays with their significant other because they enjoy being beaten.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The relevant Practices, particularly when used together, do indeed provide accurate and comprehensive information. Your examples appear to stretch credulity in order to artificially limit mages' capabilities (the spouse likes being beaten?).<br /> <br /> The issue is not whether mages know or can easily learn the most intimate or hidden details about their non-mage friends, family or anyone else, but rather if they have the right to do so, particularly since the Quiescence normally prevents Sleepers from ever giving truly informed consent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T10:57:38-07:00","id":659539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659529#post659529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The relevant Practices, particularly when used together, do indeed provide accurate and comprehensive information. Your examples appear to stretch credulity in order to artificially limit mages' capabilities (the spouse likes being beaten?).</div> </div> </div> </div>The examples were based off of common stereotypes that some people believe. Mages are not all Intelligence 5 with Empathy 5. An example from the Fallen World Chronicle Fiction Anthology, for instance, has a mage really upset that people can have guns in the midst of a rash of spiritually-compelled shootings. Why should anyone be able to own a gun? He was unable to understand why another mage would be for the ownership of guns, all without once noting that he is a walking, talking weapon of mass destruction that can kill roomfuls of Sleepers because it might be easier than killing one of them and whose spells drive people insane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue is not whether mages know or can easily learn the most intimate or hidden details about their non-mage friends, family or anyone else, but rather if they have the right to do so, particularly since the Quiescence normally prevents Sleepers from ever giving truly informed consent. </div> </div> </div>This issue was from you suggesting they understand situations as well as they know them, where I'm backing up Ephsy's point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Awakened mages actually will know if someone's bad for someone else; they see the Truth\u2122. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-10-2015, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T11:21:53-07:00","id":659604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659539#post659539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are not all Intelligence 5 with Empathy 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing spells grant understanding even to a mage with low intelligence or empathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T11:58:01-07:00","id":659643,"title":"","content":"Let's examine the original situation used as an example of mage hubris, whether a friend of the mage should be dating an particular individual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=658377#post658377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a slippery slope from &quot;He's no good for you; I read his thoughts, he's cheating on you&quot; to &quot;No way, I'm not even going to give him a chance with you&quot; or &quot;Here are the types of guys you can date, <i>if </i>they pass my inspection.&quot; And that's just a mild slope!</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of the mage's Intelligence, Empathy or Path, the relevant Practices, individually and even moreso combined, will provide accurate and pertinent information. The mage will actually learn if an individual is cheating or abusive, his or her true history and intentions, if a particularly relationship has a doomed or horrible destiny, etc. This information might be <i>sensed</i> differently by the various Paths, but the actual information and knowledge remain the same. Intelligence and Empathy might affect how a mage chooses to use the knowledge, but again, the ability to ascertain accurate information is determined solely by the basic Arcanum (and Gnosis) and inherent abilities as an Awakened.<br /> <br /> The real Hubris is a mage determining what he wants to know and how he intends to learn, all without the knowledge or consent of anyone else, and further failing to acknowledge that acquiring such information from Sleepers might damage them because of the Quiescence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T12:39:39-07:00","id":659727,"title":"","content":"The knowledge magic imparts is without flaw, unless cheated by some supernatural force. A given mage's interpretation of that knowledge, and the decision about how to act upon it, varies from mage to mage, of course. A mage with high Empathy might alert her friend about the infidelity and then do her best to console the friend. A less tactful mage might confront the friend with this knowledge and demand better of their loved one. A would-be &quot;protector&quot; might then start &quot;screening&quot; potential mates with her magic. From there, it's not too far to tell the loved one just exactly who they can date, if they pass your rather strict requirements\u2014which fewer and fewer suitors do as time goes on. A truly vengeful mage might decide that the cheating bastard deserves punishment for his actions. A presumptuous one might decide that it's better to erase the memories of the betrayal\u2014indeed, the entire ruinous relationship\u2014from a devastated loved one's mind.<br /> <br /> All of this could stem from simply looking into an unfaithful spouse's mind and revealing the infidelity. Power can be a slippery slope. If knowledge is power, then a mage is standing on a muddy slope in heavy rain, trying to push a boulder up a hill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T12:39:57-07:00","id":659728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659464#post659464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends how you define &quot;cheating.&quot; According to the <i>Gospels of Dave</i>, the only means for a Sleeper to no longer be subject to the Quiescence is for them to Awaken or somehow acquire an inherent supernatural merit, advantage or template (including the one dot Sleepwalker Merit).<br /> <br /> However, if you mean that in <i>your</i> chronicles, Sleepers can use mundane means to escape the Lie, that fine, but it's clearly not the canon Mage setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is an issue that me and Dave have spared on quite a bit. The Lie is a hard coded thing that covers all supernatural activities that humanity has no hope of ever recognizing (let alone setting up compacts or cells) because they are too stu- I mean helpless to do anything about it.<br /> <br /> Which is fine, He's the dev of the gameline and thus can write Mage how he sees fit. Just find it rather annoying in creating a mechanic that kills stories rather than creates them when it comes to Mages fucking up and having to deal with external confirmation of their hubris. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:06:42-07:00","id":659753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659728#post659728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is an issue that me and Dave have spared on quite a bit. The Lie is a hard coded thing that covers all supernatural activities that humanity has no hope of ever recognizing (let alone setting up compacts or cells) because they are too stu- I mean helpless to do anything about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's exactly what Dave said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659728#post659728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is fine, He's the dev of the gameline and thus can write Mage how he sees fit. Just find it rather annoying in creating a mechanic that kills stories rather than creates them when it comes to Mages fucking up and having to deal with external confirmation of their hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>... or it could be that it enforces the themes of isolation from humanity as well as giving them a legitimate reason for their hubris?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:10:31-07:00","id":659760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659727#post659727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The knowledge magic imparts is without flaw, unless cheated by some supernatural force. A given mage's interpretation of that knowledge, and the decision about how to act upon it, varies from mage to mage, of course. A mage with high Empathy might alert her friend about the infidelity and then do her best to console the friend. A less tactful mage might confront the friend with this knowledge and demand better of their loved one. A would-be &quot;protector&quot; might then start &quot;screening&quot; potential mates with her magic. From there, it's not too far to tell the loved one just exactly who they can date, if they pass your rather strict requirements\u2014which fewer and fewer suitors do as time goes on. A truly vengeful mage might decide that the cheating bastard deserves punishment for his actions. A presumptuous one might decide that it's better to erase the memories of the betrayal\u2014indeed, the entire ruinous relationship\u2014from a devastated loved one's mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for clearing that up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:16:44-07:00","id":659772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659760#post659760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for clearing that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly I just wanted to explain how the game's theme reinforces its mechanics, and vice versa. The magic itself opens the way to knowledge; it is objective in this regard. How mage <i>interprets </i>that knowledge, and what she does with it, well, that's subject to a given individual's perspective. Do you console your wounded friend? Do you &quot;ease&quot; her burden (without her consent) via magic? Do you take revenge on the transgressor or decide to &quot;protect&quot; your friend with your superior knowledge and position? Do you decide that it was her own shortcomings that led to this, and thus try to &quot;improve&quot; her?<br /> <br /> <b>Mage </b>is fantastic for wrestling with this kind of drama. Yours is lordship over the Fallen World with a connection to the one, true Supernal World. What does that mean for a character once ensnared by the very same Lie that now holds most everyone you know captive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:20:47-07:00","id":659776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659772#post659772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mostly I just wanted to explain how the game's theme reinforces its mechanics, and vice versa. The magic itself opens the way to knowledge; it is objective in this regard. How mage <i>interprets </i>that knowledge, and what she does with it, well, that's subject to a given individual's perspective. Do you console your wounded friend? Do you &quot;ease&quot; her burden (without her consent) via magic? Do you take revenge on the transgressor or decide to &quot;protect&quot; your friend with your superior knowledge and position? Do you decide that it was her own shortcomings that led to this, and thus try to &quot;improve&quot; her?<br /> <br /> <b>Mage </b>is fantastic for wrestling with this kind of drama. Yours is lordship over the Fallen World with a connection to the one, true Supernal World. What does that mean for a character once ensnared by the very same Lie that now holds most everyone you know captive?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get it, there's a Dr Doom comic page I'd link but I can't find the image. Second edition has given me a newfound appreciation for Mage, but I'm still a Forsaken fan at heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-10-2015, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:33:58-07:00","id":659799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659728#post659728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is an issue that me and Dave have spared on quite a bit. The Lie is a hard coded thing that covers all supernatural activities that humanity has no hope of ever recognizing (let alone setting up compacts or cells) because they are too stu- I mean helpless to do anything about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not at all sure that the Lie and Quiescence leads either directly or inevitably to this. In fact, a lot of what Dave said leads to the opposite. There are lots of Sleepers who know Mages exist, and a fair few more who've realized it, including Hunters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:52:37-07:00","id":659836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659753#post659753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's exactly what Dave said.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not what he said but given the description of 2ed so far, it's fairly close to the point and the focus of my complaint. Mortals are hard coded to forget the supernatural even exists which leads to various issues going down the pipe. This is a social norm of seeing something and refusing to tell anyone lest people think you insane but forgetting that said thing ever happened which irks immensely as simple human agency (and ability) is the thing that I find so attractive in nWoD. Even Kindred elders can be felled with a few swings of a angry mortal taking a knife and supernatural effects can be dispelled with either spending/burning willpower. Granted, Joe blow will die 9 out of 10 times but the 10th one redeems the rest.<br /> <br /> Taking away that aspect, in my view, cheapens the world of darkness and it worse off for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659753#post659753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... or it could be that it enforces the themes of isolation from humanity as well as giving them a legitimate reason for their hubris?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bare in mind, I am not asking for the Lie's removal, only that an enemy that works totally and completely as an antagonist is a rather poor one when even when involving mere mortals, especially given the experience that Hunters have seen.<br /> <br /> The Lie works fine as it is written in Mage and as a theme within it. The issue lies beyond Mage's pages and when it enters Hunters, or when you want to involve mortals as a focus on why Magi should not be so reckless with their spells. Which is why I am happy with saying that the Lie doesn't take effect until after the scene is over but totally and completely right then and there irks me.<br /> <br /> Allows mortal ability deal with the Mage/supernatural with the Lie taking hold after covering the tracks short after. Willpower being spent is enough to keep my happy on this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T13:57:12-07:00","id":659840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659728#post659728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, this is an issue that me and Dave have spared on quite a bit. The Lie is a hard coded thing that covers all supernatural activities that humanity has no hope of ever recognizing (let alone setting up compacts or cells) because they are too stu- I mean helpless to do anything about it.<br /> <br /> Which is fine, He's the dev of the gameline and thus can write Mage how he sees fit. Just find it rather annoying in creating a mechanic that kills stories rather than creates them when it comes to Mages fucking up and having to deal with external confirmation of their hubris.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Quiescence does not prevent Sleepers from knowing about supernal magic or the Awakened, albeit the memory recall and Breaking Point issues when witnessing such magic renders it difficult. The Sleeping Curse does not trigger when witnesses other Fallen supernatural effects,<br /> <br /> Sleeper Hunters can certainly hunt the Awakened, the are just <b><i>very</i></b> difficult prey for the lower tiers who normally have no supernatural assistance, as are most other major templates such as vampires and werewolves.<br /> <br /> Moreover, as others have stated, the Quiescence doesn't kill <i>Mage</i> chronicles that are consistent with the game's own themes and setting, and most certainly doesn't immunize mages when &quot;fucking up and having to deal with external confirmation of their hubris.&quot; Most of the arguments involve <i>Mage</i> setting and mechanics making it difficult to play <i>Hunter</i> chronicles in a manner some would prefer. That is not something that Dave, as the Mage developer, needs to or should prioritize over his own game line.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659727#post659727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The knowledge magic imparts is without flaw, unless cheated by some supernatural force. A given mage's interpretation of that knowledge, and the decision about how to act upon it, varies from mage to mage, of course. A mage with high Empathy might alert her friend about the infidelity and then do her best to console the friend. A less tactful mage might confront the friend with this knowledge and demand better of their loved one. A would-be &quot;protector&quot; might then start &quot;screening&quot; potential mates with her magic. From there, it's not too far to tell the loved one just exactly who they can date, if they pass your rather strict requirements\u2014which fewer and fewer suitors do as time goes on. A truly vengeful mage might decide that the cheating bastard deserves punishment for his actions. A presumptuous one might decide that it's better to erase the memories of the betrayal\u2014indeed, the entire ruinous relationship\u2014from a devastated loved one's mind.<br /> <br /> All of this could stem from simply looking into an unfaithful spouse's mind and revealing the infidelity. Power can be a slippery slope. If knowledge is power, then a mage is standing on a muddy slope in heavy rain, trying to push a boulder up a hill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the additional explanatory comments. They are always helpful in these types of discussions.<br /> <br /> As an aside, your &quot;presumptuous mage&quot; example reminded me of <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Molly_Carpenter\" target=\"_blank\">Molly from <i>Proven Guilty</i> in the Dresden Files</a>, and how she thought she was helping her friends by using magic to try to cure their drug addictions, but was only making the problem worse.<br /> <br /> It would certainly be interesting to envision or play Mage incorporating the DF's <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Seven_Laws_of_Magic\" target=\"_blank\">Seven Laws of Magic</a> either as Gold or Silver Laws under the Lex Magica and/or the basis for Wisdom Breaking Points (more so than they are now). The uses of Mind, Death, Life and Time, and many offensive uses of all the other Arcanum against Sleepers, would certainly need to be more creative or furtive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":".  forgot to add Mind as one of the problematic Arcana under the Seven Laws of Magic. 09-10-2015, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:04:15-07:00","id":659846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659836#post659836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortals are hard coded to forget the supernatural even exists</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they forget details about particular magical acts, and that's it. They don't forget everything else that they know about the target. Remember that Dave said that the Orders will be semi public organizations in 2ed. They have Sleepers working for them that know they are mages, that know about magic, and also know that if they <i>witness</i> said magic they will be psychologically damaged. Hunters don't need to remember all the details about a spell to know that a mage is a mage, there is enough corollary information to put it together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:04:22-07:00","id":659847,"title":"","content":"Don't the Third and Fourth Laws of Magic basically ban the entire Mind Arcanum for all uses that aren't &quot;buff yourself&quot;? I feel like that wouldn't fly in a setting where fully one-fifth of all Mages necessarily have some facility with the Mind Arcanum, and several non-Mastigos Mages also do.<br /> <br /> Mind, from what I remember from Tome of the Watchtowers, the ethos and philosophy of Path Mastigos is very much in line with the fourth law - autonomy and self-determination is basically sacrosanct to a proper Mastigos, and not just their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:06:06-07:00","id":659851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659840#post659840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would certainly be interesting to envision or play Mage incorporating the DF's <a href=\"http://dresdenfiles.wikia.com/wiki/Seven_Laws_of_Magic\" target=\"_blank\">Seven Laws of Magic</a> either as Gold or Silver Laws under the Lex Magica and/or the basis for Wisdom Breaking Points (more so than they are now). The uses of Death, Life and Time, and many offensive uses of all the other Arcanum against Sleepers, would certainly need to be more creative or furtive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought the Seven Laws were made by asshole Obrimos mages. Let's them do all their stuff, but significantly hinders most of the other Paths.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:17:35-07:00","id":659859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659836#post659836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not what he said but given the description of 2ed so far, it's fairly close to the point and the focus of my complaint. Mortals are hard coded to forget the supernatural even exists which leads to various issues going down the pipe. This is a social norm of seeing something and refusing to tell anyone lest people think you insane but forgetting that said thing ever happened which irks immensely as simple human agency (and ability) is the thing that I find so attractive in nWoD. <b>Even Kindred elders can be felled with a few swings of a angry mortal taking a knife and supernatural effects can be dispelled with either spending/burning willpower. Granted, Joe blow will die 9 out of 10 times but the 10th one redeems the rest</b>.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I must not be reading the same books, particularly if your vampire reference is 2e. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Absent wild and near supernatural providence, skill, attributes,and resources, a mere &quot;angry mortal with knife&quot; will not present a realistic threat, no less be victorious against, a vampire elder, even during the day. It's one of the reasons why Hunter includes Tier 3 in order or pursue such prey, and why its monster creation system doesn't normally build monsters at the same power level of other major game line templates.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, there is a significant disconnect between portrayals and expectations of Hunters in their own game line compared to the powers, advantages, influence and resourcess of the protagonists of the other nWOD games. The Hunter 2e developer certainly will earn her pay, particularly since most of the second edition splats have received notable increases in power. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:37:11-07:00","id":659888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659851#post659851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought the Seven Laws were made by asshole Obrimos mages. Let's them do all their stuff, but significantly hinders most of the other Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you mean &quot;righteous, just and wise Obrimos mages?&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Obrimos are still pretty screwed under the SLoM. Remember, it's forbidden to kill a human with magic, even generally if it's a matter of self-defense. The use of Forces would require considerably more discretion than now. It also the reason why many mages are concerned about Harry's quite liberal use of destructive spells.<br /> <br /> Moreover, since the new Prime has some mind altering effects, it too might be limited similarly as Mind, albeit probably to a lesser degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-10-2015, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:45:29-07:00","id":659908,"title":"","content":"Is it time to reiterate the old mantra of &quot;if you need to use magic to kill someone, you're not thinking enough&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:45:47-07:00","id":659913,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd put Mages in third place for hardest PC-Splat prey for Tier 1&amp;2 Hunters.<br /> Quiescence is annoying, but can be dealth with even at that Tier and is positively a cakewalk compared to hunting a Demon that doesn't want to be found or getting rid of a Mummy and its Cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:49:02-07:00","id":659930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659840#post659840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Quiescence does not prevent Sleepers from knowing about supernal magic or the Awakened, albeit the memory recall and Breaking Point issues when witnessing such magic renders it difficult. The Sleeping Curse does not trigger when witnesses other Fallen supernatural effects,</div> </div> </div> </div>If you could point out proof that it doesn't, it would go a great way to soothing my fears. Stuff I've read about 2ed's Integrity system (and forum chats) has lead me to believe that Quiescence is not going to be limited to Mage but rather a system wide mechanic for 2ed. Which does not bode well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moreover, as others have stated, the Quiescence doesn't kill <i>Mage</i> chronicles that are consistent with the game's own themes and setting, and most certainly doesn't immunize mages when &quot;fucking up and having to deal with external confirmation of their hubris.&quot; Most of the arguments involve <i>Mage</i> setting and mechanics making it difficult to play <i>Hunter</i> chronicles in a manner some would prefer. That is not something that Dave, as the Mage developer, needs to or should prioritize over his own game line. </div> </div> </div>Apologies then, I was unaware of the &quot;Mage vs Mage&quot; in the title line. Perhaps I should read more carefully then.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:53:51-07:00","id":659936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659930#post659930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you could point out proof that it doesn't, it would go a great way to soothing my fears.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how it is and how it has always been.<br /> It's why all the development blogs specifically talk about the Lie being about Supernal magic. Could you show the official statement that makes you believe the lie applies to all supernatural effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 09-10-2015, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T14:54:29-07:00","id":659937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659930#post659930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you could point out proof that it doesn't, it would go a great way to soothing my fears. Stuff I've read about 2ed's Integrity system (and forum chats) has lead me to believe that Quiescence is not going to be limited to Mage but rather a system wide mechanic for 2ed. Which does not bode well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like the 2e Integrity rules are changing. Witnessing the supernatural is already an Integrity Breaking Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:03:44-07:00","id":659943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659930#post659930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you could point out proof that it doesn't, it would go a great way to soothing my fears. Stuff I've read about 2ed's Integrity system (and forum chats) has lead me to believe that Quiescence is not going to be limited to Mage but rather a system wide mechanic for 2ed. Which does not bode well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proof like the two 2ed game lines that are already out and don't have anything like this?<br /> <br /> Also, what about Dave saying that there are Sleepers that work for mages and know about them and magic?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:05:00-07:00","id":659944,"title":"","content":"Indeed it is! The difference is that witnessing <i>Supernal</i> and <i>Abyssal</i> supernatural effects is <i>always</i> an Integrity Breaking Point, rather than a heavily suggested one like everything else from a ghost turning up to a vampire's Celerity.<br /> <br /> Quiescence only applies to those two things. Dissonance only applies to those two things (although it works in reverse on the Abyss - Sleepers witnessing Abyssal entities heal them over time rather than slowly dispelling them).<br /> <br /> A Sleeper who sees a ghost for the first time will <i>probably</i> have a Breaking Point, and as GMC, Innocents, and plenty of other places say will feel the urge to not talk about it, but that's not the same thing as definitely suffering a breaking point and outright forgetting about it that comes from contact with the Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:09:10-07:00","id":659946,"title":"","content":"Dave, since you're here, I'll go ahead and say this.<br /> <br /> You are a fantastic writer and even though I have strong opinions about this subject, I've always admired your work.<br /> <br /> and there are no butts about this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:13:53-07:00","id":659958,"title":"","content":"Actually, this is another place where things feel inconsistent to me:<br /> \u00b7 Dave has said that the &quot;witness the supernatural&quot; Breaking Points in Integrity are a weaker manifestation of the Sleeping Curse.<br /> \u00b7 Dave has said that the Sleepwalker Merit doesn't exempt you from those those Breaking Points; only from Breaking Points caused by Supernal Magic.<br /> At least, that's how I remember it. But that feels utterly inconsistent to me: if the Integrity Breaking Points for witnessing supernatural phenomena really are part of the Curse (and a weaker part at that), then why <i>wouldn't</i> the Sleepwalker Merit exempt you from them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:23:40-07:00","id":659962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659958#post659958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, this is another place where things feel inconsistent to me:<br /> \u00b7 Dave has said that the &quot;witness the supernatural&quot; Breaking Points in Integrity are a weaker manifestation of the Sleeping Curse.<br /> \u00b7 Dave has said that the Sleepwalker Merit doesn't exempt you from those those Breaking Points; only from Breaking Points caused by Supernal Magic.<br /> At least, that's how I remember it. But that feels utterly inconsistent to me: if the Integrity Breaking Points for witnessing supernatural phenomena really are part of the Curse (and a weaker part at that), then why <i>wouldn't</i> the Sleepwalker Merit exempt you from them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume because Lie or no Lie, seeing a ghost is traumatic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:27:14-07:00","id":659964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659944#post659944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed it is! The difference is that witnessing <i>Supernal</i> and <i>Abyssal</i> supernatural effects is <i>always</i> an Integrity Breaking Point, rather than a heavily suggested one like everything else from a ghost turning up to a vampire's Celerity.<br /> <br /> Quiescence only applies to those two things. Dissonance only applies to those two things (although it works in reverse on the Abyss - Sleepers witnessing Abyssal entities heal them over time rather than slowly dispelling them).<br /> <br /> A Sleeper who sees a ghost for the first time will <i>probably</i> have a Breaking Point, and as GMC, Innocents, and plenty of other places say will feel the urge to not talk about it, but that's not the same thing as definitely suffering a breaking point and outright forgetting about it that comes from contact with the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just based on the way you're saying this I have to ask, for clarity's sake, do you mean there's <i>always </i>a Breaking Point check as in, they roll to see if they lose Integrity? Or there's always a Breaking Point as in, they automatically lose Integrity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-10-2015, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:34:58-07:00","id":659969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659962#post659962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would assume because Lie or no Lie, seeing a ghost is traumatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>More traumatic than witnessing a Supernal Spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:41:09-07:00","id":659973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659962#post659962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would assume because Lie or no Lie, seeing a ghost is traumatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lie also causes memory loss, and as we discussed earlier, unlike &quot;basic&quot; supernatural events, even a recording of supernal effects or attempts to recover memories will cause additional Breaking Points over and over again.<br /> <br /> Exposure to the supernatural is generally emotionally traumatic for normal humans. Exposure to supernal or abyssmal manifestations is much worse, as it directly damages the soul and has other deleterious effects.<br /> <br /> A mortal can inure themselves to the most of the supernatural over time or with effort, but there's no escaping the Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:48:26-07:00","id":659978,"title":"","content":"Right. But right now, I'm talking about Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> I'd find it consistent if a Sleepwalker was free from basic supernatural Breaking Points as well as Supernal ones; I'd also find it consistent if the Sleepwalker had Supernal Breaking Points downgraded from &quot;mandatory&quot; to &quot;strongly encouraged&quot; while basic supernatural Breaking Points remained in the &quot;strongly encouraged&quot; category. What strikes me as inconsistent is the idea that Sleepwalkers still suffer from basic supernatural Breaking Points but not from Supernal ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:55:15-07:00","id":659983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659969#post659969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More traumatic than witnessing a Supernal Spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the spell. Some spells would probably still be Breaking Points for Sleepwalkers. Not because they're supernal magic, but because you just don't watch someone blow someone else's head up with their mind and walk away fine. Likewise, witnessing the supernatural is not <i>necessarily</i> a Breaking Point for a Sleepwalker, but it can be, if they are traumatized by what they saw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T15:59:40-07:00","id":659986,"title":"","content":"What do you classify as &quot;basic&quot; supernatural breaking points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T16:17:08-07:00","id":660008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659978#post659978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. But right now, I'm talking about Sleepwalkers.<br /> <br /> I'd find it consistent if a Sleepwalker was free from basic supernatural Breaking Points as well as Supernal ones; I'd also find it consistent if the Sleepwalker had Supernal Breaking Points downgraded from &quot;mandatory&quot; to &quot;strongly encouraged&quot; while basic supernatural Breaking Points remained in the &quot;strongly encouraged&quot; category. What strikes me as inconsistent is the idea that Sleepwalkers still suffer from basic supernatural Breaking Points but not from Supernal ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Non-supernal or abysmal supernatural events are normally emotionally traumatic because of fear and surprise, not some inherent supernatural damage (with exceptions like Lunacy). Sleepers and Sleepwalkers should both react according to their own personal experience (and Integrity levels), with no discernible difference based on their status.<br /> <br /> Since Sleepwalker are at least partially free of the Lie and immune to the Quiescence, witnessing supernal magic does not injure their souls, and their reaction should be no different than witnessing all other supernatural events.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T16:25:57-07:00","id":660027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=659986#post659986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you classify as &quot;basic&quot; supernatural breaking points?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Witnessing anything obviously unnatural and frightening, everything from a materialized ghost or spirit or a vampire shapechanging to gibbering tentacled horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T16:27:31-07:00","id":660028,"title":"","content":"Put another way, anything that's supernatural but not Supernal and not Abyssal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T16:28:29-07:00","id":660029,"title":"","content":"You might use the term Fallen World, or Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T16:31:06-07:00","id":660040,"title":"","content":"In general, my understanding is that Integrity breaking points are caused by something that shakes your understanding of how the world works. Someone who doesn't believe in vampires discovering unequivocal proof that Vampires exist would experience one, and probably another one if they witnessed a vampire feeding for the first time (it's one thing to work out that the bloodsuckers must in fact suck blood, but it's another thing to witness how exactly it goes down), especially if the feeding was particularly brutal or violent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T17:12:41-07:00","id":660085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Juhn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=660040#post660040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, my understanding is that Integrity breaking points are caused by something that shakes your understanding of how the world works. Someone who doesn't believe in vampires discovering unequivocal proof that Vampires exist would experience one, and probably another one if they witnessed a vampire feeding for the first time (it's one thing to work out that the bloodsuckers must in fact suck blood, but it's another thing to witness how exactly it goes down), especially if the feeding was particularly brutal or violent.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of it. Ultimately, Breaking Points are just traumatic events. Having your worldview shaken can be traumatic, but it's not the only thing that can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T17:40:45-07:00","id":660131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=660028#post660028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Put another way, anything that's supernatural but not Supernal and not Abyssal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, but as noted, there are some non-supernal or abyssal supernatural effects that still are inherently dangerous apart from the standard emotional shock and fear, such as Lunacy (although a 800lb raging werewolf could potentially still cause a less experienced wolf-blooded human or mage a Breaking Point without any need for Lunacy).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T03:31:04-07:00","id":660573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=660085#post660085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's part of it. Ultimately, Breaking Points are just traumatic events. Having your worldview shaken can be traumatic, but it's not the only thing that can.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically why babies cry all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T07:59:38-07:00","id":660710,"title":"","content":"i<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=660131#post660131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally, but as noted, there are some non-supernal or abyssal supernatural effects that still are inherently dangerous apart from the standard emotional shock and fear, such as Lunacy (although a 800lb raging werewolf could potentially still cause a less experienced wolf-blooded human or mage a Breaking Point without any need for Lunacy).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages don't have Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T08:10:30-07:00","id":660719,"title":"","content":"So, they lack a wisdom trait, or they aren't called as such but there is a mechanic that depletes it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T08:31:45-07:00","id":660730,"title":"","content":"Hubris, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T08:50:30-07:00","id":660749,"title":"","content":"Dave made a comment in the dev blogs about it: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/sophias-choice-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/sophias-choic...the-awakening/</a> look for &quot;As I say in the blog, you can commit non-magical acts of hubris.&quot;<br /> <br /> The thing is, if there's a roll-based mechanic that determines if your mage loses Wisdom it's a Breaking Point by any other name. Saying something as intriguing as &quot;Mages don't have Breaking Points&quot; feels disingenuous and disappointing if that's the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:15:26-07:00","id":660778,"title":"","content":"Acts of Hubris trigger from actions the Mage takes. They're not going to suffer a Breaking Point from exposure to rampaging Werewolves. The rules for Wisdom and Integrity are very different in terms of what qualifies. Mages do not lose Wisdom from traumatic events. They lose Wisdom by being arrogant and careless and excessively imposing their will on the world.<br /> <br /> So Breaking Points are in\u200bdeed simply traumatic events. But they're an Integrity thing, not a Wisdom thing. The conditions that would generate them do not count as Acts of Hubris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 09-11-2015, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:16:33-07:00","id":660779,"title":"","content":"Integrity &quot;Breaks&quot;. Wisdom doesn't. Hubris has a different effect on Wisdom (from a narrative perspective) than Breaking Points have on Integrity, even if in both cases it's a number going from 10 to 0. The names are different to represent what a change in Wisdom actually IS than a change in Integrity. Humanity-loss rolls are called &quot;Detachment&quot; rolls rather than Breaking Points, because that's what's happening when you lose Humanity. You become more detached from your own humanity (and humanity at large), rather than your mental stability and worldview (i.e. integrity) breaking in response to trauma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:19:24-07:00","id":660782,"title":"","content":"As I understand it:<br /> <br /> With a sleeper, a Breaking Point is your soul trying to deal with something it isn't equipped to deal with. Your Integrity is shattered.<br /> <br /> With a mage, an Act of Hubris is your soul trying to deal with you making Supernally unwise decisions. Your Wisdom is compromised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6770,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","user":"Midgardener","date":". 09-11-2015, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:25:24-07:00","id":660793,"title":"","content":"Your soul, technically, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:31:58-07:00","id":660798,"title":"","content":"From what I remember spells that affect Wisdom are Death-based rather than Mind-based specifically because Wisdom measures the health of the soul, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:54:48-07:00","id":660826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=660793#post660793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your soul, technically, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent point. Edited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T11:52:38-07:00","id":660949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=660710#post660710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i<br /> <br /> Mages don't have Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, yes indeed, mages make degeneration checks for acts of Hubris.<br /> <br /> I'm still confused over what events that would cause a Sleeper or otherwise human Sleepwalker to risk Integrity also require a mage degeneration check, particularly since the relevant traits are no longer tied to morality (although acts like murder still seem to apply to both traits).<br /> <br /> As per my original example, a wolf-blooded who would otherwise be immune to Lunacy, but has the Integrity trait, would still apparently suffer a breaking point if confronted by a rampaging werewolf due to the psychological trauma (at least the first time such an event occurred). Would a mage similarly need to make a degeneration check her first time confronting such a supernaturally dangerous and frightening situation, or is Wisdom only potentially compromised when a mage ignores the consequences of her actions (and certain other highly unethical acts?) ?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T12:54:43-07:00","id":660983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=657044#post657044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the sake of the white room, we must ignore rotes. If the master has her instant-death spell as a rote, then she's re-rolling failures on the spellcasting roll.<br /> <br /> And if she gets an exceptional success, one of the things she can do is remove the Withstood property of the spell. In which case, our increasingly-beleaguered Werewolf is simply shit out of luck.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know it's a little late for open development, but, I have some pretty big issues with this. Basically, being able to remove the withstood property with an exceptional success seems to undermine a lot of the design intent of the new spell casting system in the first place. What's the point having to guess your opponent's withstand trait and spell factoring appropriately, when you can make it irrelevant with an exceptional success? Especially in the case of a &quot;save or die&quot; effect. Now you have the option to make it just die? How is a storyteller supposed to introduce conflict to a group of players once they become masters? How am I to have cool fight scenes involving my Adamantine Arrow mage when the solution is &quot;I cast my death spell, I win.&quot;. I know that game balance isn't a concern in cross over, but this seems to blow things up in terms of my ability as a story teller to introduce legitimate threats to my players without resorting to the exact same type of tactics, which, reducing violent conflicts to an initiative roll (or contest of wills roll in the case of both of them having &quot;I go first&quot; effects) doesn't sound like fun at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T13:41:47-07:00","id":661041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=660983#post660983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I know it's a little late for open development, but, I have some pretty big issues with this. Basically, being able to remove the withstood property with an exceptional success seems to undermine a lot of the design intent of the new spell casting system in the first place. What's the point having to guess your opponent's withstand trait and spell factoring appropriately, when you can make it irrelevant with an exceptional success? Especially in the case of a &quot;save or die&quot; effect. Now you have the option to make it just die? How is a storyteller supposed to introduce conflict to a group of players once they become masters? How am I to have cool fight scenes involving my Adamantine Arrow mage when the solution is &quot;I cast my death spell, I win.&quot;. I know that game balance isn't a concern in cross over, but this seems to blow things up in terms of my ability as a story teller to introduce legitimate threats to my players without resorting to the exact same type of tactics, which, reducing violent conflicts to an initiative roll (or contest of wills roll in the case of both of them having &quot;I go first&quot; effects) doesn't sound like fun at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be fair, even ignoring the instant kill type effects this only really applies to Master level mages or mages with decent amounts of prep. Anything else is simply lacking the dicepool to ever realistically be able to pull this off consistently.It's a pretty do or die/all or nothing style tactic. If you spend no dice modifying the spell purely in an attempt to get an exceptional success you'll either succeed and have it work or you'll fail and it will do nothing since you didn't put anything into potency.<br /> <br /> Also, just throw things at them that cause Clash of Wills. Even if the spell isn't Withstood it can still be clashed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T14:03:14-07:00","id":661061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wild-Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=660983#post660983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I know it's a little late for open development, but, I have some pretty big issues with this. Basically, being able to remove the withstood property with an exceptional success seems to undermine a lot of the design intent of the new spell casting system in the first place. What's the point having to guess your opponent's withstand trait and spell factoring appropriately, when you can make it irrelevant with an exceptional success? Especially in the case of a &quot;save or die&quot; effect. Now you have the option to make it just die? How is a storyteller supposed to introduce conflict to a group of players once they become masters? How am I to have cool fight scenes involving my Adamantine Arrow mage when the solution is &quot;I cast my death spell, I win.&quot;. I know that game balance isn't a concern in cross over, but this seems to blow things up in terms of my ability as a story teller to introduce legitimate threats to my players without resorting to the exact same type of tactics, which, reducing violent conflicts to an initiative roll (or contest of wills roll in the case of both of them having &quot;I go first&quot; effects) doesn't sound like fun at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The design of the new spell system explicitly provides for instant death effects. However, they require mastery of an Arcana and actually rolling an exceptional success if Withstood mechanics are rendered void. In order to generally have a chance on the roll with such a spell, it requires the master to spend XP to purchase a relevant rote for a 5 dot spell, and even the rote hardly guarantees rolling an exceptional success. If you gambled on an exceptional success and failed, likely not taking any spellcasting penalties to increase potency (although other roll penalties might have been necessary for issues such as target size as with the earlier Garau-form example), the spell will have absolutely no effect on your likely very powerful and angry adversary.<br /> <br /> Simply, the circumstance of which you complain only involves very high level and already extremely powerful characters, who've intentionally spent substantial XP for a very specific type of attack, using it hardly ensures an exceptional success guaranteeing a &quot;die, no save&quot; effect, and gambling on such a success and failing usually renders the spell useless and the mage vulnerable.<br /> <br /> I really don't see the problem, with or without crossover.<br /> <br /> Edit: And as Ashenrogue correctly observes, a target may indeed have a particular immunity or resistance to such an attack or an ability that provides a Clash of Wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-11-2015, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T16:16:46-07:00","id":661216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=661041#post661041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, even ignoring the instant kill type effects this only really applies to Master level mages or mages with decent amounts of prep. Anything else is simply lacking the dicepool to ever realistically be able to pull this off consistently.It's a pretty do or die/all or nothing style tactic. If you spend no dice modifying the spell purely in an attempt to get an exceptional success you'll either succeed and have it work or you'll fail and it will do nothing since you didn't put anything into potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because known twinks* won't just make the use of those spells with a rote and take every precaution to be as conflict-crushing as possible. And with all the conditions that make rolling exceptional successes on 3 instead of 5 successes? Please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 09-11-2015, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T19:09:02-07:00","id":661371,"title":"","content":"If you're having trouble with twinks then chances are you'd have trouble with them regardless of whether Withstood could be removed or not. If you want to deal with that problem then <i>deal with that problem</i>. Don't bother trying to treat the symptoms of the issue, go deal with the source of the issue itself. If you have someone gaming the system in a way that makes it less enjoyable for everyone else, talk to that player about it.<br /> <br /> Now if twinking a PC isn't a problem, who cares? Let them do it, just design encounters with that in mind. You cannot prep for everything. It is literally impossible. Play your cards close to your chest, and keep some twists in store just in case. And has there been anything mentioned so far that lets you get an exceptional success on 3 rather than 5 on a spellcasting roll? If so I'm not recalling it off of the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T19:33:23-07:00","id":661387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=661371#post661371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And has there been anything mentioned so far that lets you get an exceptional success on 3 rather than 5 on a spellcasting roll? If so I'm not recalling it off of the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Praxes gain an exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 (and don't cost a point of mana to cast if not of a mage's ruling Arcanum), <br /> <br /> Note that rotes and praxes do not stack. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/545969-making-rotes-a-straight-dice-bonus?p=547483#post547483\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/545969-making-rotes-a-straight-dice-bonus?p=547483#post547483\"> Making Rotes a straight +dice bonus - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/545969-making-rotes-a-straight-dice-bonus?p=547483#post547483\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/545969-making-rotes-a-straight-dice-bonus?p=547483#post547483 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm currently rewriting parts of the mage system to conform more to my noWoD world I'm building (an amalgam of the old world of darkness and the new world of darkness) and since I've never really liked how rotes are handled in Awakening, I thought about remaking them into a straight up die bonus instead of </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T19:47:20-07:00","id":661398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=661387#post661387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Praxes gain an exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 (and don't cost a point of mana to cast if not of a mage's ruling Arcanum),<br /> <br /> Note that rotes and praxes do not stack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/545969-making-rotes-a-straight-dice-bonus?p=547483#post547483\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/545969-making-rotes-a-straight-dice-bonus?p=547483#post547483\"> Making Rotes a straight +dice bonus - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/545969-making-rotes-a-straight-dice-bonus?p=547483#post547483\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/545969-making-rotes-a-straight-dice-bonus?p=547483#post547483 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm currently rewriting parts of the mage system to conform more to my noWoD world I'm building (an amalgam of the old world of darkness and the new world of darkness) and since I've never really liked how rotes are handled in Awakening, I thought about remaking them into a straight up die bonus instead of </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>So Praxes make it at least reasonably possible (not necessarily likely) to pull it off at lower levels, but are completely outmatched by rotes come Mastery. But, without the free Reach from rotes it will be a bit more dangerous to cast in a single turn (requiring 2 Reach) since you'll need to go beyond what you can safely cast and cause paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T19:57:29-07:00","id":661404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=661398#post661398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Praxes make it at least reasonably possible (not necessarily likely) to pull it off at lower levels, but are completely outmatched by rotes come Mastery. But, without the free Reach from rotes it will be a bit more dangerous to cast in a single turn (requiring 2 Reach) since you'll need to go beyond what you can safely cast and cause paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that the re-roll failed rolls mechanic (rote action) only apply to rotes used by the master who created them or if cast from a grimoire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T20:09:07-07:00","id":661415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=661404#post661404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that the re-roll failed rolls mechanic (rote action) only apply to rotes used by the master who created them or if cast from a grimoire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. When I was referring to rotes I was talking about a Masters personal rotes. If you're only going after exceptional successes you'd probably be best off using a Praxis pre-Master rote. The -2 to exceptional success requirements should usually equal or outweigh the dice you'd get from just adding a skill (unless you magically increased your skill rating beyond base limitations). making it more efficient when looking to remove the Withstood property altogether. At mastery though, you get the all important rote action which will probably do more for you assuming a decent starting dicepool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T19:34:56-07:00","id":662552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/644997-hunters-vs-mages?p=661371#post661371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're having trouble with twinks then chances are you'd have trouble with them regardless of whether Withstood could be removed or not. If you want to deal with that problem then <i>deal with that problem</i>. Don't bother trying to treat the symptoms of the issue, go deal with the source of the issue itself. If you have someone gaming the system in a way that makes it less enjoyable for everyone else, talk to that player about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My usual outlet for gameplay is online, in massive chronicles where said twinks slip thru the cracks and then fuck your shit up with gleeful &quot;Lulz&quot; OOC comments after ludicrous rolls that, in the first edition of games? wouldn't be Instant-Death at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T02:57:38-07:00","id":1512704,"title":"","content":"As a postmortem for this topic: when <b>Mage: the Awakening 2e</b> finally came out, it included a \u201cFitful Slumber\u201d Merit (p.306) that requires a Sleeper to experience three Breaking Points due to exposure to the Supernal or Abyss and then spend the experience needed to buy the one-dot Merit. The character is then considered to be a Sleepwalker, and gets a +2 bonus to resist Supernal or Abyssal Breaking Points.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, when <b>Hunter: the Vigil 2e</b> finally came out, it turned out that The Code is now the defining feature that sets hunters apart from regular mortals (not Practical Experience as I had suggested in this thread; and in fact, Practical Experience didn't even make the cut for the Second Edition), as it modifies Integrity to make the persistent hunting of supernatural creatures more tolerable: in particular, Breaking Points for witnessing supernatural phenomena are, at least for hunters, explicitly only made for first-time encounters, thus short-circuiting the death spiral of repeated exposure that was discussed in this thread.<br /> t<br /> Supernal/Abyssal Breaking Points aren't explicitly addressed in <b>Hunter 2e</b>; and that's to be expected. But in keeping withvi<br /> the observations made in this thread, they should be an<br /> exception to the \u201cfirst time only\u201d modification to Integrity Breaking Points that <b>Hunter</b> establishes: whenever the Quiescence clouds a person's memories, he gets reset to \u201cfirst time\u201d status the next time he encounters it. If you want hunters who aren't in an Integrity death-spiral against Awakened phenomena, that's what the aforementioned Fitful Slumber Merit in <b>Mage</b> is for. Presumably, the \u201cfirst time\u201d principle still applies to Supernal phenomena once Fitful Slumber is in place: Sleepwalker status doesn't make you <i>immune</i> to Supernal Breaking Points; it just means that they're no more severe or persistent for the Sleepwalker than regular exposure to supernatural phenomena would be.<br /> <br /> As well, there's a \u201cFreeing Mind\u201d Tactic (pp 160\u2013161) which can be triggered by \u201ca Mental or Social effect imposed by a supernatural power or phenomenon\u2026 [such as] unnatural memory loss.\u201d This effectively encompasses the \u201cAfter Action Report\u201d idea I floated in this topic, and gives hunters who <i>don't</i> have Fitful Slumber a way to cope with Quiescence \u2014 unless the Storyteller decides that it wouldn't apply, due to the nature of Quiescence. <br /> <hr /><br /> I'm satisfied with this. Fitful Slumber provides a way for hunters who repeatedly go up against the Awakened to develop Sleepwalker status on their own, but in a way that doesn't treat it as something that would happen to <i>every </i>Sleeper frequently exposed to Awakened phenomena, or even to most of them; only a select few. And it does so in a way that's compatible with the notion of every hunter in a cell developing it if that cell has prolonged exposure to Awakened phenomena. In fact, in conjunction with <b>Hunter 2e</b>'s Group Beats (which, among other things, are earned whenever multiple members of a cell experience a breaking point in the same scene), it's to be expected that a hunter cell that experiences prolonged exposure to Awakened phenomena will likely end up with all of its members having Fitful Slumber. And Freeing Mind helps in cases where Fitful Slumber isn't in place, while still retaining the notion that Sleepers overcoming Quiescence is anything but routine: Tactics require the principle actor to risk Willpower, and the target must spend Willpower to benefit from Freeing Mind. <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that hunters will now trounce mages whenever they encounter each other, of course; far from it. But Quiescence is no longer the absolutely insurmountable barrier that it was originally going to be; and the games have not suffered for it.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}